window.AKK_AFTER_TRANSMIGRATING_AS_A_TYCOONS_WIFE_MY_THOUGHTS_ARE_HEARD_BY_THE_WHOLE_FAMILY_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AFTER_TRANSMIGRATING_AS_A_TYCOONS_WIFE_MY_THOUGHTS_ARE_HEARD_BY_THE_WHOLE_FAMILY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301: Anyway, they both know it","paragraphs":["Ji Fei was truly stunned by the gossip she was consuming, never expecting another person to be involved in this complex web of ethical relationships.","The Qin family, on the other hand, was shocked by Ji Fei's thoughts, so much so that they couldn't control their facial expressions.","Who?","Yu Yi, the youngest son of the Yu Family patriarch?","Having an affair with his older brother's new wife?","Originally, they thought it was just Ke Yun'er's wild imagination, trying to dabble in some stepmother romance.","Now they realized, it was actually an earlier case of brother-in-law and sister-in-law drama.","Just then, the reception time was almost over, and Yu's Father returned to the venue.","He looked displeased, mumbling to himself.","Probably complaining about his son and younger brother being unreliable, leaving him to greet the guests alone, unaware of his poor health.","Yu's Father didn't notice the continuous sympathetic glances from the Qin family.","After all, being married to someone who constantly cheats on him is quite pitiful.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei was sorting through the complex gossip information, the most crucial being that she hadn't even met Ke Yun'er yet, so many details were missing, making her gossip-eating experience quite frustrating.","However, Qin Xian was a mature assistant, pulling Ji Fei towards the balcony.","Bai Xiaoxi seemed to have realized something, her eyes still teary, about to speak, but Qin Xian shushed her with a gesture.","Fortunately, Bai Xiaoxi was naive enough, still immersed in her own emotions, not questioning why the two suddenly appeared here, acting so casually and eavesdropping.","Her mind was full of Yu Yue agreeing to consider having a child with someone else, while next door, Yu Yi was also questioning this matter.","She knew she was the one who caused this, she knew it was all her fault, she could compensate Ke Yun'er in any way, but Yu Yue... Yu Yue...","She didn't want to let him go.","Yet, she couldn't help but waver.","She naturally believed that Yu Yue wouldn't change his heart, she knew Yu Yue loved her, but... maybe Yu Yue also wanted his own child.","After all, Yu Yue never had a complete family since he was young.","And that was something she could never give him.","Bai Xiaoxi bit her lip in pain, tasting blood, a pain unknown to outsiders.","She thought, maybe Yu Yue still wanted to be with her, but being with her meant he couldn't have his own offspring, so he hesitated, wanting to use this method to leave behind a child of his own, without her knowing.","The more Bai Xiaoxi thought, the more resentful she became, yet she felt she had no right to resent.","She had always been naive, well-protected by her family and Yu Yue, completely isolated from these real-life issues, not given much chance to think deeply, but that was like a layer of illusionary bubbles, destined to burst one day.","She just didn't expect this setback to be so unbearable.","If she asked Yu Yue to only be with her, not to agree to Ke Yun'er's demands, wouldn't that be selfish?","However, Bai Xiaoxi seemed to have forgotten one thing, the photo that caused Ke Yun'er's miscarriage, the fleeting suspicion she once had, was now being revealed next door.","The conversation from the next room clearly reached them.","All three heard Ke Yun'er's panicked voice.","Unlike Ji Fei and Bai Xiaoxi, Qin Xian always analyzed things objectively, so he found Ke Yun'er's tone strange.","It wasn't the way someone would speak to their lover, but rather... the panic of having a secret discovered by an outsider they barely knew.","\"You... what are you talking about, you must have misheard.\"","\"I heard it clearly, the child is gone, caused by Yu Yue's girlfriend, so you threatened Yu Yue to commit adultery with you, wanting to have another child behind my older brother's back, so he would raise your grandson as his son, you're really something, so now you're targeting Yu Yue!\" Yu Yi was full of anger, looking like a betrayed partner.","In Ke Yun'er's eyes, it was the fury of a secret being exposed by her husband's relatives.","Ke Yun'er's face turned pale, \"You, you have no proof.\"","\"You still deny it, then I'll take you to the hospital right now to see if there's still a child.\"","Ke Yun'er's tears instantly fell, truly threatened.","Seeing her cry, Yu Yi was momentarily stunned.","\"What do you want? Stop me, or expose me?\" Ke Yun'er asked hoarsely. She was at a loss for what to do now, this unexpected turn of events was something she hadn't planned for, was all her planning going to fail?","Yu Yi's expression changed several times, but he said, \"I know your goal is to continue being the Yu Family's madam, but... you have to give me an answer, that child, the one who miscarried... wasn't my older brother's, was it?!\"","Ji Fei, who had been in a daze, finally reacted upon hearing this.","[Goodness, what kind of situation is this? Two months ago at a family gathering, Yu Yi got drunk and slept in the old mansion's room, only to wake up and find himself with his older brother's new wife, immediately scared... wait, what exactly is Ke Yun'er trying to do?]","The Qin family also waited a long time for this follow-up explanation.","But this doesn't seem right.","If it was at the old mansion, everyone had their own rooms, Yu Yi in his own room, how did he end up with Ke Yun'er. And since Yu Yi was drunk, was Ke Yun'er also drunk? So this must have been Ke Yun'er's voluntary act.","But according to Ke Yun'er's earlier story, even if she had an affair, the target should have been Yu Yue, why would it be with Yu Yi...","Qin Xian's brow furrowed deeper as he listened, feeling the logic didn't add up.","[Yu Yi also couldn't understand how things turned out this way, even if he was spoiled and had a messy private life, he wouldn't cheat with his own family, so he didn't dare face Ke Yun'er, fearing she'd wake up and cause a scene, at that time he didn't have time to think about what happened, so he left as fast as he could... wow, this guy really ran faster than a rabbit! Was he afraid of being blackmailed by this outrageous woman?]","The Qin family also found it quite speechless, this man didn't seem to take any responsibility.","[After calming down, Yu Yi secretly inquired and found out that his older brother hadn't made any moves, so he slightly relaxed, thinking it was just a one-night stand, an accident that would be kept discreet, but then a month later he heard that his sister-in-law was pregnant, and that really kept him up at night, because according to the timeline, the child could also be his, but he didn't dare to question, just hid like a turtle.]","Qin Family: If you want to be a turtle, be one properly, now that the child is gone, you have the face to come and question. Are you regretting it, wanting to confirm whose child it was?","\"What do you mean by asking like that, that child... that child was definitely my husband's.\" Ke Yun'er immediately became nervous.","\"Was it? My older brother's fertility has long been an issue, who knows if he was still functional when he was with you, maybe that's why you were at the old mansion that night...\"","\"You!\" Ke Yun'er's face turned pale in an instant.","Yu Yi paused, not bearing to say more. Anyway, they both knew the truth!"]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302: Is this plan to make Yu Yue take the blame","paragraphs":["【So that's how it is. Since he heard that Ke Yun'er was conspiring with Yu Yue for such a thing, he has already begun to suspect that the night in question was Ke Yun'er deliberately coming to his room and climbing into his bed. After all, he remembers being completely drunk that night, and it was Yu Yue who helped him back to his room. So, there's no way he could have forced Ke Yun'er.】","【And Ke Yun'er being in bed with him must have been premeditated. They barely spoke before, so it must have been for some ulterior motive. Perhaps, to solidify her position, she wanted to get pregnant with his child!】","Qin Family: Is that really the case?","Qin Xian was slightly taken aback. Yu Yue was involved in this story? Why did he suddenly have a strange thought?","Could it be...","Qin Xian was full of suspicion but remained calm, quietly taking out his phone.","Bai Xiaoxi, lost in her own thoughts, was listening in a daze, eventually becoming fully absorbed.","Bai Xiaoxi: Isn't that child Uncle's?!","If she and Yu Yue were caught up in this, wouldn't it be a huge joke?","Bai Xiaoxi's expression froze.","Yu Yi paused and continued, \"I only want the truth. If you tell me the truth, I can promise you... this secret won't be revealed.\"","Ke Yun'er was stunned, looking at Yu Yi in disbelief. She didn't trust that he would be so kind; maybe he had other demands.","Seeing her guarded expression, Yu Yi said impatiently, \"Would it benefit me to reveal it? I'm not stupid.\"","【You're not stupid, but you've got other ideas. I never thought you'd be such a turtle—not hiding your head, but sticking it out to eat meat!】","Ji Fei's inner thoughts immediately turned sarcastic, clearly seeing through something.","The Qin Family was curious: What does that mean? Isn't Yu Yi just trying to find out if the child is his?","Qin Xian raised an eyebrow, smirking. Why does he need to know?","【Tsk tsk tsk, just because of that incident, he's been carefully observing Ke Yun'er for a long time. With the connection of a possible shared child, is it because he's developed feelings, or is it that wretched possessiveness? He feels that even if Ke Yun'er wanted to use someone else to have a child, she shouldn't have gone after Yu Yue; she should have continued with him.】","【If Ke Yun'er chooses Yu Yue over him now, he'll feel like he's lost to his nephew. It'll bother him, as Ke Yun'er was once his woman, and almost the mother of his child. Even if their relationship can never be public for safety reasons, he doesn't want Ke Yun'er to hook up with Yu Yue.】","【So now, is he awkwardly hinting, reminding, and subtly offering himself? I'm laughing. Earlier, I thought he wasn't trying to deliberately give his brother a green hat, but now...】","Ji Fei's complaints about Yu Yi didn't seem to end.","The Qin Family almost burst out laughing.","They looked even more sympathetically at Yu's Father, who was preparing for a wedding in the distance.","Do you know your brother is thinking about continuing the family line for you? It's like a competition for the position!","Living in the high-society circle, the Qin Family knew that the moral compass of the wealthy was fluid, but this was the first time they'd seen it shift so quickly.","It was barely tolerable as an accidental setup before, but now it's actively writing incestuous romance?!","One word: incredible!","Without Ji Fei's inner thoughts, Bai Xiaoxi, as the only one hearing the conversation, was completely confused, not understanding what Yu Yi was trying to convey.","Naturally, Ke Yun'er, who was talking to Yu Yi, also couldn't figure it out. She only thought that Yu Yi believed exposing them wouldn't benefit him, so he might use it as leverage.","Ke Yun'er could only think of family inheritance battles; perhaps Yu Yi could be her ally. Since he hadn't completely shut the door, she still had a chance to turn things around.","As Ke Yun'er pondered, Yu Yi grew impatient, ready to just lay it all out. He even took a step forward, wanting to get closer to Ke Yun'er.","Then, Ke Yun'er suddenly spoke in a low voice, \"Your guess is correct. That's the child of me and Yu Yue.\"","Those words were like a thunderclap, shocking everyone in both rooms.","Ji Fei and Qin Xian: Impossible!","Bai Xiaoxi's face lost all color. The uncomfortable moments she had seen between Ke Yun'er and Yu Yue finally connected, leading to that photo and... Yu Yue's recent words about considering it.","Her heart felt like it was being squeezed, tears falling silently.","Yu Yi also froze, looking at Ke Yun'er in disbelief. \"You... him...?\"","Could it be that they had been involved for a long time?!","Ke Yun'er didn't understand his reaction, continuing, \"Why are you acting like this? Isn't this the truth you wanted? You already knew. At the old mansion, I slept with Yu Yue. It was... an accident, but you're right, your brother couldn't have made me pregnant. It was that night's accident. Only now, the child is gone, and it was Bai Xiaoxi who caused it! That's why I asked Yu Yue to give me another child, but he... maybe he doesn't want to make that mistake again.\"","Bai Xiaoxi could barely stand, collapsing to the ground.","Ji Fei and Qin Xian were left speechless.","Facing this explanation, Yu Yi's face showed a mix of emotions, stuttering for a while before saying, \"You... how... it's him? Wait, no, it wasn't an accident. So that night, you originally planned to get into Yu Yue's bed? You set up Yu Yue! Why? How...?\"","Ke Yun'er's face finally showed unease, as if her cover had been torn off. \"It wasn't a setup. I just... just...\"","Ke Yun'er couldn't find the words to explain.","Ji Fei couldn't hold back anymore. This twisty, explosive revelation was too much! Her inner thoughts poured out.","【So... Ke Yun'er got the wrong person. She thought she slept with Yu Yue, thought the child was theirs. No wonder she's always been that way with Yu Yue! I get it now. Yu Yi said he left early that morning, so Ke Yun'er never found out the truth. She thought Yu Yue ran away because he didn't want to face it, convinced that Yu Yue knew what happened and that the child might be his. That's why things have been so confusing.】","【Yu Yi's rambling just now accidentally revealed the truth. Wait, now Yu Yi seems to be backing off. Since Ke Yun'er was mistaken from the start, why take the risk? No one knows he was involved, so he can hide again? You're really good at passing the buck, planning to let Yu Yue take the blame?!】"]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303: The Love Story from Ke Yun'er's Lips","paragraphs":["The Qin family was stunned upon hearing this, and just as they spotted Yu Yue coming downstairs to look for someone, their sympathetic gaze shifted from Yu's Father to Yu Yue.","One wearing a green hat, the other bearing the black pot—it was truly an unlucky father and son duo!","Qin Xian hadn't expected so many misunderstandings to be involved. It seemed that some people only saw what they wanted to see, never questioning whether there was anything unreasonable about it.","However... Ke Yun'er had indeed been targeting Yu Yue from the beginning, so there had been a connection between them before, though Yu Yue didn't remember this girl.","As he was pondering this, he heard Ke Yun'er finally speak up next door.","Perhaps Yu Yi's expression was too varied, making Ke Yun'er feel uneasy.","Ke Yun'er was quite skilled at reading people. Observing that Yu Yi seemed more emotional and somewhat macho, she thought that playing the sympathy card, acting pitiful, and seeking compassion might be more effective.","So, facing the questioning she had misinterpreted, she ultimately chose to confess.","\"I didn't mean to,\" Ke Yun'er's voice trembled.","\"That night, I really... just wanted to leave one last beautiful memory, to bring an end to our feelings, so I took advantage of him being drunk... I never expected to get pregnant, and I didn't plan to have Yu Yue acknowledge the child, so I never discussed it with him. I just didn't expect the child to be unlucky and not make it into this world, leaving us all in trouble instead.\" Ke Yun'er's voice was mournful, evoking pity, and even Yu Yi was momentarily stunned.","\"What do you mean? Did you two know each other before? Did you have some kind of emotional entanglement?\" Yu Yi was genuinely curious and surprised, more than anything else.","“Yes, we knew each other long ago, and we were together once,” Ke Yun'er’s voice was exceptionally serious.","[What's going on? Lying, Ke Yun'er must be lying to deceive Yu Yi, since Yu Yue doesn't remember her at all, how could... Could she be a plastic surgery freak, with a changed identity?!】","Qin Xian raised an eyebrow; it was impossible. Perhaps, like that one night's accident, Ke Yun'er merely believed there was an emotional connection.","After all, since college, their small circle had known each other's situations, and everyone knew that Yu Yue's life had only revolved around Bai Xiaoxi from the start.","They were inseparable in college.","Later, the two went abroad to study. Originally, they had planned to go to the same country, but Bai's family unexpectedly changed Bai Xiaoxi's destination, resulting in a long-distance relationship.","Even so, they stayed in constant contact daily, until Yu Yue couldn't take it anymore. In less than half a year, he dropped out of school and ran to find Bai Xiaoxi. That clingy intensity, how could there be room for another woman?","Ji Fei and Qin Xian both dismissed the idea from their perspectives, only to hear faint sobs.","It was then that they noticed Bai Xiaoxi was there.","At this moment, Bai Xiaoxi seemed on the verge of collapse.","Due to the photos that had influenced her first, she couldn't fully trust Yu Yue as Ji Fei and Qin Xian did.","She covered her mouth with her hands, but still couldn't suppress her sobs.","Ji Fei quickly crouched down, hugging Bai Xiaoxi and letting her cry in her arms, while comforting her, \"It must be fake, all fake, you have to believe in Yu Yue, we'll go ask him clearly later.\"","Such matters were easy to resolve. If it weren't for the ongoing drama next door, Ji Fei could have taken Bai Xiaoxi to find Yu Yue right away.","But since Ke Yun'er had already started spreading lies and rumors, they had to uncover the whole lie, asking everything clearly to avoid any misunderstandings and further problems.","Leaving such loopholes was something that only happened in cheesy dramas. With the gossip master Ji Fei here, that definitely wouldn't happen.","The conversation next door continued.","Yu Yi naturally couldn't believe Ke Yun'er's story.","This time, Ke Yun'er presented a poignant love tale.","It turned out that Ke Yun'er and Yu Yue had been high school classmates. One was from an ordinary family, the other a wealthy young master, and they weren't even in the same class, just the same grade, so it was unlikely they would have known each other.","At that time, Yu Yue hadn't met Bai Xiaoxi yet. He was still that rebellious, world-weary scion, often skipping classes to nap in the infirmary, then staying out late partying.","Ke Yun'er first saw him in the infirmary. She had fainted during gym class due to anemia and was brought in to rest. Lying in the bed next to Yu Yue, she glimpsed him through the fluttering curtains, describing him as a handsome young master who looked like an angel fallen to earth, yet exuded an aura of loneliness.","When Ji Fei heard this description, she momentarily shifted from her mocking mood to being amused.","[An angel? An angel fallen to earth??】","Qin Xian's mouth twitched; perhaps this was what they called \"beauty is in the eye of the beholder.\"","Bai Xiaoxi's expression, however, finally changed, showing a hint of envy. Perhaps she was envious that Ke Yun'er had met Yu Yue earlier than she had...","\"At that time, I fell in love with him at first sight. I secretly inquired about him and learned about his situation. It turned out he had lost his mother since childhood, and his father didn't care about him, which was why he seemed so lonely. I felt sorry for him and wanted to make him less lonely, so I often went to the infirmary to see him.\"","\"At first, I didn't dare talk to him, but one day, he had a fever and was thirsty in his sleep. That's when I finally got to know him. The time we spent in the infirmary became our secret. He was very nice to me then, often sharing food and drinks, but he never talked about his inner turmoil. He would just occasionally stare outside. I really wanted to get closer to his heart, but time was too short. We went to different universities, and I didn't even get to say goodbye before I lost contact with him.\"","[Although it sounds like a melancholy teenage crush, why does it feel so strange? If they really spent so much time together, how come Yu Yue doesn't remember? He hasn't lost his memory; about high school, he barely had the mood to make friends, his memories are mostly of his underlings and hangers-on.]","Qin Xian: Maybe it's beautifying memories.","[And most importantly, that was ages ago; what kind of contact information didn't they have? How did they lose touch? Did Yu Yue never give her any contact details? Not even adding each other as friends?]","Qin Xian almost laughed out loud: Ji Fei spotted the blind spot.","But Ke Yun'er's story was so moving that even Bai Xiaoxi was swayed, even feeling that they might have had a beautiful, fleeting moment during their high school days.","What about herself, who had been pursued by Yu Yue right after starting university?","Of course, Bai Xiaoxi wasn't the only one affected; even the clueless Yu Yi was moved. He asked, \"Then what do you mean by 'being together'? When was that?\"","Ke Yun'er lowered her eyes and said, \"I tried hard to find out about him, but by the time I found him, he was already dating Bai Xiaoxi. So I could only quietly watch from afar, never daring to approach again, until I heard he went abroad to study without Bai Xiaoxi, and then I appeared before him once more.\""]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304: So... is it another one of Ke Yun'er's own delusions","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Ji Fei didn't know how to evaluate Ke Yun'er.","【So... what level of infatuation is this? Uh... it's quite inspiring, actually. For a man, she worked hard to study, save money, and even went to the same school abroad. Not many people can go to such lengths for someone they secretly love.】","The Qin Family, quietly enjoying the drama, couldn't help but admire Ke Yun'er. Did she really follow him all the way to a foreign country?","Qin Xian, however, raised an eyebrow. During that time, there was no news of anyone appearing by Yu Yue's side. Instead, he was flying back and forth to see Bai Xiaoxi every few days, as if he were suffering from lovesickness.","Back then, Yu Yue's catchphrase was, \"One day apart feels like three autumns.\"","And at this moment, Bai Xiaoxi seemed to recall that period as well.","At that time... she hadn't deliberately broken their promise. It was because her health had taken a turn for the worse, and her family decided to secretly take her elsewhere for treatment. That's why she hadn't studied with Yu Yue. But later, Yu Yue still followed her.","Back then, Yu Yue's feelings were so sincere. How could he have fallen for someone else just because she wasn't by his side?","Could it be that he found out about her condition and wavered?","Bai Xiaoxi didn't want to think that way, but she couldn't help but feel inferior.","Ke Yun'er's reminiscences were like slow knives for Bai Xiaoxi, and now, the knife was about to pierce her heart.","\"They weren't broken up at that time, were they?\" Yu Yi asked doubtfully.","Ke Yun'er, however, chuckled bitterly. \"I only found out after I arrived, but at the same time, I learned something else.\"","Her tone suddenly changed, and Yu Yi was taken aback. \"What?\"","\"Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi were together solely because your family elders forced him. The goal was to forge a marriage alliance with the Bai family. You treated him as a tool for marriage, depriving him of his freedom and the right to be happy.\" Ke Yun'er spoke as if she were deeply pained for Yu Yue, even directing her resentment toward Yu Yi.","【What marriage alliance? What forced arrangement? So, Ke Yun'er really meant that when she talked to Bai Xiaoxi before? How did she hear about it, and how did she come to that conclusion?】","The Qin Family found this quite laughable. If Yu Yue wanted to deceive someone, he wouldn't need to go to such lengths.","Even as outsiders, they could occasionally see the sweet, pure happiness between the two fools. How could that be an act?","Even if we take a step back, does Yu Yue need to act? He's too lazy to pretend to be filial to his father, and he only returns to the Yu family when absolutely necessary. Could he be threatened?","What is Ke Yun'er doing? Is she deceiving Yu Yi, or is she deluding herself?","Qin Xian had already concluded that it was self-deception. Perhaps, out of initial resentment, hearing malicious speculations from others, she found a way to justify her immoral attempt to pursue someone else's boyfriend.","After all, outside the wealthy circles, some people love to gossip, imagining everything is driven by interests, and everyone is a tool for marriage.","And Bai Xiaoxi, hearing this, became even more dazed. Ke Yun'er was so confident in her words. Could it be...","At this thought, Bai Xiaoxi shook her head desperately, even as her trust in Yu Yue was on the verge of collapsing. She still couldn't help but believe in that person's sincere love for her.","Maybe it was just an accidental lapse with Ke Yun'er, or maybe Yu Yue was just a bit bothered by her condition. Maybe...","If Bai Xiaoxi were a completely healthy person, she wouldn't doubt herself to this extent.","It was the accumulation of small misunderstandings and accidents that gradually destroyed her confidence and innocence.","Faced with Ke Yun'er's claims, Yu Yi was speechless. After all, he spent little time at home, so he had no idea what was going on.","But it was true that the Yu family was very keen on the marriage alliance with the Bai family. Because of their relationship, the two families had collaborated on many projects, with the Bai family even making additional concessions. It could be said that the Yu family was determined to see this marriage through, even if Yu Yue wanted to break up now.","\"So, Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi were just putting on an act. While abroad, you two secretly got together, didn't you?\" Yu Yi said.","But Ke Yun'er didn't nod in agreement. Instead, she directly said, \"Yu Yue is a good person. Even if he was forced, he wouldn't step on two boats. It's just that he was too depressed. I remember that period, he was always preoccupied, absent-minded. Finally, one day, he couldn't hold it in anymore. He drank and cried, and I stayed with him, letting it all out. That night, he held me and said he loved me, that he really loved me, and that he wanted to be with me. Then I... But the next day, he disappeared. When I returned to school, I heard he had dropped out. He was forced by your Yu family to make a decision and went back to Bai Xiaoxi...\"","Ke Yun'er spoke with such sincerity that even Qin Xian was momentarily swayed.","If it weren't for Ji Fei's complaints, Qin Xian might have started to doubt his friend.","【Uh, Ke Yun'er, although you seem to have told a heartbreaking story, the gossip I heard from Yu Yue tells a similar story, but it's completely different from yours!】","The Qin Family suddenly perked up. Finally! So, what's the truth?!","Even Qin Xian felt his heartbeat quicken with curiosity.","【He was indeed often preoccupied and absent-minded when he first went abroad. That's because this guy is a die-hard romantic. All he could think about was Bai Xiaoxi. He was constantly adjusting to the time difference to stay in touch. Making friends, partying, studying—all these things were completely forgotten by Yu Yue. Except for being occasionally dragged out by a few wealthy acquaintances who were also studying abroad, he had no other social life.】","The Qin Family: So... it's all Ke Yun'er's own imagination again?","Qin Xian: He still doesn't remember Ke Yun'er. So, Ke Yun'er was just one of those forgettable background characters in his social circle?","【As for that \"breaking down and crying,\" if we go by the timeline, the next day he dropped out of school, that was around the time of Bai Xiaoxi's incident.】","In an instant, everyone who could hear the thoughts was puzzled. Is there more to the story?","Ah, Yu Yue truly loved Bai Xiaoxi. Bai Xiaoxi was tricked by her family to study abroad and seek medical treatment elsewhere. At that time, she didn't even know what was wrong with her. She thought it was just severe menstrual pain and needed regulation, so she was embarrassed and never let Yu Yue know when he came to visit.","But Yu Yue loved Bai Xiaoxi so much that he naturally paid attention to any changes in her. Eventually, it made Yu Yue suspicious and he started investigating. Initially, Bai Xiaoxi's family lied and said it was just for rest and recuperation. But how could Yu Yue not want to know about Bai Xiaoxi's health? After investigating, he found out that Bai Xiaoxi's uterus was damaged, and the treatment was to save her life, but she would never be able to have children again.","The Qin Family and Qin Xian were shocked to hear this news. The Bai family had kept this secret tightly, not wanting their precious daughter to be looked at with pity or strange eyes. So, no one in the domestic wealthy circles knew about it.","It was only now, through the gossip system, that this information was revealed unexpectedly.","Qin Xian also understood why Bai Xiaoxi's confidence in Yu Yue's feelings had wavered so much. It was because she thought Ke Yun'er had really been pregnant with Yu Yue's child, something she couldn't give him.","Deep down, she carried a huge sense of guilt, always feeling she had wronged Yu Yue, unworthy of his love.","Perhaps not all women necessarily need to have children, but she was different. She had always known about Yu Yue's family issues. She knew Yu Yue wanted to be a good parent with her, to love and nurture their child together. And she also loved children very much. But..."]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305: Two people who loved each other so deeply, once also had a breakup.","paragraphs":["Upon discovering the truth, Yu Yue pretended as if he knew nothing and continued his sweet romance with Bai Xiaoxi. After all, compared to the fact that he couldn't have children, he was more worried about Bai Xiaoxi finding out and being heartbroken.","The Qin family was moved by this.","Qin Xian, however, wasn't surprised. In Yu Yue's eyes, Bai Xiaoxi was the most beautiful existence in the world. His greatest dream was to protect this pure and innocent beauty, hoping that Bai Xiaoxi would live a carefree life forever.","\"Alas, Qin Xian and the others don't know that these two deeply in love individuals once broke up.\"","This thought immediately piqued everyone's curiosity. Weren't they indifferent?","\"Bai Xiaoxi was only clever once, but it happened to be at the worst possible time. She found out about her condition and, heartbroken, decided to break up with Yu Yue. That's why Ke Yun'er mentioned that big cry and the withdrawal from school—it was because Bai Xiaoxi cut off contact with Yu Yue, who then gave up everything to stay by her side.\"","The Qin family breathed a sigh of relief. What a dramatic love story! It was tough on these two young people. Wait a minute, who did Ke Yun'er say she slept with? Could it be that Yu Yue was so devastated that he lost control after drinking and mistook Ke Yun'er for Bai Xiaoxi? How clichéd!","Qin Xian quickly realized the truth. Earlier, Ji Fei's thoughts had revealed a crucial piece of information: Yu Yue had only ever been with Bai Xiaoxi. So, no matter how convincing and well-argued Ke Yun'er's claims were, they couldn't change the fact that Yu Yue had never been with her.","Ji Fei seemed to think of this too and couldn't help but complain.","“Clearly, in that study abroad memory, there was no trace of Ke Yun'er. Yu Yue first officially met Ke Yun'er when she became his stepmother. This means it’s highly likely that, just like the previous misunderstanding between brother-in-law and sister-in-law, Ke Yun'er once again mistook someone else for Yu Yue. Wow, she really treats every man she sleeps with as Yu Yue? That’s... hehe, truly beyond belief.”","Fortunately, Bai Xiaoxi is simple and easy to coax. Yu Yue repeatedly demonstrated to her that he actually disliked kids and had only said otherwise to go along with her. This misunderstanding didn't affect him at all. He loves their two-person world and is even afraid that a child would compete for her affection. Under such sweet-talking, Bai Xiaoxi, being a bit silly, was easily coaxed back, and the two returned to being the lovable goofy couple they were.","\"The reason why the Bai family hasn't agreed to their marriage yet is due to concerns. During their relationship, the Bai family has repeatedly given benefits to the Yu family. They know that the Yu family values having many children and the bloodline. If Yu Yue truly wants to be with Bai Xiaoxi, they can only adopt children in the future.\"","The Qin family thought the Bai family was quite sensible.","Qin Xian figured that if the Yu family knew the truth, they certainly wouldn't agree to Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi being together. No wonder Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi have been staying abroad for so long—it's to escape the Yu family's control.","\"The Bai family is also honest. What's the point of giving benefits to the Yu family? Yu Yue doesn't have a good relationship with them. If they knew what Yu Yue has done for Bai Xiaoxi, they'd probably worship the Yu family. We should find a chance to remind them, so they don't get taken advantage of.\"","The Qin family nodded in agreement.","Qin Xian, however, was momentarily stunned. He paid attention to every word his wife said, so he immediately caught on to something: What did Ji Fei mean by \"what Yu Yue has done for Bai Xiaoxi\"? Has Yu Yue done something that no one else knows about?","But since Ji Fei wasn't thinking along those lines, everyone else couldn't hear it.","Meanwhile, Ke Yun'er was still accusing, seemingly in tears, as if her love with Yu Yue had been repeatedly crushed and hurt.","\"After he left, I tried to contact him, but there was never any response. I even came to work at Yu Yue's company, waiting for him. But fate played a cruel joke—my brother-in-law fell for me. My parents sold me out, and I could no longer be with Yu Yue openly. Yet, I couldn't let him go. I wanted him to be happy, even if it wasn't with me. So, I had to hide all my feelings and quietly play the role of his stepmother, pretending not to know him.\"","Yu Yi listened in a daze. Ke Yun'er's story sounded so sincere that he completely believed it. He never expected his nephew to hide so deep, watching his own father marry the woman he once loved.","He even slept with his stepmother, got her pregnant, and planned to have another child. Was he trying to maintain this incestuous relationship?","Yu Yi couldn't help but complain. He felt like he had forgotten how close he had been to his nephew just moments ago.","“It's not our fault. It's your Yu family's oppression that forced Yu Yue to play along with Bai Xiaoxi. And I only wanted more leverage to help Yu Yue escape your control,” Ke Yun'er spoke with righteous indignation.","This left Yu Yi a bit puzzled. Even though he didn't interact much with Yu Yue, he could see that Yu Yue really loved Bai Xiaoxi.","So, was his nephew acting all along? No wonder he's been dragging his feet about getting married.","Suddenly, Yu Yi thought of something and, feeling sympathetic toward Ke Yun'er's sorrow, couldn't help but blurt out, \"Don't worry, they won't be together.\"","This statement surprised Ji Fei and Qin Xian, who were eavesdropping.","Ke Yun'er suddenly looked up, as if finding a lifeline, her eyes gleaming with a strange light as she looked at Yu Yi with eager anticipation.","Yu Yi directly said, \"I accidentally found out—Bai Xiaoxi can't have children.\"","\"Damn, he actually knows. Oh, it turns out that Yu Yi's mother is quite skilled in household strife. She has the means to hide and targeted the most promising couple for political marriage in the family. After investigating, she discovered Bai Xiaoxi's health issues. According to the Yu family's tradition, such a daughter-in-law, no matter how good, is useless. So, this mother was very 'kind' to keep the secret, hoping that Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi would be locked together, childless. Unexpectedly, her son revealed it.\"","The Qin family frowned. After all, it was Bai Xiaoxi's family secret. Yu Yi was just a loose-lipped person. He probably had some hidden desire to please Ke Yun'er.","Qin Xian also frowned. He was now very curious about Ke Yun'er's reaction.","The next moment, they heard Ke Yun'er immediately ask excitedly. After Yu Yi explained, Ke Yun'er was silent for a long time before saying, \"I understand.\"","Her voice sounded a bit hoarse.","Yu Yi seemed to realize he shouldn't have exposed this, but then he quickly comforted himself. At least he knew the secret of the stepmother story and could let his mother continue to manipulate Yu Yue. And looking at Ke Yun'er, she didn't seem like the type to use such a secret to threaten anyone."]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306: He even bought the plane ticket, ready to make a run for it.","paragraphs":["【Tsk, I bet Ke Yun'er's mouth is about to split from smiling so much right now. She's probably already plotting how to use this news to force Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi to break up, all while pretending to be a righteous savior who rescued Yu Yue. What a hassle! But I'd really like to see what kind of face she'll make when she exposes everything and Yu Yue still firmly chooses Bai Xiaoxi. No, no, no, better not. That's Bai Xiaoxi's wound, best not to reopen it.】","As she was thinking, Ji Fei felt Bai Xiaoxi's body trembling in her arms.","It must have been happening earlier, but Ji Fei was too engrossed in the drama to notice. Now, Bai Xiaoxi's emotional turmoil was growing stronger, making it impossible for Ji Fei to ignore.","Ji Fei immediately looked at Bai Xiaoxi and felt her heart ache. The once bright and lovely girl now looked like a lost soul, her pain so tangible that it seemed to materialize on her face.","Her eyes were vacant, her gaze shattered, her face flushed from emotional breakdown, veins bulging on her forehead, as if she might faint from the intensity of her emotions at any moment.","Ji Fei was completely at a loss.","Qin Xian sighed silently. Bai Xiaoxi probably didn't even realize it herself. As a pure-hearted person, if no one else had noticed her hidden pain, it meant her family and Yu Yue had managed to shield her from it so completely that she didn't even care about it herself.","Unfortunately, an unexpected encounter with Ke Yun'er had destroyed everything those who loved her had worked so hard to build.","It was just bad luck.","At that moment, Bai Xiaoxi's phone vibrated in her pocket. Ji Fei, sharp-eyed, saw the caller ID and didn't hesitate. She grabbed the phone, ended the call, and then sent a message to Yu Yue, telling him to hurry over. His wife needed him to comfort her. If he didn't come soon, it might be too late.","Although Yu Yue was also innocent, this mess was his fault, and he had to take responsibility.","When Yu Yue saw the message with the address next door to the room they had just left, he started sweating. When it came to Bai Xiaoxi, he didn't dare to take any chances. Ignoring the small group he had been talking to, he got up and ran.","Just moments ago, they had been subtly reminding Yu Yue to keep his distance from Ke Yun'er, but now he was gone.","\"What's going on?\" Jing Yan asked curiously.","\"It's rare to see him so panicked that his face turned white. What kind of trouble is he in?\" Luo Fei said.","Guo Yalan didn't waste any time analyzing. She immediately stood up and pulled Cen Ting along.","Cen Ting was startled. \"What are we doing?\"","\"I have a feeling there's a juicy gossip!\" Guo Yalan immediately raised an eyebrow. \"Maybe that vixen is up to something again. Let's follow Yu Yue and keep an eye on him. If he dares to hurt the innocent and lovely Xiaoxi, you guys take care of him.\"","Jing Yan and Luo Fei, hearing this, had no choice but to follow.","They couldn't help but wonder if their small group had always been this obsessed with gossip.","The group of them followed Yu Yue's figure in a grand procession.","On the other side, Yu Yi had said everything he needed to say to Ke Yun'er, whether it was appropriate or not. Ke Yun'er seemed preoccupied and claimed she was tired.","From start to finish, Ke Yun'er never understood what Yu Yi was trying to achieve. After venting, Yu Yi didn't threaten her, so she dismissed him, saying the ceremony was about to begin and someone would come soon.","Yu Yi, whose mind was also in turmoil due to a big secret he was hiding, took the opportunity to leave.","As soon as he stepped into the corridor, he saw Yu Yue rushing over.","Yu Yi's expression immediately became somewhat complicated.","\"Why are you here?\" Yu Yue asked.","Yu Yi raised an eyebrow playfully, ready to taunt him a bit, but then saw the small group following behind Yu Yue and was momentarily stunned.","What was going on? Wasn't Yu Yue rushing here to meet Ke Yun'er in secret? After all, they had some unsavory dealings and unfinished business. Why did he bring a whole group of people with him?","Yu Yi assumed he must have misunderstood and thought maybe they were just looking for a quiet place to rest since it was noisy downstairs.","He didn't bother with them and walked past them.","Yu Yue, of course, had no interest in the group behind him and rushed straight into the room.","The moment he opened the door, he was stunned.","He didn't notice Ji Fei and Qin Xian in the room, but the sight of Bai Xiaoxi crying broke his heart. After all, Bai Xiaoxi hadn't cried this hard since their breakup years ago.","Yu Yue's mind was filled with terrible scenarios, and he quickly rushed over to explain.","Fortunately, after the conversation next door ended, Qin Xian had already closed the balcony window, so there was no need to worry about eavesdroppers.","The small group following Yu Yue was equally shocked when they saw the three people inside.","Guo Yalan, quick to react, immediately pushed everyone into the room, closed the door, and excitedly said to Ji Fei, \"There really is a juicy gossip!\"","Ji Fei's mouth twitched. How did so many people end up here?","Meanwhile, Yu Yue was already holding Bai Xiaoxi, his words a jumble of affection and concern.","\"Xiaoxi, why are you crying? Did you hear something? Did you misunderstand something? I can explain everything. Just remember, I love you, and only you. I... I...\"","Seeing Bai Xiaoxi just crying, Yu Yue didn't know what else to say.","Luo Fei stepped forward to ask Qin Xian, \"What's going on?\"","Jing Yan said, \"Did you come here to find Xiaoxi?\"","Cen Ting, seeing Bai Xiaoxi crying so hard, went to fetch a towel and hot water.","Guo Yalan leaned in front of Ji Fei, her eyes sparkling, making Ji Fei feel the pressure.","Qin Xian, seeing that Yu Yue couldn't get his words together, directly said, \"About fifteen minutes ago, we accidentally found Xiaoxi crying here. She probably overheard the conversation next door.\"","Everyone was immediately curious.","Yu Yue finally regained his composure and quickly said, \"Did you hear what I said to Ke Yun'er?\"","Bai Xiaoxi's tears flowed even more profusely.","Yu Yue cupped Bai Xiaoxi's face, his heart aching as he said, \"Believe me.\"","Bai Xiaoxi paused, her tears actually stopping.","\"That was all a lie to Ke Yun'er. I was worried that crazy woman would expose the miscarriage, and I was afraid the Yu Family would blame you and force me to break up with you. But I definitely can't leave you. I was just afraid they would tarnish your eyes, so I've already planned to take you back to our little home abroad right after the wedding, completely cutting off ties with here. That's why I said I'd consider it, to keep that woman from causing trouble. My dear, how could I possibly mess around with her? Am I that immoral? I've said it before, I hate kids. There's no way I could have a child with her.\"","The group, not knowing the full context, was left in a fog, but the explosive information still left their heads buzzing.","Various questions and doubts started pouring out.","Ji Fei had to step in to provide some background for the gossip.","\"What? Xiaoxi caused it? No way. Based on my experience with gossip, it must have been that woman's fault,\" Guo Yalan immediately said.","\"How disgusting to make such a request,\" Cen Ting couldn't help but curse.","Luo Fei said, \"Does she really think she can marry your father without anyone saying anything?\"","\"His father is currently suffering from the pain of being childless. He might not side with Yu Yue and could even be turned against him. Leaving might be the right choice. Don't get tangled up with bad people,\" Jing Yan analyzed.","After Yu Yue finished speaking, he saw Bai Xiaoxi just staring at him, tears still silently flowing. He was desperate and immediately took out his phone to prove himself. He had already booked tickets, showing that everything he said was true.","But the next moment, Bai Xiaoxi cried even harder, repeatedly calling Yu Yue's name, showing just how much she loved him, how much she didn't want to lose him, and how heartbroken she was.","She wanted to speak, but the pain made it impossible for her to form words.","Yu Yue was frantic, scratching his head in desperation.","\"Maybe you should listen to this first,\" Qin Xian said, taking out his phone."]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307: A Detailed Explanation","paragraphs":["Just at the beginning, Yu Yue's expression went blank.","The phrase \"I'm carrying Yu Yue's child\" directly caused Yu Yue's brain to crash.","Everyone else present immediately widened their eyes and stared intently at Yu Yue.","At this moment, their minds probably all flashed the four words: \"Step-Mom Literature.\"","\"Is she crazy? What... what nonsense is this!\" Yu Yue's face turned red with anger, feeling so wronged that he almost spat out a mouthful of blood.","Then, as if remembering something, his expression twisted.","[Poor guy, too poor. He must have realized what Ke Yun'er's strange attitude towards him was all about. No matter how hard he thought, he wouldn't have guessed that Ke Yun'er had such a hidden agenda.]","\"Xiaoxi, you wouldn't believe her nonsense, would you? What relationship do I have with her? How could that child possibly be mine?\" Yu Yue said anxiously.","Hearing him say this, everyone else breathed a sigh of relief.","\"What is she up to? Is she deliberately tricking your uncle? Or spreading rumors about you?\" Guo Yalan asked.","\"How would I know!\" Yu Yue was on the verge of tearing his hair out, feeling completely wronged by these baseless rumors.","The recording continued, and Ke Yun'er brought up the accident at the old mansion that night.","Yu Yue immediately exclaimed, \"That night? No, that's not right. I wasn't that drunk; I was just pretending to be drunk. I even called Xiaoxi to say goodnight before going to sleep.\"","Bai Xiaoxi seemed to have regained some composure and thought of their nightly goodnight calls when they weren't together, her face showing a look of confusion.","\"So, she's completely fabricating the story?\" Cen Ting asked.","Jing Yan said, \"Probably. You can't exactly not know who you're sleeping with, right?\"","Everyone listening to the recording didn't feel anything unusual, so they didn't suspect Yu Yi's abnormal tone in the recording.","So Ji Fei directly said, \"By the way, don't forget, Ke Yun'er mentioned that Yu Yue's father can't have children anymore, so she must have had someone else. Maybe she wasn't lying.\"","Yu Yue immediately looked at Ji Fei, crying out in protest, \"Sister Fei, don't you dare frame me!\"","Ji Fei was speechless, \"I'm just saying, don't you think about whether there's any condition that might have caused her to mistake someone else for you?\"","\"Was she drunk too?\" Guo Yalan suggested, \"Did she sleep with the wrong person? Ah, could it be Yu Yue's uncle?\"","This remark immediately made Yu Yi's presence stand out.","Right, in this whole situation, why did Yu Yi suddenly pop up?","Yu Yue paused for a moment, then suddenly said, \"I remember now. My uncle was drunk, and when I took him to his room, he threw up on the bed. There was no way, so I had to take him to my room to rest. After the servants cleaned up, he wouldn't leave, so I had to go to his room to sleep.\"","Luo Fei said, \"If the lights were off, and you and your uncle are about the same age and build, if she left early the next morning, it could easily lead to this kind of misunderstanding.\"","Yu Yue immediately felt a sense of vindication and grabbed Bai Xiaoxi's hand, saying, \"You hear that? The truth must be this. How could I ever do anything to betray you? Now, are you relieved?\"","Yu Yue smiled.","The others, however, became curious about the relationship between Yu Yi and Ke Yun'er.","The music below seemed to have started, and the ceremony was about to begin.","But they were all too engrossed in this juicy gossip to care about the ceremony outside.","As for Yu Yue's father being framed with a cuckold story, with his own son not caring, they certainly wouldn't either.","At this point, the conversation had moved on to Ke Yun'er exposing her emotional entanglement with Yu Yue.","Yu Yue was once again dumbfounded: \"I didn't even know her before. She's my stepmother now. If I were to sleep with my father's woman, I'd be disgusted to death. What is she talking about?\"","Bai Xiaoxi looked aggrieved at Yu Yue, still wanting to get to the bottom of it. But before she could ask, Ke Yun'er's recording began to recount the high school days of youth.","As they listened, the others couldn't help but look at Yu Yue with suspicion.","Yu Yue was left gaping, trembling at some of the descriptions. Upon closer inspection, he was literally covered in goosebumps.","\"Did I lose my memory? I did like sleeping in the school clinic and avoiding people, but... let me think... there was indeed a period when there was a regular visitor to the clinic. I thought she was like the others, knowing my identity and trying to curry favor with me, becoming my follower. After all, I was quite generous, usually giving some reward for running errands. Could she have been the one running errands for me?\"","It seemed that Yu Yue didn't even bother to remember the names of those who flattered him, so he never even exchanged contact information with them.","\"So, for Ke Yun'er, it was a teenage romance drama, but in your eyes, it was just a young master and his errand runner?\" Guo Yalan summed it up accurately, nearly laughing herself to tears.","The others also had twitching lips, not knowing what to make of this situation.","Ji Fei also couldn't help but chuckle, [So this is what they mean by \"unrequited love is a one-person war\"? I think I'm going to have a psychological shadow towards unrequited love stories from now on.]","When Bai Xiaoxi heard this, she finally found the courage to speak up and immediately said, \"You really don't remember her, but what about when you were abroad...?\"","\"Ah? Abroad?\" Yu Yue was once again dumbfounded.","The recording continued to play, revealing another story to Yu Yue.","The first sentence was enough to make Yu Yue react strongly.","\"What do you mean by an arranged marriage? I found my own wife, okay!\" Yu Yue said indignantly.","After all his efforts to find true love, he thought it was the luckiest thing in the world, only to be slandered like this. It was enough to make him furious.","Jing Yan sneered, \"Before this, the Yu family and the Bai family had no connections at all. She must have only found what she wanted to see and ignored everything else.\"","This remark immediately resonated with Ji Fei.","[I always felt it was strange. So many years of misunderstandings, so many coincidences that could rival a TV drama. Was there really no flaw? Or did Ke Yun'er deliberately avoid all the flaws?]","Qin Xian: Obviously, some people are trapped in their own woven dreams.","Guo Yalan smiled and said, \"Yu Yue, you're not a celebrity, yet you still attract stalkers. It's hard to believe she's so delusional, following you abroad.\"","Yu Yue was now frantically trying to recall, \"Did I ever meet her? Or is she just making this up?\"","It was only then that Qin Xian spoke up, \"I had someone investigate earlier, and it turns out Ke Yun'er and you were in the same high school, and later, the same overseas university.\"","Yu Yue didn't question why Qin Xian would suddenly investigate Ke Yun'er but instead frowned and tried hard to recall.","He truly looked like he couldn't remember at all.","Until the recording played a segment that made both Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi's faces change.","They both remembered that most painful memory."]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308: The Unrevealed Secret","paragraphs":["Yu Yue immediately became nervous and looked at Bai Xiaoxi, finally realizing why she was so upset. No wonder Bai Xiaoxi was so distressed—she must have been reminded of that incident and was thus easily led astray by Ke Yun'er's lies.","\"Damn it, Ke Yun'er, what the hell is she babbling about! How many times is she going to tarnish my reputation? She must be crazy, a total lunatic!\" Yu Yue was furious, then pointed to the sky and swore, \"I definitely never touched her. I don't even remember her existence. Xiaoxi, I only have you. Don't worry, I don't need you to believe me emotionally; I'll prove it with evidence. I'll contact my classmates from abroad right away. I refuse to believe there's no one who can vouch for me!\"","At this moment, seeing Yu Yue's reaction, everyone present firmly sided with him.","Bai Xiaoxi finally cried and threw herself into Yu Yue's arms.","\"I'm sorry, Ah Yue. I'm sorry. It's my lack of confidence, it's me...\"","Yu Yue didn't want Bai Xiaoxi to say those words or recall those events. His precious girl should remain forever pure and beautiful.","Holding Bai Xiaoxi, Yu Yue's eyes were filled with cold fury. That crazy woman, Ke Yun'er, had made his beloved so heartbroken. He would definitely make her pay.","When they heard Ke Yun'er say she wanted to protect Yu Yue, everyone couldn't help but mock her, and Yu Yue even let out a disdainful laugh.","Guo Yalan couldn't help but complain, \"She sure imagines herself quite nobly, but is it possible that everyone just falls in love, either at first sight or over time, within their own social circles? Do they really have to choose someone from a completely different world, like her, to prove it's true love?\"","\"That kind of thing is more like an impulsive, irrational whim,\" Cen Ting coldly added.","At this moment, Qin Xian suddenly stopped the recording, and the others curiously looked at him.","\"Is it over?\" Luo Fei asked.","Qin Xian nodded calmly.","\"I thought they would discuss some conspiracy,\" Jing Yan sneered.","\"They might not be on the same page. If Yu Yi was the one with Ke Yun'er that night, then he should have realized the truth by now. So he's also hiding everything, making Yu Yue take the blame,\" Luo Fei said, then looked at Yu Yue. \"This situation is quite troublesome. How do you plan to handle it?\"","Yu Yue raged, \"I'll find a way to expose her affair with Yu Yi. Those two idiots, scheming against me!\"","\"What if she uses the child as leverage?\" Cen Ting asked.","\"You're overthinking it. With the recording, the child isn't Yu's Father's, so how can it be her shield?\" Guo Yalan replied.","\"But if we want to prove the child isn't hers, we can only use the recording, and then Yu Yue might find it hard to clear his name,\" Jing Yan said.","\"By the way, what's the deal with the child? Xiaoxi, tell us in detail,\" Guo Yalan immediately became curious.","Bai Xiaoxi had now stopped crying and suddenly remembered the photo.","Now it seemed that the photo must have been taken during the last day of their overseas student gathering, when they were drunk, and someone snapped a picture of the two of them together.","At that time, Yu Yue was preoccupied with his own thoughts and didn't pay attention to who was sitting next to him.","But others wouldn't think that way. If the photo and recording were combined, it could become a double-edged sword, potentially backfiring on Yu Yue.","The situation was indeed very tricky.","\"That guy must have done it on purpose, setting a trap for you. Pretending to be pulled down, just like in those palace dramas,\" Guo Yalan said.","\"I'm not really clear about the situation at the time. I just lost my head and wanted to grab the phone to see,\" Bai Xiaoxi said guiltily, regretting her impulsiveness.","Yu Yue immediately comforted his wife, \"Ah, my precious was so concerned about me that she lost her mind. She must really love me so much.\"","Bai Xiaoxi immediately blushed.","The others silently gave Yu Yue a thumbs up.","But as for what to do, no one had any ideas.","Yu Yue eventually looked at Qin Xian and Ji Fei.","\"Do you have any suggestions?\"","Ji Fei was just here to enjoy the drama; she had no ideas. The funniest part was that she hadn't even met Ke Yun'er yet, thinking she might check her out later.","Qin Xian, however, said, \"I suggest you stick to the original plan and take Bai Xiaoxi away first. After investigating and gathering evidence, privately warn Yu Yi and Ke Yun'er to face reality and stop bothering you.\"","Yu Yue immediately objected, \"Why should I let them off so easily!\"","\"You can secretly take revenge on them if you want, but I advise against making it public. It will only complicate things,\" Qin Xian continued. \"I'll send you the recording and information later; you can decide for yourself.\"","Ji Fei also didn't understand Qin Xian's approach, wondering if he thought it was all just a self-deceptive fantasy, and since the child was gone, it wasn't worth making a big deal out of it.","Yu Yue actually trusted Qin Xian a lot. Usually, when Qin Xian gave advice, Yu Yue would follow it.","But this time, the other friends didn't understand Qin Xian's approach.","Since it was Yu Yue's personal matter, the final decision was up to him.","With the music outside having stopped, it was clear the wedding ceremony was over, and the reception might have started. They decided to head downstairs, giving the couple some space to discuss what to do next.","Before leaving, Qin Xian walked last and said something to Yu Yue.","The others didn't hear it, but Ji Fei couldn't resist her curiosity and leaned in to listen. Qin Xian noticed but didn't stop her.","Yu Yue still looked puzzled at Qin Xian, clearly not understanding his almost lenient suggestion.","Then, in the next second, Qin Xian's words stunned him, and his face changed abruptly.","\"The recording isn't over. Bai Xiaoxi's health condition has been exposed.\" After saying this, Qin Xian left with Ji Fei.","Ji Fei finally understood.","\"Oh, if Ke Yun'er is pushed to the brink, she might break and expose Bai Xiaoxi's secret. Compared to Bai Xiaoxi causing Ke Yun'er to miscarry, the fact that Bai Xiaoxi can't have children is even more serious for the Yu family. Even with all the benefits, the Yu family would reject the marriage. No wonder Qin Xian gave such advice. Oh, my husband is so thoughtful and gentle, considering everything so thoroughly. I forgot about this, hehehe.\"","Ji Fei immediately became a bit infatuated, clinging to Qin Xian and staring at his handsome profile.","Qin Xian, praised to the point of feeling like his heart was filled with honey, blushed under the intense gaze. He turned to look at Ji Fei, only to meet a radiant smile.","Feeling that he had made his wife happy, Qin Xian thought he deserved a reward.","So, unexpectedly, he gently kissed her.","At this moment, the small group, realizing they were lagging behind, turned back and were shocked.","It was almost as big a surprise as the earlier drama.","Although they all knew the relationship between Qin Xian and Ji Fei was special, especially Qin Xian's feelings for Ji Fei, seeing them kiss was a first for them. Qin Xian, usually so composed and businesslike, looked like a shy teenager.","For those who had known him for years, this scene was so fresh that they wanted to pull out their phones and take a picture.","However, despite being married for years, the two of them seemed like newlyweds, both shy and avoiding each other's gaze, especially when they noticed everyone looking.","It seemed their own wedding would have to wait a bit longer.","Downstairs, Yu's Father was angry. \"That Yu Yue is too much. Where did he run off to?\"","Ke Yun'er also scanned the room, as Yu Yue, as Yu's Father's son, should have been present during the ceremony.","At this moment, everyone was speculating whether Yu Yue was opposed to the wedding.","Ke Yun'er, however, couldn't help but feel a flutter of hope. Could it be that Yu Yue was wavering and didn't want her to marry Yu's Father?"]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309: Not Crazy, But Evil, Truly and Sincerely Evil","paragraphs":["Ji Fei's attention was momentarily diverted by Qin Xian's sudden kiss, but it immediately snapped back when she saw Ke Yun'er in her wedding dress.","Her eyes lit up almost like a cat spotting fresh fish, and she thought, **Ke Yun'er, finally I get to see you in person!**","Her expression made Qin Xian, who was watching her, feel a tiny pang of jealousy.","Qin Xian: When will Ji Fei look at me with such a passionate gaze?","Meanwhile, the piercing thoughts finally reached the Qin family, who had just been toasted. They were no strangers to big scenes and instantly understood that Ji Fei had finally laid eyes on Ke Yun'er.","The Qin family's gaze on Ke Yun'er grew more intense, all wondering what kind of juicy gossip was about to unfold.","By the way, only little Qin Xi couldn't hear the thoughts.","At that moment, he was being praised by Yu's Father and Ke Yun'er for his auspicious words and was even given a red envelope.","After they left, Qin Xi couldn't help but say, \"Mom, I don't think that aunt really likes Grandpa Yu.\"","The Qin family almost burst out laughing. What aunt? What grandpa? The way Qin Xi addressed them was indeed awkward, but his observation was interesting. They all looked at Qin Xi in surprise.","Although Qin Xi usually couldn't hear Ji Fei's thoughts, he often sat on the living room carpet playing games while surrounded by people gossiping and eating snacks, so he had picked up a keen sense of perception.","\"Why do you say that?\" Qin Yan couldn't help but ask.","\"I just felt like she was quite disdainful of Uncle Yu. When Uncle Yu tried to put his arm around her, she deliberately moved away to avoid it,\" Qin Xi explained.","Qin's Mom chuckled, \"Our little Xi is really sharp in his observations.\"","\"Ahem, shh, keep it down,\" Qin's Father quickly signaled for silence, afraid that the surrounding guests might hear and cause a scene.","However, the Qin family couldn't help but feel a sense of mockery as they watched the newlywed couple walk away. They wondered what Ke Yun'er's usual behavior was, but it seemed she had become a bit too ambitious.","Of course, what they were most curious about was whether Ji Fei could dig up some fresh juicy gossip.","Even though they knew today might not turn into a major scandal, they still wanted to be the first to get their hands on the freshest gossip.","Ji Fei didn't disappoint. The first big reveal came with her exclamation.","**This is insane! I hadn't noticed before, but Ke Yun'er did mention once that Yu's Father wasn't capable of getting her pregnant. Now that I think about it, her certainty is quite suspicious. Turns out, she was that ruthless. Is this... also in the name of love?**","This statement, without much elaboration, made those who could hear the thoughts instantly grasp the key point.","So, Yu's father's complete loss of fertility wasn't natural but artificially induced? And it was Ke Yun'er who did it? She never intended to have Yu's father's child from the start?","**After being forced to marry Yu's Father, she continuously fed him rejuvenating drugs, the most harmful kind, along with incompatible foods, finally cutting off his chances of having children. She believed that since Yu Yue had been sacrificed by the Yu family to marry into the Bai family, he should inherit everything, not have to share it with others. She didn't want to have a child for Yu's Father either; she came to this family just to be by Yu Yue's side.**","Ji Fei quietly looked at Yu's Father, who was still smiling and toasting, occasionally giving a loving glance to Ke Yun'er's now flat stomach.","Rest in peace.","The Qin family: This is crazy, too crazy, absolutely bonkers~","Qin Xian: Pity for my buddy!","But it's also strange. If Ke Yun'er was really so infatuated with Yu Yue, why would she use the child in her belly to frame Bai Xiaoxi? After all, she always believed the child was Yu Yue's.","Was it really an accident, or is Ke Yun'er just that insane?","This was also a point Ji Fei was very focused on, so she skipped other matters for now and looked into the incident of Bai Xiaoxi pushing Ke Yun'er.","**Damn! Guo Yalan was right after all. Ke Yun'er deliberately grabbed Bai Xiaoxi's hand and pretended to fall, because at that time, she knew the child was already dead in her womb.**","The Qin family: This... we've only heard of messy relationships and various frame-ups in some wealthy families, but this time, we've seen it in real life.","Qin Xian's eyes flickered, and he thought of a way to help Yu Yue.","Before, there was no way to prove it, so it was easy to be manipulated. Now, as long as they carefully investigate whether Ke Yun'er secretly visited other hospitals and had a diagnosis of fetal death, and when that happened, they could find the truth.","Thanks to Ji Fei's thoughts, without this piece of gossip, no one would have thought to investigate a grieving pregnant woman who had lost her child after such an accident.","**What a pretentious excuse! She even thought that framing Bai Xiaoxi like this was to help Yu Yue break free from the shackles of an arranged marriage. After all, if she had a miscarriage, the Yu family wouldn't easily accept Bai Xiaoxi, who might be seen as someone trying to harm the family's offspring for personal gain.**","The Qin family: Hmm, we don't really believe that. If she really thought that way, why didn't she reveal it sooner? Why keep it hidden?","Qin Xian could completely guess how Ke Yun'er would deceive herself. Her so-called righteous design was nothing but a blatant frame-up.","Even if she tried to deceive herself on the surface, deep down, as long as she wasn't completely confused, Ji Fei could dig it out.","**Heh, actually, at that time, Ke Yun'er had already sensed that Yu Yue's feelings for Bai Xiaoxi might not be what she imagined. Indeed, Yu Yue's obvious affection for Bai Xiaoxi was so clear that only a blind person couldn't see it.**","**Just as the dead fetus inside her stimulated her, she feared she would never be able to bind Yu Yue again and thus hatched a malicious plan. She used the incident to make Bai Xiaoxi take the blame for the miscarriage, trying to break up Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi. At the same time, she hoped to manipulate Yu Yue into giving her a healthy child, so they could be truly bound together. Some relationships, once started, are hard to stop. Even if Yu Yue wanted to stop, Ke Yun'er could use what had already happened to continue threatening him and maintain this stepmother saga.**","The Qin family was stunned. They really were driven by desire, daring to do such things.","Qin Xian coldly laughed in his heart. This person was no longer just infatuated or crazy; she was downright evil, truly evil.","**Ah, no, in her view, it wasn't a threat but a reason and an excuse for Yu Yue to indulge. In Ke Yun'er's mind, she and Yu Yue still had a past, so she thought the stepmother saga could work. As for Yu Yue's feelings for Bai Xiaoxi, it was just a matter of time, a gradual affection. So she was still quite narcissistic, thinking that because of recent events and the fact that she was now truly married to Yu's Father, Yu Yue was also starting to be unable to let go.**","**Oh my god, how can she be so delusional! Daydreams might be free, but you can't just indulge in them like this!**"]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310: Ex-Wife's Sister Comes to Cause a Scene","paragraphs":["The Qin Family was too tired to even comment. Everyone looked over and saw that Yu's Father and Ke Yun'er had noticed the small group descending the stairs, spotting Yu Yue among them.","Ke Yun'er gazed at him with infatuation, while Yu Yue initially gave her a cold, piercing glare. However, under her obsessive gaze, he eventually faltered, feeling extremely uncomfortable and had to avert his eyes, desperately looking at Bai Xiaoxi to cleanse his vision.","The others in the small group also noticed Ke Yun'er's resentful gaze and were genuinely disgusted, yet they couldn't help but find it amusing.","Poor Yu Yue, what a tragic man!","Following Qin Xian's advice, Yu Yue had no choice but to endure for the time being, focusing on getting through the current situation.","Little did he expect that his father would call him over to toast together.","Well, given his status, Yu Yue had no choice but to comply. Under the sympathetic gazes of his friends, he walked toward what felt like his execution.","When everyone returned to their seats, they had no appetite for the feast. Instead, they were all fixated on the unfolding drama.","After all, such a battlefield was a rare sight.","Yu's Father, oblivious to the tension, stood in the middle while the bride, completely enamored with her stepson, fantasized about discussing having a child with him later.","Meanwhile, the stepson, Yu Yue, was visibly uncomfortable, wishing he could be a hundred thousand miles away from Ke Yun'er. His father had to glare at him several times, reminding him to stay closer.","[Let's mourn for Yu Yue for three seconds. Hahaha, did Ke Yun'er just try to brush against Yu Yue during the turn, attempting to create some secret flirtation? Yu Yue was so startled he almost jumped. He’ll probably throw away these clothes later.]","Qin Xian didn’t want to be so unsympathetic, but he couldn’t help but laugh at Ji Fei's comment.","The Qin Family, after hearing Ji Fei's live commentary, also joined in dissecting the details.","Qin's Mom: \"Did Ke Yun'er just try to flirt with her eyes, but Yu Yue immediately turned his head away?\"","Qin Yan: \"Look! Did Ke Yun'er try to switch glasses with Yu Yue under the guise of refilling drinks, only for Yu Yue to swiftly snatch his glass back?\"","Qin's Father: \"Yu Yue is even wiping sweat now? Oh! She’s actually trying to hand him a handkerchief in front of her husband...\"","[Hahaha, Yu Yue is really walking on thin ice here!]","The small group also began to notice something was off.","Bai Xiaoxi, seeing Yu Yue being so coveted, was so upset she could barely sit still.","Guo Yalan complained, \"Yu Yue is so pitiful. Are we just going to watch?\"","\"What else can we do?\" Luo Fei raised an eyebrow helplessly.","Jing Yan coughed lightly, \"He’ll protect his virtue.\"","Cen Ting almost spat out his tea.","Soon, the trio arrived at their table for the toast.","Bai Xiaoxi immediately stood beside Yu Yue, looking at him with concern, then turned to glare at Ke Yun'er like a cat trying to appear fierce despite its tail between its legs.","However, Bai Xiaoxi’s eyes were still slightly swollen from crying earlier.","Ke Yun'er, who had been entirely focused on Yu Yue, naturally noticed Bai Xiaoxi.","Her eyes lit up upon seeing her.","Ji Fei, who had just taken a sip of the toast wine, caught Ke Yun'er's thoughts and immediately started coughing, startling everyone.","Qin Xian quickly patted Ji Fei's back.","Yu's Father, as the elder, showed concern, \"Are you alright?\"","Ji Fei finally stopped coughing but didn’t dare to say anything. Internally, she was screaming.","[Of course, I’m not alright! I’m so grossed out by your wife! Her thoughts are so ridiculous... Ke Yun'er thinks Bai Xiaoxi has been crying because Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi had a fight, and she’s convinced it’s because of her. She’s even smugly speculating that she’s surpassed Bai Xiaoxi in Yu Yue’s heart.]","Qin Xian shot Ke Yun'er an annoyed look, irritated that her delusional thoughts were upsetting his wife.","\"Hehe, I’m fine, just choked,\" Ji Fei said.","Yu's Father gave her a strange look before moving on to the next table.","Qin Xian was quite sensitive to how others looked at Ji Fei and wondered what Yu's Father’s final glance meant. He then noticed Ji Fei had also caught it.","[What’s that look supposed to mean? Haha, I’m laughing. So, the old man has heard my rumors too. Now that everything’s going smoothly, he’s feeling smug, thinking it’s all just a joke. Even if it’s not, he believes it proves his marriage is a success. Oh, Yu's Father, you’re really... too confident.]","The Qin Family also found it amusing. The drama was huge, and the old man probably couldn’t handle it.","Not exposing everything on the spot could be considered an act of mercy.","Many people in the room were probably disappointed. After all, at a wedding of this caliber, so many young people had likely come hoping to witness some juicy gossip, expecting to see some real-life drama.","Well, at least it didn’t escalate, or Ji Fei’s reputation would’ve been further tarnished.","Just as they were thinking this, a commotion erupted at the entrance.","A lavishly dressed woman stormed in, shouting at Yu's Father, \"Old Yu! You can’t marry this shameless woman! She’s deceived you! The child in her belly isn’t yours!\"","Her words were like a thunderclap, shocking everyone in the room.","Ji Fei’s jaw dropped.","Those who knew the inside story were also stunned.","They had all planned to get through the wedding peacefully, but now a wild card had appeared out of nowhere.","\"Who is that?\" Qin Xian asked, voicing Ji Fei’s curiosity.","Jing Yan, who was more knowledgeable about such matters, explained, \"That’s Yu Yue’s previous stepmother. Yu's Father divorced her after setting his sights on Ke Yun'er.\"","He then revealed the name and background of the ex-wife.","[A nurse? A nurse!!! So that’s how it is.]","The Qin Family was buzzing with excitement. How? How did the ex-wife find out such a secret?","Qin Xian was also suspicious.","[Actually, although Ke Yun'er was the one who caused Yu's Father to lose his fertility, she wasn’t entirely sure whose child she was carrying. So, she had secretly done a paternity test. She couldn’t find anything belonging to Yu Yue, but she could use Yu's Father’s DNA to prove it wasn’t his child. In her mind, there were only two possibilities: Yu's Father or Yu Yue. The test results, of course, showed it wasn’t Yu's Father’s child, so she concluded it must be Yu Yue’s.]","[However, to keep the test secret, she went to a private hospital, unaware that it was the same hospital the ex-wife had invested in after her divorce. The ex-wife had naturally investigated who had taken her place and recognized Ke Yun'er. This was a perfect opportunity to expose her and get revenge, choosing this exact day to crash the wedding.]","Sure enough, the ex-wife dropped an even more explosive bombshell.","\"Not only is the child not yours, but it’s also related to you by blood. Do you know what that means? She’s been cheating on you with someone in your family!\"","This was like adding fuel to the fire.","Everyone in the room was utterly shocked.","The drama had truly exploded!!!!"]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311: Everything That Shouldn't Be Exposed Has Been Exposed","paragraphs":["Yu's Father was probably in a daze from the moment he heard the first words from his ex-wife's sister, and by the second sentence, he could hardly stand.","Fortunately, Yu Yue supported him.","Yu Yue was also stunned at this moment. He had already swallowed his anger, feeling frustrated, but now the previous aunt suddenly showed up and exposed everything. He really didn't know how to thank her!","Hahaha, anyway, it wasn't him who exposed it, and it was directly revealed that the child wasn't his father's. Whether the child had fallen or not wasn't something people cared about anymore.","Meanwhile, the others in the small group were giving Yu Yue a sidelong glance.","Did Yu Yue forget that Ke Yun'er has always believed the child is hers? If she starts talking nonsense later...","On this point, Qin Xian didn't think it was something to worry about. Originally, he thought it would be hard to prove, but since someone here had already done a paternity test, they must have kept the samples. If they were falsely accused later, they could just do the test again.","On the other side, the whole place was already buzzing with discussions, and other members of the Yu family quickly stood up to help maintain order.","Yu's Father snapped back to reality and immediately flew into a rage: \"I compensated you when we divorced! What are you causing a scene for now?\"","【He's not even doubting?!】","The Qin family also found it incredible. Was it out of concern for face, or was he blinded by beauty?","Qin Xian, however, could analyze Yu's Father's mindset. After all, he had just found out that he had completely lost his ability to have children. If the last child he thought he had wasn't his own, he couldn't accept it. So, he subconsciously chose to believe that his ex-wife was trying to destroy his family.","Next to him, Ke Yun'er's face looked terrible. She was feeling guilty, so she was nervously looking at Yu Yue, as if hoping for a mutual understanding glance.","Yu Yue naturally felt the intense gaze from beside him. He trembled, but inside, he was gloating even more, almost wanting to roll his eyes at Ke Yun'er.","Seeing that Yu Yue wouldn't even look at her, Ke Yun'er couldn't help but feel wronged. She bit her lip and turned to the newcomer: \"I know you hate me, but you can't slander my and my child's innocence with such things.\"","The ex-wife's sister naturally knew she wouldn't admit it easily, so she directly presented the evidence.","She opened the paternity test report and practically slapped it in Yu's Father's face for him to see clearly.","Ke Yun'er's face turned ashen in an instant, while the ex-wife's sister looked smug.","\"You probably didn't know that the hospital where you did the paternity test is under my control. Hehe, I'd like to see how you, this shameless bitch, will try to weasel your way out with the evidence right in front of you.\" The ex-wife's sister sneered.","Ke Yun'er was now truly frozen in fear. She instinctively tried to look for Yu Yue, only to see that he was also intently reading the report, his eyes even lighting up.","Ke Yun'er didn't have time to think deeply; she only felt like her world was collapsing. The best scenario she had envisioned was ruined by this bitch in front of her.","No, she couldn't admit it.","\"How is that possible? This is fake! Husband, it must be fake. She's fabricating this to slander me. She works at the hospital, so it's easy for her to frame me. Husband, you have to believe me.\" Ke Yun'er immediately started crying pitifully.","Yu's Father was still in a daze.","But others weren't buying Ke Yun'er's story.","After all, the ex-wife was so confident, and there was evidence. Plus, people didn't know that the child was gone, so they thought the ex-wife had no reason to lie about something that could be easily verified. Moreover...","Many people's gazes, which should have been focused on the main characters, were now filled with awe as they glanced at Ji Fei.","Earlier, they had been caught off guard by the big reveal, but now everyone had caught on.","The gossip king of the wealthy families was here, so this juicy piece of news was bound to be true.","So at this moment, everyone had skipped the process of verifying the truth and started thinking about the ex-wife's sister's words.","If it's not a father-son relationship but a kinship, holy crap! Someone in the Yu family is giving Yu's Father a green hat! And they want Yu's Father to raise someone else's child!","It must be about inheritance! They're familiar with this; they just saw someone almost becoming a stepfather recently!","In the small group, Luo Fei suddenly sneezed and then continued watching the drama unfold with everyone else.","【Yo, yo, yo, I think no one's expression is as interesting as Yu Yi's right now. After all, he's not sure if he'll be exposed either. He's just praying that if things get messy later, Ke Yun'er will stick to her story and blame Yu Yue. And since Yu Yue was drunk that night, maybe he won't remember anything. Plus, with their past relationship, Yu Yue will be left speechless. Yu Yi's calm expression right now is all thanks to these points.】","In fact, many people were trying to figure out who had given Yu's Father the green hat.","At the moment, Yu Yue seemed the least suspicious, as his love for Bai Xiaoxi was well-known. Many women had tried to seduce Yu Yue, only to be turned down, so people weren't paying much attention to him.","The remaining Yu men, however, felt like they were being watched like hawks.","One by one, they jumped out and demanded: \"Brother, what's going on here?!\"","\"This matter must be cleared up, or else what will happen to our Yu family's reputation?\"","\"It has nothing to do with me. I'm meeting the new sister-in-law for the first time today.\"","The women beside those men couldn't help but start giving their own husbands suspicious looks. After all, the Yu family believed in having many children for prosperity. In other words, compared to other families, the Yu family would be more lenient towards having illegitimate children. So, except for Yu Yue, none of the Yu men were exactly faithful.","But even so, such a ridiculous thing shouldn't happen.","Yu's Father was trembling all over as he turned to look at Ke Yun'er. Ke Yun'er was crying like a pear blossom bathed in rain, shaking her head desperately, and finally added: \"If you doubt me, then let's get a divorce. This position of madam can be taken by whoever wants it. I don't care.\"","With that, she acted as if she were heartbroken and was about to leave.","【Oh, she's got some acting skills, huh? No wonder she can dish out such a juicy piece of gossip.】","But clearly, the current situation wasn't going to fall for her act.","Especially since the ex-wife's sister was here only to cause trouble and seek revenge, not to try and win the man back.","\"What are you crying about? Do you think I'd really wrong you? Let's just go and do the test again right now. If I've wronged you, I'll kneel down and apologize to you.\" The ex-wife's sister said, turning to Yu's Father: \"After all, we were once husband and wife. I heard you've hurt your body and can't have children anymore. I just couldn't bear to see you being kept in the dark. There's a green hat right beside you. Be careful of becoming someone else's stepfather.\"","Hahaha, this big sister is a genius! She's exposing everything, even the stuff that shouldn't be revealed. Although some people already knew about the fertility issue, not everyone did. Now it's like a full-on gossip buffet!","Indeed, Yu's Father's face turned green. If this had happened under normal circumstances, he would have tried to cover it up and investigate secretly. After all, he couldn't let himself lose face in public.","But now, with his ex-wife shoving it in his face, even if he wanted to temporarily suppress it, the other innocent members of the Yu family wouldn't allow it.","Sure enough, before he could speak, the other Yu wives started supporting the ex-wife's sister."]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312: Shifting the Conflict, Unable to Authenticate","paragraphs":["\"Right, Ke Yun'er, can crying serve as proof? Just go for a paternity test to clear your name, otherwise, people will keep gossiping about you.\"","\"That's right, Ke Yun'er, don’t be afraid. If the facts prove you’ve been wronged, our Yu Family will definitely compensate you.\"","\"I don’t care about the rest, but my husband is definitely innocent. I need to prove it for him, so no one can talk behind our backs.\"","The women of the Yu Family spoke in a sarcastic tone, eyeing each other suspiciously, each doubting the other’s husband.","Their husbands, of course, were willing to cooperate, as they knew in their hearts whether they were involved or not.","Yu Yi, who had no wife, was surprisingly overlooked for the moment.","Perhaps it was because Yu Yi had always been known to mingle with young, carefree girls, so they subconsciously didn’t think he’d be interested in Ke Yun'er.","But Yu Yi’s expression was slightly complicated.","What if they dug deeper? Wouldn’t he be exposed then?","Meanwhile, the happiest person in the Yu Family at that moment was Yu Yue.","So, when Ke Yun'er sent another desperate plea for help, Yu Yue ignored it and even turned to Bai Xiaoxi, exchanging meaningful glances with her.","At that moment, Ke Yun'er felt as if a string in her brain had snapped. Her face darkened, and she completely forgot to maintain her fragile, innocent facade.","Yu's Father was furious, but he still hadn’t completely doubted Ke Yun'er. In his eyes, she had always been delicate and unlikely to have the courage to do such a thing. So, in this tense atmosphere, Yu's Father could only say, \"Fine, let’s do the test. But if you’re lying to me...\"","He shot a menacing look at his ex-wife.","The ex-wife, however, wasn’t fazed at all. After all, she was telling the truth and even gestured for Yu's Father to proceed.","Just as Yu's Father was about to grab Ke Yun'er, she noticed that Yu Yue remained indifferent. Unable to bear the pressure any longer, she shouted, \"Don’t touch me!\"","Yu's Father was startled, his expression instantly changing as he looked at Ke Yun'er. \"So, you really...\"","\"No, the child was yours, but... our child... is gone,\" Ke Yun'er said, covering her face and bursting into tears. \"I had a miscarriage while you were abroad.\"","Yu's Father wasn’t even sure about the child’s identity yet. What if it really was his last child?","The news hit him like a thunderbolt, and he immediately grabbed Ke Yun'er’s arm, demanding, \"What are you talking about? How could you have a miscarriage? Didn’t you follow the doctor’s orders and have people take good care of you? How dare you...\"","Everyone was stunned.","What?","The child is gone?","Wait, isn’t this plot moving too fast? Weren’t they just trying to figure out who the father was?","\"Ha, Old Yu, still can’t figure it out? What a coincidence, huh! I think she realized after the test that the child wasn’t yours. She was too scared to let you know she’d been messing around with your family behind your back, so she got rid of the child on purpose,\" the ex-wife said bluntly. \"Once you marry her, she’ll fake another accident and pretend to lose the child. Don’t let her fool you.\"","Her explanation made perfect sense. Everyone couldn’t help but nod, feeling that this was probably the truth.","\"Shut up!\" Yu's Father was now beyond caring. If the child was still here, he’d have some hope. But with the child gone, did it even matter whose it was? \"Tell me what really happened!\"","Ke Yun'er trembled, finally lowering her hands from her face, her eyes darting around.","Things were moving too fast. Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi hadn’t expected it to escalate to this point, leaving them unprepared.","The next second, Ke Yun'er pointed at Bai Xiaoxi. \"It was Miss Bai who accidentally pushed me, causing me to fall. That’s why I lost the child. I really didn’t mean to. It was my child too, wuwuwu...\"","The crowd was choking on their metaphorical popcorn. One moment they were shocked by the news of the child’s loss, and the next, they heard that the loss was connected to Yu's Father’s future daughter-in-law.","Was this another case of family drama in a wealthy household?","This was a chain of scandals!","They didn’t even know which part to focus on anymore.","They couldn’t help but marvel at how the scandals in wealthy families were never small.","The first to react were the Bai Couple, who were doting parents. They had come as future in-laws to attend the wedding, but now their precious daughter was being dragged into the Yu Family’s mess. If it weren’t for Yu Yue’s genuine affection for Bai Xiaoxi, the Bai family would have been utterly disgusted by the Yu Family’s situation.","The protective couple immediately rushed to their daughter’s side, shielding her from both sides.","\"Nonsense!\"","\"How could our Xiaoxi push you?\"","But before they could defend her further, they noticed that Bai Xiaoxi’s face had turned pale.","Even though they had confirmed that the child wasn’t Yu Yue’s, the thought of possibly being responsible for a child not being born weighed heavily on Bai Xiaoxi’s conscience.","Being publicly accused like this only made her look worse.","In contrast, Yu Yue’s face darkened instantly.","[Ah, as expected, she’s still targeting Bai Xiaoxi, trying to use her as a scapegoat. This woman is really... It was all her own plan. We can’t let her succeed, but what can we do?]","Ji Fei was getting anxious, but the next moment, someone wrapped an arm around her shoulders and whispered in her ear, \"Don’t worry, leave it to Yu Yue. He’ll protect his own wife.\"","Ji Fei didn’t think much of it and instinctively felt reassured.","The rest of the group was on edge, unsure of how to help.","Meanwhile, Ke Yun'er continued her accusations, addressing the Bai Couple. \"I know Miss Bai didn’t mean to do it. It was truly an accident. If I hadn’t been forced into this situation today, I wouldn’t have brought it up. But it’s because of Miss Bai that I lost my child. Now that I’m being falsely accused, I just... wuwuwu!\"","If what she said was true, then she was truly unfortunate.","After all, in everyone’s mind, since the child was gone, there was no way to conduct a paternity test.","Before the ex-wife could expose the absurdity of this claim, Yu's Father turned to Bai Xiaoxi and asked, \"Was it you, Xiaoxi?\"","The Bai Couple tensed up. Seeing their daughter’s expression, they knew there might have been some kind of accident. They were about to say something when suddenly, Yu Yue spoke in a cold, low voice.","\"Don’t throw any dirty water on my precious girl.\"","\"I’ve already investigated. Before the incident, your prenatal check-up report showed that the child was already in distress. Regardless of whether Xiaoxi accidentally pulled you or not, that child was never going to be born. So, I have every reason to suspect that you deliberately used the child to frame Xiaoxi.\"","Actually, this wasn’t true. Qin Xian had thought of it earlier and sent a message to Yu Yue, suggesting he look into it. Yu Yue was just bluffing now."]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313: The First Slap in This Scene Actually Came from the Ex-Wife's Sister","paragraphs":["Ke Yun'er was a very cautious person. Apart from regular check-ups, which she conducted at hospitals associated with the Yu family, she always switched to different hospitals for other examinations. This was why she had accidentally been caught by the Ex-wife.","As for the final check-up of the fetus, it was even more secretive. Ke Yun'er had borrowed someone else's identity to get it done.","However, because of the Ex-wife's interference, Ke Yun'er was no longer as confident about keeping the matter confidential.","So when Yu Yue firmly exposed the truth, Ke Yun'er thought he had genuinely discovered it.","Ke Yun'er's eyes instantly turned bloodshot, and she stared at Yu Yue in disbelief. But Yu Yue had already walked over to Bai Xiaoxi, wrapping his arm around her as if he wanted to shower her with the most tender care in the world.","Ke Yun'er was so jealous that it felt like her heart was bleeding.","She couldn't understand why Yu Yue would do this. The child was his. How could he bear to push her into such a predicament?","Was it just to protect Bai Xiaoxi from harm? How unfair!","\"Using a stillborn fetus to frame our daughter, you are scheming and full of lies! We demand an explanation from the Yu family,\" Bai's parents, who were fiercely protective of their daughter, were immediately furious.","\"Yu Yue, is this true? What exactly is going on? Did you already know the child was gone?\" Yu's Father finally found his voice and loudly questioned.","Yu Yue coldly looked at Ke Yun'er and calmly lied, \"At first, I was also deceived. I thought it was caused by an accident involving Xiaoxi, so I had to keep it hidden temporarily while I investigated further. Eventually, I stumbled upon Ke Yun'er's previous medical records and discovered that the fetus had already been stillborn and was supposed to be aborted.\"","In truth, Yu Yue had been somewhat uncertain before, as there was no concrete evidence. The whole situation seemed unbelievable, and it was just Qin Xian's speculation.","But after speaking, seeing Ke Yun'er's expression, Yu Yue knew he was right.","How dare she deceive them and make Xiaoxi suffer for so long? She deserved to die!","So now, lying came without any burden.","Bai Xiaoxi, still naive, thought Yu Yue had truly uncovered the truth in such a short time. Recalling Ke Yun'er's schemes and slander against them, Bai Xiaoxi couldn't help but glare fiercely at the wicked woman.","Meanwhile, Ke Yun'er, under Yu Yue's repeated accusations, was in tears, looking utterly heartbroken.","Her demeanor was directed at Yu Yue, genuine and emotional, but since Yu Yue and Yu's Father were standing close together, Yu's Father thought she was addressing him. His shattered heart began to feel a hint of pity.","Many onlookers also felt sympathy, but the next moment, they all subtly glanced at Ji Fei.","Ji Fei was like a weather vane. As the gossip queen of the elite circles and the judge of the entertainment industry, whoever Ji Fei sided with was innocent, and whoever she didn't support was undoubtedly in the wrong.","At least, that's how it had always been in the past.","So even though Ke Yun'er now resembled the tragic heroine Dou E, everyone remained cautious.","Yu's Father couldn't help but speak up, \"Stop crying. Tell us, what exactly is going on?\" He tried to salvage his pride, still hoping for a miracle.","Ke Yun'er was on the verge of breaking down but still managed to defend herself.","\"It was me... I found out the fetus had stopped growing, and I was too scared... too scared to take responsibility. Then I got into a scuffle with Bai Xiaoxi and took advantage of the situation... I was cowardly, but the child was really yours, husband.\"","With no evidence to prove otherwise, Ke Yun'er naturally wouldn't foolishly admit to anything.","At the same time, she felt a deep sense of sorrow. Even though Yu Yue had abandoned her, she still refused to expose him, protecting him like this. Yet, he was protecting another woman. It felt like she owed him from a past life.","At this moment, Ji Fei happened to witness the scene.","She was utterly disgusted.","[Seriously, are you still addicted to playing the tragic heroine? Anyone would think Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi are the scumbag and the villainess!]","The Qin family, seasoned in gossip, suspected that Ke Yun'er might still be hoping for the day Yu Yue would abandon Bai Xiaoxi, leading to a fiery reunion.","Qin Xian could only be thankful that Yu Yue couldn't hear Ji Fei's inner commentary, or he would have been so disgusted that he might have punched someone on the spot.","Meanwhile, Yu Yi, who had been keeping a low profile, was feeling incredibly conflicted. He had just realized that Ke Yun'er had used their unborn child to get close to Yu Yue, and it made him sick to his stomach.","Earlier, he had felt sorry for Ke Yun'er, who was being ganged up on, and had considered taking a risk to help her. But now, he decided to stay out of the mess. After all, there was no way he could be implicated, so he saw no point in getting involved.","Yu's Father was also struggling, unsure of how to handle the situation.","Ke Yun'er quickly added, \"I know now. It must be this woman who found out our child was gone and fabricated a false report to slander me. She wants to leave me with no way to defend myself.\"","Hearing this, Yu's Father's eyes lit up, as if this was the only way to save face.","[Watching Ke Yun'er fight alone like this is quite impressive. She managed to find such an angle to counterattack. But the Ex-wife came prepared too.]","As soon as Ke Yun'er finished speaking, the Ex-wife smirked disdainfully and fired back, \"You didn't think that losing the child would make it impossible to verify, did you?\"","Ke Yun'er's sobbing paused almost imperceptibly. That was exactly what she had thought. Wasn't it the case?","\"Tsk tsk tsk, you had the test done at my hospital. Did you think I wouldn't keep the samples you provided? Don't worry, everything is intact. Take your husband and the possible affair partner for a check-up, and the truth will come out.\"","[A direct hit. Now there's no way to refute it. I wonder if she'll expose the affair partner.]","The Qin family was also curious. If she did, the name would undoubtedly be Yu Yue. Once that happened, more arguments would ensue, and more juicy gossip would be revealed... making it a feast for everyone present.","By now, the entire room was buzzing with excitement over the twists and turns of the drama.","It was truly a rollercoaster. Otherwise, it would have been hard to definitively conclude that Ke Yun'er was in the wrong.","Now, the truth could finally be revealed, depending on whether Ke Yun'er dared to go through with the test.","But... it seemed unnecessary.","Because, in front of everyone, Ke Yun'er finally broke down. Her legs gave way, and she collapsed to the floor, shouting in disbelief, \"You... you bitch!\"","The next second, the Ex-wife slapped her across the face. \"Watch your mouth! I'm not as shameless as you, cheating on your husband and trying to make him raise another man's child. Who's the real bitch here?\"","Ke Yun'er was stunned, and no one had expected the first slap of the drama to come from the Ex-wife."]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314: Because I Didn't Sleep in My Room That Night at All","paragraphs":["The ex-wife had just delivered a satisfying act of revenge. She turned to Yu's Father, her eyes filled with mockery, though her words were cloaked in righteousness. \"Old Yu, next time you marry, make sure to keep your eyes open. Oh, wait, you can't have children anymore, so what's the point? Just forget it. No need to play the cheap father figure again.\"","The ex-wife harbored deep resentment for this couple and wasn’t about to let either of them off easily. Her words were meant to cut deep.","Ke Yun'er's reaction had already been an indirect admission of guilt. Now, with the ex-wife's biting sarcasm, Yu's Father was on the verge of collapsing.","Others rushed to support him, keeping him upright. After all, it was his wedding, his wife—he had to deal with this mess himself.","Once he caught his breath, Yu's Father lunged forward and, before Ke Yun'er could react, slapped her twice across the face.","\"You wretch! After all I’ve done for you, you betray me like this? Tell me, who’s your lover? Don’t waste my time making me investigate!\" Finally facing reality, Yu's Father was consumed by humiliation and rage, ready to destroy the woman who had embarrassed him so publicly.","Ke Yun'er had never endured such humiliation, especially in front of so many people. She lost all restraint and screamed, \"You’ve been good to me? You’re nothing but a lecherous old man!\"","\"What? You were the one who seduced me! You wanted to climb the ladder!\" Yu's Father shot back, gasping for breath.","His words only made Ke Yun'er more hysterical. \"I respected you like an elder, cared for you like one! But you took advantage of my kindness. If it weren’t for your inappropriate intentions, my parents wouldn’t have drugged me and sent me to your bed. You shameless old man! Did you really think I’d willingly climb into your bed? I was forced into this from the start!\"","Yu's Father's face turned green with anger. \"I’ve never forced a woman in my life. If your family set this up, that’s on them. If you were truly forced, why didn’t you speak up afterward? You could’ve sued! Instead, you played the devoted girlfriend and even agreed to marry me. Did I force you into that?\"","On this point, Yu's Father wasn’t wrong. He was known for his womanizing ways, but he never resorted to coercion.","Still, both parties had their share of grievances in this situation.","Ke Yun'er broke down. \"What was I supposed to do? The damage was done. You ruined any chance I had with the man I truly loved. I had no choice but to settle for you.\"","After all, it wasn’t just anyone—it was a father-son relationship. She knew she could never openly marry Yu Yue. If she wanted to stay close to him, she had to settle for his father.","Yu's Father, however, felt like he’d been played. \"This isn’t some ancient drama! It’s not all my fault. I feel like I’ve been scammed!\"","To everyone else, Ke Yun'er's story sounded far-fetched. No one had ever heard of a young, beautiful woman doting on a notorious womanizer like a father figure. It was bound to be misunderstood.","But those who knew the truth understood that Ke Yun'er had indeed treated Yu's Father like a future father-in-law, hoping to win his favor and perhaps even become his daughter-in-law.","Unfortunately, Yu's Father mistook her kindness for flirtation, leading to this mess. It was a situation too absurd to comprehend.","\"I don’t care about your twisted excuses. I’ve done nothing wrong. You’re the one who owes me an explanation! Tell me, who is it?\" Yu's Father demanded, his fiery gaze sweeping over the other men in the Yu family, his expression dark.","Ke Yun'er, however, fell silent, still playing the martyr for love.","But the other men in the Yu family weren’t about to let this slide. They needed answers.","Yu Yi’s heart raced. Based on what Ke Yun'er had said earlier, it seemed she and Yu Yue had been involved, even discussing having another child. That night, Yu Yue had also been drunk. Maybe, like him, Yu Yue didn’t remember what happened. Perhaps this could be brushed off as a misunderstanding.","But when Yu Yi looked up, he saw Yu Yue completely ignoring Ke Yun'er. Was he really that confident?","This made Yu Yi uneasy.","\"Not talking? Fine, we’ll investigate this together!\" Yu's Father roared.","Ke Yun'er panicked. She was sacrificing herself for love and had to protect Yu Yue at all costs. She quickly glanced at him, expecting him to step in now, no matter how indifferent he’d been before.","But instead, she saw Yu Yue showing something on his phone to Bai Xiaoxi, pinching her cheek affectionately and urging her to relax.","Bai Xiaoxi, engrossed in the phone, shot him an annoyed look. Yu Yue laughed, then pretended to pout, prompting Bai Xiaoxi to stand on her tiptoes and kiss him.","The sight burned Ke Yun'er’s eyes. While she was suffering, they were... How could they? Why?","Now, Ke Yun'er was too exhausted to wonder why Yu Yue was so confident.","She suddenly laughed, her laughter growing wild and bitter, feeling utterly betrayed.","\"If you’re going to be this heartless, don’t blame me for being ruthless. Even if I go to hell, I won’t go alone,\" Ke Yun'er shouted at Yu Yue, her words instantly drawing everyone’s attention to him.","\"That child I lost wasn’t yours—it was your son’s! You almost became a grandfather!\" Ke Yun'er sneered at Yu's Father, her expression bordering on madness.","Everyone except those who already knew the truth was stunned, unable to process what they’d just heard.","The room fell silent.","They had suspected every man in the Yu family—except Yu Yue.","After all, Yu Yue’s obsession with Bai Xiaoxi was practically a cautionary tale among the elite. Who would neglect their family business just to dote on their wife?","But that was exactly what Yu Yue did, always orbiting around Bai Xiaoxi. So the idea of him cheating with Ke Yun'er was hard for anyone to swallow.","The Bai family reacted first, looking at Yu Yue without outright suspicion but clearly waiting for an explanation.","Yu's Father, however, stared at his son in shock. He had never been close to Yu Yue and knew the boy resented him for his mother’s death.","So when Ke Yun'er made her accusation, Yu's Father was inclined to believe it, wondering if this was Yu Yue’s revenge.","But the next second, Yu Yue scoffed, \"Am I blind? Why would I sleep with you? Don’t flatter yourself—it’s disgusting.\"","Yu Yue had been wanting to curse at Ke Yun'er for a while, and now she’d given him the perfect opportunity.","Hearing such cruel words, Ke Yun'er froze, as if the person she’d imagined had shattered before her eyes.","They had shared something, so how could he say something so brutal?","\"Why... why would you say that? Don’t you believe the child was yours? Don’t you remember that night at the old house? We both drank, I went to your room, and even though you left in the morning, you slept with me. Can you deny that?\" Ke Yun'er pleaded like a scorned woman, questioning her betrayer.","\"I drank, but I wasn’t drunk.\"","\"No! That’s impossible! You’re just refusing to admit it!\"","\"Why wouldn’t I admit it? Because I wasn’t even in my room that night. Right... Uncle Yu Yi?\" Yu Yue turned to Yu Yi."]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315: Don't Dump Every Shit and Piss Pot on Me","paragraphs":["Yu Yi, suddenly called out in the crowd, was startled and felt a pang of guilt. But since even Ke Yun'er, the person directly involved, had mistaken the situation, he thought there was no way Yu Yue could know the truth.","“Huh? Why are you asking me? I don’t remember anything from that night,” Yu Yi shamelessly pretended to be clueless.","“Really? You were indeed very drunk that night. You vomited all over your room, so I kindly brought you to my room to settle in. Later, when your room was cleaned up, you refused to leave, so I went to your room to rest. That’s why, when Ke Yun'er just said she entered my room, the person she was with must have been you,” Yu Yue didn’t give him a chance to play dumb and directly revealed what had happened that night.","At this moment, Ke Yun'er was stunned. Her heart pounded like a drum, her face gradually turned pale, and she slowly turned to look at Yu Yi.","That night, she had been too afraid to turn on the lights. Seeing the figure sleeping soundly on the bed, she had embraced it. When she woke up the next morning, the person was already gone...","Suddenly, Ke Yun'er remembered Yu Yi’s strange attitude and words when he had approached her earlier. It felt like a thunderbolt had struck her, leaving her completely disoriented.","The secrets of the prominent family were now exposed, and the onlookers were utterly captivated.","Their gazes followed Yu Yue’s and landed on Yu Yi.","Just moments ago, they thought it was a story of a stepmother’s inappropriate behavior, but now it had turned into a scandal between an uncle and his sister-in-law?!","“This is too explosive! So, it was Yu Yi?”","“Yu Yi slept with his sister-in-law in his nephew’s room?”","“Didn’t you notice the details? Ke Yun'er admitted she sneaked into Yu Yue’s room. What was she trying to do? Seduce her stepson?”","“So, she wanted to sleep with Yu Yue but ended up with Yu Yi instead?”","“She slept with the wrong person?! No wonder she insisted the child was Yu Yue’s. She got it all wrong.”","Ke Yun'er shook her head in disbelief and shouted at Yu Yue, “If you don’t want to admit it, fine! But why push me onto someone else? That night, it was you! The person I was with was you! The child is yours!”","“Oh, really? I’m willing to take a paternity test,” Yu Yue said indifferently.","Ke Yun'er froze, completely at a loss. She teetered on the edge of a breakdown as she began to accept the possibility that it might not have been Yu Yue that night.","Yu Yi’s face stiffened, and he felt a surge of guilt. He quickly tried to shift the blame, “You said I was drunk that night. You can make up any story you want. I’ve heard that you and Ke Yun'er had an unclear relationship before. Not only were you high school classmates, but you also studied abroad together. You’ve been sneaking around behind my brother’s back for a long time. Nephew, take care of your own woman. Don’t pin this on me.”","The crowd was stunned. There was even more drama to uncover!","So, Ke Yun'er’s obsession with seducing her stepson was because they had a history?","Had Yu's Father been wearing a green hat all along?","At this moment, Yu's Father was trembling with rage, overwhelmed by the waves of shocking revelations. He pointed at Ke Yun'er, then at Yu Yue, “You... you...”","By now, Ke Yun'er had nothing left to lose. “Yes, Yu Yue and I were together before. When we were studying abroad, we...”","Yu Yue shrugged and sneered, “You two created this mess, and now you’re trying to dump it on me? You really love playing the victim, don’t you?”","With that, he coldly glared at Ke Yun'er.","Ke Yun'er’s eyes still held a trace of desperate love for Yu Yue, but she was met with his scornful laughter. “To be honest, before returning home this time, I had no idea who you were. I don’t know where you got the nerve to fantasize about a relationship with me. You’re like a deranged stalker—even a sasaeng fan isn’t as terrifying as you.”","These humiliating words made Ke Yun'er’s blood run cold.","In her self-deluded world, Yu Yue had feelings for her. Even if he rejected her on the surface, how could he insult her so harshly?","“Yu Yue, are you denying everything we had? That night, you said you loved me!” Ke Yun'er finally broke down and burst into tears.","But Yu Yue casually replied, “I suggest you make sure who you’re sleeping with next time, you idiot.”","With that, he took out his phone and played two voice messages in front of everyone. These were the messages he had just received, allowing him to stand tall in front of Bai Xiaoxi.","The conversation was simple. Yu Yue had asked the organizer of their last gathering before he dropped out about who Ke Yun'er had been with that night.","Yu Yue knew he had left early that night, so he had no reason to worry.","The organizer’s tone was teasing.","“Ke Yun'er? Oh, you finally noticed her? It’s a bit late, don’t you think? We all knew she had a crush on you, but you were completely oblivious, always thinking about your fiancée. That night, I remember she was probably trying to give up on you, so she sat next to you and drank. But you left early, remember? After that, she drank with Jie. You probably didn’t know Jie liked her, so that night, she was probably with Jie. Later, Jie tried to pursue her, but she rejected him harshly. Jie was heartbroken and stopped hanging out with us.”","When the voice message ended, the room fell silent.","The onlookers understood that this was evidence clearing Yu Yue’s name, but they were still confused about the details. One thing was clear: this stepmother had been lusting after her stepson for a long time.","Now, everyone began to realize that her previous closeness to Yu's Father might have been purely out of respect for an elder.","But the way she shamelessly pursued Yu Yue, despite his very public relationship with Bai Xiaoxi, showed she wasn’t a decent person.","The crowd’s gazes grew increasingly disdainful, and Ke Yun'er’s face was now as pale as a corpse.","If the incident at the old house had been an accident, she could have consoled herself with the thought that her past relationship with Yu Yue couldn’t be erased.","But the voice message shattered her delusions.","Jie—she remembered him, the man who had pursued her. But at the time, her heart and mind were consumed by Yu Yue, who had suddenly dropped out of school. She hadn’t paid any attention to Jie’s words or actions.","Now, she vaguely recalled Jie offering to take responsibility, but she had completely ignored him.","She had convinced herself that it was a night of heartfelt confessions between her and Yu Yue, the closest they had ever been. How could she admit that she had been utterly confused and heavily drunk that night?","“Did you hear that? Don’t dump your mess on me. I’m not taking the blame. From start to finish, I’ve only ever been with Bai Xiaoxi. I don’t even know you,” Yu Yue said, ignoring the devastated Ke Yun'er. He turned to the dazed Yu Yi and said, “Uncle, stop changing the subject. I can prove I have nothing to do with her. But you—are you willing to take a paternity test to see if that child is really yours?”"]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316: Because I Am a DINK","paragraphs":["The crowd, which had almost been led astray, instantly focused their attention on Yu Yi.","Yu's Father also turned to look at his youngest brother.","Under the gaze of countless eyes, Yu Yi's face turned red, and he took a step back in fright, momentarily at a loss for words.","He glared resentfully at Ke Yun'er, that crazy woman. How was he supposed to know that the so-called youthful love story was all a figment of her imagination?","Yu Yue had nothing to do with her!","And he had been fooled by this fantasy—what terrible luck!","Yu Yue could produce both witnesses and evidence, so there was no point in trying to argue further.","\"I... I...\" Unable to withstand the pressure, Yu Yi immediately addressed Yu's Father, \"Brother, you can't blame me for this. You heard it yourself—I was completely drunk and passed out. If someone climbed into my bed, how was I supposed to know who it was? I was completely dragged into this. It was this woman who wanted to set up Yu Yue. I’m just a victim of your family drama. What did I do to deserve this?\"","As he spoke, Yu Yi's eyes welled up with tears, feeling wronged. After all, having an affair with his sister-in-law was a scandal that would haunt him for the rest of his life.","But he was also innocent—he had been caught up in this mess for no reason.","Although the onlookers were shocked by the drama, they couldn’t help but feel that Yu Yi had been unfairly implicated.","Now that the truth was out, it was clear that Ke Yun'er was the one who had caused all the trouble.","Yu's Father was so furious that he felt like he was on the verge of collapse. His wife had coveted his son, and she had even slept with his younger brother. If the child hadn’t been lost, he would have been raising a child that wasn’t his own for the rest of his life. He had never suffered such a humiliating insult.","Yu's Father, who had been so enraged that he seemed to age decades in an instant, suddenly sprang up, his face twisted with anger. He punched Yu Yi and then kicked Ke Yun'er, who was sitting on the floor.","Ke Yun'er was nearly sent flying by the force of the kick, showing just how much strength Yu's Father had put into it.","Yu Yi, who had been beaten, now sat quietly, playing the role of the victim.","But Ke Yun'er, who had gotten back up, didn’t beg for mercy or argue. Instead, she seemed to be in a trance as she suddenly lunged at Yu Yue.","Yu Yue, naturally, dodged with Bai Xiaoxi in his arms, and Ke Yun'er crashed into the table, creating a mess. Amid the chaos, her frantic screams could be heard.","\"No, it’s not someone else—it’s you! Every time, it’s been you! My child is yours too! You just don’t want to admit it! I know you’re still worried about the alliance between our families. You don’t dare to break ties with the Bai family. You’re still bound by family responsibilities, so you don’t dare to admit your feelings for me!\"","[What a joke. Even at this point, she’s still deluding herself.]","Qin Xian sneered inwardly. In fact, Ke Yun'er had long known about Yu Yue’s feelings for Bai Xiaoxi.","The most telling evidence was that when she had initially schemed to cause Bai Xiaoxi to miscarry, she didn’t immediately expose Bai Xiaoxi to ruin the relationship between the two families. Instead, she chose to hide it and try to have another child. This was because she knew that Yu Yue loved Bai Xiaoxi and wouldn’t leave her over this. She knew she had no chance, so she settled for trying to secure some benefit for herself.","It could only be said that Ke Yun'er was truly a master of self-delusion, a paranoid obsessive.","Naturally, none of the onlookers believed Ke Yun'er now.","Yu Yue, with disgust in his eyes, said, \"Stop being so narcissistic, okay? Everyone knows that the only person I’ve ever loved is Bai Xiaoxi. I’ll only ever marry her. I...\"","Before Yu Yue could finish his bold declaration, Ke Yun'er finally shouted, \"You’ve been deceived, Yu Yue! You’ve been deceived! Let me tell you, actually...\"","It happened so quickly that no one could react to what Ke Yun'er was about to say. It felt like she was about to reveal some huge secret.","But the next second, an abrupt cry interrupted everything.","\"Ah!\"","Everyone was startled and turned to look at the source of the sound, instantly surprised to see that it was Ji Fei.","Ji Fei was now breathing rapidly, her heart racing as if it were about to explode.","[It’s not that I wanted to interrupt, but this woman is truly evil. She was about to publicly reveal that Bai Xiaoxi can’t have children. She’s still deluding herself, thinking that if she exposes this, Yu Yue won’t marry a woman who can’t bear children, and he’ll come back to her. Even if that doesn’t happen, she wants to make sure the Yu family completely rejects Bai Xiaoxi.]","The Qin family, who had been wondering what Ji Fei was doing, instantly felt their anger rise. How could there be such a woman who couldn’t stand to see others happy?","After all, society is harsh on women. Not every woman is strong enough to face gossip and slander without being affected. This was why the Bai family had worked so hard to keep it a secret—they didn’t want their daughter to be the subject of gossip, nor did they want outsiders bothering them about having no heirs.","Bai Xiaoxi was already sensitive about this issue. If too many people found out, even if they could fend off the malicious ones, the well-meaning advice from others would still hurt her deeply.","So the best solution was to keep it a secret forever.","But for the sake of her own selfish desires, Ke Yun'er was willing to expose Bai Xiaoxi’s secret in public, even though it had nothing to do with the conflict at hand. It was truly despicable.","Qin Xian had also figured out what Ke Yun'er was about to say almost at the same time, but Ji Fei’s system was faster. He immediately gave Yu Yue a look.","Yu Yue’s face instantly turned pale as he understood.","Although Ji Fei had reacted quickly, she could only manage to interrupt for a moment. However, the sudden interruption left her without a suitable excuse.","After two awkward seconds, Ji Fei decided to sacrifice Qin Xian.","\"Honey, you stepped on my foot,\" Ji Fei said awkwardly, looking at Qin Xian.","Qin Xian: \"...Sorry, I was too absorbed in listening.\"","The onlookers: ?","The gossip queen is quite delicate, isn’t she? Stepping on her foot made her scream as if she’d been seriously hurt.","Back to the matter at hand—what was Ke Yun'er about to reveal?","Ke Yun'er, now realizing what had happened, immediately shouted, \"Yu Yue...\"","[Oh no, what do we do now...] Ji Fei had managed to interrupt once, but she hadn’t figured out how to handle the situation. Asking Qin Xian for help seemed too late.","But then she heard Qin Xian’s voice softly in her ear, \"Don’t worry, take it easy.\"","Qin Xian still held to his principle: protect his own wife. Besides, they had bought Yu Yue a few seconds. If he couldn’t handle it, there was nothing more they could do.","Fortunately, Yu Yue didn’t disappoint.","Before Ke Yun'er could urgently reveal her so-called truth, Yu Yue calmly said, \"Yes, I was deceived by you. I thought the child you were carrying was my father’s, my younger sibling. That’s why I was somewhat patient with you, my stepmother. Did my care make you misunderstand? What a tragedy—I have no special feelings for you. I only cared because of my younger sibling. Do you know why?\"","The crowd was momentarily confused by the sudden change in topic.","Ke Yun'er was also stunned.","Yu Yue continued nonchalantly, \"Because I’m a DINK—I decided long ago that I wouldn’t have children. I had a vasectomy several years ago. I used to feel a little guilty about it, but when I heard you were pregnant, I thought I could make up for it by being a bit kinder to you. Oh, and by the way, this also proves that it wasn’t me that night. I couldn’t have gotten you pregnant—I don’t have the ability.\""]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317: The Mere Existence of Some People is the Most Beautiful Thing for Others","paragraphs":["Yu Yue's candid confession left everyone present utterly stunned.","The abrupt shift in the topic was the least of their concerns. What truly baffled them was that Yu Yue, a scion of the Yu family, had made such a decision that went against the traditions of his ancestors. It was almost inconceivable.","For one, the distribution of the Yu family's wealth was tied to the number of children, which meant that no one would ever consider being childless.","But since Yu Yue had dared to announce this in such a grand setting, everyone believed him without question.","They couldn’t help but find it amusing. Just moments ago, Ke Yun'er had been adamant that Yu Yue was the father of her child. Who would have thought that he couldn’t even have children anymore?","【Holy crap, Yu Yue, you’re a legend! Is this your way of shutting down Ke Yun'er’s schemes? Since he can’t have kids, who cares if Bai Xiaoxi can or not? This is a masterstroke.】","Meanwhile, Bai Xiaoxi and her parents were staring at Yu Yue in shock.","They were aware of Yu Yue’s decision to remain childless, though he had led Bai Xiaoxi to believe it was his own choice. Her parents knew the truth—he had done it for her. What they hadn’t known was that Yu Yue had secretly undergone surgery to ensure it.","While the procedure could be reversed, the sheer determination behind his actions deeply moved the Bai family.","They understood that Yu Yue didn’t need to go to such lengths. After all, Bai Xiaoxi couldn’t get pregnant. But he had done it to shield her from any future pressure or scrutiny from the Yu family, ensuring he could always be her safe harbor.","“Why... didn’t you tell me?” Bai Xiaoxi asked anxiously.","Yu Yue made up some random excuses to placate her, then smiled and said, “Good thing I had the foresight. Otherwise, this false accusation would’ve been hard to clear up.”","“Yu Yue, have you lost your mind?” Yu's Father exclaimed, finally snapping out of his shock. He couldn’t have children, but did that mean he couldn’t have grandchildren either? “I don’t care how rebellious you are. You’re going to reverse this as soon as possible.”","The rest of the Yu family, though not eager to share the family wealth with more children, also tried to persuade him.","Amid the chorus of persuasion, Bai Xiaoxi’s face turned pale. She couldn’t bear to see Yu Yue shoulder this burden alone, especially since it was all because of her. But just as she stepped forward to admit her own infertility, Yu Yue gently pulled her into his arms, holding her tightly and silencing her.","“Given the example you set for me in my childhood, why would I ever want to have kids? You’ve traumatized me,” Yu Yue said calmly to his father. “Instead of worrying about me, maybe you should deal with your own mess. You didn’t even bother to investigate before marrying, and you almost ruined my life. If it weren’t for sheer luck, we’d both be the laughingstock of this family.”","Yu Yue had always been rebellious, capable of anything, so no one knew how to persuade him. They decided to address the matter later and focus on resolving the immediate issue.","But Ke Yun'er kept her eyes locked on Yu Yue. “You... you’ve gone this far for her? You’ve really...”","“I suggest you stop talking nonsense, or I won’t hesitate to slap you,” Yu Yue warned, his gaze sharp.","Ke Yun'er looked at him, his expression fierce, and suddenly let out a bitter laugh. She finally understood why Yu Yue had revealed his vasectomy. In that moment, she was forced to confront the undeniable, unapologetic love Yu Yue had for Bai Xiaoxi.","“What does she have that I don’t? Do I not love you more? Haven’t I done more for you? I’ve worked so hard for you, why won’t you even look at me? What’s so special about her?” Ke Yun'er cried out in anguish.","Yu Yue only held Bai Xiaoxi tighter. “Because I love her, that’s all. Bai Xiaoxi’s existence is everything to me.”","It was direct and without explanation.","To outsiders, Bai Xiaoxi might seem like a sheltered princess who hadn’t made any sacrifices for their love.","But for some people, just their presence is enough to make life beautiful.","Bai Xiaoxi had pulled Yu Yue out of the dark, depressive world he had been trapped in. She hadn’t done anything extraordinary—just her sweet smile had turned his world upside down.","Yu Yue felt that, given how messed up he had been, being loved by Bai Xiaoxi was the greatest fortune he could ever have.","So, he cherished everything they had and would never allow anything to destroy it.","This final response seemed to shatter Ke Yun'er completely. After hearing his answer, she broke down in tears and eventually fainted. It seemed her body hadn’t fully recovered from the earlier ordeal, and she began to bleed.","Amid the chaos, an ambulance was called, and Yu's Father had to accompany her, as they were now legally married.","The wedding ended abruptly in this dramatic fashion.","Apart from the Yu family, the guests left with stifled laughter, their phones glowing as they shared the juicy gossip.","The upper-class circle was undoubtedly abuzz with this scandal.","The conversations all started similarly, with people asking if Ji Fei had really been there.","Everyone was gossiping with their friends, trying to catch a glimpse of the mysterious figure, as if just seeing her would grant them some kind of mystical insight.","But all they saw were a few members of the Qin family leaving with the crowd. There was no sign of Qin Xian or Ji Fei.","Ji Fei had slipped away early, not wanting to be treated like a spectacle.","Yu Yue, too, didn’t want to stay and deal with the aftermath, avoiding a lecture from the elders. So, he left early with Bai Xiaoxi, inviting the rest of their group to join them for dinner since they hadn’t eaten yet.","At the private restaurant, Yu Yue was in high spirits, raising a toast to Qin Xian and Ji Fei to express his gratitude.","Everyone joked around, but Ji Fei was a bit annoyed. She had already seen herself being mentioned in various gossip groups.","“I thought today wouldn’t turn into a spectacle. Now I’m being labeled as some kind of oracle,” Ji Fei complained while sipping her drink.","The others thought she was upset about the label, but then they heard her say to Qin Xian, “From now on, it’s going to be so hard to enjoy live gossip! All I wanted was to be a quiet spectator, but they keep dragging me into it.”","Everyone burst into laughter.","Qin Xian simply smiled tenderly, letting Ji Fei vent her frustrations.","“I’m really curious, though. How do you always manage to stumble upon these big scandals? It’s such a coincidence,” Guo Yalan remarked.","Ji Fei stammered slightly, “It’s... it’s just coincidence. I’m just really into gossip, so I’m more attuned to these kinds of situations.”","It made sense, as no one really believed in anything supernatural.","It was just that Ji Fei had a keen eye for spotting trouble, and her sense of justice led to the current situation.","While the others didn’t pay it much mind, Guo Yalan enthusiastically declared herself a devoted follower of the “Fei Sect.”","As the evening wound down, Yu Yue suddenly bid everyone farewell. It was then that they remembered he had mentioned leaving immediately after the wedding to take Bai Xiaoxi away—their plane tickets were already booked."]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318: Leaving Ji Fei's Heart in Turmoil","paragraphs":["Just as they were about to leave, everyone seemed puzzled.","“The truth is out now, and you still want to leave?” Luo Fei asked, confused.","“Is it because of the DINK issue? Are you worried about your family’s reaction?” Jing Yan inquired.","Guo Yalan chimed in absentmindedly, “Are you really planning to go DINK? Did you and Xiaoxi discuss this?”","Cen Ting also looked at them curiously.","Ji Fei and Qin Xian, however, didn’t seem surprised.","[It seems they’re trying to prevent Ke Yun'er from going crazy and exposing Bai Xiaoxi’s secret later, so they’re leaving early to avoid hurting Bai Xiaoxi. They’re really trying to protect Bai Xiaoxi completely.]","Bai Xiaoxi felt guilty and was about to say something, but Yu Yue took her hand and interrupted her. This time, however, Bai Xiaoxi felt sorry for Yu Yue and took back the conversation.","“Actually, it’s me...”","After Bai Xiaoxi finished explaining the truth, the room fell silent.","Ji Fei had expected this and couldn’t help but feel a little amused.","[Although it wasn’t intentional, I bet they’re feeling really guilty now. They’ll probably wake up in the middle of the night and slap themselves, haha.]","Qin Xian, who had been expressionless, almost laughed when he heard Ji Fei’s comment.","Finally, Yu Yue wrapped his arm around Bai Xiaoxi and said with a smile, “I’m going to treat Xiaoxi like my precious child from now on. Hehe, you guys can have more kids and help us meet the quota. We’ll be godparents. Xiaoxi, let’s make a bet on who’ll be the godmother first.”","Guo Yalan immediately seized the opportunity, “I think I’m the most likely.”","“What are you talking about? You’re not even married,” Yu Yue retorted.","“Who says you need to be married to have kids?” Guo Yalan shot back. “If I want to, I can have one, and it’ll be faster than going through the whole dating and marriage process.”","Luo Fei burst out laughing.","Guo Yalan immediately countered, “What are you laughing at? You’re still single and nursing a broken heart. You might not be the first, but you’ll definitely be the last.”","Luo Fei clutched his chest, “Hey, no need to hit below the belt. Besides, I’m not the only single one here!”","Everyone’s eyes immediately turned to the other two in the room—Jing Yan and Cen Ting. There was something subtle between them.","Cen Ting spoke up directly, “I’m also considering the DINK lifestyle.”","Jing Yan was taken aback but quickly added, “I’ll fully respect my partner’s wishes, so I’m undecided. You’d better count on Qin Xian and Ji Fei.”","The mood shifted, and Bai Xiaoxi was distracted, her eyes sparkling as she looked at Qin Xian and Ji Fei. “When you have kids, can I be the godmother?”","Qin Xian, who never wanted to pressure Ji Fei, was about to change the subject when Ji Fei said, “Of course!”","Qin Xian’s heart raced. Even if it was just a casual response, Ji Fei’s words made him incredibly excited.","Did this mean Ji Fei was willing to be with him and even have children together?","After answering, Ji Fei herself was momentarily stunned.","A fragment of memory flashed through her mind—a game of playing house. She was the wife, and she had a little husband. In front of them were three stuffed toys, acting as their children.","Ji Fei wasn’t sure where that memory came from. She had always been uncomfortable with the idea of love, and the thought of having children made her think of pressure and constraints, which she had always avoided.","But suddenly, the idea of having a child with Qin Xian didn’t seem so daunting. It felt like she wouldn’t have to worry about anything, so she had casually agreed.","Ji Fei couldn’t help but steal a glance at Qin Xian, only to find his deep eyes gazing intently at her.","They were filled with so much love that she felt like she might drown in them.","Could she really understand Qin Xian’s usually reserved emotions? Was he really that happy?","Ji Fei felt her breathing quicken, and her cheeks flushed. It could have been the alcohol, but she wasn’t sure.","She was starting to feel more and more comfortable with the idea of sharing a future with Qin Xian.","Ji Fei’s response sparked excitement among the group.","Yu Yue laughed, “I’d say you two should get married first. Even though we’re leaving soon, if you have a wedding, we’ll fly back to attend.”","This time, it was Qin Xian who responded. “Yes, we’ll have one. Wait for the announcement.”","That night, for some reason, Ji Fei drank a bit too much.","With alcohol came boldness.","The last thing Ji Fei remembered was pushing Qin Xian down. It was a long, lingering kiss that left her breathless.","After that, she couldn’t remember anything.","All she knew was that she had something she really liked, something so precious she wanted to devour it.","When she woke up, a phrase seemed to echo in her ears.","It was a voice so hoarse it made her heart tremble.","“Feifei... are you... trying to kill me?”","The tone was so pitiful that Ji Fei’s still-groggy mind was filled with confusion.","But thinking back to the fragments of her memory, Ji Fei shifted in bed, unsure.","Apart from her swollen lips and sore teeth, she didn’t feel any physical discomfort.","[Did nothing happen?!]","Suddenly, the bathroom door opened, and Qin Xian walked out in a bathrobe. Seeing her awake, he paused, looking slightly uncomfortable. There were dark circles under his eyes, clearly indicating he hadn’t slept well.","“How are you feeling? Are you okay?” Qin Xian asked as he approached the bed.","Ji Fei looked at Qin Xian’s bitten lips, knowing it was her doing, but he was asking if she was okay.","Ji Fei felt inexplicably frustrated.","[Come on, you didn’t do anything. How am I supposed to feel anything?]","Qin Xian, who was about to get her some water, froze. Suppressing his own frustration, he continued, “You drank too much last night. Hangovers can give you a headache.”","Ji Fei pouted, her mind still wandering. [So even after drinking, there was no drunken escapade...]","Qin Xian tried to hold back his frustration and handed her the water. But as he moved, the collar of his bathrobe loosened slightly.","Qin Xian had been wearing his bathrobe strangely all morning, with the collar almost up to his throat, completely covering his neck.","But now, his collarbone was exposed.","Ji Fei, who was drinking water, accidentally glanced at it and immediately choked, spitting out the water.","Qin Xian was startled and quickly sat down beside her, patting her back. But the next second, his chest felt cold as someone boldly pulled open his robe.","Qin Xian was stunned.","Ji Fei was even more stunned.","She had seen a bite mark on Qin Xian’s collarbone and wanted to get a closer look, but she never expected there to be more than just one!","On his firm, fair chest were at least a dozen bite marks of varying depths.","His beautiful body looked as if it had been mistreated, exuding a strange, alluring beauty that tempted her to add more marks.","Ji Fei was transfixed by the sight, and vaguely remembered hearing intermittent groans in her ears—low, restrained sounds that had left her heart in turmoil."]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319: The Qin Family's Secretive Actions Behind Their Backs","paragraphs":["Ji Fei was flustered, her mind filled with incoherent thoughts, as if her brain had flown off into outer space.","[Did I actually do something to Qin Xian last night...]","This absurd thought was interrupted before it could fully form by Qin Xian’s actions.","Ji Fei held her forehead and saw Qin Xian blushing deeply, looking at her with an expression that was hard to describe.","Ji Fei forced a dry laugh, “Was it all me?”","Qin Xian pursed his lips, seemingly a bit aggrieved, but nodded silently.","“That must’ve hurt. Why didn’t you resist?” Ji Fei felt even more awkward. No wonder her teeth were sore—Qin Xian’s firm muscles must’ve been tough to bite into.","Ji Fei truly couldn’t understand how she had developed a habit of biting people.","But Qin Xian muttered softly, “You like it...”","It seemed that as long as Ji Fei liked it, Qin Xian wouldn’t resist no matter what she did to him.","[Ahhh, my inner wolf is about to go wild!]","Qin Xian felt uncomfortable hearing this and fumbled to adjust his collar.","[Wait, that’s not right.]","Qin Xian paused, sensing that Ji Fei’s gaze had turned strange.","[If he likes me, and I’ve already done this much, why hasn’t he made a move? Is it because... he’s incapable?]","Qin Xian: “...”","He gave Ji Fei a meaningful look, and in the next second, he flipped her over and pinned her beneath him.","The sudden closeness made Ji Fei’s heart race. Staring at his handsome face just inches away, she stammered, “Wh-what’s going on?”","Qin Xian’s gaze was practically glued to Ji Fei, his deep, magnetic voice overlapping with her memories.","“There’s another reason I didn’t stop you.”","“Huh?”","“I thought there would be more.”","Ji Fei was stunned.","“But after you did what you wanted, you fell asleep.”","Ji Fei instantly realized what he meant.","Qin Xian pressed his forehead against hers, his tone growing more pitiful. “And then, you left me all alone...”","Ji Fei gasped.","[So, I teased him for so long, only to fall asleep afterward...]","“You bullied me,” Qin Xian’s voice came again, completely devoid of his usual domineering aura. Instead, he sounded like a pitiful puppy, making Ji Fei feel like a heartless woman who flirted without taking responsibility.","So, it wasn’t that Qin Xian was incapable—it was her!","Ji Fei forced another dry laugh, feeling the need to say something comforting. “Next time... next time, I’ll make it up to you.”","Qin Xian’s eyes lit up, instantly locking onto Ji Fei. She suddenly felt like prey being targeted by a hunter.","“Now?” Qin Xian’s voice grew huskier, unable to hide his excitement.","Ji Fei could even feel the heat radiating from his body pressing against hers, and a certain part of him was becoming unmistakably noticeable.","Ji Fei immediately choked on her own saliva in nervousness.","She was good at talking big after the fact, and she had no problem acting shamelessly when drunk. But doing something while sober? That was a death sentence for Ji Fei.","Her face turned bright red, and her entire body stiffened involuntarily.","Qin Xian noticed Ji Fei’s discomfort and paused. Quickly regaining his composure, he suppressed his aggressive demeanor, stood up, and smiled reassuringly. “It’s okay, we’ll take it slow. This is fine for now.”","Qin Xian never forced her, and Ji Fei knew that. Seeing Qin Xian head to the bathroom, she realized that someone had spent last night the same way, and her face turned even redder.","Ji Fei couldn’t help but cover her face and giggle, rolling around in the blanket. When she realized what she was doing, she wondered if she had lost her mind.","After that, the Qin family noticed that the atmosphere between the two had changed again.","Ji Fei would unconsciously glance at Qin Xian, and when they sat together, she would naturally lean into his arms. When their eyes met, everyone around could feel the sweetness in the air.","The most ridiculous part was that even when Ji Fei was lazing around at home and Qin Xian was busy at work, they would often keep a video call open. They didn’t necessarily talk much, but they would occasionally exchange a few words.","Naturally, strange rumors began circulating at the company. Some said Qin Xian was henpecked, while others claimed Ji Fei was overly controlling. There were all sorts of stories.","But none of these rumors ever reached their ears.","The Qin family members were constantly excitedly placing bets on when things would finally fall into place.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei felt like she was about to lose her grip. Every night, she would be kissed until her legs went weak by Qin Xian. Even though she had been the one to act shamelessly first, Qin Xian had quickly mastered the art and advanced at an astonishing pace. It seemed that smart people excelled at everything faster than ordinary folks.","Ji Fei didn’t want to fall so quickly. After all, she had seen enough drama to worry about losing herself in his charm and becoming a lovesick fool. To distract herself, Ji Fei, who had always been a couch potato, started actively asking Sister Pei for work.","Their studio was doing well. The two talented women they had recruited were making waves in their respective fields, and it was said that they were soon to receive prestigious awards. As Sister Pei put it, bringing these two on board had made the studio a goldmine.","Sister Pei even suspected that Ji Fei might have been blacklisted by the wealthy elite, which was why she was so bored and wanted to return to the entertainment industry to gossip and judge.","Ji Fei found it hard to explain, but it was true—the high society in their city had been unusually quiet lately, with almost no events.","Was it just a coincidence, or were they avoiding her? Ji Fei suspected the latter, especially since she had noticed that other members of the Qin family were secretly discussing something behind her and Qin Xian’s backs, and their expressions weren’t exactly cheerful.","Once, they even tried to convince her to take Qin Xian on an overseas trip, claiming it was to strengthen their bond as a pre-wedding vacation.","Ji Fei was, of course, baffled.","At some point, Ji Fei had stopped prying into their secrets. After all, they were family, and it was important to respect their privacy.","So, Ji Fei decided to ask directly!","Faced with Ji Fei’s question, the three Qin family members at home looked somewhat uneasy.","Finally, Qin’s Father sighed. “Well, we might as well tell Ji Fei sooner or later. There’s no point in hiding it.”","Qin’s Mom also sighed. “Ji Fei, you probably haven’t noticed, but ever since you came to our family at fifteen, there’s always been a period each year when we’re not home.”","Ji Fei suddenly felt awkward. Now that she thought about it, that did seem to be the case.","The memories she inherited from her past self were mostly about obsessing over Qin Xian. When it came to other people’s matters, she had been indifferent, so her memories were hazy.","Speaking of the memories she inherited, it was quite strange. The memories of her falling head over heels for Qin Xian and relentlessly pursuing him were vivid, but her recollections of her life with her parents before that were blurry, as if obscured by a veil. She could only remember the general outlines.","Even when she tried to recall details, Ji Fei couldn’t remember her biological parents clearly. However, she didn’t dwell on it too much, as the original body had been in a car accident with her parents, so memory loss was a possibility.","Ji Fei snapped back to reality and asked, “So, is it the same reason this time? You’re all going away?”","Qin’s Father replied, “Yes, every year we return to Y City to attend my father’s—their grandfather’s—birthday banquet. However, Qin Xian doesn’t attend.”"]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320: Qin Xian's Past","paragraphs":["Ji Fei was taken aback, looking at the three people present with surprise. Qin Xian wasn’t going to attend his grandfather’s birthday banquet?","Unable to hold back, Ji Fei asked, “Why? Does he have issues with his grandfather?”","“No, strictly speaking, it’s that he won’t go back to Y City,” Qin Yan replied, her eyes filled with worry.","The Qin family had originally risen to prominence in Y City, where they were a prominent clan. Due to historical policies and various other reasons, Grandpa Qin knew they couldn’t remain stagnant or be left behind by the times. Thus, the Qin family was among the first to shift their business focus to this new location.","At that time, however, Grandpa Qin was already getting on in years, so he had to entrust the task to his children.","Qin’s Father, the second eldest among his siblings, had a very harmonious relationship with his brothers and sisters. It was during this period that he took on the responsibility of leading the Qin family, bringing most of the family’s resources to this new city and stabilizing the Qin family’s business empire.","Many of the Qin family’s extended relatives also gave up their long-established lives in Y City during that time, following Qin’s Father to seek new opportunities and development here.","Of course, it’s unwise to put all your eggs in one basket. Y City, as well as overseas, still had Qin family businesses, which were left to Qin’s Father’s other siblings to manage.","Only Qin’s Father moved his entire family to settle permanently in this new city.","Grandpa Qin, along with his eldest aunt and third uncle, remained in Y City, while the fourth uncle was in a neighboring city, and the fifth and sixth uncles were abroad.","Usually, the Qin family only managed to gather in full during Grandpa Qin’s birthday celebrations.","But ever since Qin Xian came to this city, he had never returned.","As Ji Fei listened to everyone’s words, her brows furrowed into a deep frown. She couldn’t help but feel there was a big story here.","However, the thought that this might be related to Qin Xian made her somewhat uneasy, as such a story likely wouldn’t be a good one.","The Qin family didn’t beat around the bush either. Given how close Ji Fei and Qin Xian were now, it was best for her to understand certain things.","“Actually, it’s all my fault,” Qin’s Mom began, her emotions threatening to overwhelm her as she recalled the past.","“It’s not your fault. It’s our responsibility as parents,” Qin’s Father immediately comforted her.","This only made Ji Fei even more anxious.","“Let me explain,” Qin Yan stepped forward, taking on the task.","The origin of the matter was also tied to the Qin family’s decision to shift their business focus. When Qin’s Father came here to build their new life, Qin’s Mom naturally followed to support him.","At that time, Qin Yan was already five years old and could attend kindergarten, so bringing her along wasn’t a problem. However, Qin Xian was still very young, only two or three years old. Bringing him along would have been too much for Qin’s Mom to handle, especially since Qin Xian had already been identified as a high-IQ child, much like Qin Xi, and required specialized nurturing and guidance.","Thus, Grandpa Qin made the decision for the couple to leave Qin Xian in their hometown. After all, Y City was indeed the most developed in every aspect at the time, making it more conducive to fostering a child prodigy. Besides, with their closest family members there, taking care of Qin Xian wouldn’t be an issue.","Qin Xian had always been exceptionally intelligent and understanding, to the point where it was heartbreaking. When the reasons were explained to him, he didn’t cry or make a fuss. Reluctantly, Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom left with Qin Yan to start their new life.","Here, it’s worth mentioning one person—Grandma Lv, Grandpa Qin’s second wife.","The six Qin siblings all shared the same biological mother, who passed away after giving birth to the sixth child. Grandma Lv had originally been a close companion to the late Mrs. Qin, and after Mrs. Qin’s passing, she stayed with the Qin family, helping to care for each of the children. She was deeply respected by the family.","She later married and had a child, but her husband passed away early, so she lived in the Qin family with her only daughter.","There was no drama here—Grandma Lv was a woman of the old era, deeply rooted in traditional values of loyalty and service. It was Mrs. Qin’s dying wish that Grandma Lv marry Grandpa Qin, fearing that any other stepmother might mistreat her children. Grandpa Qin, wanting to honor his wife’s wishes, agreed. Both were decent people, and they spent their lives together in harmony.","To show that she would never bear children who might compete with Mrs. Qin’s children for the family inheritance, Grandma Lv secretly took a sterilizing agent before the marriage. Thus, all the Qin siblings, except for the daughter Grandma Lv brought from her previous marriage, were full siblings.","This harmonious family dynamic meant there was never any internal strife within the Qin family, making them somewhat of an anomaly in Y City.","It was also because of this environment that Grandma Lv took care of the grandchildren with all her heart, which was why Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom felt comfortable leaving Qin Xian in their hometown.","However, as Qin Xian grew older, problems began to surface in his personality.","At first, it was thought that his high IQ made it difficult for him to integrate into the world around him, so he gradually became less talkative. But the situation worsened. By the time Qin Xian was five or six, Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom realized they couldn’t leave him there any longer and decided to bring him to live with them.","Unfortunately, at that time, Qin’s Mom was pregnant with Qin Zhao, and the pregnancy was particularly difficult, requiring her to be hospitalized for extended periods. Thus, the plan to bring Qin Xian over was postponed.","After that, Qin Xian’s condition deteriorated further. He barely communicated with anyone, and during that time, the family in their hometown began to suspect something was wrong. They tried various solutions, such as sending Qin Xian to a summer camp for high-IQ children. However, when he returned, he barely ate or drank and showed no emotional response.","Grandpa Qin immediately sought out a psychologist for Qin Xian, who diagnosed him with autism accompanied by memory confusion and a gradual loss of emotions. That year, Qin Xian was eight years old.","Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom dropped everything and took Qin Xian to seek medical help everywhere. However, at that time, the field of psychology wasn’t as advanced, and mental illnesses were difficult to treat. The only explanation they could find was that Qin Xian’s condition was due to a lack of parental companionship. From then on, Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom kept him by their side.","It was also when Qin Xian was nine that he met the oblivious little Ji Fei.","Over time, Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom noticed that Qin Xian wasn’t emotionally detached—he was just holding back. There was still a spark of vitality within him; it just needed to be ignited.","As time passed, Qin Xian gradually returned to normal. However, whether the person he became was his true self or a result of his psychological struggles, no one could say for sure.","But one lingering effect remained: Qin Xian refused to return to Y City.","At first, when Qin Xian’s emotions were muted, he rarely expressed likes or dislikes. The first time he clearly expressed his feelings was when they tried to take him back to Y City—he vomited, then developed a fever and fell into a coma.","Hearing this, Ji Fei finally spoke up after a long period of stunned silence.","She asked, tense and defensive, with a hint of hostility, “Was it because he had a bad childhood in Y City? Was someone secretly mistreating him?”","Qin Yan replied, “We asked him. He said no.”"]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321: These two guys are feeding us dog food again","paragraphs":["Ji Fei was momentarily stunned, unable to make sense of the situation.","【No bad memories, just an instinctive resistance to going back?】","The whole family shared Ji Fei's thoughts.","Qin Yan said, \"Actually, we’re not sure if there’s truly nothing, or if his memories have just become blurred.\"","Even though the Qin family had a close-knit relationship, suspecting them was a painful ordeal. Qin's Father and Qin's Mom had secretly investigated due to Qin Xian's reactions.","However, whether it was the surveillance footage from that time or the testimonies of former household staff, everything proved that everyone in the family treated Qin Xian well—whether it was the stern Grandpa Qin, the doting Grandma Lv, or other relatives living in the house.","Being smart and handsome, his siblings had initially adored him, making him the center of attention.","Even Grandma Lv’s daughter, who was studying abroad and had no blood relation to them, would always spend time with Qin Xian whenever she returned, helping him with his studies. When she discovered Qin Xian’s psychological issues, she actively offered her support, deeply concerned.","The findings from the investigation left Qin's Father and Qin's Mom with no choice but to stop suspecting their family. They could only assume that returning to Y City might have triggered Qin Xian’s trauma of being abandoned by his parents.","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom felt guilty, so they never forced Qin Xian to go back. In fact, they stopped mentioning it altogether, forming an unspoken agreement. They would simply return themselves to celebrate the birthdays, and that was it.","However, the relatives back in their hometown still cared deeply about Qin Xian.","The reason Ji Fei hadn’t gone in the first two years was that the relatives in the hometown had heard about the truth behind Qin Xian and Ji Fei’s marriage and were very disapproving of her. They were protective and didn’t want to see Qin Xian suffer such an injustice, believing that Qin's Father and Qin's Mom had once again let Qin Xian down.","Since Qin Xian wasn’t coming back, they didn’t need to see Ji Fei either.","But this time, the rest of the Qin family had enthusiastically invited Ji Fei.","The drastic change in attitude was entirely due to Qin Xian’s doting behavior toward his wife, which had already spread through the Qin Corporation. How could the rest of the Qin family not know about it?","Because they loved Qin Xian, they naturally wanted to see the new lady of the house.","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom were eager to show her off, as Ji Fei had truly brought out the best in Qin Xian.","However, Qin Xian couldn’t bear to be apart from Ji Fei now, especially with the whole family returning to Y City. They were hesitant and thought it might be better to wait until the wedding to bring everyone over.","They also had a small concern: while the extended Qin family couldn’t hear Ji Fei’s thoughts, what about the immediate family?","Ji Fei’s peculiar situation was still unclear, so it was best not to involve too many people.","At this point, the Qin family naturally wanted to consult Ji Fei’s opinion.","Ji Fei’s mind was completely occupied with Qin Xian. She seemed to finally understand why Qin Xian had been emotionally reserved and indifferent at first, seemingly uninterested in others’ affairs but quietly helping behind the scenes—introverted and silent. So that was it.","Ji Fei’s heart ached intensely, and she suddenly wanted to hug Qin Xian.","When the Qin family asked for her thoughts, Ji Fei replied directly, \"Wherever my husband is, I’ll be there. I refuse to be apart from him.\"","She declared it with exaggerated determination, just as Qin Xian arrived at the doorstep and overheard her.","Qin Xian blinked, frozen at the door, his face flushing red. He coughed lightly and finally said, \"I’ve told you, if you want to accompany me to the company, it wouldn’t be a distraction.\"","Ji Fei: ...","The Qin family, realizing Qin Xian hadn’t heard the earlier conversation, breathed a sigh of relief. They couldn’t help but laugh and cry at the same time—these two were feeding them dog food again.","Of course, Qin Xian wasn’t that oblivious. He had also noticed that the rest of the Qin family was planning to return to Y City.","He remembered Grandpa Qin’s birthday. Every year, he sent gifts and occasionally video-chatted with the old man, but he simply couldn’t bring himself to go back.","Thinking of that place, Qin Xian’s emotions were now much calmer, but if asked whether he wanted to go, the answer would still be no.","However, thinking of Ji Fei, his heart tingled with warmth. Such an occasion would be the perfect opportunity to take Ji Fei with him.","Just as Qin Xian was unusually indecisive, Grandpa Qin called.","Qin Xian was handling documents when the phone rang. He smiled and said, \"Fei Fei, can you answer the phone for me?\"","Ji Fei, who was indeed accompanying him at work and browsing online entertainment gossip, picked up the phone.","Before she could speak, she heard a hoarse, aged voice on the other end. \"Qin Xian, are you not planning to attend this old man’s birthday banquet again?\"","Ji Fei was momentarily stunned but quickly responded politely, \"Hello, Grandpa Qin. This is Ji Fei. Please hold on, I’ll pass the phone to Qin Xian.\"","The other end seemed surprised, but Ji Fei, not wanting to engage in small talk with an unfamiliar elder, quickly handed the phone over.","Qin Xian, recognizing the voice, took the phone and said, \"Grandpa.\"","Grandpa Qin sounded intrigued. \"Was that your wife just now? You’re together during work hours? And you let her answer your phone? Seems the rumors are true.\"","Though Grandpa Qin’s tone sounded lighthearted, his speech was somewhat labored, and the background noise included the sound of a breathing machine.","\"Fei Fei is accompanying me at work. Grandpa, why are you calling...\"","Ji Fei watched Qin Xian cautiously as she heard Grandpa Qin’s slightly deeper voice on the other end. \"This year is my ninetieth birthday. The gathering of relatives and guests will be the most complete and largest ever. As the current head of the Qin family, shouldn’t you and the lady of the house make an official appearance?\"","Qin Xian’s eyes flickered as he glanced at Ji Fei.","Ji Fei shrugged, indicating she didn’t mind.","【I don’t care about making an appearance. If Qin Xian doesn’t want to go, then we won’t. Everything else is irrelevant.】","Qin Xian felt a warmth in his heart and couldn’t resist pulling Ji Fei into a one-armed hug, savoring her presence.","Not hearing a response, Grandpa Qin continued, \"I know my body well. I’m not sure if I’ll have the chance to host another birthday banquet next year. I want to take this opportunity, while I’m still around, to support you, stand by your side, and pave the way for you...\"","Grandpa Qin’s intentions were indeed well-meaning. Among all his descendants, Qin Xian was the only one who received a personal call from him, and it was delivered in such a persuasive tone, entirely due to Qin Xian’s unique circumstances.","After all, Qin's Father had retired early, and Qin Xian, at such a young age, had taken charge of the vast Qin Corporation. While his capabilities were undeniable—he had even elevated the company to new heights—his lack of experience often led to some people causing trouble.","Grandpa Qin wanted to use this occasion to let everyone meet face-to-face and ensure that the Qin family, both now and in the future, remained loyal. After all, human hearts were unpredictable. While the current generation might be fine, who knew what ambitions the next might harbor?"]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322: This Is the Right Way to Unlock Her Golden Finger","paragraphs":["Even if it meant resorting to emotional manipulation, Grandpa Qin wanted Qin Xian to make the trip. After all, if someone asked why the head of the family hadn’t shown up, and the answer was “because of childhood trauma,” it would be downright embarrassing. People wouldn’t sympathize.","The more he thought about it, the more he felt that Qin Xian’s parents were being overly cautious.","After all these years, wasn’t Qin Xian doing just fine? He had become such a young and outstanding business leader. How could he not handle a trip to Y City?","Grandpa Qin came from a generation that believed enduring hardship was the key to greatness.","“After all I’ve said, you understand my intentions, right? Can you come?” Grandpa Qin asked wearily.","Qin Xian closed his eyes for a moment before finally replying, “Alright, I’ll go with Ji Fei.”","Grandpa Qin breathed a sigh of relief, his voice brimming with joy. “Good, good, good.”","After hanging up, Qin Xian looked down at Ji Fei, who was nestled in his arms, and smiled. “We’re going to spend a month in Y City with the family.”","Ji Fei’s gaze met his, deep and thoughtful.","“What’s wrong? Don’t want to go?” Qin Xian asked.","[I feel so bad for him. He’s the one who doesn’t want to go.]","Qin Xian paused, feeling a warm flame ignite in his heart. He leaned down and gently kissed Ji Fei’s lips.","When Ji Fei’s eyes grew hazy, he coaxed her softly, “But I want to take you with me. I want everyone to know you’re my love. So, will you come with me?”","Ji Fei was so thoroughly charmed that she forgot her vow to stay rational and not turn into a lovesick fool. She nodded in agreement, her cheeks flushing.","Qin Xian’s eyes were filled with affection as he chuckled. “By the way, the high society and entertainment circles there are quite different from here. You’ll probably get to hear a lot of juicy gossip. Excited?”","Ji Fei immediately perked up. “You mean they don’t know I’m the gossip queen and the ultimate judge of the entertainment industry?”","Qin Xian laughed, clearly amused by how Ji Fei had already embraced this persona.","“Probably not,” he said, then feigned a troubled sigh. “But what I’m really worried about is the state of my aunts’ and uncles’ family affairs.”","Ji Fei pinched him in mock annoyance.","Qin Xian quickly corrected himself, “No, I mean, if there are any issues in their families, they’ll be counting on Fei Fei’s righteous judgment to save the day.”","Ji Fei giggled, but suddenly a thought flashed through her mind, too quick to catch.","When they returned to the Qin family home and everyone heard about Qin Xian’s decision, they were frozen in shock.","“Are you sure this is okay?” Qin’s Mom asked worriedly.","“Don’t force yourself. I’ll explain it for you,” Qin’s Father added hastily.","Qin Yan frowned, watching closely.","Qin Xian smiled faintly and assured them it was fine, but the family remained on edge. Even Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, who were abroad, kept checking in on the group chat, unable to relax.","After that, Qin Xian threw himself into work, preparing for the month-long absence. While much of it could be handled remotely, there was still a lot to do beforehand.","On the day before their departure, Qin’s Mom and Dad were still worried Qin Xian might suddenly fall ill.","It wasn’t until they boarded the private plane and it took off without incident that everyone gradually began to relax.","They chatted about how Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were flying directly from abroad to Y City. They had left earlier and would arrive first to pick everyone up.","Just then, Qin Xian yawned.","“You’ve been working too hard lately. You stayed up late last night. Why don’t you go inside and take a nap?” Qin’s Father suggested.","They were sitting in the sofa area, with a private room behind them that had a large bed.","Qin Xian was indeed exhausted. Once the plane stabilized, he got up and went to the back, soon falling into a deep sleep. Everyone in the main cabin tried to keep their voices low.","“Fei Fei, why don’t you go in and stay with him?” Qin’s Father suggested.","Qin’s Mom added anxiously, “Keep an eye on his temperature. I’m worried he might suddenly get a fever.”","Qin Yan chimed in, “Call us if anything happens.”","Ji Fei nodded and headed to the back. As she walked, she could hear Qin’s Mom and Dad whispering, silently praying that Qin Xian would be fine once they arrived in Y City. Then they began to blame themselves.","Ji Fei knew Qin’s Mom and Dad still carried guilt over Qin Xian’s past. But...","[It’s not certain if it’s even their fault... Wait! I’ve got it! This is the perfect opportunity for me to investigate. Since I’m not close to them, I have every reason to suspect if they treated my Qin Xian poorly in the past. If everything’s fine, then it’s all good. But if there’s a problem, hmph!]","Ji Fei finally realized what had flashed through her mind earlier. This was the perfect way to use her “gossip queen” skills.","The Qin family had been so adamant about taking responsibility that Ji Fei had almost stopped questioning them. But logically, she should remain skeptical of everyone. After all, without her gossip radar, who knows if the person standing in front of her is friend or foe?","As Ji Fei opened the door to the private room, she left the three Qin family members and little Qin Xi staring in stunned silence.","Qin Xian, fast asleep, heard nothing. He only felt a familiar presence approaching.","His sleep was restless, as if he were trapped in a silent, oppressive place, bound by invisible chains that he couldn’t escape.","To fight the fear, his emotions seemed to hollow out until he felt nothing... but it was so cold. He hated that bone-chilling coldness.","Suddenly, he felt a sharp pain in his collarbone.","Qin Xian woke up to find someone warm and cozy in his arms, her familiar scent bringing him an indescribable sense of security.","Looking down, he saw Ji Fei, still half-asleep, nibbling on his collarbone.","Somehow, she had developed a habit of biting him.","The icy expression on Qin Xian’s face, a remnant of his nightmare, melted away. His eyes overflowed with tenderness as he nuzzled Ji Fei’s forehead with his nose, finally getting her to release his collarbone.","Ji Fei had originally gone in to keep an eye on Qin Xian and make sure he was okay, but the long flight made her drowsy. Before she knew it, she had fallen asleep, even more deeply than Qin Xian.","In her sleep, she kept snuggling closer to Qin Xian, who tried to keep his composure. After all, they were on a plane with family just outside. He couldn’t afford to lose his cool.","Fortunately, the plane was about to land.","When the announcement came, Qin Xian gently woke Ji Fei.","Still groggy, Ji Fei reached up to touch Qin Xian’s face. “How are you feeling? Are you okay?”","The scenery of Y City came into view, and the three Qin family members outside the room grew tense again.","At the airport, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong met the relatives who had come to pick them up. The group was large and made quite a scene, with even some paparazzi sneaking photos.","The relatives kept asking Qin Zhao and Qin Rong to confirm, “Is Qin Xian really coming?”","Though worried, the two maintained their composure. “He said he’s bringing his wife to meet everyone. Of course, he’s coming.”","Meanwhile, in the private room, Qin Xian looked at Ji Fei’s sleepy face and couldn’t help but laugh. He cupped her face and kissed her, proving that he was perfectly fine and there was nothing to worry about."]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323: Love is Quite Nourishing","paragraphs":["Seeing Qin Xian and Ji Fei emerge smoothly, the Qin Family breathed a collective sigh of relief.","As the family walked out of the passageway, they spotted Qin Zhao and Qin Rong standing in the middle of a crowd, waving enthusiastically at them.","Everyone’s attention first fell on Qin Xian. Seeing him in good spirits, they couldn’t help but reflect on how it had been twenty years since he last left this city—back when he was only eight or nine years old. Although many relatives had met him elsewhere over the years, seeing him in their hometown held a different significance.","Once they confirmed Qin Xian was fine, their focus quickly shifted to Ji Fei, who was holding his arm, and of course, the little star of the show, Qin Xi.","The news of Qin Yan reclaiming her son, Qin Xi, had naturally been shared with the family. However, the previous family reunion banquet had been hastily arranged. The Qin Family had intended to host it in their hometown, but due to Qin Xi’s schooling and integration into their social circle, it was held locally instead, with only relatives from the same city attending.","The closest relatives, for various reasons, hadn’t been able to attend and had instead sent gifts. So, like Ji Fei, this was their first time meeting Qin Xi.","Naturally, their curiosity was piqued by Ji Fei.","Their feelings toward this woman were complicated. After all, Ji Fei’s rise to her position hadn’t been honorable, and she had married the head of the Qin Family. Many had disapproved of such a woman becoming the matriarch, but it seemed that over time, the two had grown genuinely fond of each other.","As relatives, they were supposed to love what their family loved, so on the surface, they wouldn’t cause Ji Fei any trouble or embarrassment. Doing so would be akin to slapping Qin Xian in the face, and they wouldn’t go that far to harm family ties. Still, deep down, they had their reservations.","They hoped that through this gathering, they could get to know her better.","At first glance, she made a decent impression—always smiling, good-looking, and sharing a natural chemistry with Qin Xian. It was hard to believe she was the type of girl who would resort to underhanded tactics.","Just as they were thinking this, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong rushed over. Qin Zhao greeted the family with a smile.","Qin Rong was even more direct, immediately linking arms with Ji Fei. “Second sister-in-law, I’ve missed you so much!”","Qin's Mom and Qin Yan instantly feigned jealousy. “What about us?”","“I’ve missed everyone!” Qin Rong replied with a sweet smile.","“Has Rong Rong gotten prettier?” Ji Fei teased.","Qin Rong’s eyes sparkled as she looked at Ji Fei, practically radiating adoration.","[Could it be... she’s in love? Please don’t let her get fooled again!]","Qin Rong: Ugh, don’t bring up my past mistakes!","When the whole family looked at her curiously, Qin Rong quickly shook her head to deny it.","“Why are you shaking your head?” Ji Fei asked, intrigued.","Qin Rong pouted at her.","“She’s probably wondering if she’s seeing things because you’ve gotten prettier too,” Qin Zhao chimed in, still teasing.","“So you think I’ve gotten prettier too?” Ji Fei laughed.","Qin Zhao chuckled. “Of course, but that’s probably thanks to my second brother. Love does wonders, doesn’t it?”","He nudged Qin Xian playfully, taking advantage of the rare opportunity to tease him in person rather than through text.","Qin Xian’s eyes softened with a smile. “Fei Fei has always been beautiful.”","Qin Zhao immediately made an exaggerated face, as if the sight of his usually stoic brother being so affectionate was too much to handle.","Though blushing from Qin Xian’s compliment, Ji Fei wasn’t about to let Qin Zhao off the hook.","[Of course, we’re thriving on love. Unlike you, Qin Zhao. Judging by your lack of progress, I’m guessing you haven’t even dared to contact her—probably just staring at her school gate from afar.]","Qin Zhao: ...I surrender, big sis!","Qin Xian’s cheeks turned pink. Love really was nourishing.","The rest of the Qin Family stifled their laughter.","As the other Qin relatives approached and observed the interactions, they were somewhat surprised.","It gave them a clear sense that, regardless of the rumors, the second branch of the Qin Family had genuinely accepted Ji Fei as one of their own.","When Ji Fei stepped out and saw the crowd, she immediately put on her brightest smile.","She was ready for the family reunion that would come with the New Year celebrations.","However, in such a public setting, it wasn’t appropriate to introduce everyone individually. Instead, the elders exchanged greetings on behalf of the group, and they all headed out, planning to formally introduce everyone once they reached the old family estate.","The second branch of the Qin Family was all seated in one car.","As soon as they were together, the conversation flowed endlessly, filled with laughter and chatter.","The atmosphere in the other cars was quite different.","The eldest branch, representing the aunt’s family, didn’t have any elders present. Since the aunt and uncle were older, they had opted not to travel back and forth.","Instead, their cousins had come. The eldest cousin, Qin Wenqiang, had brought her husband and child, along with her still-single younger brother.","“Wenqiang, Qin Xian seems to be in good spirits this time. Do you think we should bring up the investment opportunity with him?” her husband said as he drove.","Qin Wenqiang frowned. “Didn’t we bring it up before? He didn’t think it was suitable.”","“That was all done remotely. Now that we’re meeting in person, maybe after a few drinks and some warm hospitality, he’ll reconsider. It’s a really good project—maybe he just doesn’t fully understand it yet,” her husband pressed.","Qin Wenqiang replied impatiently, “It’s already a big deal that Qin Xian is here for Grandpa’s birthday celebration. Let’s not put him in an awkward position.”","Her husband’s tone grew more urgent. “How would it be awkward? You can’t just dismiss it because it’s not part of Qin Corporation. This is our investment company—something we’ve worked hard on.”","“What are you implying?” Qin Wenqiang snapped. “If I didn’t care, I wouldn’t have brought it up with Qin Xian in the first place. Grandpa himself said that no one in our family has a better business sense than Qin Xian. He’s a genius.”","Her husband’s expression stiffened. “Your younger brother is a genius too.”","Qin Yi, who was sitting in the backseat playing a musical game with his niece, looked up with a faint smile. “I can’t compare to Qin Xian. At best, I’m talented in music, but Qin Xian is genuinely brilliant. I still remember how he solved math problems meant for an eight-year-old when he was only four.”","Qin Wenqiang couldn’t help but laugh. “You’re one to talk. You’d beg your four-year-old brother to help with your homework because you were too busy practicing the piano.”","“Uncle, are you really that bad? Even a four-year-old could do better than you?” the little niece asked innocently.","Qin Yi playfully pinched her nose. “You’re a year older than the new kid, Qin Xi, but I hear he’s pretty smart too. If you can’t do your homework, don’t come to me—ask him to outsmart you.”","“Don’t you dare corrupt my daughter,” Qin Wenqiang said with a laugh."]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324: Three Households' Situations","paragraphs":["“Exactly, I’m not stupid either. I’ll compete with him, but even if he’s smarter than me, it’s fine. I can ask him for help with what I don’t know. As long as I learn, I’m not losing to him!” Yang Weiwei said proudly.","“That’s amazing!” Qin Yi immediately pinched her cheek with a smile.","Just as the atmosphere in the car was about to improve, Yang Feng, the brother-in-law, brought up work again: “Qin Yi, don’t you think we should ask Qin Xian for help? We just want to achieve something on our own. Always working under Qin Corporation, always under Qin Xian’s control... it’s not bad, but there’s no challenge. We want to do something of our own.”","Qin Yi noticed her niece’s visible disappointment and frowned slightly, her gaze falling on the back of Yang Feng’s head.","Qin Wenqiang was about to say something in displeasure when Qin Yi spoke up: “Brother-in-law, you know I don’t get involved in Qin Corporation’s affairs, and I don’t understand them. But I think if Qin Xian says something won’t work, it probably won’t. At least, under his leadership, no new project in Qin Corporation has ever failed. Is it so hard to accept someone’s criticism?”","Qin Yi’s words were gentle but effectively shut Yang Feng down.","She continued, “Doesn’t my sister have her own judgment?”","Qin Wenqiang was taken aback but quickly replied, “That’s true. Husband, I thought your project proposal was flawed from the start, but you didn’t believe me. You insisted on asking Qin Xian, and he also said it wouldn’t work. Why won’t you listen?”","Yang Feng’s expression darkened further.","Qin Yi glanced at him in the rearview mirror and found it amusing. Her brother-in-law really didn’t know his place. In terms of business acumen, he couldn’t even compare to her sister, let alone Qin Xian. Why was he so stubborn? Anyone in the industry who received a rejection from either of the Qin siblings would immediately reconsider their project. It wasn’t like they were stopping him from doing something else.","“Alright, alright, I won’t say anymore,” Yang Feng said, his temper flaring. Qin Wenqiang quickly ended the conversation to save her husband some face.","Meanwhile, the atmosphere at Third Uncle Qin’s house was also tense.","Third Uncle Qin had personally come to pick them up. Normally, he would have brought his wife along, given how much he valued Qin Xian, but she wasn’t feeling well and stayed home.","Third Uncle Qin brought his son, Qin Han, and daughter, Qin Jiaxi, to greet them.","Qin Han’s expression was sour. “I still think today’s reception is too much. If it weren’t for certain limitations, would you have mobilized the entire family? When Second Uncle’s family returned, we didn’t go to such lengths. Is it just because Qin Xian is here this time? Even if he’s managing Qin Corporation now, you and Fourth Uncle are elders. Was it really necessary to come personally? From what I can see, he doesn’t seem to care much.”","Third Uncle Qin was a stern father. Hearing this, he immediately rebuked, “What have I taught you? You have no sense of propriety. Qin Xian’s current temperament is partly our responsibility as elders. Back then, if Second Brother and Second Sister-in-law hadn’t needed to shift the family’s focus, they wouldn’t have left Qin Xian alone in the old mansion at such a young age. Without his parents, he developed psychological issues. Now that he’s finally overcome his fears and come back to see your grandfather, it’s only right that we show him respect.”","Qin Han rarely dared to argue with his father, but this time he couldn’t hold back. “I’m just curious. Why would you choose someone with psychological instability as the head of the family? Waiting a few more years wouldn’t have hurt. If Second Uncle wanted to step down, couldn’t you or Fourth Uncle have taken over?”","“Enough! He’s your cousin. What are you thinking?” Third Uncle Qin’s tone carried a warning.","Qin Han clenched his fists and muttered, “I’m just curious... that’s what people outside are saying.”","Third Uncle Qin sneered, “People in Y City don’t usually deal directly with Qin Xian, so they don’t know. Do you think your Second Uncle stepped down because he wanted to? He knew he couldn’t match Qin Xian’s abilities. Staying would have been pointless. You’ve only just started working at Qin Corporation and don’t have the clearance to interact with him yet. Once you’ve worked with your cousin a few times, you’ll understand.”","Seeing the pride on his father’s face, Qin Han’s fists tightened. It was because of Qin Xian that his usually reserved father was even talking to him like this.","But he couldn’t accept it. Was Qin Xian really that exceptional? He didn’t think his father was inferior to Second Uncle, so naturally, he didn’t think he was inferior to Qin Xian. Qin Xian just had a few years’ head start.","“You used to idolize him when you were little. Don’t you remember?” Third Uncle Qin asked, worried about his son’s arrogance.","Qin Han forced a laugh. “I don’t remember.”","Third Uncle Qin thought about it. It made sense. By the time Qin Han was old enough to remember, Qin Xian had already become withdrawn.","“Anyway, you’ll learn a lot from him. Follow his lead, and you’ll achieve more than our generation ever could. Your eldest aunt’s daughter has always done that, and Fourth Uncle’s two children, who joined the company a year before you, have grown rapidly under Qin Xian’s guidance. He may not show much emotion, but he’s always looked out for family.”","Qin Han felt like talking to his father about this would drive him mad. In other families, there was fierce competition, but in the Qin family, it seemed like everyone was content to be led by one or two smart individuals.","However, there was one area where Qin Xian didn’t seem so smart—he had been tricked into marrying a woman with no background, no education, and who had even become a comedian. In that regard, Qin Xian would always lose to him.","Qin Han didn’t want to discuss this further and changed the subject. “By the way, about you and Mom adopting a goddaughter, can we bring it up in front of the whole family this time? We were supposed to bring Xinxin with us, but you said it wasn’t appropriate.”","Qin Han complained, completely unaware that his sister, Qin Jiaxi, who had been silent in the corner, flinched at his words.","Third Uncle Qin frowned slightly. “I’m still considering it. I’ll talk to your grandfather first. If he disagrees, we’ll drop the matter.”","Qin Han immediately snapped, “But she saved Mom’s life!”","“Enough. I’ll handle it,” Third Uncle Qin said, not noticing his daughter’s discomfort. She had been unusually quiet for some time now.","The liveliest atmosphere was in Fourth Uncle Qin’s car. Having been widowed in middle age, Fourth Uncle Qin had brought his two daughters, Qin Jing and Qin Xiaoyu, to pick them up.","Fourth Uncle Qin laughed. “Why are you two so quiet? Weren’t you excited about Qin Xian coming?”","Both girls were smiling, but their eyes were glued to their phones, their fingers typing furiously.","Qin Jing said, “I am excited. Can’t you see I can’t stop smiling? Second Brother is my idol. Every time I see him, I’m struck by his charisma. His personal aura is no joke.”","Qin Xiaoyu added, “I’m excited too. I’ve secretly taken a few photos of Second Brother and Second Sister-in-law. Even though Third Brother is ridiculously handsome, I have to admit Second Brother’s looks are on another level. Combined with his abilities, he’s practically the perfect man.”","“More perfect than your boyfriend?” Qin Jing teased her twin sister.","“Definitely more perfect than you,” Qin Xiaoyu shot back. “Second Sister-in-law is beautiful too. I feel like she’s my kind of person. If you like someone, you should find a way to get them.”","Both men in the car immediately frowned and said in unison, “You can’t do that! You could get arrested if you cross the line!”","Qin Xiaoyu waved her phone with a laugh. “Don’t worry, I’m not taking that route. My guy is willing.”","“Probably because you’re throwing money at him,” Qin Jing teased again.","“At least he’s not some online stranger I’ve never met! You’re truly one of a kind among the rich third generation!” Qin Xiaoyu fired back.","The siblings immediately started bickering, leaving Fourth Uncle Qin with a headache.","Soon, the luxury cars entered the sprawling, ancient estate, a place where every inch of land was worth a fortune."]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325: It Turns Out I Really Married into a Wealthy Family and Reached the Pinnacle of Life","paragraphs":["At first, the Qin Family was a bit nervous. After all, it was in this old mansion that Qin Xian gradually became silent and withdrawn, almost like he had shut himself off. They were worried that returning here might trigger something in him.","However, as soon as they passed through the outermost gate, Ji Fei’s inner thoughts began to spill out uncontrollably, shattering any tension in the air.","[Wow, is this a mansion or a park? What’s with the endless stretch of trees? Wouldn’t you get lost here?]","[Oh my god, there’s a small bridge, a flowing stream, fountains, a swimming pool, a horse riding field, a children’s playground...]","[Finally, I see the main building. Wait, is this really a place to live? It’s so massive that it’s hard to take in all at once. The blend of Chinese and Western architectural styles—are we sure this isn’t some landmark?]","[I knew the Qin Family was wealthy, and I’ve been to a few luxurious mansions before, but this is on a whole other level of extravagance!]","Ji Fei kept her gaze fixed out the window, trying not to appear too inexperienced. Little did she know, her thoughts were practically leaking out for everyone to hear.","The grandeur of the place was so overwhelming that even Qin Xian’s brothers would have been impressed.","Ji Fei mechanically turned her head to look at Qin Xian.","[He’s the Master of Qin Family, and this is his estate. Oh my god, everyone’s been so low-key about it. I really did marry into a wealthy family and hit the jackpot in life. Suddenly, Qin Xian seems incredibly attractive today.]","The Qin Family members: *Snickers* Did you just realize that now?","The initially tense atmosphere in the car dissolved into suppressed laughter. Everyone was struggling to hold it in, their shoulders shaking with amusement.","Qin Xian’s lips twitched imperceptibly, and he sighed inwardly. It seemed he needed to keep earning more money to stay attractive in his wife’s eyes.","Seeing that Ji Fei genuinely seemed to like the place, Qin Xian asked, “What do you think of it?”","The family members in the car were shocked. Qin Xian was actually initiating a conversation about this place?","Ji Fei gave a thumbs-up, genuinely impressed.","Qin Xian thought for a moment and then added, “Do you want it?”","The Qin Family: !!!!! Suddenly, they felt they shouldn’t have been so cautious. Why did it sound like Qin Xian would give this place to Ji Fei if she wanted it, even if it held painful memories for him?","Wait, though you’re the Master of Qin Family, haven’t you always avoided competing with other family members over property? If Ji Fei wants it, are you really going to fight for the ownership rights?","Well, if Qin Xian wants something, it’s definitely going to be his, considering he now holds the authority in the Qin Family.","But Grandpa Qin is still alive! He’s living here! Isn’t it a bit inappropriate to discuss this now?!","Ji Fei thought for a moment and shook her head. “It’s just really impressive, that’s all.”","[It’s probably worth a fortune, but living in such a huge place would be so inconvenient. It’s already been five minutes since we drove in, and we’re still not at the entrance. The living quarters must be even bigger. It’d probably take over ten minutes just to walk from the bedroom to the dining room. Someone as lazy as me would definitely lose weight living here.]","The Qin Family: Your perspective is truly unique.","[And such a massive place feels like it’d be haunted.]","A few of the Qin Family members who were afraid of ghosts immediately shrank back. A problem they’d never considered before had just been pointed out. Damn it, they wouldn’t dare sleep alone tonight.","Qin Xian: ...No worries, I have my wife to keep me company.","Amidst the banter, the car finally stopped in a large square. As they stepped out, they were greeted by an enormous entrance gate.","Soon, other cars arrived, and everyone gathered to open the gate and step into the grand reception hall.","From afar, Ji Fei spotted a dignified, white-haired man sitting solemnly in the main seat of the sofa. Despite his age, Grandpa Qin was full of vitality. His sharp eyes flickered as they entered, especially when they landed on Qin Xian. A glimmer of tears seemed to appear, and his body shifted slightly, but he maintained his composed demeanor.","This was Grandpa Qin.","Beside him sat Grandma Lv, her face filled with kindness, though her eyes were red. Unlike Grandpa Qin, Grandma Lv couldn’t sit still. As soon as they approached, she stood up from the sofa and walked over eagerly, heading straight for Qin Xian.","“Ah, Xian, you’re finally here. It’s good that you’ve come. Was the journey smooth? Oh, and this must be Fei Fei. She’s so beautiful, even more so than on TV.”","Qin Xian supported Grandma Lv, his expression still calm but his eyes gentle. Grandma Lv didn’t mind his reserved demeanor and instead happily patted his hand repeatedly. Then she turned to Ji Fei, examining her with delight, clearly overjoyed.","Grandma Lv’s warmth and affection immediately softened Ji Fei’s heart. For a moment, she almost convinced herself that such a kind and loving grandmother couldn’t possibly have treated Qin Xian badly.","But the next second, Ji Fei steeled herself. She had already researched Grandpa Qin and Grandma Lv’s backgrounds, so she quickly checked the key information in her mind.","[Hmm... Grandpa Qin, Grandma Lv—they pass the test!]","Qin Xian was momentarily confused, unsure what Ji Fei meant, but he quickly glanced at the other Qin Family members present.","The members of the Qin Family’s second branch naturally understood what Ji Fei was doing. Hearing her thoughts, they all breathed a sigh of relief.","They couldn’t bear the thought that Grandpa Qin might be involved in anything harmful, and Grandma Lv, who had devoted so much to the family, was someone they couldn’t imagine causing harm to Qin Xian.","Thankfully, she wasn’t.","However, they quickly glanced around to gauge the reactions of others in the room.","It seemed... no one else had reacted. They felt reassured. After all, Ji Fei’s thoughts had been so abrupt that anyone who heard them would have had some reaction.","They had suspected before that not all Qin Family members could hear Ji Fei’s thoughts. After all, when Qin Xi’s situation had come up earlier, a few Qin Family relatives had visited, and none of them had been able to hear her inner voice.","This only confirmed their theory further.","Perhaps it was because they held a special place in Ji Fei’s heart.","The Qin Family members couldn’t help but feel a sense of pride, as if they had been acknowledged in some way.","After showering Qin Xian and Ji Fei with attention, Grandma Lv naturally didn’t forget Qin Xi, who was visiting for the first time. If her health had allowed, Grandma Lv would have picked Qin Xi up. “Oh, little Xi looks so much like Xian did when he was a child. So adorable. Poor child, you’ve had a tough time outside, but now you’re back. Everything’s going to be alright.”","Grandpa Qin cleared his throat, signaling Grandma Lv to calm down.","“Aunt Lv, you’re so focused on the younger generation that you’ve forgotten us old folks,” said a middle-aged couple sitting on the sofa. They were the Eldest Aunt and Eldest Uncle, who hadn’t gone to greet them earlier. They stood up and warmly invited everyone to sit down.","However, the second branch of the Qin Family only visited once a year, so they had to pay their respects to Grandpa Qin properly, especially Qin Xian, Ji Fei, and Qin Xi.","Despite Grandpa Qin’s stern demeanor over the phone, in person, he maintained his authoritative presence. He nodded solemnly and then handed out thick red envelopes.","Qin Xian immediately passed his to Ji Fei, who held the brick-sized envelope with a genuine smile. The joy on her face was exactly the kind of reaction the elders loved to see."]},{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: Hehe~ Gossip~","paragraphs":["Little Xi and Ji Fei were immediately pulled by Grandma Lv to sit on either side of her and the Old Master on the main sofa.","The others gradually took their seats.","Auntie's family, being older, mostly lived with the Old Master in the ancestral home. Third Uncle's family originally lived in Y City, so they often visited. Fourth Uncle's family lived in the neighboring G City, so they also came frequently. At the moment, only Fifth Aunt and Sixth Uncle were missing.","\"Fifth Aunt's husband has encountered some business issues, so their family is currently abroad dealing with it. They’ll probably arrive later. Sixth Uncle's family is waiting for their little princess to finish her exams before returning home. And Seventh Sister's family is still abroad,\" Auntie explained with a smile.","Ji Fei took a moment to recall that Seventh Sister referred to Lu Meihe, Grandma Lv's youngest daughter, whom they all called Seventh Sister.","Qin's Father chimed in, \"I’ve heard about that. By the way, let’s have Qin Xian and Qin Xi introduce themselves to everyone first. Otherwise, these two little ones won’t know how to address everyone properly.\"","\"I’ll handle it, Dad,\" Qin Xian volunteered, causing a momentary hush in the room. Although many of those present had professional dealings with Qin Xian and exchanged polite greetings, it was rare to see him take the initiative in such a personal setting. It felt quite unusual.","Qin Xian held Ji Fei's hand, silently reassuring her, and began introducing everyone starting with Auntie's family.","Auntie's family included Auntie, Uncle, their eldest cousin Qin Wenqiang, her husband Yang Feng, and their daughter Yang Weiwei. There was also the eldest cousin Qin Yi.","Ji Fei maintained a polite smile, greeting everyone and matching names to faces.","[Auntie's family... huh, passed the test.]","Qin's second family breathed a sigh of relief.","Qin Xian: ?","Qin Yan also prompted Qin Xi to greet everyone. When introducing Yang Weiwei, the two children quickly bonded, likely ready to play together soon.","Auntie smiled and said, \"Earlier, Dad and Grandma Lv insisted we all watch some show—the one Ji Fei and Qin Zhao performed in. You guys were amazing! You even won the championship!\"","With Auntie's revelation, everyone realized that the Old Master and Grandma Lv had been watching the mainland variety show Ji Fei and Qin Zhao participated in. While the older generation might not have grasped the nuances or followed the live comments, they knew the duo had won every time.","[Thank goodness. From their expressions, it seems they’re unaware of the online drama surrounding the show. Otherwise, I wouldn’t be able to enjoy my gossip in peace.]","Qin's second family couldn’t help but chuckle, playing along with Auntie's topic.","But someone lacked tact. Yang Feng suddenly spoke up, \"By the way, Qin Xian, about that new project I mentioned earlier—what exactly didn’t you like about it?\"","Qin Wenqiang and Qin Yi's expressions froze.","It was unclear whether Yang Feng was overly ambitious or just oblivious, as the introductions were about to move on to Third Uncle's family.","Qin Xian replied coolly, \"We don’t discuss business at home.\"","His tone carried an implicit authority, shutting Yang Feng down. Yang Feng, though visibly displeased, could only force an awkward smile.","Ji Fei noticed Yang Feng's hostile demeanor and couldn’t help but let her thoughts wander.","[So obsessed with work? Let me check... Oh, juicy gossip?!]","Qin's second family collectively perked up. Although they had mentally prepared for Ji Fei’s presence and the possibility of uncovering family secrets, they hadn’t expected it to happen so quickly.","While their main focus was uncovering details about Qin Xian's childhood, now... well, Yang Feng had walked right into the line of fire.","What gossip? What happened? Tell us, tell us!","Qin Yan, Qin Zhao, and Qin Rong were practically reaching for the snacks on the coffee table.","[Auntie’s family successor is the eldest cousin, Qin Wenqiang, a decisive and formidable woman. But it seems she’s unaware that her husband has been cheating on her and even has a bunch of illegitimate children.]","Qin's second family: ...","Not entirely surprising, but the more they thought about it, the more they wanted to stand up and punch someone.","Wow, just wow. Back then, Yang Feng had gone to great lengths to pursue Qin Wenqiang. After marrying her, he had worked diligently for the Qin family. Even when Qin Wenqiang chose to have only one child due to health concerns, Yang Feng had never publicly complained, earning a reputation as a model son-in-law.","Truly, appearances can be deceiving. Who would have thought he could deceive someone as sharp as Qin Wenqiang for so long? It’s almost unimaginable.","[So, here’s the deal: he runs a new company under the guise of a joint venture with his wife, but in reality, Qin Wenqiang has no stake in it. It’s all for his mistress and their children, as well as various relatives and connections. He’s avoiding the risk of bringing them into Qin Corporation.]","[He’s also preparing for the worst—if things ever go south with Qin Wenqiang, he’ll have this company as a fallback. That’s why he’s so desperate to siphon funds from Qin Xian to prop up his own business.]","Qin's second family glared at Yang Feng, their expressions darkening.","Yang Feng, who had just regained his composure, was baffled by the hostile stares. All he wanted was to secure some benefits for his new company through Qin Xian. Why were they looking at him like he was the enemy?","[This brother-in-law is like a rat, sneaking things from the Qin family to his own nest. Absolutely unacceptable! That’s essentially stealing my money too!]","Qin's second family: Well done! You’ve truly embraced the role of the family matriarch!","[You scoundrel, you’ve crossed the wrong person. I’ll make sure to expose you sooner or later!]","Qin's second family: Yes! Expose him!","Qin Xian: ...Are they planning to break up a family right after arriving?","He quietly pulled out his phone and sent a message. After all, he had people he could mobilize here. Exposing a scoundrel starts with gathering evidence.","Yang Feng shivered inexplicably. All he did was bring up an ill-timed project proposal. Why did he feel a chill down his spine? The way the family was looking at him was downright terrifying.","Perhaps sensing the awkward tension, Qin Yi, known for his gentle demeanor, quickly shifted the conversation by asking Qin Xi if she played any musical instruments.","Since the scoundrel wasn’t worth their attention and divorce was already on the horizon, Ji Fei was soon distracted.","[This cousin is a vocal music professor at a top conservatory and a renowned baritone. Oh, suddenly I realize he’s just as handsome as Qin Zhao, but in a refined, artistic way. His charm is different from Qin Xian and Qin Zhao’s. Hmm, eye candy!]","Qin Xian: !","Qin Zhao: Hey hey, how is he just as handsome as me? I’m younger!","The other women in Qin's second family: Hmm? True, we hadn’t noticed before. Ji Fei has an eye for beauty!","[I wonder if this cousin gets asked to perform during family gatherings.]","Qin Zhao: ...Let’s not go there. Thankfully, my family doesn’t do that.","Qin Xian: I think I’ve seen him get asked before.","[Pfft, so that’s why he’s been taking time off—not just to visit relatives, but to dodge a romantic entanglement.]","Qin's second family: What gossip have you stumbled upon now?","They remembered Qin Yi was a staunch bachelor, having no interest in marriage even at thirty. What romantic entanglement could he possibly have?","Qin Xian glanced curiously at his cousin.","[He was confessed to by his most dedicated student at the conservatory! No wonder he’s been avoiding things.]","Qin's second family: Hehe~ Juicy gossip~","Qin Yi, completely unaware that his secrets had been laid bare, shivered. Why did he suddenly feel a cold wave of dread?"]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Was It Unanimously Agreed Upon by Your Entire Family","paragraphs":["Since Qin Yi changed the subject, Qin Xian smoothly took over and began introducing Ji Fei to Third Uncle's family.","Third Uncle's family includes Third Uncle and Third Aunt. Although they married early, they had children relatively late. Their eldest son, Qin Han, just graduated with a master's degree this year, while their daughter, Qin Jiaxi, is only a freshman in college.","Ji Fei naturally scanned through the information she was most concerned about first.","*[Third Uncle's family, the people present... hmm, they pass. But it's hard to say about Third Aunt since she's not here.]*","The Qin family's second branch breathed a brief sigh of relief.","Qin Xian paused for a moment, glancing at Ji Fei out of the corner of his eye, deep in thought.","Third Uncle was the first to speak up and explain, \"I apologize. Third Aunt was supposed to join us today, but...\"","At this point, a rare softness and awkwardness appeared on Third Uncle's usually stern face.","\"Dad, everyone, Zi Xuan is pregnant. She's already three months along.\"","The room erupted in surprise, and the joy of welcoming a new life filled the hall.","*[Wow, Third Uncle and Third Aunt aren't exactly young anymore, and they're having another child...]*","As she thought this, Ji Fei's gaze shifted to Qin's Father and Qin's Mom.","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom immediately stiffened. No, they couldn't possibly—they were in their fifties, definitely too old for that! Besides, they already had enough children; among the Qin siblings, they had the most kids.","The other siblings stifled their laughter.","Third Uncle continued, \"A while ago, Zi Xuan was in a minor car accident, which caused some instability with the pregnancy. That's why we didn't dare tell anyone until now. She's still recovering, so we'll bring her over once she's more stable.\"","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom immediately assured him there was no need to rush, while Grandpa Qin and Grandma Lv were overjoyed.","\"Zi Xuan is already an older mother, so your family must take extra care of her and spend more time with her. She can come for the big birthday celebration,\" Grandpa Qin said excitedly, as this might be the last newborn he would see in his lifetime.","Seeing his grandfather so happy, Qin Han suddenly became enthusiastic. \"Grandpa, you don't know this yet, but during that accident, it was actually a girl who saved Mom. If it weren't for her, who knows what might have happened? She saved both Mom and my unborn sibling. Mom and I feel we owe her a great debt, so we're thinking of having the family adopt her as a foster daughter.\"","The abrupt introduction of this topic brought the room to a stunned silence.","Grandpa Qin was also taken aback. \"Oh? Is that so?\" he said, turning to Third Uncle.","Third Uncle's expression shifted slightly, and he shot Qin Han a displeased look. \"There was indeed a girl who saved Zi Xuan. She's also Jiaxi's friend. She used to visit our home occasionally because the orphanage she grew up in was supported by Zi Xuan's charity work. She's always been grateful to Zi Xuan and was with her during the accident. It was this girl who bravely pulled Zi Xuan out of the wrecked car.\"","\"Hearing this, she sounds like a brave, kind, and grateful child,\" Grandma Lv said softly, clearly moved.","Third Uncle, however, added, \"Originally, we planned to prepare a generous gift to express our gratitude...\"","\"Dad, Mom already said that giving money would be an insult. She's been so sincere with our family—why can't she become our daughter? I already see her as a younger sister,\" Qin Han argued immediately.","Third Uncle cut him off, \"Enough. Adopting a child isn't a simple matter. I'll discuss this later with your grandfather... and Qin Xian.\"","Clearly, Third Uncle didn't want to finalize anything on the spot. The other relatives remained silent, while the younger generation exchanged uncertain glances.","*[Huh? That's strange. Third Uncle seems unusually reluctant to agree to this.]*","The Qin family's second branch, however, found Third Uncle's hesitation unsurprising.","Soon, Ji Fei figured it out.","*[Ah, I see. The Qin family's interests are closely intertwined. Adopting a child would mean she could enjoy the benefits of the Qin Corporation, something even that cheating brother-in-law wouldn't dare dream of. This would affect everyone's interests. While no one would mind a small foster daughter potentially gaining some assets, Third Uncle is a cautious and strict man. He doesn't want to create any lingering resentment among the family.]*","*[If he makes an exception, it could open the floodgates for other relatives to adopt children, and that would cause chaos. His initial idea was to give her money—ensuring her a comfortable life in exchange for saving Zi Xuan should be enough. Why insist on adoption?]*","The Qin family's second branch naturally didn't care much about this issue, but they couldn't guarantee that others wouldn't have opinions, so they chose not to voice their thoughts.","However, when Qin Han heard that his father planned to consult not only Grandpa Qin but also Qin Xian, he immediately felt unbalanced.","The next moment, Grandpa Qin also spoke up, \"I'm old now. You can discuss this matter with Qin Xian later.\"","The Qin family's second branch was momentarily speechless. Grandpa Qin was clearly avoiding the responsibility and passing it on to Qin Xian.","Qin Xian, however, remained completely unfazed, calm and composed as always.","The others didn't seem to mind, as the only person in the room who might challenge Qin Xian was that foolish cousin.","Third Uncle also gave Qin Xian a look, indicating they would discuss this privately later.","Finally, Qin Han realized that in this family, while Grandpa Qin was the nominal head, the real authority now lay with Qin Xian.","Qin Han hadn't expected that getting a sister would require the approval of a cousin. Unwilling to let the matter drop, he pressed on with a forced smile, \"Second Brother already has so many siblings. Surely you wouldn't mind if our family added one more, right?\"","Oh? This guy seems really unconvinced. Ah, I see—he thinks his father has contributed just as much to the Qin family as Qin's Father, so he believes he's on equal footing with Qin Xian.","The Qin family's second branch wasn't too bothered. It was normal for a large family to have a few rebellious members; such unity rarely lasted beyond two generations.","However, Ji Fei seemed a little annoyed.","*[You just graduated with a master's degree at this age? My husband was already taking over the company by then. Who gave you the confidence to act so self-important?]*","The Qin family's second branch: Oh~ of course, your husband is the best.","Qin Xian's lips curved into a slight smile.","Seeing Qin Xian's suddenly softened expression, Qin Han thought the matter might be easier to resolve. \"Yu Xin is truly a wonderful girl. She deserves to be a daughter of the Qin family.\"","*[He's so enthusiastic about this. Does he really like this sister that much? What's even stranger is Qin Jiaxi. Among the younger generation, she's the only one who hasn't said a word. Everyone else is lively and engaged, but as the Qin family's eldest daughter, why is she so reserved? Wasn't it her friend who used to visit often? Shouldn't she be the one most actively advocating for this? This is really odd. Let me investigate further.]*","In fact, the Qin family's second branch also found the reactions of Third Uncle's children rather peculiar.","Qin Xian raised an eyebrow slightly, buying time for Ji Fei's investigation. \"Is the addition of a new member something your entire family has unanimously agreed to?\""]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Is This the Standard Setting for a Tragic Heroine","paragraphs":["Saving a life and adopting a girl shouldn’t be a big issue. At most, we can limit the acceptable assets to the current scope of Third Uncle Qin’s family, so other relatives won’t have anything to say. If the girl has the ability to work, we can nurture her well—more effort, more reward.","However, the key problem is that the girl’s arrival is welcomed by the entire family.","Qin Xian is protective, but first and foremost, he protects the Qin family.","Upon hearing this, Qin Han immediately chimed in enthusiastically, “Mom and I both agree. Dad doesn’t oppose it, right?”","After saying this, Qin Han vigorously signaled to his father with his eyes.","Third Uncle Qin paused, giving a vague response. He didn’t oppose it, but deep down, he felt something was off, though he couldn’t quite put his finger on it.","With this support, Qin Han turned to Qin Xian, looking confident and determined. “See?”","Qin Xian’s expression remained unchanged, and he stayed silent.","After waiting a few seconds, Qin Han lost his patience. “Is there still a problem?”","Qin Zhao, who had been watching from the side, couldn’t take it anymore. He wasn’t known for his patience, and Qin Han’s attitude toward Qin Xian was already grating on his nerves. Qin Han’s current behavior made him want to roll his eyes, so he spoke bluntly, “Oh, so your family only consists of three people now?”","Qin Han was momentarily stunned, not immediately grasping the sarcasm in Qin Zhao’s words.","Meanwhile, Qin Rong, who was about the same age as Qin Jiaxi, couldn’t help but interject, “Brother Han, why didn’t you ask Jiaxi for her opinion? Second Brother clearly said it should be the whole family.”","It seemed Qin Jiaxi’s presence was so inconspicuous that everyone had momentarily forgotten she hadn’t voiced her opinion yet.","At this reminder, all eyes turned to her.","Qin Jiaxi clearly wasn’t used to being the center of attention. She felt extremely uncomfortable, as no one had ever asked for her opinion before. Now, being questioned by relatives from Second Uncle’s family, she was at a complete loss.","Qin Han reacted quickly, a flicker of disdain crossing his face. He was sitting right next to Qin Jiaxi but didn’t bother to ask her directly. Instead, he said dismissively, “What does she know? Her opinion doesn’t matter.”","As soon as these words left his mouth, the Old Master’s expression darkened. “What kind of nonsense is that? Every child in the Qin family’s opinion matters.”","Qin Han’s face flushed red. He hadn’t expected to be reprimanded and, in his embarrassment, redirected his anger. He immediately grabbed Qin Jiaxi’s arm and snapped, “Well? What’s your opinion?”","Qin Han’s attitude toward Qin Jiaxi made the surrounding relatives uncomfortable. However, since the two were siblings, and no one knew how they usually interacted, no one dared to overstep Third Uncle Qin’s authority.","Third Uncle Qin merely blinked, showing no reaction. To him, this attitude wasn’t unusual. In his eyes, his daughter was too reserved, always lost in her own thoughts.","Qin Jiaxi’s eyes welled up with tears, but she quickly lowered her head, her thick bangs hiding her emotions. “I... I have no opinion. I’ll listen to whatever Mom and Dad decide.”","Qin Han let out a sigh of relief, a hint of smugness on his face. Thankfully, he had disciplined Qin Jiaxi harshly earlier, making sure she behaved and wouldn’t oppose Yu Xin entering the Qin family. Otherwise, who knew what kind of trouble she might stir up?","“Is that settled now?” Qin Han asked, already subconsciously acknowledging Qin Xian’s authority. It seemed that as long as Qin Xian nodded, the matter would be resolved.","However, he noticed that Qin Xian’s expression remained unchanged, and his gaze toward Qin Han grew colder. Not only Qin Xian, but the entire Second Uncle’s family was also looking at him with disapproval, making him feel inexplicably uneasy.","[What the hell? Are you seriously choosing a romantic interest over your own sister? It’s fine to want to take care of Yu Xin since you’ve known her since childhood through Third Aunt’s charity work at the orphanage. But letting your own sister suffer because of an outsider? That’s just inhuman.]","With Qin Han and Qin Jiaxi right in front of him, many pieces of the puzzle fell into place, revealing the truth.","[Yu Xin is nothing but a scheming, malicious woman. She officially entered their lives during high school, and from that point on, Qin Jiaxi’s life turned into a living hell. Yu Xin would pretend to be bullied by Qin Jiaxi in front of Qin Han, while secretly taunting and provoking Qin Jiaxi behind the scenes, pushing her to react. Then, Yu Xin would play the victim in front of Qin Han, sowing discord and framing Qin Jiaxi. The once cheerful girl has been reduced to this gloomy, depressed state—all because of Yu Xin’s manipulations.]","The members of Qin Second’s family were shocked. It was hard to believe someone could so easily deceive others.","Ji Fei also found it unbelievable. After all, this was his own sister.","[Even if Yu Xin is an exceptional actress, shouldn’t family be the ones you trust the most? How could he be so foolish as to believe an outsider without verifying the truth when there are conflicting accounts?]","[And it’s not just him. In Qin Jiaxi’s memories, Third Aunt was also completely fooled, siding with Yu Xin. What kind of topsy-turvy world is this?]","Qin Second’s family couldn’t help but gasp. What on earth was going on? Was Third Aunt also clueless? And what about Third Uncle?","[Third Uncle, busy with work, rarely spent time with his daughter. He left all family matters to his wife and was often absent from home. Over time, he grew numb to the situation, assuming his daughter’s personality had simply changed. He had no idea his daughter was enduring domestic bullying.]","Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom couldn’t help but shoot Third Uncle Qin a sidelong glance. Work is important, but you idiot, you can’t neglect your children’s upbringing!","[Wait, there’s even school bullying?]","Qin Second’s family shuddered. Could Yu Xin really control people at school? Was she that untouchable, or was Qin Han aiding her from afar?","[What the hell? Her boyfriend, Su Ze, is the school heartthrob, so she’s being bullied by other socialites at school? Wait, the school doesn’t know her identity because Third Aunt and Qin Han forbade her from revealing it, fearing that Yu Xin, who attends the same school, would face discrimination? I... I can’t make sense of this logic. Were Qin Jiaxi and Yu Xin switched at birth?]","Qin Second’s family was also baffled. Su... that must be the Su family, one of Y City’s prominent families, on par with the Qin family. So, Su Ze is a young master from a wealthy family?","There’s no issue with him being Qin Jiaxi’s boyfriend, but how could it lead to her being bullied? And what on earth is Third Aunt thinking?","If Qin Jiaxi didn’t resemble Qin Yan, Qin Rong, and Fourth Uncle’s daughter, they might have joined Ji Fei in questioning whether Qin Jiaxi and Yu Xin were switched at birth.","[I can’t bear to watch this anymore. Is this the standard setup for a tragic heroine? A father who’s absent, a mother who doesn’t care, a brother who’s indifferent, and a rocky relationship with her boyfriend—no wonder she looks so depressed and insecure. Now, the woman who’s been tormenting her is about to become part of her family. It couldn’t get any worse. Why did she agree to this?!]"]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: How can you have the nerve to adopt another daughter when you've raised your own daughter like this","paragraphs":["【So, she thought her opposition wouldn’t matter anyway, since her mom and brother liked Yu Xin more. If she objected, she’d just be blamed. Oh my, such a pessimistic mindset. What has she been through to have no ability to resist at all?】","The Qin Second family all furrowed their brows in unison.","This made Qin Han think that his family was truly petty, making such a big deal out of adopting someone.","【What the—my eyes! Are they even family?!!!!】","Ji Fei’s inner thoughts suddenly exploded. The Qin Second family, unaware of what she had seen, looked even more uneasy.","【...Not long ago, when Yu Xin took the clothes her father had given her and Qin Jiaxi wanted them back, Yu Xin pretended to fall and cry, even tearing the clothes in the process. This instantly triggered Qin Han’s temper, forcing Qin Jiaxi to kneel and apologize. When Qin Jiaxi refused, Qin Han slapped her hard. Ugh!】","Ji Fei clenched her fists, and the Qin Second family’s eyes began to burn with anger as they glared at Qin Han.","A brief silence of just a few seconds made the atmosphere even more tense, causing everyone else to quiet down, unsure of what was happening.","【And Third Aunt didn’t even care about her daughter’s suffering, still demanding that she apologize to Yu Xin? If she didn’t apologize, she’d act all disappointed and angry. To Qin Jiaxi, this was even more painful than her brother’s slap, and in the end, she had to numb herself and apologize to Yu Xin. Ugh! This makes me so mad!】","【Anyway, I won’t agree! If such a lowly person enters the Qin Family, my husband’s earnings will have to be shared with her as dividends. No way!】","Qin Xian lowered his gaze, no longer looking at Qin Han. He quietly reached out to hold Ji Fei’s hand, silently comforting her, not wanting his wife to get worked up over such scum.","The Qin Second family’s icy gazes swept toward Third Uncle Qin.","Third Uncle Qin felt as if he had been struck by several invisible arrows. He guessed that the Qin Second family was blaming him for not controlling Qin Han, who was being overly aggressive in pressuring Qin Xian to make a decision. He also felt it was inappropriate.","“Alright, the first step is that the whole family doesn’t oppose it. I’ll discuss it further with your cousin later,” Third Uncle Qin said sternly to Qin Han.","Just as Qin Han was about to speak, Qin’s Mom suddenly interrupted with a smile, “Oh, Third Uncle, your family must really dote on your daughter, right?”","“Huh?” Third Uncle Qin was momentarily confused, not catching on.","Qin Han also frowned and looked over.","Qin’s Mom, having heard Ji Fei’s thoughts, couldn’t hold back and directly spoke up for justice, “Surely no one would neglect their own daughter and instead favor an outsider, rushing to adopt and pamper someone else’s child. That’s why I thought your family must treat Qin Jiaxi like a little princess, just like how we treat Qin Rong, raising her with all the love and care.”","As Qin’s Mom spoke, Qin Rong nestled into her mother’s arms, radiant and sunny, like a child raised in a honeypot, her eyes shining with light. Not just Qin Rong, but even Qin Yan, who had been worn down by marriage, had recently recovered well.","Not to mention them, even Qin Wenqiang, the eldest cousin, and the daughters from Fourth Uncle’s family carried themselves with confidence and pride, clearly the daughters of the Qin Family.","In contrast, Qin Jiaxi seemed completely out of place. If not for her resemblance to the family, she would have looked like a frail, helpless, and spiritless girl.","The corners of everyone’s mouths twitched: What kind of “little princess” is this? To put it bluntly, Qin Jiaxi didn’t even compare to a maid serving a princess.","Qin Yan chimed in, supporting her mom, “Third Uncle and Third Aunt must have given Qin Jiaxi so much love and security that they feel confident enough to adopt another child.”","Love? Security?","Without comparison, it wasn’t obvious, but now the difference was striking. Usually, Qin Jiaxi was quiet and low-key, so no one paid much attention to her. But now... the elders gradually turned their gazes to Third Uncle Qin.","Their expressions were clear: How could you raise your own daughter like this and still think about adopting another?","Third Uncle Qin finally realized what had felt off earlier. Adding another daughter would make his own daughter’s position awkward. Unless the original daughter was the one eagerly asking for a sister, this situation would always feel wrong.","And his daughter... Had they failed in raising her, causing her to turn out this way?","Third Uncle Qin couldn’t help but glance at Qin Jiaxi, who was curled up in the corner of the sofa, looking so small and pitiful. Then he looked at the other girls of her generation...","Having always left the upbringing of their children to his wife, Third Uncle Qin felt a wave of uncertainty for the first time.","【Amazing! I can tell Mom and Big Sis are mocking them. Even without knowing the details, just looking at Qin Jiaxi’s state, it’s clear that adopting another girl makes no sense! Third Uncle seems to be realizing something, but I wonder about that ungrateful brother...】","Looking at Qin Han, his face was indeed dark, clearly catching the subtext. However, he shot a glare at Qin Jiaxi.","【Ohoho, he’s blaming Qin Jiaxi, thinking she’s putting on an act to sabotage the adoption. Is this guy even her real brother? How can he think his own sister is so malicious?】","Hearing this, the Qin Second family was livid.","Qin’s Father arrived and directly addressed Third Uncle Qin, “Third Uncle, it’s best to think this through carefully.”","His tone made it clear that Qin Second did not support this matter.","Third Uncle Qin took a deep breath. “Let’s forget it. I don’t think it’s appropriate.”","Qin Han, who hadn’t even gotten a word from Qin Xian, was furious at how things had turned out. “Dad, you just agreed! How can you go back on your word? Have you forgotten? If it weren’t for Yu Xin, Mom and the baby in her womb might not have been okay. Our Qin Family has always been about repaying kindness. If outsiders find out, they’ll laugh at us!”","Third Uncle Qin’s face immediately darkened. “Enough! With so many elders here, have you no shame?”","Qin Han was startled by his father’s sudden sternness. The authority in his father’s voice was enough to silence him.","【Hah, serves him right. Always bringing up the so-called debt of gratitude. Who would’ve thought that such a despicable girl like Yu Xin would be so self-sacrificing... Wait, what?!!!】","Just as the Qin Second family was relieved by Third Uncle Qin’s change of heart, they suddenly perked up at this.","Was there more to the story? Spill it, quick!","【Did Yu Xin save Third Aunt and Qin Han in a past life? How could they go this far for her?????】","The Qin Second family: What? How far did they go?","Even Qin Xian was curious now.","Then they heard Ji Fei’s voice, dripping with disdain.","【Ugh! This so-called life-saving favor, I’m dying of laughter. It turns out it was all a setup by Third Aunt and Qin Han to get the Qin Family to adopt Yu Xin. They staged a fake car accident, took some photos and videos, and made Third Uncle believe that Yu Xin had helped Third Aunt out of a smoking, wrecked car. It was all a lie!】"]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: This Family's Love Affairs Are Anything but Conventional","paragraphs":["Qin Second's Family: !!!!!","Damn! The life-saving favor was fabricated! Are they messing with the Qin family?!","Has Qin Third's wife and son lost their minds?!","Qin Xian suddenly let out a silent, cold laugh. Whether Third Aunt Qin and Qin Han had gone mad or not, he needed to thoroughly investigate Yu Xin's relationship with the two of them.","There’s no such thing as senseless idiocy in this world!","At the very least, he needed to find evidence of what the so-called \"life-saving favor\" looked like and show it to Third Uncle Qin. Let him see how those closest to him were scheming against him.","Ji Fei, having seen the truth through Qin Han, was also furious.","[To go to such lengths for an outsider, even deceiving Third Uncle Qin, while being so cruel to their own flesh and blood, Qin Jiaxi—Qin Han, that beast who thinks with his lower body, I’m not surprised. But Third Aunt Qin, what kind of person could do such a thing? I’m really looking forward to meeting her. Hopefully, Qin Xian’s issues have nothing to do with her, otherwise... hmph! Thankfully, Third Uncle Qin is still clear-headed, or else Qin Jiaxi would be in real trouble.]","Qin Xian, as usual, listened to Ji Fei’s internal ranting but suddenly froze.","Qin Second's Family, standing nearby, immediately tensed up. They sneakily glanced over and saw Qin Xian staring intently at Ji Fei.","Qin Xian’s gaze deepened as if he had confirmed something.","His hand, which had been holding hers, gradually interlaced their fingers.","A faint smile began to gather at the corners of his eyes.","Seeing this, Qin Second's Family finally let out a sigh of relief.","The matter of adopting a daughter was left unresolved due to Third Uncle Qin’s decision, but it had already ruined the atmosphere of the family gathering. Qin Han, leaning back on the sofa, was busy on his phone, likely contacting someone, his face sour, but no one paid him any attention.","“The Fourth Uncle’s family hasn’t been introduced yet,” the eldest aunt awkwardly changed the subject.","Qin Xian took the cue and began introducing Ji Fei to them.","The Fourth Uncle’s family of three seemed completely unaffected by the earlier drama, happily chatting away.","Ji Fei couldn’t help but chuckle inwardly: [They’re really carefree, the three of them. They were totally engrossed in the drama earlier. Just from that, I can already vouch for their reliability... haha, they’ve passed the test!]","Qin Xian smiled faintly, his fingers gently caressing the back of Ji Fei’s soft hand.","You’ve worked hard, my dear~","He knew it—all the psychological reactions, the missing memories, the possibility of having endured something traumatic in his childhood. It wasn’t hard to deduce, but he had never actively investigated because he didn’t think it mattered. His psychologist, however, had told him this was abnormal and even suspected he might have subconsciously suppressed something.","But he truly lacked the motivation to dig into it. Now, it seemed his wife was worried about him. Maybe he should try harder to remember.","But... every time he tried to recall, it felt like there was a barrier blocking him...","After Ji Fei finished assessing the Fourth Uncle’s family and since there were no more relatives to meet, she decided to treat everyone equally and dug into the gossip about the Fourth Uncle’s family as well.","[Fourth Aunt passed away years ago, so Fourth Uncle poured all his energy into his work and raising his two children. Look at the contrast—Fourth Uncle, being both father and mother, managed to raise his kids with no apparent psychological issues and a harmonious relationship. Unlike Third Uncle... even though Third Uncle is said to be second only to Qin Xian in business acumen, it’s still quite pitiful.]","Qin Second's Family thought the same. The twins from Fourth Uncle’s family were truly outstanding, with impeccable manners and always wearing bright smiles.","Qin Xian was also familiar with the twins, having already started working with them. They had been educated with a keen business sense and were definitely worth nurturing for the future.","[Haha, their love lives are so amusing! But Fourth Uncle doesn’t mind, as long as his children are happy.]","Qin Second's Family, hearing this, immediately grew curious. What kind of love lives were so funny?","However, Ji Fei didn’t share everything in her mind, so Qin Second's Family had to satisfy their curiosity by asking directly. Luckily, such questions could be brought up openly.","“You two will be turning twenty-seven this New Year, right? Do you have partners yet?” Qin’s mother asked with a smile.","The twins immediately blushed. Grandma Lü and the eldest aunt, sensing there was more to the story, quickly chimed in, asking if they could bring their partners to their grandfather’s birthday celebration.","To everyone’s surprise, the twins spoke at the same time, each pointing at the other.","Qin Xiaoyu said, “My brother’s girlfriend is from an online relationship—they haven’t even met in person yet!”","Qin Jing countered, “My sister’s boyfriend is a gamer—she spent a fortune to win him over!”","They immediately started arguing.","Qin Jing: “We’ve video-called and talked on the phone, we just haven’t met in person yet!”","Qin Xiaoyu: “We’re pursuing our esports dreams together, and I even made money investing in the team!”","Their bickering had everyone in stitches.","Third Uncle Qin, observing the twins' tacit understanding, couldn't help but compare them to his own children. Despite the age difference, his son showed no tolerance toward his younger sister. Clearly, something was wrong.","Ji Fei was also thoroughly entertained, unable to resist adding her own internal commentary.","[Online dating? They’re officially a couple but haven’t met in person? Aren’t they worried about catfishing or AI face-swapping? But since he’s planning to meet his girlfriend and bring her to the grandfather’s ninetieth birthday, I can only hope his online romance doesn’t crash and burn.]","[As for the sister, she’s secretly dating an esports player, completely smitten by his looks and skills, throwing money at him left and right. It’s like a rich heiress and her esports star love story. Seems like she’s also planning to bring him to the birthday celebration.]","Thanks to the Fourth Uncle’s family’s antics, the atmosphere remained lively until dinner. Everyone ate together, chatted for a while, and then prepared to rest for the night.","Qin Xian’s family and the Fourth Uncle’s family naturally stayed in the main house of the estate.","The eldest aunt and her husband also stayed, and Qin Yi, seemingly afraid to return to his own home, decided to stay as well. However, the eldest cousin and her family returned to their own residence, and Third Uncle Qin’s family also went back to their home.","But two people unexpectedly stayed behind.","One was Yang Weiwei, who had become good friends with Qin Xi and wanted to spend more time together. The eldest cousin entrusted Yang Weiwei to her parents, so the two kids continued playing in the estate.","The other was Qin Jiaxi, whom Qin Rong had insisted stay, claiming she was afraid to sleep alone.","Since Qin Yan was staying with her son, Qin Rong couldn’t very well impose on her mother or sister-in-law. She was also worried that Qin Jiaxi would be mistreated if she went back, so she persuaded her to stay.","Before Third Uncle Qin could say anything, Qin Han was the first to object. Qin Second's Family, seeing the look on his face, knew he was up to no good—probably planning to take his frustrations out on Qin Jiaxi once they got home. There was no way they could let her leave!","Thankfully, Third Uncle Qin didn’t object, and Qin Jiaxi stayed without incident.","In truth, Qin Jiaxi had already prepared herself for the worst. She had anticipated that things wouldn’t go as her mother and brother had hoped, and she knew what her fate would be. She just hadn’t expected to be intercepted from the very beginning, leaving her utterly bewildered.","When her father and brother finally left, she turned around to find the younger generation waiting for her in the living room, ready to chat and drink. Though she still didn’t say much, no one pressured her, and the natural, harmonious atmosphere was something she hadn’t experienced in years.","That night, everyone was in high spirits, sharing gossip and drinking to their hearts’ content. In the end, Qin Xian carried Ji Fei back to their room to rest.","Suddenly, Ji Fei stirred in his arms, as if trying to wake up.","“What’s wrong? Are you feeling unwell?” Qin Xian asked, helping her lie down.","Ji Fei frowned and mumbled, “Where... are we sleeping?”","Qin Xian paused. “The new building.”","Ji Fei’s eyes were still closed, her brow furrowed as if deep in thought. After a moment, she relaxed. “Is this your first time staying here too?”","Qin Xian hesitated, his eyes softening. “Yes, it’s my first time.”","They were staying in the newly built modern villa on the estate, not the main house.","In truth, only the old master and Grandma Lü lived here permanently, so there was no need for additional buildings. But they had insisted on building it, hoping that one day Qin Xian would visit and wanting to spare him any discomfort by avoiding the old house where he had stayed as a child.","Although Qin Xian didn't say anything outwardly, he was deeply moved inside. The fact that Ji Fei, even while drunk, could still think of him made his heart flutter.","Just as he was about to lean in to kiss Ji Fei, she suddenly lifted her head, accidentally bumping into Qin Xian's forehead.","Qin Xian sighed helplessly and reached up to gently rub Ji Fei's forehead. Then, he heard her mumble, \"Hmm, I need to take a bath... Husband, I can't move. Help me wash.\"","Qin Xian: !"]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: I still haven't seen all of him yet","paragraphs":["Even though their relationship had made significant progress, helping each other bathe was a level of intimacy that was too high, especially when Ji Fei wasn't fully conscious. Qin Xian felt it was inappropriate.","So, Qin Xian took out his phone and contacted his sisters, hoping they could come over to help.","Almost simultaneously, the two sisters vented their frustrations in the family group chat, which didn't include Qin Xian and Ji Fei: \"Family, can you believe it? Qin Xian actually asked me to come over and help bathe his wife!\"","Qin's Father: \"Pathetic!\"","Qin's Mom: \"How did I raise such a son!\"","Qin Zhao: \"Are you sure it's not that Ji Fei deliberately gave Qin Xian an opportunity? You guys better not go.\"","And so, the two sisters pretended not to see the messages and didn't reply at all.","After waiting for a long time with no response, Ji Fei, who was lying on the bed, grew increasingly frustrated. After a day of fun, her body felt sticky and uncomfortable. With no one to help her, she decided to undress herself.","By the time Qin Xian gave up on contacting anyone and decided to simply wipe Ji Fei down to get through the night, he turned around and froze.","The moonlight streamed through the window, illuminating the soft bed and Ji Fei's fair, delicate skin. Her beautiful, unclothed body was trying to sit up.","Qin Xian's brain short-circuited for a few seconds, unsure where to look, until he saw Ji Fei losing her balance and about to fall. Panicked, he rushed forward and caught her in his arms.","In that moment, Qin Xian felt a sudden warmth in his nose. Before he could think further, Ji Fei struggled in his arms, muttering, \"I need a bath! I need a bath! I'm so uncomfortable!\"","Qin Xian was at a loss, feeling his entire body heat up. At this point, he could only try to remain calm and carry her to the bathroom.","However, as soon as they entered the bathroom, he caught a glimpse of his disheveled self in the mirror.","His face was flushed, and to his shock, he noticed blood trickling from his nose. His body had also reacted the moment he saw his wife.","To make matters worse, Ji Fei, still in his arms, was restless and unbearably teasing during the bath.","In the end, Qin Xian, being only human, couldn't resist any longer. He pressed her against the cool bathroom wall and kissed her passionately.","When Ji Fei woke up, it was already midday. Her hangover headache was torturous, but her body felt clean and comfortable. She got up and noticed Qin Xian wasn't there. Checking her phone, she saw a message from him: his grandfather had called him over for a talk. He asked her to contact him once she woke up so he could pick her up.","Ji Fei couldn't help but laugh to herself. Was she a child who needed to be picked up and dropped off?","As she got up, her silky nightgown fell smoothly. For a moment, Ji Fei felt like she had forgotten something. When she went to the bathroom to freshen up, toothbrush in mouth, she glanced around and saw the bathroom next door. Suddenly, memories of the previous night came flooding back.","In an instant, Ji Fei felt her entire body burn with embarrassment.","Last night, they had been in there... in there...","The passionate kiss wasn't the main point; what mattered was that Qin Xian, unable to control himself, had kissed her while dealing with his own reaction.","His low, heavy breathing had drowned out the sound of the shower, and Ji Fei, still drunk and dazed, hadn't reacted at the time. But now, recalling it, her face turned crimson.","Her mind seemed to automatically piece together the sensual scene from the bathroom, leaving her both excited and deeply embarrassed, her thoughts filled with wild imaginings.","So, when Qin Xian walked into the room, he heard Ji Fei's inner voice screaming:","\"Damn it! Is he really not into me? I was standing there naked, and after all that, he still took care of himself. Don't I have any dignity?!\"","Qin Xian: \"...\" He had initially thought his actions were disrespectful to Ji Fei and had deeply reflected on them after sobering up.","When Ji Fei heard movement, Qin Xian was already standing behind her. She turned around and met his shy yet tender gaze, instantly silencing her bold thoughts.","However, her eyes still showed dissatisfaction, especially when she noticed Qin Xian was fully dressed in casual summer attire, leaving no room for any \"peeks.\"","\"This is unfair. He's seen me naked, but I haven't seen him yet!\"","The more Ji Fei thought about it, the more curious she became. Her gaze drifted downward, causing Qin Xian to stiffen.","\"It must be... big, right?\"","Qin Xian: \"!!!! What is she thinking?!!!!\"","Well... it seemed only she could think such thoughts legally and appropriately.","Qin Xian felt like he was about to combust and tried to change the subject.","But before he could speak, he heard Ji Fei's inner voice, as if she had made a firm decision.","\"I'll find a way to get him drunk, strip him while he's helpless, and then give him a bath while having my way with him. Hehehe...\"","Qin Xian's throat went dry. He couldn't speak, his head slowly lowering as he subconsciously calculated... how many drinks it would take for him to get drunk.","Neither of them brought up what happened the previous night, each harboring their own little secrets.","When it came time to get dressed, Ji Fei felt a bit shy, realizing that Qin Xian had helped her put on her underwear earlier.","She thought that was the end of it, but when she went downstairs and met the other young members of the Qin Family, she noticed Qin Yan, Qin Zhao, and Qin Rong looking at her with knowing smiles. Later, during the family meal at the old house, even Qin's Father and Qin's Mom were subtly glancing at them.","Initially, Ji Fei felt a bit embarrassed for sleeping in, but she soon realized that the elders were looking at them with teasing expressions.","Ji Fei grew suspicious and couldn't help but whisper to Qin Xian, \"Is there some gossip I don't know about?\"","Qin Xian, of course, knew what they were referring to. He had already been subjected to various sarcastic remarks from the family that morning. He wasn't sure what his parents or grandfather had said, but everyone seemed to be looking at him with a sense of pride.","Faced with Ji Fei's question, Qin Xian honestly explained how he had initially asked his sisters for help.","Ji Fei immediately gave him a disapproving look.","\"Is he really that concerned about my reputation? Does he want to divorce me or something?\"","At the dining table, all the adults in the Qin Family suddenly started coughing at the same time, no matter what they were eating or drinking.","The others looked at them strangely, wondering how the entire family could choke in unison.","Qin Xian's expression froze, and he quickly tried to dispel Ji Fei's doubts. Under the table, he took her hand and leaned in to whisper, \"You were drunk and uncomfortable. I was afraid... afraid I wouldn't be able to control myself, and you'd suffer...\"","His words instantly made Ji Fei's ears burn, and she was immediately soothed.","\"Hehe, I knew it. He said he likes me!\"","Qin Xian's gaze softened, his eyes practically radiating how much he adored Ji Fei.","Watching the two of them being affectionate, the rest of the table was showered with metaphorical dog food. The relatives who had initially been unsure about the couple now felt reassured.","No matter how their relationship had started, at least now they were deeply in love.","Without any spoilsports around, the lunch was even more enjoyable. In the afternoon, the family planned to take the newcomers out for some fun.","However, halfway through, Qin Yi received a phone call.","His expression instantly changed, and his gaze shifted toward Yang Weiwei, who was taking photos with everyone in the distance.","At that moment, only Qin Xian was sitting beside Qin Yi, as if the two of them were the adults supervising a group of children. Qin Xian was checking messages on his phone from his subordinates. The day before, he had issued several investigation orders, and the first one to be completed was the investigation into Yang Feng's infidelity. He had just received a pile of evidence.","Noticing his cousin's troubled expression, Qin Xian asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Qin Yi stood up in a panic and said, \"Yang Feng had an accident during an inspection. He's in critical condition and undergoing emergency treatment!\""]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: Should Yang Feng Divorce Qin Wenqiang Right Now","paragraphs":["As relatives, a large group of people rushed to the hospital without hesitation.","Ji Fei sat in the car, her brows furrowed.","[Is this karma? Before I could expose him as a scumbag, something happened to him first. Let me see... He was hit by a heavy object while inspecting the construction site... This project was the one he previously proposed to Qin Xian. No wonder Qin Xian wasn’t optimistic about it. The location is poor, and the construction is challenging. Without a top-tier team, it’s hard to pull off. And the teams capable of handling such projects are already booked for other jobs. So, starting this project anytime soon is unrealistic. Yet, Yang Feng just kept pushing Qin Corporation to invest more money, while he half-heartedly assembled a team. Now look, before the project even started, he’s the first to suffer due to poor site preparation.]","The Qin family, including Qin Yi and his siblings, overheard these thoughts and couldn’t help but frown. The situation was a mess, but it was his own doing, and he had no one else to blame.","When they arrived at the hospital, they saw an elderly couple giving Qin Wenqiang a hard time. Yang Weiwei, who had already heard about her father’s accident, saw her mother being scolded and rushed over. “Grandpa! Grandma!”","The elderly couple showed no warmth upon seeing their granddaughter. Still consumed by grief, they continued to berate Qin Wenqiang.","“It’s all your fault! If you hadn’t dragged your feet and refused to ask Qin Corporation to invest in the project, my son wouldn’t have gone to the construction site today to try and figure things out. You’re the reason this happened! Our Yang Family has only one heir. If something happens to him, I won’t survive either, and you’ll have to pay for it! Waaah!” Grandma Yang wailed, her curses filled with despair.","Grandpa Yang, though silent, glared at Qin Wenqiang with red, resentful eyes.","If it weren’t for Ji Fei’s earlier thoughts, the Qin family might have believed the elderly couple’s accusations. But now, at least the Qin family saw them as unreasonable and just looking for someone to blame.","Qin Yi immediately stepped forward to support Qin Wenqiang, who was barely standing. Seeing his sister in such distress, he felt deeply pained. He addressed the elderly couple firmly, “I understand you’re worried about your son-in-law, but my sister is just as worried. No one wanted this to happen, but you can’t blame her for it!”","The couple was about to lash out again when they heard the sound of approaching footsteps. Turning around, they saw a large group of people walking toward them.","“You should sit down and wait for news. If you keep causing a scene, the hospital might ask you to leave,” Qin Zhao said, raising an eyebrow.","“This hospital has investments from Qin Corporation. If you keep harassing my cousin, it won’t help her handle things for your son-in-law,” Qin Jing added.","“Oh dear, there are children here. You should watch your language,” Qin Xiaoyu said bluntly, clearly displeased with the elderly couple.","The others didn’t need to say much. Their collective support for Qin Wenqiang was palpable, and the elderly couple felt outnumbered. They finally backed down, no longer daring to make a scene.","With no one pulling at her, and with her family by her side, Qin Wenqiang quickly gathered herself and began asking around for updates. Even though she knew she had to wait for the surgery results, she still wanted to know more.","Soon, the surgery ended. There was no miracle. The doctor came out, shaking his head, indicating that they had done all they could but couldn’t save him. The family was told to go in and say their goodbyes, as there wasn’t much time left.","The hallway was immediately filled with wails of grief.","Even Ji Fei and the others, who hadn’t thought highly of Yang Feng, felt a pang of sorrow upon hearing that someone was about to die.","They didn’t enter the hospital room, choosing to wait outside instead.","The twins were instructed to fetch their aunt and uncle-in-law, as they were also Yang Feng’s in-laws and should be there to bid him farewell.","Soon, relatives from the Yang Family arrived as well.","With the hallway now crowded, Qin Xian suggested that Qin Zhao and Qin Rong stay to keep an eye on things while he took Ji Fei out for some fresh air. Qin Yan naturally followed, bringing Qin Xi along.","Qin Xi was still holding Yang Weiwei’s bag, her expression filled with sorrow.","In the hospital garden, many patients and their families were taking walks. Qin Yan found a bench for herself and Qin Xi to sit on, while Ji Fei, feeling restless, began pacing. Qin Xian walked alongside her.","Ji Fei was lost in thought. [He’s about to die. When should I tell my cousin about his affair? If I say something, will she blame me? What if she’d rather remember him as a loyal husband? But if it were me, I wouldn’t want to be deceived! Ugh, this is so frustrating. Maybe I should hint at Qin Xian to investigate. Then he can share this burden with me. After all, we’re married, and she’s his cousin!]","Qin Xian, not wanting his wife to worry, spoke up. “There’s something I need to tell you...”","Ji Fei looked up, startled, only to see Qin Xian frowning as he glanced toward a bench not far away.","On the bench, a beautiful woman was crying, holding her daughter. Three sons, their eyes red, surrounded her. A man stood nearby, pacing back and forth. “Sis, shouldn’t we go up? He’s about to die. If we don’t go now, who knows what will happen!”","“I want to go too, but if we expose ourselves now, it might make things worse! It’s all his fault. Why wasn’t he more careful? I told him to prepare everything for us, but he...”","Ji Fei frowned. Something about their conversation felt off.","Qin Xian pulled Ji Fei back a few steps, ensuring their conversation wouldn’t be overheard.","“Feifei, that woman and those children are Yang Feng’s mistress and illegitimate children,” Qin Xian said directly.","Ji Fei’s mind went blank for a moment, her mouth forming a silent “Huh?”","Qin Xian calmly explained, “When Yang Feng came to me about the project, I noticed something odd about his new company’s structure. It seemed like he was secretly profiting behind your cousin’s back. I found it suspicious, so I had someone investigate, and then...”","“You found out he had a mistress and illegitimate children?!” Ji Fei exclaimed, shocked that Qin Xian’s investigative skills were almost as efficient as a system’s.","Qin Xian nodded. “I just received their information today, so I recognized them immediately.”","Ji Fei was now fully alert. “So... what do we do?”","Qin Xian frowned. “We’ll have to tell your cousin, but it’s a matter of timing. If they stay quiet, we’ll wait until she’s through this ordeal. But if they cause trouble, we’ll have to let her know immediately.”","Ji Fei nodded. It made sense not to overwhelm her with too much at once.","“But if they act out, we’ll have to tell her right away, or else...”","Before Ji Fei could process this, the woman’s phone rang. She answered immediately. “Mom, how’s Yang Feng?”","Ji Fei froze. Was she calling Grandma Yang?","“What? You want Yang Feng to divorce Qin Wenqiang right now?!”","Ji Fei and Qin Xian: !!!!!"]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Calculating Divorce Before Death","paragraphs":["What kind of move is it for a dying man to ask for a divorce?","Is this Yang Feng's parents' idea?","Are they going to reveal the affair and the illegitimate child?","Ji Fei and Qin Xian couldn't understand it. Ji Fei was just about to use the Gossip System to investigate.","But the mistress, on the other hand, was getting more and more excited, even showing a smile on her face.","\"Alright, we'll cooperate, absolutely cooperate... but, Mom, do we really not need to see Yang Feng one last time? We really can't bear to part with him, sob...\" Though her smile was barely concealed, she still pretended to be crying.","Finally, she hung up the phone with a sad expression.","\"Sis, what's going on?\" the mistress's younger brother asked anxiously.","The mistress suppressed the curve of her lips, shooed the children away, and then explained to her brother, \"Yang Feng still has a conscience. Before he dies, he wants to arrange things for us. He plans to divorce Qin Wenqiang in his final days and make her leave with nothing.\"","\"What?!\" The brother was stunned. \"How is that possible?\"","Ji Fei and Qin Xian were equally baffled, sharing the same question as the brother.","\"He's about to die, so why not? Qin Wenqiang has not only marital assets but also a lot of pre-marital property. The things she brought from the Qin family can't be touched, but everything else could be left to Yang Feng if she agrees.\"","The brother still found it hard to believe. \"She wouldn't agree to that, would she?\"","\"Yang Feng will team up with his parents to persuade Qin Wenqiang. The divorce is just a legal process to transfer all the assets to Yang Feng. After he dies, the inheritance will go to his parents. This is to reassure them so they won't be left with nothing after their only son passes away.\"","\"With Qin Wenqiang's personality, she'll probably swear to take care of her in-laws until their death, maybe even sign an agreement,\" the brother said doubtfully.","The mistress smirked, \"But Yang Feng said he's worried she might remarry and have children with someone else. She can't guarantee that, can she? Besides, the Qin family is so wealthy. Why would they care about these assets? Leaving everything to the elderly would comfort them. And the old folks promised that after they die, the property will go to their granddaughter. It's just to give them peace of mind in their remaining years.\"","\"Ah? Everything to that little brat?!\" The brother panicked. \"Didn't those old folks hate that kid the most?\"","\"Don't be stupid. It's all an act for the mother and daughter. By saying that, Qin Wenqiang will feel reassured and indulge Yang Feng's last wish. She'll think it's all for her daughter anyway. But once the assets are in the hands of those old folks, how they transfer them to us later is none of her business. Her daughter won't get a single cent. Meanwhile, we can let them take care of the old folks on their deathbeds. Hahaha.\"","The brother finally understood and got excited. \"So we're going to be rich? Wait, what if the Qin family finds out and retaliates?\"","\"We didn't do anything. It's all their plan. After this, we'll just go abroad and wait for the old folks to send us money. We'll live the good life.\" The mistress was getting more and more excited. After all, being a mistress and having to please a man was such a hassle. Now that the man is dying, the good life is finally here.","By now, Ji Fei finally understood what the divorce was all about and was so angry she could spit blood.","Qin Xian, halfway through, had already silently taken out his phone and started recording, as if it were second nature.","The mistress and her brother laughed and called their children to leave the hospital. It was only then that Ji Fei realized the children's earlier tears weren't for their dying father but because they were copying their mother's distress.","Now that they heard everything was fine, that their father's death wouldn't change their lives, and that they could leave the dreary hospital, they started clamoring to go eat somewhere. Their upbringing was truly appalling.","One of the kids even asked, \"But what if Dad's money runs out? If Dad dies, who's going to make money for us?\"","\"Don't worry, that day will never come. But if it does, remember, you still have a sister from the Qin family who can support you. My children are destined to live a pampered life, always taken care of, living the good life.\"","After the mistress finished speaking, the group left the hospital laughing and in high spirits.","Ji Fei's face turned pale with anger. She gritted her teeth and turned to Qin Xian, not knowing where to start.","Qin Xian put away his phone. \"Don't worry. Even if Cousin Qin Wenqiang is tricked into agreeing, it will take time for the lawyers to come. They won't succeed.\"","\"Then let's hurry and tell Big Cousin.\" Ji Fei immediately grabbed Qin Xian's hand and turned to head back to the ward.","But as soon as they turned around, they froze.","Yang Weiwei was standing not far behind them.","She was holding her bag, which Qin Xi had been carrying earlier. It seemed she had come down to retrieve it.","[What a tragedy. Earlier, she had gone out with everyone and bought a gift for Yang Feng, which she had placed in her bag. Now, in these final moments, as they were trying to persuade Qin Wenqiang to divorce, they had sent Yang Weiwei away. She wanted to give her father his last gift, but instead, she overheard...]","The little girl's face was as pale as paper, her eyes bloodshot, but her expression was blank. Tears streamed down her cheeks as she cried silently.","Ji Fei rushed over, and Yang Weiwei seemed to snap out of her daze, suddenly breaking into loud sobs.","Clearly, Yang Weiwei had heard everything.","At just over ten years old, how could she bear such a blow?","No matter how Ji Fei hugged or comforted her, it was no use. Qin Xian, who wasn't good with children, could only stand silently by. Yang Weiwei's wailing was so loud that it attracted Qin Yan and Qin Xi from a distance.","\"I thought you went back?\" Qin Yan asked, shocked. \"What's going on?\"","Qin Xi immediately stepped forward to comfort her little cousin.","But Yang Weiwei turned and rushed into the hospital.","Ji Fei and the others had no choice but to follow.","When they reached the ward, they found Qin Yi waiting outside, frowning. Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were also there, looking puzzled, especially at the sight of Yang Weiwei crying and running.","Qin Yi was about to hug the approaching Yang Weiwei, but she twisted away and burst into the room.","At the same time, voices from inside could be heard.","\"Wenqiang, this is my last request. My parents aren't smart or calm. They don't understand anything. This is the only way to reassure them and let me go in peace. After all, everything will go to Weiwei in the end. Just indulge me this one last time. Call the lawyer. I don't have much time left. You wouldn't want me to die with regrets, would you?\" Yang Feng said weakly.","\"But... this doesn't make sense!\" Qin Wenqiang sobbed in pain.","\"I... *cough cough*... just agree, please! I'm begging you! *cough cough*...\"","\"Don't say that... Alright, I'll agree. I'll call the lawyer now.\" Qin Wenqiang's crying suddenly stopped as Yang Weiwei hugged her. \"Mom, don't!\""]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: Only Widowed, Never Divorced","paragraphs":["The three people who were initially thrilled that Qin Wenqiang had finally agreed to their persuasion were instantly shocked and angered by the sudden interruption. At such a critical moment, the last thing they needed was a disruption.","\"Vivi?\" Qin Wenqiang was already feeling heartbroken. After all, her husband was on the brink of death, and now he wanted a divorce. How could anyone accept such a thing? She could only assume that her husband, in his final moments, was overwhelmed by fear and confusion, swayed by his parents' whispers, and trying to secure a stable future for them.","Although Qin Wenqiang was certain that her morals would never allow her to seize her husband's inheritance, her in-laws didn't trust her and were making a scene, disrupting her husband's final days.","Forget it. In the end, everything would belong to Vivi anyway. If they had to go through this process, she didn't mind. To her and Yang Feng, they were still husband and wife. The so-called divorce was just a legal safeguard for the assets.","Faced with her husband of over ten years making such a request in his final moments, even a strong woman like Qin Wenqiang couldn't help but feel suspicious.","But now...","Seeing her daughter's expression, Qin Wenqiang assumed that Yang Weiwei had accidentally overheard their discussion about divorce and misunderstood. She quickly reassured her, \"Vivi, don't cry. Your dad and I aren't really getting a divorce. We're still your loving parents.\"","Yang Feng, struggling to speak, added, \"Vivi, don't be stubborn. This is something your mom and I have agreed on. Don't waste any more time.\"","But Yang Weiwei was trembling uncontrollably, almost speechless. She turned to look at the frail man on the hospital bed, who could barely speak yet was using his final moments to scheme against her and her mother, paving the way for his mistress and illegitimate children.","Having grown up in a wealthy family, Yang Weiwei had seen more than most people her age.","Moreover, the adults had already laid out the pros and cons. Even if she didn't fully understand, she knew that if her parents divorced, it would mean she and her mother would be at the mercy of those who wished them harm.","\"I don't agree! Dad, are you really going to divorce Mom and leave her with nothing?\" Yang Weiwei cried, tears streaming down her face as she looked at Yang Feng.","For a moment, Yang Feng felt a pang of guilt under his daughter's gaze.","But then he thought about his other four children. At least Yang Weiwei still had Qin Wenqiang. He had to secure a future for the others.","\"Dad! Are you really going to give everything to someone else?\" Yang Weiwei shouted.","Those with ill intentions are naturally more sensitive. Yang Feng's parents were immediately provoked. \"Your dad is about to die. Isn't it natural for him to think about us, his parents? How are we 'someone else'? How can you be so cold-hearted at such a young age? Are you so afraid of losing your money? Do you even care about your dad and us?\"","Ji Fei, who had just arrived at the door, couldn't help but curse inwardly.","[Isn't it you two old fools who are afraid of someone taking your money? It's you three who don't care about Yang Weiwei, you heartless beasts! How are you still breathing?]","The other members of the Qin family were also at the door, stunned by Ji Fei's harsh thoughts. After all, Ji Fei rarely showed such ferocity.","What had the Yang family done to provoke Ji Fei like this? It seemed like Ji Fei had developed a deep hatred for them. They remembered Ji Fei mentioning Yang Feng's affair and illegitimate children before. Could it be related to that?","Qin Yi was still somewhat confused. Seeing them berate Yang Weiwei, he immediately spoke up, \"What are you talking about? How could Vivi mean that? You're the ones thinking about inheritance before your son is even dead. Don't assume everyone is as greedy as you!\"","The two elders turned pale with anger, but seeing their son on the verge of death, they were both heartbroken and desperate. They channeled all their grief and rage into their words, fearing that if the agreement wasn't signed in time, they would be at the mercy of others. They turned to Qin Wenqiang and wailed, \"Hurry up and arrange it! Do you really want our son to die with regrets?\"","With that, the two elders broke down in tears. This wasn't an act; their only son was dying, and those present who didn't know the full story couldn't bring themselves to say anything more.","Yang Weiwei, still a child, was overwhelmed by the situation. She stood there in stunned silence, unable to comprehend why her father and grandparents would treat her and her mother this way. Was it because they weren't good enough?","Qin Wenqiang closed her eyes, wiped away her tears, and picked up her phone to call a lawyer, urging them to come as quickly as possible.","Qin Yi wanted to say something but decided against it, feeling it was his sister's decision to make.","Finally, the two elders rushed to their son's bedside, clutching his hands and weeping. Yang Feng also seemed to relax slightly, now fully confronting the reality of his impending death, and he too was overcome with grief.","Ji Fei couldn't hold back any longer and stepped forward, ready to speak, but Qin Xian stopped her and said, \"Cousin, Aunt and Uncle are here. Come out for a moment.\"","Qin Yi initially wanted to go greet them but caught Qin Xian's glance and hesitated.","Qin Wenqiang was mentally exhausted and didn't think much of it. As she turned to leave, she noticed her daughter still standing there in a daze. She decided to explain the situation to her parents and clear things up for her daughter to avoid any lasting psychological damage.","So the Qin family members left the room.","But once outside, there was no sign of anyone else.","Qin Wenqiang looked at Qin Xian in confusion, but he simply opened the door to an empty room nearby and gestured for her to enter.","Qin Yi and the other Qin siblings wanted to follow, but Qin Xian shut the door behind them.","Inside the empty room, Qin Wenqiang and Yang Weiwei were puzzled.","Without wasting words, Qin Xian handed his phone to Qin Wenqiang, indicating for her to watch.","\"It's not complete, but I think you'll understand what's going on,\" Qin Xian said calmly.","Qin Wenqiang took the phone and pressed play. The people in the video were strangers, but as the conversation unfolded, the color drained from her face, and her eyes turned from sorrowful to furious.","She trembled as she listened to the final part of the conversation, where they shamelessly talked about how they could still rely on Yang Weiwei, their half-sister, in the future. Overwhelmed, she stumbled backward.","Ji Fei quickly caught her.","\"Mom! Mom!\" Yang Weiwei, who had regained her composure while watching the video, cried even harder seeing her mother like this.","\"This isn't real, right? Tell me it's not!\" Even the strongest woman would struggle to accept being deceived so thoroughly.","But the response didn't come from Qin Xian or Ji Fei.","Yang Weiwei sobbed, \"Mom, it's true. I saw it with my own eyes. They're Dad's... He's not my dad; he's their dad. He only loves them, not me! Mom, I tried to stop you. I didn't want to give them anything. Why should they get what you worked so hard for? Why?\"","[What a tragedy. The so-called inheritance was built on the foundation of Qin Corporation, primarily through Qin Wenqiang's efforts. Yang Feng was just a high-level employee. His parents already have more than enough. How greedy can they be, trying to steal everything Qin Wenqiang worked for and hand it over to his mistress and illegitimate children, leaving nothing for his own daughter? The audacity is beyond belief.]","Outside the door, the Qin family couldn't hear the conversation clearly, but they could make out Ji Fei's thoughts. They were stunned and glanced at Qin Yi.","Qin Yi wasn't one to eavesdrop, but seeing their expressions, he couldn't help but ask, \"What did you hear?\"","The three exchanged glances, not daring to say much. They understood why Qin Xian had taken Qin Wenqiang aside.","As the saying goes, even the wisest judge struggles to settle family disputes. The best they could do was reveal the truth when a loved one was being manipulated, and then let them decide. After all, there are those who, out of pity for the dying, might choose to play the fool, unwilling to face the truth and preferring to deceive themselves for the sake of appearances.","So, before their cousin made a decision, it was best for them to pretend they knew nothing.","Yang Weiwei was inside the room, expressing her emotional breakdown incoherently, looking truly pitiful.","Qin Wenqiang finally understood why Yang Weiwei had acted so strangely earlier in the hospital room.","Perhaps it was the strength of a mother—after being forced to accept reality, Qin Wenqiang looked at her distraught daughter, gritted her teeth, and held her tightly.","\"Weiwei, don’t be afraid. Weiwei, Mom is here! I won’t let anyone... anyone hurt you! Yang Feng, you beast, you monster!\"","Hearing Qin Wenqiang’s words, Qin Xian and Ji Fei breathed a sigh of relief.","Qin Xian said, \"Cousin, before the lawyer arrives, make your decision as soon as possible. If there’s anything you need help with, just let us know.\"","Though tears welled in Qin Wenqiang’s eyes, they now gleamed with a sharp, determined light.","When the hospital room door opened again, the three members of the Yang family inside saw Qin Wenqiang return. Perhaps out of some lingering shred of conscience, Yang Feng even tried to pull his wife and daughter aside to talk.","\"I’ve wronged you. If there’s a next life, I’ll make it up to you.\"","Qin Wenqiang walked up to Yang Feng and let out a light chuckle. \"Oh? I don’t pray for the next life. I only care about this one.\"","Just as Yang Feng was moved and about to say more, Qin Wenqiang added, \"Oh, by the way, I told the lawyer not to come. I’ve thought about it—when I married you, Qin Wenqiang, I made a vow. I promised to stand by you through thick and thin. In this life, there’s only death that parts us, never divorce.\""]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: Only the Two of You Can Compete with Cousin and Vivi for the Inheritance","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Yang Feng's parents immediately became anxious. This was something their son had fought for with his life—how could they just go back on their word like that?","\"Is it because your parents don't agree? My son is about to die! How can you people from wealthy families be so petty and calculating?\"","\"Call your parents in here! I want to see how they can even bring themselves to speak!\"","The two of them looked ferocious, their ugly behavior on full display as they jumped around in agitation.","The others who had followed them in looked on with disgust.","Qin Yi was the most confused among them. He held Yang Weiwei's hand as she kept her head down in silence, completely unable to understand his sister's actions.","Although he also thought the idea of divorce was absurd, he knew Qin Wenqiang wasn't someone who acted on impulse or made promises lightly.","Moreover, Qin Wenqiang didn't care about those assets at all. Since she had agreed, why would she suddenly change her mind?","Qin Yi glanced back at the members of Qin Second's family and saw that they all had expressions of anticipation, as if waiting for a show to unfold. This only added to his confusion.","Meanwhile, Yang Feng, who had been stunned by Qin Wenqiang's words, gradually began to sense that something was wrong. After all, he had been married to Qin Wenqiang for many years, and he could tell whether she was angry or grieving.","But Qin Wenqiang wasn't just angry now—she was furious, her gaze so intense it seemed as if she wished him dead.","Yang Feng's lips began to tremble. He was already at the end of his strength, barely able to speak, but he still managed to ask, \"Wife, what's... what's wrong? Why all of a sudden... You know me, I never really wanted to divorce you, I just...\"","\"You know me? After all these years of marriage, you know me...\" Qin Wenqiang murmured, then suddenly bent down, leaning close to the patient on the hospital bed. In a voice filled with cold determination, she said, \"I know you. You're a good husband, a good father. So, everything we've worked for together will ultimately belong to our daughter, right?\"","\"You... you woman! All you care about is money!\" Yang Feng's parents continued to curse, but no one paid them any attention.","When they tried to approach Qin Wenqiang, Qin Xian and Qin Chaohui immediately stepped in front of them, blocking their path to their sister-in-law.","The two men, clearly from a prestigious background, exuded an intimidating aura that made the older couple hesitate, leaving them to desperately shout at Yang Feng instead.","But Yang Feng seemed to have stopped hearing them.","A dying man was already hanging on by a thread, waiting for his plans to succeed. Now, it seemed he realized that his schemes might never come to fruition.","And so, that last thread was about to snap.","\"Wife, that's my hard work too. You can't... you can't just...\"","Qin Wenqiang looked at Yang Feng's hypocritical, pitiful face and smiled. \"Since you dared to do it, why can't I? You married a daughter of the Qin Family. How could I let some stray cats and dogs take advantage of my daughter? You really underestimated me.\"","Yang Feng's face was already pale with the pallor of death. In what seemed like a final burst of energy, his eyes widened—whether to curse, beg for forgiveness, or continue his act of playing the victim, no one could tell.","But Qin Wenqiang didn't give him the chance to speak. \"Shh, be quiet. Watch from above and see how I'll make all your plans come to nothing.\"","As soon as she said this, the room fell silent.","Yang Feng's parents seemed to finally understand what was happening. The mask had been torn off—had everything been exposed?","\"Wenqiang...\" Yang Feng's parents were now panicking, trying to say something, but the monitors connected to Yang Feng's body began to sound alarms.","In an instant, the room was filled with noise and chaos. Qin Wenqiang coldly stepped back, turned, and went to embrace her daughter, leaving Yang Feng's parents to collapse by his bedside, wailing.","Yang Weiwei didn't look at the hospital bed; she just cried quietly.","Gradually, everything faded to nothing.","Qin Yi looked at his deceased brother-in-law, unable to feel grief. His expression was grim. \"What do you mean? From what you just said, did Yang Feng... did he do something to betray you?\"","Qin Wenqiang's face was icy, her gaze fixed on her late husband. Finally, she was a widow.","She let out a bitter laugh and leaned in to whisper in Qin Yi's ear, \"Go, help me find the hospital director. It's time to take care of things.\"","Qin Yi's eyes widened as he listened to Qin Wenqiang's instructions.","The members of Qin Second's family couldn't hear what the siblings were saying, but they had their own source of gossip—Ji Fei.","[Quick, ruthless, decisive—Big Sister is amazing! She's going straight for cremation and a funeral in one go!]","The three siblings from Qin Second's family were shocked.","Qin Xian, however, wasn't surprised. After all, delays could lead to complications, and Big Sister was always one to consider such things.","So when the twins from Fourth Uncle Qin's family arrived with Auntie and Eldest Uncle, they saw hospital staff preparing to wheel away a body covered with a white sheet, while Yang Feng's parents were making a scene, trying to stop them.","Yang Feng's parents didn't actually understand Qin Wenqiang's intentions—they just couldn't bear to let their son go without a proper farewell. Now that everything had been exposed, they thought their grandchildren should at least come to say goodbye to their father.","But Qin Wenqiang didn't give them the chance. She coldly called in bodyguards to clear the way, and by the time Auntie and Eldest Uncle realized what was happening, the body had already been taken away.","\"What on earth is going on...?\" Auntie asked anxiously, feeling that everything was strange.","Eldest Uncle, on the other hand, was more concerned about his daughter and granddaughter's emotional state.","When Qin Wenqiang saw her parents, she finally let her guard down and broke down in tears, telling them about the injustices she and Weiwei had suffered.","[Sigh. Back then, Qin Wenqiang had agreed to Yang Feng's pursuit partly because of her parents' relationship. Eldest Uncle had married into the Qin Family, but the couple had always supported each other, never letting the fact that the wife was more successful cause any friction. So Qin Wenqiang thought she could also find happiness by marrying someone of a lower status. But reality had slapped her hard in the face.]","Qin Yan and Qin Rong could relate deeply. Like Qin Wenqiang, they had been too sheltered by the Qin Family, growing up surrounded by harmonious relationships among their elders. They had never thought there was anything wrong with marrying men who were less accomplished than themselves. At first, they had believed that true love could overcome any obstacle.","But now, they had to admit that the likelihood of a woman being unhappy in a marriage where she \"married down\" was far higher than in a marriage of equals.","So they couldn't use Eldest Uncle as an exception to prove the rule.","After hearing Qin Wenqiang's story, Auntie and Eldest Uncle were so angry their blood pressure spiked. If Yang Feng hadn't already been dead, they would have lunged at him and torn apart the scoundrel who had deceived their daughter for so many years.","How dare he try to use their daughter's hard-earned money to support a mistress and illegitimate child! The nerve!","\"Did you know all along that your son was having an affair and raising a love child? Was it all because you wanted a grandson?\" The usually mild-mannered Eldest Uncle pointed at Yang Feng's parents and shouted, \"I always knew you were no good! The apple doesn't fall far from the tree!\"","\"Hmph! We've tolerated your Yang Family relatives leeching off the Qin Family for long enough, but to dare betray my daughter? You really have no sense of shame!\" Auntie scolded.","Now that the mask was off, the two troublemakers decided to go all out.","\"So what if we did? Your daughter couldn't give us a grandson. Were we supposed to let the Yang Family line die out just because we married into your family? If your daughter wouldn't give us a grandson, we had to find a way ourselves! In the end, it's your daughter who failed Yang Feng. We could have had him divorce her, but we were kind enough not to!\"","\"And what about your daughter? My son's last request, and she wouldn't even grant it. She watched him die without lifting a finger. She's a heartless viper! But it doesn't matter. It's my son's inheritance, and even if we can't take all of it, we'll still get the lion's share!\"","[Holy crap, these two old geezers are shameless! But they probably don't know that Yang Feng is already ashes. The only ones left to fight Big Sister and Weiwei over the inheritance are the two of you.]"]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: Is There a Paternity Test","paragraphs":["Qin Xian heard Ji Fei's muttering and couldn't help but smile. That's exactly how it was.","The second branch of the Qin family seemed to have realized what Qin Wenqiang had done.","However, Qin Wenqiang didn’t reveal anything to avoid alerting anyone. Instead, she simply took her family and left that unlucky place.","After all, Yang Feng was now just a handful of ashes, and he didn’t deserve Qin Wenqiang to handle his funeral arrangements.","Without Qin Wenqiang, there were still the mistress and illegitimate children. When they found out they couldn’t inherit all the assets, they were resentful but had no choice. They could only put on a show, coaxing the elderly couple to arrange Yang Feng’s funeral in hopes of gaining more benefits.","They also took the opportunity to make an appearance in front of Yang’s relatives, proving the existence of herself and her children, so that when the lawyer came to divide the estate, it would save them some trouble.","A pair of domineering elders and a mistress who rose to power through her beauty—none of them seemed to realize the legal issues at hand.","Some of Yang’s relatives had already noticed the problem, but because these people’s behavior was so disgusting and they were so guarded against anyone trying to claim a share of the inheritance, no one was willing to remind them.","Not that it would have made a difference anyway.","On the day of the funeral, many people showed up.","Yang Feng had been a figure of some standing in Y City’s business circles, so naturally, his business associates came to pay their respects.","But as soon as they arrived, they were shocked to see the mistress and a group of illegitimate children. They truly hadn’t expected Yang Feng to be so bold. The oldest illegitimate child seemed only slightly younger than his legitimate child.","To make matters worse, the mistress acted like the lady of the house, greeting them with such grace that it made them extremely uncomfortable. Weren’t they just setting themselves up to offend the Qin family?","But since they were already there, they had no choice but to grit their teeth and enter.","Once inside, they didn’t even need to ask. Yang Feng’s parents put on a dramatic performance, condemning Qin Wenqiang for neglecting her duties as a wife. They claimed she hadn’t lifted a finger to prepare her husband’s funeral, leaving it all to the kind, gentle, and filial ‘mistress.’","They also accused Yang Weiwei of being unfilial, saying she hadn’t shown any concern for her father’s death, unlike the four younger children who had stayed by his side, crying every day.","In short, they spared no effort in painting Qin Wenqiang and her daughter as heartless, while praising the mistress and her children for their dedication.","But who cared? They were businesspeople. Would sympathizing with the mistress and illegitimate children improve their future business prospects? Don’t be ridiculous. This was the Qin family they were dealing with—no one dared to cross them.","They guessed that Qin Wenqiang and her daughter must have discovered Yang Feng’s long-hidden misdeeds and left in anger.","During the days leading up to the funeral, Qin Wenqiang hadn’t shown her face at all. It wasn’t until now that she arrived with her daughter, Yang Weiwei, flanked by a group of bodyguards, given the number of troublemakers present.","The Qin family had already been briefed on the situation, so none of their relatives attended the funeral. They had assumed only Qin Yi would accompany his sister.","But when they saw a group of young people arrive and stand at the entrance, watching without paying their respects, the Yang relatives were confused.","They probably never expected people to come to a funeral just to watch the drama unfold.","Because of this strange turn of events, the other guests became curious as well. What was supposed to be a solemn funeral quickly turned into a spectacle.","[Wow, the mistress and illegitimate children are all here. Are they really this bold? Coming here was definitely the right decision—there’s quite a show to watch!]","Except for Qin’s parents, who stayed at the old house with Qin Xi, everyone else had come.","The twins from Fourth Uncle Qin’s family had tagged along on their own—they loved a good drama.","As for Qin Jiaxi, she had been dragged along by the others and was still a bit dazed. This was her first time experiencing such a conflict. She had thought her cousin would choose to let bygones be bygones, but instead, she had arrived with such a dramatic entrance.","For some reason, Qin Jiaxi felt a strange warmth in her heart.","By now, the funeral hall was buzzing with activity.","Qin Wenqiang faced the mistress for the first time.","The mistress put on a pitiful act, ignoring Qin Wenqiang and instead pulling her four children forward to address Yang Weiwei: “Weiwei, hello. Come meet your younger siblings. This is your first time meeting them, but from now on, you’ll only have each other. You must support one another...”","Before the mistress could finish, Yang Weiwei, who had already had a heart-to-heart with her mother, coldly retorted, “Auntie, what are you talking about? I’m an only child. Where would I have younger siblings?”","[Pfft! I was worried Yang Weiwei might be overwhelmed by seeing these people, but she’s already become a carbon copy of her mother. Betrayal truly forces women to evolve. Even the father-daughter relationship has had a significant impact. Poor little Weiwei, carrying burdens far beyond her age. I really feel like scattering Yang Feng’s ashes to the wind.]","The title “Auntie” elicited several stifled laughs from the crowd, turning the mistress’s face green with anger. But she couldn’t lash out, so she turned to Qin Wenqiang with a pleading expression. “Sister Qin, it’s all my fault, but the children are innocent. They’re the closest family you have. You should explain this to Weiwei. Yang Feng always hoped the children could support each other. After all, they share the same blood...”","Before she could finish, the slap arrived—better late than never.","Two resounding slaps echoed through the funeral hall, sending the mistress sprawling to the ground. The crowd gasped, and the illegitimate children began screaming.","The oldest boy rushed at Qin Wenqiang, but Yang Weiwei, who had been itching for a fight, swung her arm and delivered a solid slap to his face.","When the others tried to make a scene, the bodyguards stepped forward, intimidating them into silence. All that remained were cries and curses.","“Hmph! You became a mistress—didn’t you expect to get slapped? What are you crying about?” Qin Wenqiang sneered at the mistress. “And who told you to call me ‘sister’? Are your brains still stuck in ancient times, dreaming of being a concubine?”","[No, no, no. At best, she’s a kept woman—not even a concubine.]","The Qin family wanted to laugh but maintained their composure, quietly enjoying the drama.","“Qin Wenqiang, are you really going to cause a scene here? Don’t you want my son to rest in peace?” Grandma Yang exclaimed in agitation.","“Why should I wish for him to rest in peace? Does he deserve it?” Qin Wenqiang shot back.","Grandpa Yang then turned to Yang Weiwei. “Weiwei, don’t let your mother brainwash you. They really are your younger siblings. You have to acknowledge them.”","Yang Weiwei’s gaze toward her grandparents grew increasingly filled with hatred. She had already heard from the family lawyer that legitimate children had a legal obligation to support their illegitimate siblings.","The thought that her grandparents were only bringing this up now made her sick to her stomach.","“I said I don’t have any younger siblings. If you say they are, where’s the proof?” Yang Weiwei demanded.","This left the legally ignorant crowd momentarily stunned. Proof? What kind of proof could there be?","At that moment, the lawyer responsible for dividing the estate arrived.","Qin Wenqiang smiled coldly. “Weiwei, Yang Feng’s parents, and I are legally entitled to participate in the estate division. But anyone else who wants a share will need to provide evidence... Oh, right, evidence. It’s not enough to just say it. You claim these children are Weiwei’s siblings, meaning they’re Yang Feng’s children. So... do you have a paternity test?”"]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: The money spent on others hasn't been recovered yet","paragraphs":["Qin Wenqiang's statement plunged the entire room into dead silence.","It seemed that the mistress finally realized something was amiss. No longer feigning fragility, with tears still streaking her face, she rushed to the lawyer and demanded, \"Lawyer, you're Yang Feng's lawyer, right? You know these are Yang Feng's children, don’t you? They have every right to participate in the inheritance division, don’t they? You can’t break the law just because you’re afraid of the Qin family!\"","The lawyer, sweating profusely, replied, \"Madam, we naturally follow the law. But if what Ms. Qin says is true, and these children haven’t undergone paternity tests with Mr. Yang Feng, then they cannot participate in the inheritance division.\"","[Oh, so this lawyer has met the mistress before. In the past, Yang Feng often had this lawyer handle properties and finances for the mistress and his illegitimate children. However, due to confidentiality principles, the lawyer never informed Qin Wenqiang. Similarly, he wouldn’t help the mistress break the law now—he’s just following the rules.]","The Qin family, particularly Qin’s second uncle, finally understood why the mistress had been so confident earlier. She must have thought the lawyer was on her side, but in reality, he was just doing his job.","Meanwhile, the twins, though unable to hear Ji Fei’s inner thoughts, were excitedly discussing the situation.","\"Big Cousin is amazing! She stayed so calm and made such quick, decisive moves—total annihilation!\" Qin Xiaoyu exclaimed.","\"It’s too bad Yang Feng died so quickly. If there had been more time, Big Cousin would have divorced him and left him with nothing. Now, she has to split the assets with those two old folks. It’s so gross,\" Qin Jing chimed in.","Qin Jiaxi, who had been quiet all this time, couldn’t help but reflect on the situation. The more she thought about it, the more she admired her cousin.","Back then, Big Cousin had agreed to an immediate divorce and leaving with nothing because she was willing to cooperate. But what if the situation had been reversed?","If Big Cousin had gathered evidence of her husband’s infidelity and demanded he leave with nothing, Yang Feng would never have agreed. Since he couldn’t take her to court anymore, he would have settled for a legal division of assets. Thus, Big Cousin was destined to be widowed, not divorced.","Once she understood her predicament, Big Cousin began strategizing to secure the maximum benefits for herself and her daughter under the circumstances of widowhood.","Qin Jiaxi found herself wondering, \"Does this... even matter?\"","Though she muttered it softly, almost to herself, those around her still heard it.","\"Of course it matters! It’s satisfying! If someone dares to treat me like a fool, I’ll make them regret it!\" Qin Xiaoyu declared. \"If I’m not happy, no one else gets to be either.\"","\"Love is gone, but why should money go to others? That would be too humiliating,\" Qin Yan added with a smile.","\"Exactly. Love is elusive, true or false, but money is something tangible that belongs to you,\" Qin Rong said earnestly.","Qin Jiaxi was stunned by their words. Is that... really how it is?","Qin Xiaoyu had always been like this, but Qin Yan and Qin Rong used to be different. Qin Xian and Qin Zhao exchanged glances, as if they had just heard Ji Fei speaking.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei was still engrossed in the drama unfolding before her.","Over on the other side, the lawyer’s statement had caused an uproar. Who would have thought to arrange paternity tests from the start? Yang Feng had died so suddenly, leaving no time for such measures.","The mistress’s younger brother’s first reaction was to grab the urn. The absurdity of his actions left everyone speechless.","Yang Feng’s parents didn’t even try to stop him. Instead, they glared at Qin Wenqiang, as if expecting her to make a move.","The lawyer, watching the chaotic scene, couldn’t help but twitch his lips. \"Everyone, there’s no need for this... The ashes can’t be used for testing. In other words, unless Mr. Yang Feng’s body is still intact and samples can be taken for testing, nothing else will hold legal weight.\"","At this, the mistress finally realized what had happened. She turned to Qin Wenqiang, her face a mix of shock and fury. \"You... you did this on purpose! You knew all along. You had Yang Feng cremated so quickly just to secure the inheritance!\"","Yang Feng’s parents also caught on and began wailing, pounding their chests and cursing Qin Wenqiang.","\"I knew there was something off about how quickly you acted! You planned this all along, you vile woman! You burned my poor son just to get your hands on his money!\"","\"Our son is dead, and you still want to destroy our Yang family’s legacy!\"","Qin Wenqiang sneered. \"You schemed to divorce me and leave me with nothing, using the money I earned to raise your illegitimate children. Did you think I wouldn’t fight back?\"","The other guests, who hadn’t expected such a juicy twist, began murmuring excitedly. They had assumed Qin Wenqiang had cremated Yang Feng’s body out of anger over his infidelity. But no—it was all part of her plan to secure the inheritance.","Everyone couldn’t help but marvel at Qin Wenqiang’s ruthlessness. She was on a completely different level compared to Yang Feng.","If they wanted to use her hard-earned money to raise his illegitimate children, she would strip those children of their inheritance rights entirely.","\"Lawyer, lawyer! We can prove it! Test us!\" Yang Feng’s parents suddenly shouted. \"Yang Feng was our only son. If we can prove these are our grandchildren, then...\"","Qin Wenqiang let out a cold laugh.","\"That won’t work,\" the lawyer said.","\"Then have Yang Weiwei take the test! If they’re proven to be siblings...\" the mistress quickly suggested.","Yang Feng’s parents immediately turned their eager eyes to Yang Weiwei, as if they wanted to drag her into the test right then and there.","Yang Weiwei, however, remained unfazed. \"Do I have any obligation to cooperate with you?\" she asked, then turned to the lawyer. \"Uncle, if I refuse, they can’t force me, right?\"","The lawyer wiped his sweat. \"Refusing the test is your right, Miss.\"","Seeing the hostile glares from the others, the lawyer felt compelled to add, \"Even if they secretly conduct a test, it won’t hold any legal weight. Only if you willingly cooperate will it be valid.\"","This effectively blocked any underhanded tactics they might have tried.","The three younger brothers and one sister, though still young, were no strangers to such schemes. They glared at Yang Weiwei with venomous eyes.","Yang Weiwei, however, wasn’t intimidated. She rolled her eyes at them, making her stance clear:","Not a chance! Keep dreaming!","From then on, no amount of curses from Yang Feng’s parents or tearful pleas from the mistress could sway Yang Weiwei. Gradually, they realized that mother and daughter were determined to make their lives miserable. All they could do was glare at them with hatred.","Just as the lawyer was about to announce the division of assets, Qin Wenqiang called out, \"Oh, and by the way, Yang Feng’s estate isn’t fully accounted for. You might have missed some things—like the money he spent on others behind my back. We’ll need to recover that too!\""]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: Your Future Pension Issues Have Nothing to Do with Weiwei","paragraphs":["The lawyer was momentarily stunned, quickly realizing what was happening.","Qin Wenqiang sneered at the mistress and said, \"I want to recover the marital assets my late husband spent on you.\"","With that, she had her secretary hand over a prepared list to the lawyer.","This was the final straw for the mistress. She erupted in a furious rage, shouting, \"How dare you! You can't do this! That money was spent on raising his child. You have no right to take it back! You...\"","The fact that her own child couldn't inherit anything had already driven the mistress to the brink of madness. Now, being told that even the money spent on her and her family would be reclaimed, she was on the verge of losing everything.","And it was Yang Feng's child! How could the money spent on the child be demanded back?","But when the mistress looked at the lawyer, she knew Qin Wenqiang wasn't bluffing.","\"If the identity of your children cannot be verified, then Ms. Qin does have the right to reclaim the assets...\" the lawyer declared coldly.","Everything seemed to hinge on the fact that Yang Feng had already been cremated.","The mistress was practically losing her mind, and her brother couldn't believe it either. He immediately said, \"Sis, don't worry. We'll fight this in court. I refuse to believe that a father can't spend money on his own child!\"","Qin Wenqiang let out a cold laugh. \"It's fine. We can drag this out. The outcome will be the same anyway.\"","The mistress burst into tears and turned to Yang Feng's parents. \"Mom, Dad, look! She's trying to drive us to ruin! Fine, I'll give up everything. I'll just take the children and leave. Is that good enough for you?\"","Yang Feng's parents were already trembling with anger, but the mistress's words struck a chord.","\"No! My precious grandchildren can't leave! Don't worry, Mom and Dad will stand by you!\" Grandma Yang immediately cried out.","Grandpa Yang tried to remain calm and stepped forward to discuss the matter with the lawyer. Even though the lawyer didn't spell it out, Grandpa Yang knew the situation was dire.","With a trembling hand, he pointed at Qin Wenqiang and said, \"Are you really going to be this heartless?\"","Qin Wenqiang held her daughter close and sneered, \"I'm just taking back what belongs to me and my daughter. You all thought you could play me for a fool. Did you really think there wouldn't be consequences?\"","Grandpa Yang was so angry his mouth twisted. Finally, he spat out, \"Fine! Very well! Let me tell you this—from now on, the Yang Family no longer recognizes you as our daughter-in-law, nor that disobedient brat of yours. They are the ones who belong to the Yang Family now. If you think you can reclaim the assets and seek revenge, think again! We will always stand by them!\"","Grandma Yang chimed in, \"That's right! Our son's estate includes our share. We'll use the money you both earned to raise them. Let's see how you like that, you vile woman!\"","Qin Yi, who had been standing to the side, was so furious he wanted to throw a punch. \"It seems you all know very well who contributed the most to their marital assets. How can you have the audacity to say such shameless things? I think Yang Feng's early death was karma!\"","His words ignited the group, and chaos erupted once again.","[Well, well, well. Look at these people, still so stubborn. They've already fallen twice. Do they really think Big Cousin hasn't considered this?]","The members of Qin Second's family, who had also been seething with anger, suddenly looked puzzled upon hearing this inner voice.","They all thought they would have to swallow their anger in the end. Could it be that Big Cousin had another trick up her sleeve?","Although Ji Fei didn't reveal anything, everyone assumed Qin Xian would know. After all, when it came to strategy, Qin Xian was the sharpest mind in the room.","So, all eyes turned to Qin Xian. After a moment of thought, Qin Xian said, \"If she wants to be ruthless, there is one way.\"","The twins and Qin Jiaxi, seeing everyone looking at Qin Xian, were confused.","The next second, Qin Xian, unable to withstand the curious gazes of the onlookers, reluctantly said, \"Perhaps Big Cousin will trick them into giving up everything else in exchange for... the company.\"","The twins, with their sharp business instincts, immediately caught on.","\"That company that wanted you to invest?\" Qin Jing asked.","\"I remember it was a company Yang Feng started independently, separate from the Qin Family,\" Qin Xiaoyu added.","Qin Zhao chuckled. \"Looks like that company is a trap—a big one.\"","Hearing their conversation, Ji Fei looked at Qin Xian with admiration and surprise. Her expression immediately told those who could hear her inner thoughts that Qin Xian had guessed correctly.","And soon, Qin Wenqiang confirmed it.","Before anyone could speak, Qin Wenqiang declared, \"I can let go of everything else, but Yang Feng's newly established company must go to me.\"","This statement made it clear to everyone that the company must be valuable. Otherwise, Qin Wenqiang wouldn't be fighting for it, especially since she had previously acted as if she wouldn't leave them anything of value.","Moreover, Yang Feng had always boasted to them about how valuable the company was, claiming it was his trump card to stand against the Qin Family if they ever found out about his illegitimate child. This had led Yang Feng's parents and the mistress to believe the company was a goldmine.","Given Qin Wenqiang's current attitude, the elderly couple immediately said, \"No way! We want that company too.\"","This only made Qin Wenqiang's expression darken. \"My and Weiwei's share of the inheritance in exchange for the company!\"","But the more Qin Wenqiang insisted, the more the elderly couple dug in their heels. Although the mistress preferred tangible assets, her brother stopped her from hesitating. After all, with the company, he could become the boss. So, he supported the elderly couple and even hyped up the company's value.","Seeing Qin Wenqiang adamantly refusing to back down, the elderly couple started playing the emotional card.","\"That was Yang Feng's final labor of love. Unlike you, we value sentiment. We only want this. Everything else belongs to the Qin Family. Only this company is part of the Yang Family. You can't take it! If you give us the company, we'll give up everything else in the inheritance.\"","After the elderly couple finished their act, the mistress and her children joined in, claiming that Yang Feng had left the company for them and that taking it away would be a betrayal of his dying wish.","By this point, the Qin Family members waiting at the door were struggling to hold back their laughter.","But Qin Wenqiang continued her act, and even Yang Weiwei played along. \"Mom, we don't need something like that.\"","Qin Wenqiang took a deep breath, feigning reluctance, and finally said with a pained expression, \"Fine, I can agree to this arrangement. But I have one condition.\"","The group looked at her warily, as if afraid she would pull some trick regarding the company.","Then Qin Wenqiang said, \"I want Weiwei's household registration removed from the Yang Family. You must also sign an agreement to sever ties with Weiwei. From now on, she will no longer be your granddaughter! Her future obligations, including your elderly care, will have nothing to do with her!\""]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339: Changing Weiwei's Surname","paragraphs":["Qin Wenqiang's request naturally made the two elders uncomfortable, and the mistress wasn't too pleased either.","Although they had spoken harshly during the argument, deep down, they knew that as long as they had this granddaughter, they wouldn't have to worry for the rest of their lives. She was the link—when Yang Weiwei grew up, she would still have to consider her grandparents' feelings and take care of her younger siblings. This wasn't something that cold, hard laws could change.","\"After all, Weiwei is still a descendant of the Old Yang Family. What you're doing is utterly immoral,\" Grandpa Yang said.","Qin Wenqiang once again witnessed their shamelessness and couldn't help but feel a pang of regret. Had she been blind all those years? How had she failed to see how despicable they were?","Yang Weiwei, furious, widened her eyes and said, \"You just said you didn't recognize me anymore. Does being old mean you can go back on your word?\"","Grandma Yang immediately retorted, \"We were just angry with your mom earlier. You're too young to understand anything!\"","But Yang Weiwei understood perfectly. She knew these shameless relatives wanted to take advantage of her for the rest of her life, and she refused to let that happen.","\"You never liked me before, and now you want to cling to me, expecting me to take care of you in your old age. I'm not clueless!\" Yang Weiwei's eyes reddened with anger, but her voice was firm and resolute. \"But you won't succeed. I'd rather die than take care of you. If you're unhappy, go ahead and sue me in court!\"","Seeing Yang Weiwei's hostility, Yang Feng's parents were furious and wanted to scold her. But Qin Wenqiang cut them off.","\"Not agreeing? Fine. Lawyer, we insist on fighting for that company. They don't know how to run it. It's only fair that it be awarded to us.\"","At this, the mistress's younger brother panicked. He was the one who wanted the company the most. After all, the other parts of the inheritance were less accessible to him, but the company was something he could directly take over. Even if he couldn't manage it well, selling it would surely fetch a hefty sum. After all, hadn't his brother-in-law mentioned something about going public? Companies that could go public were worth hundreds of millions, far more valuable than the rest of the inheritance.","He immediately turned to Yang Feng's parents and urged, \"Hurry and fight for it! With the company, money will keep flowing in. It's much better than those stagnant assets. Don't you trust the wealth your son left for us? He worked so hard to build it. And dragging Yang Weiwei along won't help. She resents you so much now. If she stays with her mom, do you really think she'll remember to take care of you in the future? You already have grandchildren from my sister. Why care about one less? Don't lose out on this!\"","The mistress herself began to waver. She thought more simply: while the inheritance was nominally left to Yang Feng's parents, they were old. If something happened to them, Yang Weiwei would have a stronger claim to the inheritance than her own children. So, if Yang Weiwei cut ties with them, it would actually benefit her children. Moreover, given Qin Wenqiang's attitude, the mistress doubted her children could ever rely on Yang Weiwei in the future.","With this in mind, the mistress also began to persuade Yang Feng's parents.","Yang Feng's parents were swayed by the arguments. Seeing Yang Weiwei's hostile and rebellious gaze, they realized she would never be loyal to them. It was better to let it go. Besides, even if they declared a severance of ties, if something really happened in the future, could Yang Weiwei really stand by and do nothing? The media would crucify her.","The more they thought about it, the more it made sense. They nodded in agreement, signed the severance agreement, and, at Qin Wenqiang's request, recorded a video as legal proof.","Finally, the inheritance was successfully divided.","[Congratulations, congratulations! It's all settled now, hahaha! What a show!]","While the other members of the Qin Family were also happy, they couldn't help but feel a lingering sense of unease, wondering if everything would go smoothly from here.","As the grand drama came to an end, the onlookers were stuffed with gossip. Having witnessed the shamelessness of the Yang Family, they silently vowed never to collaborate with them in the future. Getting entangled with them would be an unimaginable nightmare.","From this moment on, the new company they took over would face insurmountable challenges.","Qin Wenqiang didn't waste any time. She had no intention of bringing Yang Weiwei to the funeral. Instead, she had Grandpa Yang accompany her to transfer Yang Weiwei's household registration.","The rest of the Qin Family didn't follow. Shortly after returning to the old residence, they heard the news: not only had the household registration been transferred, but Yang Weiwei had also changed her surname on the spot.","Upon hearing this, the patriarch waved his hand and declared that they would celebrate that very night in honor of Qin Weiwei!","Everyone was supposed to attend, as the divorce of the eldest cousin was also a significant event.","However, only Third Uncle Qin showed up.","The patriarch frowned and asked, and Third Uncle Qin could only awkwardly explain, \"Zi Xuan needs to rest for her pregnancy, and Qin Han is staying home to keep her safe.\"","The patriarch, being shrewd, sensed something amiss but didn't press further.","When Third Uncle Qin entered the lively living room, he was taken aback.","His daughter, who usually stayed quiet and unnoticed in the corner, was now sitting in the middle of the crowd. Though she still didn't speak, her eyes were no longer hidden behind her bangs. Instead, they sparkled as she watched her siblings chat animatedly.","Her usually expressionless face now shifted with the emotions of the conversation around her.","\"When they heard about the name change, Yang Feng's dad couldn't keep his composure. It was hilarious! He never cared about our Weiwei, always favoring boys, but when it came to changing her surname, it was like his life was on the line,\" Qin Yi scoffed. \"Thankfully, Big Sister had the foresight to only bring him. If that old hag had come, she would've thrown a tantrum for sure!\"","Everyone burst into laughter.","Just then, they noticed Third Uncle Qin entering and immediately stopped their conversation to greet him.","But Third Uncle Qin saw his daughter stiffen for a moment, her eyes nervously darting behind him. Only when she saw nothing there did she relax.","Third Uncle Qin's heart sank. He remembered how, at home, the family had spoken resentfully of his daughter when she wasn't around. A suffocating feeling washed over him, and his expression darkened.","Still, he first explained to Qin Wenqiang, the star of the evening, why the others hadn't come.","Qin Wenqiang smiled indifferently and even asked after the elders' health.","The others found it a bit odd, but since she was now an older expectant mother, they didn't say much.","Meanwhile, Qin Second's family had fresh gossip to share.","[Unbelievable! Third Aunt and Qin Han wanted to bring that scheming woman to the gathering, but Third Uncle refused. So, they got angry and didn't come. Who do they think they are? Big Sister's divorce and Weiwei's name change have nothing to do with outsiders. How dare they suggest bringing someone else? Ridiculous!]"]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340: Block All Their Escape Routes in Advance with Public Opinion","paragraphs":["The Qin Second family listened to the truth and couldn't help but show disdain on their faces.","Qin Xian, however, recalled the results of the recent investigation he had ordered. Yu Xin was indeed a child from the orphanage that his third aunt had sponsored, and Qin Han had gotten to know her because of this.","But his third aunt treated Yu Xin with particular care, far beyond the ordinary sponsorship of an orphan. She treated her like an adopted daughter, providing constant care and a steady flow of money. This was something even his third uncle was unaware of, as he was too focused on his career to bother with family matters.","If it weren't for the timeline, Qin Xian might have suspected that Yu Xin was another illegitimate child.","Nevertheless, Qin Xian had his people dig deeper into Yu Xin's biological parents. If there was no connection to them, there was no reason for his third aunt to go to such extreme lengths.","In addition to this, Qin Xian had also uncovered some juicy details that even Ji Fei hadn't managed to dig up, purely by chance.","For instance, the reason Qin Han was so protective of Yu Xin was that she was already his. Their hotel check-in records had been compiled and handed over to Qin Xian.","Qin Xian had no interest in exposing their relationship, as both were technically single. But if Yu Xin were to enter the Qin family as an adopted daughter, these records would serve as the most compelling evidence against it.","Meanwhile, Qin Third Uncle asked Qin Jiaxi how she had been during her stay here, hinting at whether she wanted to return home. His wife and son had suggested he bring Qin Jiaxi back, but now he didn't want to push her, preferring to hear her thoughts.","In the past, Qin Jiaxi would have gone along with her family's arrangements. But this time, she raised her head and said, \"No... there's no need. I want to spend more time with my cousins. They rarely visit, and with the holidays almost over, I won't have much time to be with them before I return to school.\"","Her words implied that the little time she had left would be spent with her relatives, not her family.","Qin Third Uncle finally realized the extent of their family's issues. He decided to have a proper talk with his daughter when he had the chance.","After dealing with her father, Qin Jiaxi wanted to quickly return to the lively atmosphere.","Just then, her phone vibrated. Qin Jiaxi carefully took it out, afraid it might be a scolding message from her mother or brother.","But upon glancing at it, she couldn't help but smile.","It was from her boyfriend, Su Ze.","They had been out of touch for days due to his trip abroad.","Finally, he had reached out.","But when she opened the message, her smile faded.","\"What are you doing? Why are you bullying Yu Xin? You're the Qin family's eldest daughter, and she's just a poor orphan. Can't you stand to see her happy? I don't like this side of you; it's not kind. You've disappointed me. I hope this is the last time. Don't stop your father from adopting Yu Xin. Go home with him today, correct your mistakes, and work together to have the Qin family adopt her.\"","Qin Jiaxi froze. During her relationship with Su Ze, there had been times when he used such a stern tone to criticize her. It always made her feel terrible, and she would desperately reflect on herself. After all, her mother and brother adored Yu Xin, and only Su Ze had chosen her.","She felt like Su Ze was all she had.","But just as she was about to call him to apologize, she heard laughter coming from the hall.","\"I'm the Qin family's daughter. What could Weiwei and I possibly have done wrong? It's definitely their fault! You'll see soon enough. The PR team at Qin Corporation's branch isn't just for show. Get ready for a show.\" Qin Wenqiang said arrogantly.","Qin Jiaxi paused, recalling everything she had witnessed over the past few days.","Suddenly, the message felt like a sharp sting. She didn't understand anymore.","\"I don't know where you heard this, but I never stopped anything. It's the Qin family's decision. And aren't you my boyfriend? Why didn't you ask me before accusing me? Why are you siding so much with Yu Xin? Are you two close?\"","Her heart raced as she sent the message. After a while, she received a reply.","\"What are you overthinking? I'm just speaking fairly because Yu Xin is like family to you and your brother. Didn't she save your mother's life? You should be grateful. I'm trying to guide you in the right direction. Look at you now, even doubting my words?\"","Qin Jiaxi suddenly felt incredibly wronged. It was because of this so-called \"life-saving favor\" that she couldn't bring herself to oppose Yu Xin joining the Qin family. Any resistance would make her seem ungrateful.","But remembering how everyone always stood behind her cousin no matter what, Qin Jiaxi suddenly felt lonely, even with a boyfriend whom the entire school envied.","From the hall, voices rose again.","\"We can't guess, but Second Brother definitely can!\"","\"Exactly. If Cousin keeps being cryptic, we'll just ask Second Brother directly.\"","Qin Jiaxi glanced at the messages again, sensing an indescribable arrogance in them.","Feeling lost, she couldn't help but reply, \"My cousin is Qin Xian, the head of the Qin family and the one in charge of Qin Corporation. If he disagrees with something, even my father won't oppose it. Am I wrong for following his lead?\"","After sending the message, Qin Jiaxi came to her senses and quickly put her phone away, afraid to imagine Su Ze's response. This was the first time she had ever talked back to him, and it felt extremely uncomfortable. But she believed she hadn't said anything wrong.","On the other end, Su Ze didn't reply. The moment he saw the message, he threw his phone in anger.","Wasn't that a direct insult? Qin Xian's reputation was well-known even in Y City. Qin Jiaxi's words implied that Qin Xian's decisions were unquestionable, so who was Su Ze to correct anyone?","The young master of the Su family spent the night fuming.","Meanwhile, in the hall, everyone was already enjoying the latest gossip about their cousin's divorce.","By 8 PM, the most active time on Y City's entertainment networks, a sensational headline about a wealthy family scandal broke.","\"Qin Family Eldest Daughter Tears into Mistress at Funeral, Cuts Ties with Grandparents Alongside Daughter.\"","The article detailed the backstory, the scheming of the scumbag, photos of the mistress's family at the scene, and, most importantly, a notarized video of the grandparents announcing their disownment of Qin Weiwei.","The internet exploded.","Soon, the public opinion was set, and calls from Yang Feng's parents were immediately rejected.","They suddenly realized that even if they wanted to sever ties, blood relations couldn't be erased. They had hoped to use emotional blackmail or public pressure to force Qin Weiwei to comply in the future.","But now, with the entire internet condemning them, they could no longer imagine things going their way.","Back at the Qin family, everyone was laughing after reading the gossip.","[\"This is a preemptive strike to block all their escape routes. They won't be able to use moral blackmail anymore.\"]"]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341: No Wonder Students Are Tempted","paragraphs":["Ji Fei leaned into Qin Xian's embrace, laughing uncontrollably. \"This is what it means to take the moral high ground first.\"","Qin Yan chimed in, \"But isn't it still not legally acceptable?\"","Qin Rong exclaimed, \"Huh? So we're still going to be taken advantage of?\"","Qin Jing added, \"That'll only happen after Weiwei turns eighteen. If they're still alive by then, Weiwei will have to support them...\"","Qin Xiaoyu interjected, \"But they'd have to sue Weiwei to get any support money. Whatever the court decides, that's what you'll pay.\"","Qin Zhao, ever the mischievous one, quipped, \"Just give them the money in coins and make them count it one by one.\"","Qin Yi, however, had a different idea. \"Why not exchange it for food of equal value? That way, they won't starve.\"","Qin Jiaxi couldn't help but chuckle at the suggestion.","Qin Wenqiang, with a sly smile, added, \"It's not over yet. After all, the assets haven't been fully recovered. Hehe~\"","Over the years, the mistress and her illegitimate child had been spending the couple's shared wealth. With the illegitimate child unable to prove their identity, the situation was entirely in Qin Wenqiang's favor.","Once the verdict was passed and the assets were returned, not only would the mistress be left penniless, but Yang Feng's parents would also lose a significant portion of their wealth.","In the past, Qin Wenqiang and Yang Feng had showered the old couple with luxuries, allowing them to live a comfortable life. Now, they would have to tighten their belts and return everything they had squandered.","It was poetic justice, considering how they had once condoned the mistress and her child's reckless spending of Yang Feng's money. Now, they would have to pay it all back, no matter how difficult it might be.","Sure enough, it didn't take long for Qin Wenqiang to reclaim everything she had once given to these people.","Initially, the mistress's family had felt secure because they controlled the company. However, when the mistress's brother took over, he discovered that the company wasn't even turning a profit. Yang Feng hadn't secured a single project and had even delayed various payments.","This left the family in a state of panic. They scrambled to seek help, only to find that they had already been ostracized by the business community in Y City.","When the pressure from debt collectors became too much to bear, they finally realized they had no idea how to run a company. Desperate, they decided to sell it rather than manage it themselves.","But no one was willing to buy it.","In the end, they shamelessly turned to Qin Wenqiang for help. However, by that time, she had already taken her daughter abroad to expand her business overseas.","All of this, however, was a story for another time.","Currently, the gossip among Y City's elite was at its peak. Qin Wenqiang and her daughter kept a low profile, spending most of their time with relatives.","Things had been quiet for the past few days.","With the old patriarch's birthday still some time away, Qin Xian, who had recently taken over the family business, made his first trip to Y City to inspect the operations. Naturally, those involved in the Qin family's enterprises had to make time to accompany him.","This left only a few people behind: Ji Fei, Qin Zhao, Qin Rong, Qin Yi, and Qin Jiaxi. As the eldest cousin, Qin Yi took on the role of tour guide, while Qin Jiaxi tagged along as the playful companion.","However, Qin Jiaxi couldn't join them today as she had classes to attend.","This left only the four of them.","After much deliberation, they still couldn't decide what to do. Qin Yi, recalling a message he had just received, hesitated before suggesting, \"Actually, the students at my academy are putting on a performance at the concert hall today. Would you like to go and watch?\"","As soon as Qin Yi finished speaking, the other three turned to look at him. Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, remembering the gossip they had heard from Ji Fei, immediately showed interest.","Qin Zhao, who was more knowledgeable about music, asked for details. After hearing the explanation, he exclaimed in surprise, \"This kind of performance is crucial for students like them. Don't you need to be there the whole time?\"","Qin Yi, feeling a bit awkward, rubbed his chin and replied, \"I took some time off to be with you all. Besides, there are other teachers there to supervise.\"","[Pfft, haha! So that's what's going on. His favorite student sent him a message, begging him to come watch the performance. But Qin Yi doesn't want to give them false hope, yet he's still worried about how his student will perform. That's why he's so conflicted.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong exchanged knowing glances, their smirks making Qin Yi even more uncomfortable.","\"Since it's your student's performance, let's go and have a look. We can't think of anything else to do anyway,\" Ji Fei said, trying to suppress a smile.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong nodded in agreement.","They weren't there to indulge in some teacher-student romance fantasy—they were just there for the gossip.","And so, the four of them set off to watch the performance.","The concert hall was filled with students from the music academy. The front rows were reserved for influential figures in the music industry, there to scout for promising talent. A glowing review from them could open doors to a bright future, with some even offering to take students under their wing on the spot.","As a renowned baritone, Qin Yi would have normally been seated in the front row. However, since he had initially planned not to attend, no seat had been reserved for him.","Upon arrival, Qin Yi arranged for them to watch from a private box rather than the general audience area. He then excused himself to check on his students backstage, wanting to offer some last-minute encouragement before they went on stage.","\"I'd like to go backstage too, if that's okay with you, cousin,\" Ji Fei eagerly suggested.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong quickly chimed in, not wanting to miss out on the juicy details.","Under the trio's expectant gazes, Qin Yi had no choice but to take them along to the backstage area.","The backstage was bustling with activity, with several waiting rooms filled with students coming and going. Upon seeing Qin Yi, they all respectfully addressed him as \"Teacher.\"","While all the performers were technically Qin Yi's students, having attended his lectures at the academy, there was only one who held a special place in his heart—a talented individual he had taken under his wing privately, hoping to nurture their potential.","Nevertheless, Qin Yi treated everyone equally, moving from room to room to offer words of encouragement and advice.","Ji Fei and the others stood by the doorway, casually observing the scene.","\"Now I see why everyone respects Cousin Qin Yi so much,\" Qin Rong remarked with a smile. \"He's amazing—he can give pointers to every single student.\"","\"And he's so precise too. Look at how those students are gazing at him with admiration. It's clear he's very popular,\" Qin Zhao added.","[I think... Qin Yi might have more than just one admirer among his students. It's no wonder—he's handsome, wealthy, incredibly skilled, and so kind-hearted. It's no surprise that students would develop feelings for him.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong nodded in agreement, though they couldn't help but feel that their cousin was destined to remain single, his heart entirely devoted to music.","As Qin Yi made his way through the rooms, he finally reached the last one. Before he could knock, he overheard a heated argument inside.","\"The performance order was decided by lottery,\" a trembling but determined female voice insisted. \"You can't just—\"","\"Zhou Rushi, do you really think being the last to perform will give you an edge? You're just a clown. With your vocal talent, how can you possibly compare to me? I'm Qin Yi's protégé—my performance has to be perfect. You're just jealous and trying to sabotage my grand finale,\" Wan Sitong sneered, her voice dripping with disdain."]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342: Everyone Likes the Teacher","paragraphs":["Qin Yi's disciple?","Who dares to say that? Could it be that beloved disciple?","Seeing Qin Yi pause at the door, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong exchanged frantic glances.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei had already started her commentary. [What on earth? This kind of bully is the one who confessed to Qin Yi? Looks like my cousin's judgment in choosing disciples isn't great either. But thankfully, he only sees her as a disciple. He probably never saw this side of her before. His face has turned dark.]","Inside, Wan Sitong continued to mock Zhou Rushi. \"Most of the audience here came because of Qin Yi and me. They're looking forward to my performance as a prodigy. Do you really think anyone will stay patiently to watch your performance after I'm done? I'm doing you a favor by letting you switch the order. You'd better be smart about this. I'm not in a good mood today. If you mess up my performance and disappoint Qin Yi, you'll regret it!\"","[Her tone is truly awful. Is this her natural disposition, or is she deliberately bullying someone to vent her anger?]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong also felt uncomfortable listening to this, silently criticizing Qin Yi's poor judgment.","Wan Sitong continued, \"Speak up! Cat got your tongue? Still not convinced? Zhou Rushi, don't think I don't know what you're thinking. I could expose everything, and then you'd really—\"","Before long, a hoarse female voice responded, \"I... I understand.\"","\"Hmph, you'd better.\"","[What? She gave in? Was she being blackmailed, or is she just scared of Qin Yi's influence? If that's the case, this disciple must have bullied many students under Qin Yi's name.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong also found the situation rather uninteresting.","Qin Yi couldn't take it anymore and pushed the door open, interrupting the conversation.","\"Ah, Qin... Teacher.\"","\"Teacher Qin?\"","Ji Fei peeked inside and saw two girls—one standing and one sitting. The standing girl wore glasses, looking delicate and refined, though she was trembling and her eyes were red, clearly upset. The sitting girl, on the other hand, had an air of superiority. She was strikingly beautiful, but her expression was one of shock, her face gradually reddening as she realized her arrogant behavior had been caught in the act.","Qin Yi frowned at Wan Sitong. \"The order was decided by drawing lots to ensure fairness for all students. What are you doing? Do you usually bully your classmates like this?\"","Qin Yi was deeply disappointed. He knew Wan Sitong was somewhat arrogant—after all, she was a prodigy—but he never imagined her behavior could be so malicious.","\"N-no, it's not like that...\" Wan Sitong clearly didn't want to show her true self in front of Qin Yi and desperately tried to explain. \"I just wanted to perform last. It doesn't make much difference to her anyway, given her level...\"","\"Wan Sitong!\" Qin Yi cut her off sharply.","Wan Sitong immediately looked at Qin Yi with a pitiful expression, her gaze anything but that of a student looking at a teacher.","\"I was just afraid you wouldn't come, afraid you'd be late. That's why I tried to delay the performance. I just wanted to perform for you.\" As she spoke, Wan Sitong began to cry.","This caught Qin Yi off guard, and he looked visibly uncomfortable.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong exchanged suspicious glances, then turned to Ji Fei.","\"Sister-in-law, what do you think?\" Qin Rong asked.","Ji Fei raised an eyebrow and said, \"She doesn't seem to be lying.\"","[Indeed, she's not lying. Wan Sitong really did delay the performance for Qin Yi. This girl is utterly infatuated with him.]","After observing Wan Sitong, Ji Fei curiously turned her attention to Zhou Rushi, the girl who had been bullied and was now fading into the background.","At first glance, it was startling.","[Wow, our cousin's charm is truly something else.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, noticing Ji Fei's interest in the other girl, immediately grew curious. Could it be...","[No wonder she seemed threatened earlier. Turns out Zhou Rushi also has feelings for Qin Yi, but she's the type to secretly admire him from afar, feeling unworthy and believing there's no chance between them. She never dares to hope, but Wan Sitong saw through her. That's why she was threatening to expose Zhou Rushi's feelings to Qin Yi. Zhou Rushi was afraid that if Qin Yi found out, he'd avoid her, and she'd lose even the chance to occasionally seek his guidance. That's why she gave in.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong couldn't help but sigh. Being a teacher like Qin Yi isn't easy—accidentally getting liked by students is a constant risk. While university relationships aren't strictly forbidden, this is still quite extreme. It must be the Qin family's exceptional genes at work.","Meanwhile, Wan Sitong was busy spinning her story to Qin Yi, as if her earlier bullying had never happened and she had only been misunderstood.","Qin Yi, not wanting to delve deeper at the moment, simply said, \"Alright, apologize to Zhou Rushi. The performance will proceed as scheduled. Both of you, get ready.\"","Though Wan Sitong was internally furious, she reluctantly apologized to Zhou Rushi.","Zhou Rushi, too afraid to even look at Qin Yi, simply nodded in acknowledgment.","Wan Sitong, however, sneered inwardly, then turned to Qin Yi with a coquettish tone. \"Teacher, after my performance, can you come back here to see me?\"","Qin Yi immediately raised his guard. \"I brought some relatives to watch the performance today, so I might not have time for post-performance guidance. We'll discuss it back at school.\"","Wan Sitong seemed to notice the others at the door for the first time and frowned, as if she should be the most important person in Qin Yi's life. \"Just for a little while, Teacher, please?\"","She pleaded so desperately that it seemed she wouldn't let Qin Yi leave unless he agreed.","Qin Yi was sweating bullets, afraid that someone might notice something amiss. In the end, he reluctantly agreed, planning to clarify things with Wan Sitong after the performance. If she still couldn't let go of her feelings, he might have to assign her to another mentor.","Wan Sitong, however, was already plotting to confess her feelings again after the performance. She refused to believe that Qin Yi, who had always been so kind to her, didn't feel the same way. After all, they were a perfect match.","Soon, Wan Sitong was led away by the staff to prepare.","Qin Yi finally breathed a sigh of relief and gave Zhou Rushi some last-minute advice before the performance.","Zhou Rushi listened attentively, though her expression couldn't hide her sadness. Qin Yi, thinking she was still upset about Wan Sitong's words, reassured her, \"Your singing skills aren't inferior to hers. You have your own unique talent.\"","He meant it. Zhou Rushi was diligent and had excellent vocal skills, though her natural voice wasn't as outstanding. Initially, Qin Yi had hesitated between the two, but Wan Sitong's prodigious talent had ultimately won him over.","Zhou Rushi nodded obediently.","[Ah, the poor girl is heartbroken after seeing how close the teacher and disciple are. My clueless cousin has no idea she likes him too.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong could only watch sympathetically.","After giving his instructions, Qin Yi led the others back to the private box to watch the performance.","Lost in thought, Qin Yi didn't notice the expressions of his companions until he overheard their whispers.","\"No way! If he could like her, he'd have to be blind,\" Qin Zhao said.","Qin Yi: \"...\"","\"What are you talking about?\" Qin Yi's face turned red.","\"We're talking about you and Wan Sitong. It's so obvious, anyone can see it,\" Ji Fei said bluntly, eager to keep the gossip going."]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343: Witnessing the Scene of My Cousin Being Confessed to by His Apprentice","paragraphs":["After all, the situation just now was quite obvious, so Ji Fei wasn’t exactly revealing her special ability. She could openly gossip with Qin Zhao and Qin Rong about it.","Listening to Ji Fei’s words, Qin Yi felt awkward for a while before finally speaking up. “It’s just that my disciple is being immature. Let’s not gossip about it.”","“She’s an adult. How could she be immature? Cousin, has she already confessed to you, but you rejected her?” Qin Zhao directly voiced the gossip he had heard from Ji Fei, framing it as a guess.","Qin Yi was left speechless and could only sigh. “Maybe I should only take male disciples from now on.”","Ji Fei really wanted to complain, but she didn’t dare to say it out loud.","[When I saw him instructing his students earlier, several of the boys were looking at him with unusual gazes. Cousin is really underestimating his own charm. If he truly wants to avoid a teacher-student romance and focus on being a good teacher, he’d better ruin his own image.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong tried hard not to laugh.","“Cousin, if Wan Sitong doesn’t give up, what will you do in the future? Aren’t you still going to be her teacher?” Qin Rong asked curiously.","“If she remains stubborn, then I really won’t be able to continue as her teacher,” Qin Yi said, glancing at the performance stage below. “Perhaps tonight is an opportunity. If her performance catches someone’s eye, another teacher might want to take her as a disciple, and I can gracefully step back.”","“But based on her behavior just now, if you stop being her teacher and hand her over to someone else, wouldn’t she cause a scene?” Ji Fei said. “You’d better handle this carefully.”","Based on Ji Fei’s years of experience in observing drama, people like Wan Sitong, with her temperament, are the most likely to go crazy. And someone as mild-mannered as Qin Yi would have the hardest time dealing with such a person.","In truth, even without Ji Fei’s reminder, Qin Yi would still be cautious. After all, Wan Sitong was a disciple he had carefully nurtured, and he wanted the best for her.","Soon, the performances below began.","Ji Fei and Qin Rong didn’t have much of an eye for this kind of thing and judged purely based on feeling.","Qin Yi and Qin Zhao, on the other hand, gave thoughtful critiques.","Wan Sitong was scheduled early, and it wasn’t long before her turn came. Her vocal talent was indeed exceptional, so much so that even non-professionals like Ji Fei and Qin Rong could tell she was on a different level compared to the other students.","Combined with her impressive singing skills, her performance elevated the ordinary student showcase to the level of a professional concert.","The audience’s reaction was the most enthusiastic yet, and even the reporters covering the event were snapping photos more frequently.","As her song ended, thunderous applause erupted. Wan Sitong confidently accepted the attention, her eyes searching the crowd for Qin Yi. However, since they were in a private box, Wan Sitong could only leave the stage with regret.","The performances that followed were rather unremarkable until the very last one.","Zhou Rushi seemed to have dressed up a bit, at least she wasn’t wearing her glasses on stage.","As soon as she began singing, Ji Fei and the others were surprised. Her powerful voice, while not as dazzling as Wan Sitong’s, still showcased her excellence compared to her peers.","Her singing technique was solid, as evidenced by the frequent nods from the professionals in the audience. However, her vocal quality was somewhat ordinary, giving off a sense of being easily lost in the crowd. It was hard to instantly recognize her voice.","The contrast between her and Wan Sitong was like a battle between hard work and natural talent.","A talented individual only needs to put in moderate effort, combined with guidance from a master, to surpass someone who has worked tirelessly.","It was unfortunate, but the spotlight of the night was destined to fall on that ill-mannered and unpleasant individual.","Once all the students’ performances were over, Qin Yi received a text from Wan Sitong urging him to meet her.","When Qin Yi turned around, he saw the three of them looking at him with gossip-filled eyes. Before he could say anything, they all volunteered to accompany him, clearly wanting to witness the drama.","Back in the hallway outside the waiting rooms, some students were dejected, while others were excited, gradually leaving the venue. A few approached Qin Yi to ask for feedback on their performances, and he patiently gave them detailed advice.","They happened to run into Zhou Rushi, who had put her glasses back on and was carrying her bag. When she saw Qin Yi, she greeted him respectfully, though there was a hint of sadness in her expression.","Thinking she might be upset about her performance, Qin Yi comforted her, “You did really well today. Keep working hard, and you’ll continue to improve.”","Ji Fei noticed the girl’s eyes light up instantly, as if a single word of praise from someone she admired gave her strength.","“Thank you, teacher,” Zhou Rushi said. Then, after glancing at Qin Yi again, she couldn’t help but add, “Teacher, you don’t look well. You should take more time to rest.”","Qin Yi was taken aback. He hadn’t expected Zhou Rushi to notice. Lately, he hadn’t been resting well due to family matters and personal troubles, so it was no wonder he looked tired.","Still, he took it as a simple gesture of concern between teacher and student and smiled more genuinely. “Thank you, I’ll take care.”","Zhou Rushi seemed unable to handle Qin Yi’s smile and quickly lowered her head before hurrying away.","As she passed Ji Fei and the others, they noticed the girl’s face had turned red.","[Her secret crush is really endearing. None of us noticed, or even that supposedly devoted disciple of his, but she actually picked up on Qin Yi’s recent poor condition.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong hadn’t noticed Qin Yi’s recent state either, but they weren’t surprised that Zhou Rushi had. When you like someone, you naturally pay close attention to them. In that sense, Wan Sitong didn’t seem to care much about Qin Yi himself.","Wan Sitong’s waiting room was empty except for her. When Qin Yi knocked and entered, Wan Sitong rushed toward him like a cheerful little bird. If it weren’t for the fact that Qin Yi had brought others with him, she might have thrown herself into his arms.","Wan Sitong’s expression stiffened as she said, “Teacher, I have something to discuss with you privately...”","She then glanced at the three unwelcome guests.","Since Wan Sitong had made it clear, Qin Yi couldn’t insist on bringing them along. He turned to the three and said, “Why don’t you wait for me in the car? This shouldn’t take long.”","When Qin Yi said this, Wan Sitong looked visibly displeased.","However, Ji Fei and the others readily agreed.","But as soon as the door closed, the three of them stopped in their tracks.","They tried to eavesdrop quietly, but the soundproofing was too good. Giving up, they sat down on a bench in the hallway to wait.","At least they could use Ji Fei’s inner thoughts to imagine what was happening behind the door.","Sure enough, Ji Fei started her gossip commentary again.","[I knew it! She’s definitely not here to talk about anything proper! Haha, Cousin is getting confessed to again. Wan Sitong really hasn’t given up.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong pretended to play on their phones while frantically discussing the juicy gossip they had just stumbled upon.","“Big news, big news! We’re witnessing Cousin getting confessed to by his disciple in real time!”"]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344: Severing the Master-Disciple Relationship","paragraphs":["\"Why not? We're so perfect for each other. I'm young, beautiful, and talented. You must have feelings for me too. Otherwise, why would you have chosen me? Why would you treat me so well? You’ve guided me, helped me with my personal problems, and taken care of me wholeheartedly. You...\"","\"It's because I wanted to nurture a talented singer. I saw potential in you and didn’t want it to go to waste. That’s why I put in so much effort. After all, you’re my first disciple. I never expected you to misunderstand. There’s not a single shred of personal affection in my actions.\"","\"No, you must be lying. You don’t have any other women around you. All your time and energy are spent on me. I’m the closest to you, so you must like me. You’re just too afraid to admit it!\"","Qin Yi had initially planned to end this misunderstanding gently, but he hadn’t anticipated how difficult it would be to communicate with Wan Sitong. Seeing her completely lost in her own assumptions, he realized that unless he spoke harshly, she wouldn’t listen.","\"Just because I don’t have other women doesn’t mean I have to like you, Wan Sitong. Wake up. You’re just my disciple, and in the future, I’ll have other disciples too! You’re not the first, nor will you be the last!\"","\"I don’t believe you. I get it now—you’re worried about what people will say because of our teacher-student relationship. Fine, I’ll drop out of school. Then we won’t have that problem anymore.\" Wan Sitong was driven to desperation by the repeated rejections. She had thought that after her successful performance today, Qin Yi would finally see her excellence and waver. Everyone said how special Qin Yi was to her, how different he treated her compared to other teachers. His gentle gaze—how could he not like her?","But the next moment, Qin Yi shattered her hopes. His face turned cold as he said, \"If you drop out, then there really won’t be any relationship between us.\"","Wan Sitong was stunned. This was the first time Qin Yi had treated her with such coldness. Her already fragile emotions completely collapsed, and she burst into tears.","Suddenly, she snapped back to reality and said, \"I get it now. You just want to use my talent to boost your own sense of accomplishment. Fine, Qin Yi, let’s make a deal. If we’re together, I’ll keep singing for you. I’ll be the talented singer in your hands, making the whole world notice what an excellent teacher you are! But if you reject me, I’ll ruin my voice. I’ll never sing again!\"","Qin Yi was truly shocked. He had always thought Wan Sitong was just a bit sharp-tongued, which wasn’t necessarily a bad thing for a girl—it made her less likely to be bullied. But now, facing this situation, he realized how deeply flawed her personality was. She was completely unreasonable.","Back when he saw her conflicts with her family, he had thought she was just a pitiable child. But now it seemed...","He had been blinded by her talent. In the future, he would have to be more careful when choosing disciples.","It pained and disappointed Qin Yi to see Wan Sitong acting so irrationally. Despite the emotional attachment he felt as her first mentor, he knew he had to cut ties decisively.","\"So singing means so little to you? This is your own life. Don’t use it to threaten me,\" Qin Yi said coldly. \"You performed well today, and I’m sure you’ll receive many offers. Find someone else to guide you. I don’t need you to prove my teaching abilities to the world.\"","Wan Sitong’s face turned pale. She had never expected Qin Yi to give up on her so easily.","In a fit of desperation, she rushed forward and hugged Qin Yi tightly, trying to kiss him.","Qin Yi was completely caught off guard. He quickly pushed her away, but Wan Sitong, wearing high heels, lost her balance and fell backward. Behind her was a makeup mirror, creating a dangerous situation. Reacting swiftly, Qin Yi reached out to protect her head, but in the process, he ended up falling on top of her.","Wan Sitong, however, didn’t care about the situation. She grabbed Qin Yi’s collar and tried to force another kiss.","Just then, the door burst open.","\"Cousin, we’ve been waiting for... oh, are we interrupting something?\" Qin Zhao’s voice rang out.","Behind him were Qin Rong and Ji Fei, craning their necks to see what was happening.","Naturally, this was all because of Ji Fei’s inner thoughts. Her sudden exclamation that \"Qin Yi is about to be forced\" had alarmed Qin Zhao and Qin Rong.","Qin Zhao had immediately stood up, saying he heard something unusual and wanted to check it out.","And so, the trio made a dramatic entrance, much to Wan Sitong’s likely fury.","With their interruption, Wan Sitong missed her chance. Qin Yi shoved her away, trembling with anger. He turned and left, saying, \"We don’t need to stay in touch after this!\"","He didn’t care how much Wan Sitong called after him. He just walked away.","Qin Yi’s mood was so dark that no one dared to joke about the incident on the ride home. When they arrived at the family estate, Qin Yi went straight to his room to rest.","However, the others weren’t about to let his unfortunate experience go unmentioned. Since he hadn’t asked them to keep it a secret, they eagerly shared the juicy gossip with the rest of the family when they returned.","When Qin Jiaxi came home, everyone stopped their chatter.","Qin Jiaxi looked terrible, her clothes half-dry and her face pale.","When asked what happened, she only said it was an accident and quickly retreated to her room.","Those who couldn’t hear inner thoughts continued discussing Qin Yi’s drama, while those who could grew increasingly grim.","[What the hell? Just because Jiaxi had a fight with her boyfriend, his so-called \"fan club\" decided to bully her? Someone pretended to clean the bathroom while Jiaxi was there, then \"accidentally\" spilled a bucket of water on her. They apologized so smoothly that Jiaxi couldn’t even call them out. But she knew—this was familiar bullying behavior.]","The Qin family’s second branch was furious. Their daughter being bullied? Unthinkable!","Qin Xian, holding Ji Fei, recalled his day. During his inspection, many people had tried to meet him, especially the Su Family. His uncle had mentioned that the Su Family was interested in a marriage alliance. After all, in Y City, the two families were the most well-matched.","According to his uncle, the Su Family had many sons in this generation. Their proposal was simple: whichever son married a Qin daughter would be groomed as the family’s heir.","[Wait, is this boyfriend of Jiaxi’s even real? He doesn’t seem to care about her at all. The fight was about Yu Xin being adopted? How close is he to Yu Xin? And after Jiaxi got drenched, she couldn’t even reach him. What’s going on?]","Hearing this, Qin Xian couldn’t help but sneer. It seemed that young master wouldn’t be inheriting anything after all.","[Not only that, but Qin Han also showed up at the school today, bringing Yu Xin with him to scold Jiaxi. He even threatened her to go home with him tonight and beg their uncle for mercy...]","The second branch of the Qin family was exasperated. They really didn’t want to admit that Qin Han shared their bloodline. Unfortunately, his resemblance to the family was undeniable. In such a large family, there were bound to be a few bad apples.","[It seems Jiaxi coming here to stay tonight is her only act of resistance.]","The second branch sighed. At least Jiaxi was making some progress, even if it was small.","Dinner was a quiet affair. Qin Yi didn’t come down, still in a bad mood.","Qin Jiaxi also stayed in her room, feeling unwell, likely due to catching a cold.","The women of the family went to check on Jiaxi, leaving the men in the main hall. Shortly after they left, the men saw Qin Yi rushing out with car keys in hand.","Qin Zhao called out to him, but Qin Yi only muttered that he had urgent business and left without another word."]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345: Innocence... Damn it It's gone","paragraphs":["What could Qin Yi say? That because he rejected his disciple's confession of love, she threatened to commit suicide by cutting her wrist, forcing him to go to her school to find her.","Just now, Wan Sitong had called him on video, showing him her frantic state after cutting her wrist.","Qin Yi was genuinely frightened. He wanted to call 120 or the police, but she had anticipated and warned him against it.","Wan Sitong demanded that he come alone before she bled out, or else she would jump off a building.","Qin Yi was truly at a loss. While calling the police might have kept him out of trouble to some extent, it would also have caused everything to spiral out of control. Even if it didn’t, it would have completely ruined Wan Sitong’s future.","After all, thanks to tonight’s performance, Wan Sitong’s reputation as a prodigy had begun to spread. If a suicide scandal were to erupt now, Wan Sitong would be truly ruined.","Qin Yi still believed that Wan Sitong might just be acting out of extreme willfulness. Perhaps there was still a chance to reason with her, and at the very least, his presence might calm her down a little.","But when Qin Yi arrived at the rehearsal room location Wan Sitong had given him and pushed open the door, he was still shocked.","Wan Sitong was lying naked on the floor, blood from her wrist already pooling on the ground.","Qin Yi didn’t have time to think about anything else. Unsure of Wan Sitong’s current state, he rushed over to her.","But just as he tried to help her up, Wan Sitong suddenly raised her hand and sprayed something onto Qin Yi’s face.","Having grown up in a wealthy family, Qin Yi had seen some tricks before. In that instant, he knew something was wrong.","But before he could react, Wan Sitong had already pounced on him.","Her bold advances only made the effects of the drug kick in faster the more Qin Yi struggled. In the process, Wan Sitong tore at his clothes, leaving them disheveled.","“Wan Sitong! Have you lost your mind?” Qin Yi roared.","Wan Sitong’s eyes were swollen, clearly from crying for a long time, and now they were filled with madness. “You’re the one who’s lost your mind. I’m your beloved disciple. How could you give me to someone else? Heh, after tonight, even if you don’t want to be with me, you’ll have no choice.”","Qin Yi shouted angrily, “Wan Sitong, calm down and think about it! Do you really think sleeping together will make me take responsibility for you? You’re being naive! And what you’re doing is a crime!”","“I don’t care! All I know is that you’ve ruined me, Qin Yi. You’ve watched me suffer and ignored my feelings. Aren’t you my teacher? Why are you treating me like this? You’re driving me to death! Why are you so cruel?”","Qin Yi felt completely unable to communicate with her. Was he ruining her just because he didn’t give in to her demands?","If anything, it was Wan Sitong who was trying to ruin him. But he could no longer speak coherently.","Qin Yi, who had always been dedicated to music and lived a clean, disciplined life, had no experience with such situations. The drug hit him hard, and he lost control. For a moment, he even flipped Wan Sitong over and pinned her beneath him.","Just as Wan Sitong thought she was about to succeed, Qin Yi caught a clear glimpse of her face. In that instant, a wave of nausea overwhelmed his physical reaction, and his rationality returned briefly.","Suddenly, he headbutted her.","Wan Sitong was knocked senseless, while Qin Yi, though dizzy from the impact, regained enough clarity to scramble off her and stumble out of the room.","His vision was blurred, but he knew he had to lock himself away and call for help immediately.","He found a nearby rehearsal room, rushed in, locked the door, and pulled out his phone to send a message... but then his consciousness faded.","He vaguely remembered hearing a woman’s voice, but he wasn’t sure if it was Wan Sitong, the lunatic, chasing after him.","Meanwhile, back at the Qin Family Mansion, Ji Fei and the others were still focused on Qin Jiaxi’s situation.","Although Ji Fei knew all the gossip, she had only heard about it from Qin Jiaxi and hadn’t met her boyfriend or Su Ze, so many details remained unclear.","But Ji Fei was still deeply suspicious.","Half of the people present knew the truth, while the other half didn’t. When they asked Qin Jiaxi, she only said it was an accident caused by a classmate. What else could she say? After all, they couldn’t retaliate against someone for a simple accident. They couldn’t even report it to the police.","But Qin Jiaxi didn’t mention how many times this kind of “accident” had happened over the past year.","Now, Qin Jiaxi seemed to be in a state of confusion, unable to articulate anything clearly because she herself wasn’t entirely sure.","On top of that, the young girl seemed oddly reluctant to seek help from others. Was it because she felt family matters shouldn’t be aired in public, or because... her past attempts to seek help had never succeeded, so she had grown accustomed to not asking for help?","[Oh, Jiaxi, Jiaxi, your suspicions are spot on! Ever since Su Ze confessed to you, you’ve been bullied by his fan club. It’s not just some girls being jealous because they have a crush on him. This has been outright bullying for over a year! Are you so used to being mistreated by your family that you can’t even recognize the severity of the bullying?]","[And you should think about two things. First, if you revealed your identity as the Qin family’s eldest daughter, no one would dare bully you. The fact that your family forbids it is already suspicious. Second, since the bullying is happening because of Su Ze, as your boyfriend, shouldn’t he step up and warn them? Is he just going to stand by and watch you get bullied?]","Ji Fei had a thousand thoughts running through her mind but couldn’t voice them.","Seeing how pitiful the girl was, she knew it would take a long time for Qin Jiaxi to wake up to the truth. In the meantime, she would continue to suffer.","As she pondered this, a sudden idea struck her, and she smiled, saying, “Let’s find an opportunity to visit your school together. Isn’t it the top-ranked university in the area? You can be our guide.”","Qin Yan and Qin Rong immediately understood Ji Fei’s intentions and chimed in to support the idea.","The others were also curious, as they had never been there before.","Qin Jiaxi, however, didn’t think much of it and simply nodded, agreeing to take them on a tour when her schedule allowed.","Seeing how exhausted the girl was, everyone decided not to press further. Once they were sure she was fine, they all went downstairs.","Downstairs, Qin Jing asked curiously, “Why did it take so long? Is Jiaxi not doing well?”","“No, we were just chatting,” Qin Xiaoyu replied.","As Ji Fei took her seat, Qin Zhao, who was always sharp when it came to gossip, smiled and said, “Cousin Qin Yi rushed off in a hurry earlier. Do you think his disciple contacted him again?”","Though phrased as a guess, everyone in the Qin family knew he was waiting for Ji Fei to spill the tea.","Hearing this, Ji Fei naturally became curious.","But as she began to investigate, the smile on her face froze before it could fully form. Those who were sneakily watching her saw her expression suddenly stiffen, followed by a look of utter shock.","[Oh my god, oh my god, oh my god! A suicide threat... naked advances...]","The Qin family: So it really happened. Qin Yi was set up again.","Qin Xian: Cousin Qin Yi probably didn’t give in.","[Oh no, oh no! He was drugged and pinned down... Oh heavens! Is there still time to save him?!]","The Qin family: !!!!","Qin Xian: ?","In an instant, several people on the sofa looked like they were about to jump to their feet.","[Thankfully, he escaped... his innocence... Oh crap! It’s gone! This is such a soap opera! What a rollercoaster!]"]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346: One Doesn't Remember, the Other Doesn't Want to Be Exposed","paragraphs":["The Qin Second family: Is this the rollercoaster in our hearts? So, is there still a need to save him? It’s already done!","Qin Xian: Who?","[Is this fate? Is it destined that cousin will lose his innocence tonight? If that’s the case, Zhou Rushi is slightly better than Wan Sitong.]","The Qin Second family: The secret admirer?!!!!","Qin Xian frowned slightly.","While this group was shocked, and the others were confused by their eerie silence, Qin Xian’s phone vibrated.","He took it out and his expression changed instantly.","“Cousin is in trouble, he’s asking us to save him,” Qin Xian said gravely, then showed the message to everyone.","It was a message from Qin Yi’s number, including a plea for help and an address.","[How is this possible? After it was over, cousin should have been unconscious... Huh? It turns out Zhou Rushi sent the message. She heard the ambulance outside and was worried someone might find out, so she asked for their help.]","At this moment, it should have been Qin Wenqiang, Qin Yi’s sister, who reacted first. But the Qin Second family had already started moving before the others could even process what was happening.","However, too many people shouldn’t go, given the sensitive situation. Qin Xian made a quick decision.","In the end, Qin Xian, Ji Fei, and Qin Zhao, led by Qin Wenqiang, rushed to the location while the others stayed home to wait for news.","Qin Zhao was responsible for driving, and he sped through the streets.","Qin Wenqiang finally reacted and immediately turned to Qin Xian, asking, “Shouldn’t we call the police?”","[In this situation, we definitely can’t call the police! If we do, cousin, being a teacher, would have a hard time explaining himself.]","Qin Xian calmly reasoned, “If he could call the police, he would have done so directly instead of contacting me. The fact that he reached out to me means it’s likely a sensitive issue that requires discreet handling. For now, it’s best to act in secret.”","Ji Fei, sitting next to Qin Xian, perked up upon hearing this.","[Wow, my husband is so smart! Indeed, when Qin Yi faced such a serious problem and didn’t know what to do, he instinctively turned to the most capable person—you! Before losing consciousness, he had already selected your contact on his phone but didn’t have time to call. That’s why Zhou Rushi, when seeking help, chose to message you. She judged that you were the person Qin Yi would most want to turn to in this situation.]","Qin Zhao: This girl is quite clever.","Qin Xian... felt his wife’s admiring gaze.","Soon, under the cover of night, they arrived at the rehearsal building.","The room was on the third floor.","There were quite a few students on the road. It seemed the ambulance had caused a stir, and everyone was talking about it.","“I heard someone attempted suicide.”","“Really? I heard someone was drugged and...”","“I heard the person involved is Wan Sitong, the genius who just made a big splash today.”","“Could it be someone jealous and seeking revenge?”","“Or maybe she got tangled up with some wealthy sponsor?”","“No way, her teacher is Qin Yi. From what I know, Qin Yi is someone of high status and influence. Ordinary people wouldn’t dare mess with him.”","“I saw Teacher Qin earlier. Did he come because he knew Wan Sitong was in trouble?”","Since people weren’t clear about the timeline, their reasoning was all over the place.","Ji Fei, however, already knew the situation.","[Oh, I see. After Wan Sitong regained consciousness, she realized she had lost too much blood from her wrist. She didn’t have the strength to get up and, fearing death, called for an ambulance. This alarmed the school staff. Many saw her being carried away in disheveled clothes. She brought this on herself.]","As she thought this, they arrived at the designated location.","Qin Zhao instinctively knocked on the door, probably afraid of what they might see.","Ji Fei was also excited and curious, wondering how things would go when they met Zhou Rushi.","After all, such situations don’t happen every day.","But there was no response from inside. Qin Wenqiang, naturally worried about her brother, pushed the door open and saw Qin Yi slumped unconscious against the wall.","His clothes were disheveled but still on, with nothing indecent exposed.","What was most surprising was that Qin Yi was alone in the room.","While Qin Wenqiang rushed to check on her brother, the others looked around but found no one else.","[What’s going on? Let me check... Damn, the girl is secretly observing from the next room... Oh? I see. She doesn’t want anyone to know what happened between her and Qin Yi.]","Qin Zhao: Why? Isn’t she Qin Yi’s secret admirer? If something happened, shouldn’t she seize the opportunity? Why hide?","Qin Xian didn’t overthink it. Instead, he checked Qin Yi’s condition and suggested they take him to the hospital themselves.","Qin Wenqiang, recalling the rumors she had just heard, began to form some unpleasant conjectures.","At a time like this, it was crucial to avoid drawing attention.","So, with Qin Xian and Qin Zhao supporting Qin Yi, they pretended he was drunk and quietly took a secluded route out of the school.","[She really... didn’t stop watching until we left the building. She’s concerned about Qin Yi but genuinely doesn’t plan to reveal herself. There’s no struggle at all. It seems that if Qin Yi had even a shred of rationality or if Zhou Rushi had a choice, this wouldn’t have happened. Even though she’s a secret admirer, Zhou Rushi is different from Wan Sitong. She doesn’t want to win her crush’s affection in such a despicable way. She feels like she took advantage of the situation and is deeply remorseful. In comparison, Wan Sitong is even more despicable.]","[But if Qin Yi remembers, this matter might not be over.]","Hearing Ji Fei’s thoughts, even Qin Zhao was curious about whether Qin Yi would remember anything and how he would handle the situation afterward.","Soon, they arrived at the Qin family’s private hospital.","After an injection, Qin Yi quickly woke up.","The moment he regained consciousness, he sat up abruptly, clutching his throbbing head, looking dazed.","“Qin Yi, how are you feeling?” Qin Wenqiang asked worriedly.","Qin Yi was startled. He turned to see everyone and, upon spotting Qin Xian, sighed in relief. “I did manage to contact you. I thought I hadn’t gotten through.”","This reaction...","Apart from Qin Wenqiang, the other three had complicated expressions.","[This is such a mess. One doesn’t remember, and the other doesn’t want it exposed. What am I supposed to do, having learned the truth? Logically... since the parties involved are handling it this way, I should probably do nothing.]","Qin Zhao: ...I’m really speechless about cousin. Can’t he tell if something happened to his own body? I was planning to enjoy the drama, but now... I can’t stir up trouble. I have to keep this secret. Otherwise, wouldn’t I be bullying the girl? After all, this is her choice.","Qin Xian also knew that if this matter were to come to light, it should be Qin Yi who discovers it or Zhou Rushi who reveals it. Others shouldn’t interfere.","“You sent me a message, and that’s how we found you.”","Qin Yi was stunned. “A message?”","Ji Fei and Qin Zhao’s hearts skipped a beat. Would he figure it out?","Qin Xian naturally couldn’t hide it, as Qin Yi’s phone had the records."]},{"number":347,"title":"Chapter 347: False Accusation with Just a Mouth","paragraphs":["Qin Yi was currently in a state of confusion, so he didn't particularly care whether he was sending a message or making a call. He simply thought he was under the influence of medication and had, in a daze, sent a message to Qin Xian. Even the unfamiliar sensations coursing through his body now were likely due to resisting the effects of the drugs.","At this moment, all his attention was focused on the matter concerning Wan Sitong.","\"I must have been blind to have encountered such a crazy woman!\" Qin Yi was truly furious, pounding the hospital bed in anger.","Qin Wenqiang immediately pressed him for details about what had happened.","Qin Yi recounted the events, and then others filled him in on what they had heard along the way.","Upon hearing that Wan Sitong had been taken away by an ambulance, Qin Yi was equally incensed.","\"That girl got what she deserved, nearly killing herself with her suicide attempt,\" Qin Wenqiang said coldly, her face stern. \"Qin Yi, I'll handle this matter for you.\"","The implication was clear: Wan Sitong was going to be taught a lesson.","The Qin family might be kind-hearted, but that didn’t mean they could be easily manipulated. Those who provoked them would pay the price.","No one played the saint here, and Qin Yi didn’t try to stop his sister. He knew his eldest sister was protective and had a good sense of judgment.","After a long night of chaos, Qin Yi was left alone in the hospital for observation, while the others returned to the family estate to rest.","Ji Fei was also exhausted, sleeping until noon.","Before she could fully wake up, there was a rapid knocking at the door, accompanied by Qin Rong's voice. \"Sister-in-law, sister-in-law, something's happened! Are you awake?\"","Ji Fei was startled and quickly got up to open the door, only to find Qin Yan, Qin Rong, and Qin Jiaxi waiting outside for her.","Ji Fei asked in surprise, \"What's going on?\"","Qin Rong anxiously replied, \"That woman has falsely accused our eldest cousin. He's been summoned by the police.\"","Ji Fei exclaimed, \"What?\"","Qin Jiaxi quickly handed her phone to Ji Fei, the screen displaying a trending post on Y City’s university student forum.","\"Sister-in-law... this has the most comprehensive and up-to-date information...\" Qin Jiaxi had only learned about the situation after hearing her classmates discuss it at school.","By the time she contacted everyone, it was already too late—the police had already gone to see Qin Yi.","\"Qin Xian and the others heard the news and rushed over from the headquarters. Eldest sister and Qin Zhao also left as soon as they heard. We came to get you so we can go together,\" Qin Yan explained.","Ji Fei was still full of questions. If anyone should be filing a complaint, it should be them against Wan Sitong.","How could Wan Sitong possibly accuse Qin Yi?","Ji Fei was utterly baffled. She quickly freshened up, changed her clothes, and set off with the others.","In the car, she took Qin Jiaxi's phone to read the post while simultaneously using her system to investigate the situation.","The post was published anonymously, but Ji Fei had already uncovered the truth through her system.","[Despite having lost so much blood last night that she fainted and was hospitalized, she still managed to angrily edit and anonymously post this defamatory content against Qin Yi in the middle of the night. This is truly a case of 'if I can't have you, I'll destroy you.' This woman is indeed a lunatic.]","In the post, Wan Sitong portrayed herself as a pure and passionate music student who had been thrilled to become Qin Yi's apprentice. However, she claimed that Qin Yi was a demon who used his position as her teacher to harass and intimidate her. She painted herself as powerless and vulnerable, while Qin Yi was depicted as a powerful figure with significant influence. She claimed that Qin Yi had tried to control and manipulate her, even attempting to force himself on her when she resisted.","Under this narrative, many photos, audio clips, and videos were posted.","The photos showed some physical contact during their past teaching sessions, but with the narrative already set, even normal interactions were twisted into something sinister.","The audio clips were taken out of context.","Two dialogues in particular were highly misleading.","\"...You're crazy! I’m your beloved student. How could you...\" This was Wan Sitong's tearful voice.","\"...Did you think sleeping with me would make me responsible for you? How naive!\" This was Qin Yi's angry voice.","As the audio played in the car, the others, who had already heard it, couldn’t help but comment.","\"That's Qin Yi's voice, right? But how could he say something like that?\" Qin Yan asked.","Qin Jiaxi, who had seen some analysis posts, said with a shaky voice, \"Someone has already verified that the audio isn’t synthesized. But we don’t know the full context of what was said.\"","Qin Rong added, \"Even though we know it’s fake and taken out of context, those words are really misleading. No wonder she dared to falsely accuse him...\"","[She dared to make this false accusation purely out of impulse, without thinking it through, and without considering the consequences. Like those who spread malicious rumors without a second thought, she acted on a whim. The dialogue actually happened last night, but she selectively edited the audio to mislead people. Who would have thought she had recorded everything in that rehearsal room? If she had succeeded last night, would she have forced Qin Yi to marry her? It’s truly disgusting.]","Those who could hear Ji Fei's thoughts were furious.","Ji Fei continued reading the post.","Sure enough, there were also videos, each only a few seconds long, but highly misleading.","The last few clips included the scene in the waiting room where she fell backward, and Qin Yi tried to catch her. It was edited to make it look like Qin Yi had intentionally pounced on her, trying to kiss her while she was in tears.","Then there was the footage from last night’s room. It was clear that Wan Sitong had gone to extreme lengths. In the video, she was crying while straddling Qin Yi, with both their bodies partially blurred. It gave the impression that she was being forced into something with Qin Yi.","The video was hard to interpret, especially since Wan Sitong was indeed not wearing any clothes, despite the blurring.","The clips were too short to determine the truth, but anyone coming across the post would naturally assume the worst.","The post concluded with Wan Sitong’s suicide attempt, which, in the eyes of the public, solidified her status as the victim.","The conclusion was almost set in stone. Although there were still voices of dissent—such as those from students and teachers who knew Qin Yi well, or people who knew his background, or even those who simply looked at Qin Yi’s face and thought he had no reason to do such a thing—the majority of strangers online were condemning Qin Yi.","By the time Ji Fei finished reading, the story had already spread rapidly online, with a flood of criticism.","Meanwhile, at the police station, many students and teachers from the academy had been called in for questioning.","Qin Yi was being interrogated.","Qin Wenqiang was furiously confronting Wan Sitong’s parents.","Qin Zhao, holding his phone, couldn’t stop complaining and showed it to Qin Xian. \"Second brother, look at this. If this continues, things will get really messy. Most people aren’t willing to judge the truth. When they see something like this, their first instinct is to side with the perceived victim and vilify the powerful. The more perfect the powerful person seems, the more people are inclined to assume the worst.\"","Rumors spread like wildfire, while debunking them is an uphill battle. Even if the truth comes out later, how many people will actually see it?"]},{"number":348,"title":"Chapter 348: I Have a Bold Idea","paragraphs":["Qin Xian glanced around, understanding that due to the lag in information, people tend to take the first impression as the main narrative. Even when faced with the truth, they might start spinning conspiracy theories.","After all, Qin Yi is a teacher, and Wan Sitong is a student. Wan Sitong is in a weaker position.","Qin Yi is the eldest son of the Qin Family, while Wan Sitong is an ordinary person. Wan Sitong is disadvantaged.","So, from the moment Wan Sitong exposed this matter, Qin Yi was already tainted. His reputation as a music teacher had been completely damaged.","Although Qin Wenqiang had already arranged for public relations to handle the online public opinion, it was difficult to control the forums and group chats circulating among university students.","As Qin Xian was pondering this, he received a message from his wife, Ji Fei, asking how things were going.","\"We're still investigating. Don't worry, we've already arranged for someone to gather evidence. This matter isn't hard to handle,\" Qin Xian replied.","Indeed, it wasn't difficult. If the Qin Family could be manipulated by such clumsy framing, it would be laughable.","Even if all the original video and audio files had been edited and deleted by Wan Sitong, they still had ways to recover them.","With some evidence of Wan Sitong's infatuation, the truth would soon come to light.","The hard part is dealing with the subsequent public opinion,\" Qin Xian honestly informed Ji Fei, letting her in on the latest developments.","After waiting for a while without a response, Qin Xian sent another message, \"Did you just wake up and get called here? Have you eaten yet?\"","Still no reply. Concerned, Qin Xian asked Qin Zhao to prepare some food and drinks, in case Ji Fei arrived hungry while catching up on the drama.","Qin Zhao, who was passionately browsing the internet, rolled his eyes at his older brother's request but obediently went to buy some nearby snacks.","Not long after, Qin Xian received a message from Ji Fei.","They had arrived, but Ji Fei had a question.","\"There are so many reporters at the entrance.\"","\"Remember to wear masks when you come in,\" Qin Xian reminded her.","Ji Fei replied, \"I suddenly have a bold idea...\"","Soon after, another group of people entered the Police Station. The staff assumed they were more relatives of the Qin Family, given their prominence, and didn't pay much attention.","Coincidentally, Qin Zhao also returned at this time.","Qin Xian took the food from Ji Fei and reminded his wife not to go hungry.","Ji Fei herself had forgotten that she hadn't eaten anything since waking up, as the whole situation had her adrenaline pumping.","\"How far along are things?\"","Just as Qin Xian was about to answer, Qin Yi was brought out. His face was grim, clearly furious at Wan Sitong's underhanded tactics.","As soon as he stepped out, he was met with a mix of students and teachers, their expressions varied. Some of the doubtful looks made Qin Yi feel utterly absurd.","Of course, some students stepped forward to express their belief in Qin Yi.","Ji Fei immediately noticed an important figure among them, \"Zhou Rushi?\"","[She's here too? Wait, that means she's living proof? Hmm... If we need to prove anything, she'd have to reveal the truth about last night. This... is tricky. Thankfully, the police only asked about Qin Yi's usual relationship with Wan Sitong, and she truthfully said Wan Sitong liked Qin Yi. If they asked what she was doing last night, the girl might not dare to lie.]","Qin Yi exchanged a few words with the students and also said something to Zhou Rushi, his attitude making things quite clear... Zhou Rushi's expression also shifted.","[It seems Zhou Rushi has realized Qin Yi doesn't remember last night. This makes her even more reluctant to reveal anything, as she truly wants to pretend last night never happened.]","Oh dear, she's looking over here. Is she looking at the Qin Family? Ah, she thinks the Qin Family can handle this, so it's best not to disclose what happened last night, lest their relationship gets dragged into the online public opinion, making the situation even more complicated.","Upon hearing these thoughts, the Qin Family couldn't help but glance back and forth between Zhou Rushi and Qin Yi.","One was clueless, the other putting on a convincing act.","Qin Xian, however, thought Zhou Rushi's reasoning was sound. If another teacher-student relationship were brought into the mix, the public opinion might not be favorable.","And even if Zhou Rushi admitted to being with Qin Yi last night... how could they prove it?","Amidst the chaos, Wan Sitong burst out, crying and screaming at Qin Yi, \"It's you! You ruined my life! You tried to force yourself on me! How dare you deny it and even slander me instead! I can't live like this, I can't!\"","Everyone was shocked. Wan Sitong looked utterly deranged, like someone who had been deeply wronged and traumatized, shaking the confidence of even those who believed in Qin Yi.","However, Wan Sitong's parents stepped forward and slapped her several times, shouting, \"You troublemaker! Who told you to call the police? Who told you to stir up this scandal? Withdraw your complaint and say it was all your delusion!\"","This only made things more chaotic, with many stepping in to break up the fight.","But Wan Sitong stubbornly refused to back down.","[Now we know why Wan Sitong is so unhinged. With parents like these, who don't even bother to verify the truth and, because of Qin Yi's status, completely disregard their daughter, treating her actions as if they bring shame to the family, it's no wonder she turned out this way.]","[Wan Sitong is also laughable. She just wanted to get back at Qin Yi, to force him to apologize. She even thought that if Qin Yi regretted his actions, she could retract her statements, not realizing that once words are spoken, they can't be taken back.]","Hearing this, the Qin Family was thoroughly disgusted. What a massive mess caused by someone so reckless, ignorant, and foolish.","Once the police finally managed to calm things down, Qin Yi spoke coldly, \"Wan Sitong, I never imagined you could be this insane. Just because I rejected you, you want to destroy me? Do you think you can get away with this? Don't worry, I won't let you off either. Your defamation and the fact that you drugged me last night, trying to force yourself on me—these are all crimes. I won't forgive you. You'll face the full force of the law.\"","Wan Sitong likely didn't expect Qin Yi to counter-sue her, assuming he'd be too busy defending himself. His cold, ruthless demeanor shook her, as she had never seen him like this before.","\"You... you hurt me, and instead of apologizing, you threaten me? No matter how powerful your family is, I will expose you... You don't deserve to be a music teacher. You don't deserve to love music.\" Wan Sitong was trying to use Qin Yi's career as leverage.","But Qin Yi, faced with her almost nonsensical ranting, simply scoffed.","\"The worst mistake I ever made was taking you on as my student.\""]},{"number":349,"title":"Chapter 349: What a Bandit Logic","paragraphs":["Qin Yi's words left Wan Sitong feeling ice-cold all over, rendering her momentarily speechless.","After that, no matter how Wan Sitong pretended to cry and complain, hinting that she might consider signing a letter of forgiveness if Qin Yi apologized and took responsibility, he ignored her completely.","To the onlookers, Wan Sitong's behavior was nothing short of laughable.","By then, Qin Corporation's team had already easily retrieved evidence from Wan Sitong's electronic devices, which had been provided by her own parents.","Of course, even without Qin Corporation, the police would have eventually found the evidence—it was only a matter of time.","It could only be said that Wan Sitong had underestimated the world, thinking her petty tricks could easily deceive everyone.","The evidence submitted by the Qin Family Legal Team was quickly reviewed, and by the time the police reappeared, Wan Sitong's fate was sealed.","Seeing this scene, Wan Sitong, already guilty and panicked, immediately began to shout.","\"He used his position as a teacher to assault me! Why aren't you arresting him? I've made myself clear enough. What more do you want? I get it—you're all in cahoots! I'm going to report you!\" Wan Sitong continued to play the victim, as if it were her greatest shield.","The police officers' expressions darkened. They had seen many criminals who tried to shift blame, but this level of ingratitude and distortion of the truth was a first. One officer sternly said, \"We have received the complete video and chat records. The edited versions circulating online have been debunked. The evidence proves that you falsely accused Mr. Qin Yi, and now we will hold you legally accountable.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, the room erupted in murmurs, and everyone turned their gaze to Wan Sitong.","Although they had mentally prepared themselves, facing such an outrageous situation still felt absurdly terrifying.","Was this the behavior expected of a promising, talented singer?","Wan Sitong froze for a moment but quickly clung to her stubborn belief that it couldn't be true—she had definitely deleted everything. \"How is this possible? You're all ganging up on me, a female student, to protect a criminal! I... I would rather die than prove my innocence!\" she screamed, even attempting to throw herself against the wall to \"prove\" her innocence.","With the police present, she naturally didn't succeed, but the officers were still shaken. She had genuinely intended to harm herself, regardless of the consequences. If something happened to Wan Sitong before the trial, the media outside would surely spin it as a coerced confession.","[This girl is truly unhinged... Well, it seems her parents' constant arguing at home, with her mother using similar threats against her father, has left its mark.]","Qin Second's family glanced at Wan Sitong's parents, who seemed utterly indifferent to their daughter's fate. It was hard to judge.","No wonder Wan Sitong, having encountered someone who genuinely cared for her, became so desperate to possess them—and if she couldn't, to destroy them. This was the behavior she had learned from her parents.","Seeing Wan Sitong still acting hysterical, Qin Xian turned to the lawyer who had just arrived and said something.","The lawyer promptly pulled out a laptop, placed it on the table, and began playing the original videos for everyone to see.","Unlike the short, edited clips circulating online, these videos included the original audio.","When Wan Sitong's voice confessing her feelings came through the video, the room fell silent.","Even Wan Sitong, restrained by the police, was stunned.","The teachers and students who had come as witnesses crowded around to watch, with even strangers pushing to the front.","Wan Sitong finally realized the police weren't bluffing. Frantically, she tried to rush forward, but the crowd was too dense, leaving her no path to intervene. She could only stare at Qin Yi with panic and resentment.","\"Don't watch! Stop watching! It's not like that, it's not like that!\"","But her screams couldn't drown out the video playing at full volume.","By the time the backstage footage from the concert finished playing, the truth was laid bare for all to see.","What followed were even more explosive videos, though due to privacy concerns, even with blurred images, they couldn't be publicly displayed without risking legal repercussions. However, the audio alone served as sufficient evidence.","Once everything had been played, there were no more doubts.","\"I've seen the edited versions online. So this is the truth? She was the one who threw herself at him, tried to force herself on her teacher, and then used her own future to blackmail him?\"","\"This is utterly disgusting. Now I understand what it means to take things out of context and twist the truth. This was a deliberate attempt to incite online harassment.\"","\"I never imagined our department's prodigy could be like this. I... I almost felt sorry for her earlier.\"","\"Wan Sitong, your teacher treated you well. How could you do this? You're utterly ungrateful!\" someone couldn't hold back and turned to berate Wan Sitong.","\"Do you realize how fortunate you were? Without your teacher's guidance, where would you be today? Instead of being grateful, you tried to ruin him!\" someone else fumed, as Wan Sitong had been given opportunities they could only dream of.","Another teacher lamented, \"Wan Sitong, you really shouldn't have done this. Qin Yi worked tirelessly to guide you.\"","But these accusations of her being heartless and ungrateful fell on deaf ears. Wan Sitong only glared at Qin Yi with venom, as if he were her mortal enemy.","\"The evidence is irrefutable. Do you have anything else to say?\" Qin Wenqiang, seeing her still daring to look at her brother like that, was furious. \"To plot such a malicious scheme against your mentor—do you have no conscience at all?\"","\"So what if I framed him? It's all his fault! His fault! I even attempted suicide for him, was willing to risk everything for him. I loved him so much, but he—cold and heartless—still rejected me. Why? After all I've done, why would he treat me like this?\" Her eyes bloodshot, she continued to scream and shout in defiance.","[It's truly baffling how some people's morals can be so twisted. Anyone with a shred of sanity would find this incomprehensible.]","Qin Second's family expressed their complete bewilderment.","The others were equally infuriated by Wan Sitong's warped logic, but fortunately, Qin Wenqiang stepped in to rebuke her.","Qin Wenqiang couldn't help but laugh bitterly. \"Over the years, countless women have admired my brother. If every one of them acted like you, would he be responsible for them all? Your actions are your own. Why should anyone else bear the consequences? Since when is love a transaction? I've seen shameless people, but you take the cake. What kind of delusional dream are you living in, thinking you can get everything by throwing a tantrum?\"","Wan Sitong turned pale with rage but continued to glare at Qin Yi with hatred.","Qin Yi met her gaze coldly.","Wan Sitong suddenly looked aggrieved. \"I hate you! If you couldn't love me, why were you so kind to me? You made me fall for you, only to reject me. This is all your fault!\""]},{"number":350,"title":"Chapter 350: Live Streaming Now","paragraphs":["Qin Yi, a man of such kindness, had truly suffered the greatest malice this time.","He had never imagined that his good intentions would turn into a blade pointed at himself.","All he had done was cherish talent, pity Wan Sitong for living in such a difficult family situation, and wish to nurture another world-class talent for the country...","Yet, all of this had brought him immense suffering.","As the saying goes, pitiable people often have their own flaws, and some are simply not worth treating well.","Looking at Wan Sitong, who remained unrepentant, he sneered coldly, \"You're right, it's my fault. So rest assured, I won't be kind to you anymore.\"","Hearing this, Wan Sitong's expression went blank.","[Heh, it should be said that no one will treat Wan Sitong well from now on. After all, once the truth of this matter is revealed, it’s like the story of the farmer and the snake. Wan Sitong has truly taught everyone a lesson—who would dare be kind to her now, only to be stabbed in the back later?]","The Qin family, including the second son’s household, agreed. Who would dare treat Wan Sitong well now? It would be sheer foolishness, wouldn’t it? Who wouldn’t fear being bitten by an ungrateful wolf?","It could only be said that Wan Sitong’s attempt to gain attention through online harassment had backfired on her.","Thinking of this, Qin Zhao, who was sensitive to online trends, stroked his chin and leaned over to his second brother, saying, \"Even if the truth comes out, won’t it be too late by the time the police conclude the investigation and release it online? The direction of public opinion is...\"","He had been discussing this with his second brother earlier, as handling public opinion was always troublesome, especially for people like them who were seen as \"powerful.\" They were more likely to be harshly judged by the public.","Even if the truth came out, people would still speculate about conspiracies.","\"If Wan Sitong were to apologize, maybe some damage could be mitigated. But looking at her crazed state, is that even possible?\" Qin Zhao clicked his tongue.","As soon as he finished speaking, he suddenly heard his sister-in-law, who was being held by his second brother, chuckle softly.","Before he could figure out why, Qin Xian smirked and nodded at the lawyer in the distance.","The lawyer, receiving the signal, suddenly spoke to Wan Sitong, \"Miss Wan, if you are willing to issue a statement admitting your mistakes and clearing Mr. Qin Yi’s name, we might consider showing leniency.\"","At this, some of the school teachers urged Wan Sitong to admit her wrongdoing.","But Wan Sitong, with her foolish temperament, would never back down. Or perhaps she didn’t fully grasp the severity of criminal charges and imprisonment, thinking that all she had done was make a scene after a failed romantic pursuit—nothing too serious. Still, she felt a twinge of guilt.","However, when her parents stepped forward and tried to force her to comply, she exploded in a fit of rage.","She pushed and shoved her parents, not daring to say anything to them directly, but screamed in anger, \"I won’t do it! Even if I’m sued, I’ll drag down the person who betrayed my feelings with me!\"","Wan Sitong turned to Qin Yi, her face twisted with madness, and shouted, \"It’s your loss for not wanting me! You were supposed to save me from this abyss, but you refused to give me a home. It’s all your fault! You deserve this revenge. I know you want to clear your name online, but forget it! As long as I don’t apologize, even if the evidence is uploaded, it won’t matter.\"","\"Those jealous worms will keep biting at you, and everyone will think it’s all fabricated. The self-righteous keyboard warriors online will keep doubting you. I can keep playing the victim. In that case, how can you keep being a teacher?\"","\"People will never fully trust you again. The fact that I, your female student, fell for you and even attempted suicide for you—that’s a stain you’ll never wash off. Hahahaha!\"","Wan Sitong’s face was twisted with madness, as if she had given up completely. Everyone looked at her as if she were a lunatic, finding her behavior unbelievable.","Yet, they couldn’t deny that what Wan Sitong said... was very likely to happen.","Even Qin Yi felt a pang of pain in his chest at her words.","The rest of the Qin family was furious.","\"Wan Sitong, you’re truly vile. Do you remember what you said when Teacher Qin took you as his student?\" Zhou Rushi suddenly stepped forward.","Seeing her beloved treated like this, Zhou Rushi’s eyes were red with anger. Though she wasn’t one to usually speak up, she couldn’t hold back anymore.","Qin Yi was stunned and turned to look at Zhou Rushi.","Wan Sitong, startled by the shout, seemed to recall something, her face flickering with confusion.","Zhou Rushi continued, \"You said that Qin Yi was your great benefactor, and that you would sing well in the future to repay his kindness. Is this how you repay him?\"","Wan Sitong felt a surge of shame and anger, as if she were being confronted with a past version of herself that she no longer wanted to acknowledge.","\"Shut up! Don’t think I don’t know about you...!\" Wan Sitong’s emotions boiled over. She wanted to expose everyone who liked Qin Yi—if she couldn’t have him, no one else could. She wanted everyone to suffer.","\"Hey, your evil plan might not work out,\" Ji Fei suddenly interrupted. \"Check your phone. It’s live-streaming. Everything you just said has been broadcasted.\"","At this, everyone in the room froze.","[I was going to let Wan Sitong keep playing the fool, but I couldn’t let this lunatic expose Zhou Rushi’s crush on Qin Yi in front of the live stream. Who knows what kind of trouble that would cause? After all, Zhou Rushi meant well, and we can’t let her suffer for it.]","But Ji Fei’s words had already caused a massive uproar.","What? A live stream?","Here? Someone’s live-streaming?","Everyone began looking around and noticed a young stranger near a laptop—someone who wasn’t part of the Qin family or the school staff—holding a phone, looking awkward.","The police naturally wanted to stop the live stream, as this was a police station.","But everything had already been broadcasted—unedited, live, and all the ugly truths had been laid bare.","When everyone picked up their phones to check, they could see the comments flying by.","People were furious, practically wishing they could personally confront Wan Sitong.","After all, the netizens had not only seen the truth but had also heard Wan Sitong’s plan to insult and manipulate them, using them as tools.","When Wan Sitong shakily took out her phone and saw the comments, her face turned as pale as paper.","\"What the hell? Who does she think we are?\"","\"I’m a keyboard warrior, not an online troll, okay?\"","\"This bitch is pure evil! Don’t worry, we won’t fall for her tricks! Since she loves online harassment so much, let’s give her a taste of her own medicine!\"","\"I’m speechless. It’s because of people like her that women who’ve actually been wronged have such a hard time seeking justice. She’s not just targeting men—she’s dragging down women too. She’s a disgrace! Any woman who sympathizes with her must be out of their mind!\"","\"People like her should be locked up for life, so they can’t harm anyone else.\"","\"Someone like her deserves to never know love!\"","If there was a 30% chance that some netizens would still believe in conspiracy theories even after the police released the truth, now the number of people who doubted Qin Yi had dropped to 0.001%."]},{"number":351,"title":"Chapter 351: It's a Lucky Star","paragraphs":["The abuse from the live stream quickly spilled over onto the internet. By the time Wan Sitong checked her phone, it was already vibrating incessantly with a flood of hateful messages.","The online storm she had orchestrated against Qin Yi had now turned against her, and she had effectively sealed her own fate with her actions.","Once, her future had seemed bright, with the potential to become a renowned singer and make a name for herself.","But now, she would be remembered throughout Y City as the ungrateful, heartless betrayer.","This time, Wan Sitong couldn't hold it together any longer and broke down in tears.","As the police dragged her away, she turned to Qin Yi and cried out, \"Do you really hate me that much? Was all the care you showed me in the past just a lie? Are you so cruel that you don't even want me to live?\"","Her final reaction left everyone stunned.","[Is she implying that what she did to Qin Yi only ruined his reputation, which is insignificant, but if Qin Yi retaliated in the same way, her entire life would be destroyed? So, in comparison, Qin Yi is the crueler one?]","The Qin Second family: What a twisted logic! She’s completely unrepentant.","Qin Xian believed that someone like her would never reflect on her actions, so he decided to hire the best lawyer for this case to ensure her prison sentence would be as long as possible, delaying her return to society and her potential to cause more harm.","After all, everyone must face the consequences of their actions.","When faced with Wan Sitong's final question, Qin Yi no longer held back. He replied coldly, \"I think you really want to live, considering you were the one who called the ambulance for yourself.\"","This was the first time anyone had heard Qin Yi speak with such biting sarcasm.","Wan Sitong was completely shattered. Her hypocritical, obsessive love was laid bare in that moment, met with nothing but ridicule.","The onlookers also realized the truth: if she had truly been driven mad by love, would she have called the ambulance to save herself?","To put it bluntly, if someone else had discovered her suicide attempt and called for help, she might have gained a bit more sympathy.","In the end, Wan Sitong kept crying and insisting that she truly loved Qin Yi, but everyone who heard her dismissed it as nonsense.","The false accusation incident came to a quiet close.","It wasn’t until everyone left that they learned the live stream had been Ji Fei's idea.","The Qin family looked at Ji Fei in surprise.","Ji Fei smiled and explained, \"When I arrived, I noticed a lot of media personnel, including some who were doing live streams. I thought waiting for the police to handle things would take too long, and justice delayed is justice denied. Reputations can’t be salvaged if the truth comes too late. So, I secretly brought a streamer in to reveal the truth on the spot. After all, only when the parties involved speak up will those who were deceived realize they’ve been fooled.\"","Qin Yi breathed a sigh of relief and stepped forward, smiling. \"Thank you, sister-in-law. I really owe you one this time.\"","Ji Fei waved her hand dismissively. \"It’s just experience from being a celebrity in the mainland.\"","At this, Qin Zhao immediately asked, \"Were we filmed just now?\"","Ji Fei reassured him, \"I warned the streamer. He wouldn’t dare. After all, he snuck into the police station to do the live stream, so he wouldn’t risk showing anyone’s face. At most, he only filmed the video evidence and Wan Sitong.\"","Before coming, Sister Pei, her manager, had reminded her that in Y City, their fame wasn’t as widespread as in the mainland. While they could enjoy some freedom here, being caught on a live stream could easily lead to exposure. If it spread back to the mainland, it might not be a big deal, but it would undoubtedly stir up a media frenzy.","Sister Pei was currently handling several major projects and didn’t have time to deal with Ji Fei’s antics, so she had urged her boss not to cause any trouble.","Ji Fei wanted to enjoy her time as a free spirit in Y City and wasn’t ready to step back into the public eye just yet.","[Thankfully, I warned the streamer beforehand, hinting that if he broadcasted anyone’s face without permission, he could face legal action. The local streamer wouldn’t dare offend the Qin family, so the risk of exposure was minimal. The only real concern was if people found out about my reputation as the \"Judge of the Entertainment Industry\" and the \"Gossip Queen of the Rich and Famous.\" If that got out, it would be hard to enjoy any juicy gossip in the future.]","Hearing Ji Fei’s mutterings, the Qin Second family struggled to hold back their laughter. So, she was worried about her identity being exposed and people being on guard, making it harder for her to indulge in gossip? Hilarious.","Qin Xian took Ji Fei’s hand, leading her out with a smile on his face.","[It’s such a bizarre coincidence. Not long after I arrived, both of my aunt’s children got into trouble. And looking at Qin Jiaxi’s demeanor, I have a feeling something else is about to happen. Do I really have some kind of supernatural aura? Will the Qin family start seeing me as a jinx?]","The Qin Second family didn’t like hearing that. To them, Ji Fei was their lucky star.","Without her help, they wouldn’t have known what challenges they might have faced.","If they had remained oblivious, some of them might have continued living their lives, but they would never have been truly happy. Given the choice, they would rather face the painful truth head-on than live in ignorance and regret later.","Even Qin Wenqiang had repeatedly expressed her gratitude, saying how fortunate they were to have Qin Xian and Ji Fei.","This time, if it hadn’t been for Ji Fei’s quick thinking with the live stream, Qin Yi wouldn’t have been able to escape unscathed.","So, they didn’t want Ji Fei to think of herself in such a negative light.","The family members exchanged meaningful glances, urging Qin Xian to reassure her.","Qin Xian didn’t need their prompting. Hearing her thoughts, he pulled Ji Fei closer and said gently, \"Feifei, you’re the blessing of our family. Without you, we wouldn’t know what would have happened. Please continue to shine your light on us.\" He then kissed her forehead.","Ji Fei was instantly dazzled by his charm.","Back at the Qin family estate, the details of Qin Yi’s ordeal naturally couldn’t be kept hidden.","After the elders learned the full story, they heaped praise on Ji Fei.","When the Qin family elders praised someone, it wasn’t just empty words—it came with tangible rewards.","The patriarch made the announcement, and Grandma Lv personally retrieved a box of antique jewelry from the safe, presenting it to Ji Fei with a proud smile. The sight of the priceless treasures made Ji Fei’s eyes light up.","But it wasn’t until she returned to her room that Ji Fei realized the true significance of the jewelry.","It was the heirloom of Qin Xian’s late grandmother.","By giving it to her, they were implicitly acknowledging Ji Fei as the future matriarch of the Qin family.","Ji Fei was genuinely surprised. \"I thought there would be some kind of intense test or something.\"","Qin Xian, who was helping Ji Fei look up the current market value of the jewelry (since his wife loved that kind of thing), replied, \"You already are the matriarch. No test is needed. These were always meant to be yours.\"","Ji Fei looked at the box of jewelry and pondered for a moment. \"Should we keep these as heirlooms, or...\"","Qin Xian hesitated before finally saying, \"If you want to sell them, I can help you find a discreet buyer. Just don’t let Grandpa find out.\"","Ji Fei: \"...Do you really think I’m that kind of person?\"","Qin Xian gave her an innocent look, knowing full well that Ji Fei had a preference for gold.","Ji Fei laughed and lay down, wrapping her arms around Qin Xian’s waist. \"I just think good things should be shared. Today, Grandpa only rewarded me, and it made me feel a bit awkward. Everyone contributed, and even though I know these were meant for the Qin family matriarch, I think...\"","\"You want to give some to the others?\"","\"Jewelry is meant to be worn. It’s only fair to share it with the women of the Qin family.\"","Qin Xian smiled and ruffled her hair. He knew this gesture meant she truly saw his siblings as her own family.","\"Alright, as long as it makes you happy.\"","Ji Fei immediately jumped up and made the rounds, giving pieces of jewelry to each of the Qin sisters. As for those who weren’t present, she decided to leave it for another time. This wasn’t about currying favor—it was simply a case of sharing the spoils with those who were there.","When Qin Jiaxi received her bracelet, her eyes lit up.","It wasn’t so much about the value of the jewelry, but the feeling of being included, of being one of the sisters.","Little did she know, wearing it would soon lead to trouble."]},{"number":352,"title":"Chapter 352: Dreaming of a Dream","paragraphs":["Because of the jewelry incident, Ji Fei was teased the very next day.","They said Ji Fei favored girls over boys, only giving gifts to the female students.","Ji Fei smiled and replied, \"When you all find someone to date, I'll send you something too.\"","Qin Zhao was immediately disarmed by Ji Fei's pointed gaze.","Qin Jing, on the other hand, claimed he was making progress, though his sister couldn't help but tease him relentlessly.","Ji Fei quickly figured it out.","[So Qin Jing had invited someone to meet in person, only to be rejected. This made me curious—could it be a case of catfishing?]","The Qin family chuckled quietly.","As they were laughing, Qin Yi finally came downstairs, unusually late today, but it was understandable. After all, he had been through so much yesterday and deserved some rest.","However, Qin Yi seemed distracted and out of sorts.","Everyone thought he was still recovering and offered some comforting words.","But Qin Yi's expression remained troubled.","This gave Ji Fei the perfect opportunity to stir things up.","With a quick investigation, Ji Fei almost burst into laughter at the dining table.","In the end, they had to cover it up with fake coughs.","[Hahaha, I knew it! How could he completely forget? It seems that as his body recovers, his memories are gradually coming back too. But poor Qin Yi still thinks it was just a wild dream, and the object of his dream is someone completely out of reach. No wonder he's so shaken.]","The Qin family also started coughing one after another.","So, this juicy gossip wasn't over yet?","They all felt a bit guilty, knowing such a big secret and keeping it from their relative.","If Qin Yi could recover his memories on his own, that would be great.","But their cousin was so clueless—how could he think it was just a dream?","Perhaps the trauma from that day had caused him to dream like that?","Qin Xian could understand, though. After all, Zhou Rushi had acted completely normal, as if nothing had happened between her and her teacher, so Qin Yi naturally wouldn't connect the dots.","Whether this counted as recovering his memories or not was still up for debate.","Out of sheer curiosity, when Qin Yi went to the school to handle some follow-up matters, Ji Fei, Qin Rong, and Qin Zhao—the three most idle members of the family—tagged along under the pretense of being concerned for their cousin. But in reality, they just wanted to stir up some drama.","Once they arrived at the school, Qin Yi headed to the dean's office, while the other three wandered around the hallway, looking around.","As luck would have it, they spotted Zhou Rushi coming out of an office.","When she saw them, she clearly recognized them and tensed up for a moment. Her eyes quickly scanned the area, and when she confirmed Qin Yi wasn’t there, she relaxed slightly.","She nodded with a polite smile, acknowledging them before walking away.","Since they weren’t really acquainted, they couldn’t exactly stop her to chat, so they watched her leave with a mix of regret and curiosity.","As soon as she was gone, Qin Zhao exclaimed, \"Huh? That office... Is she leaving?\"","Ji Fei and Qin Rong looked up and were equally shocked.","Meanwhile, inside the office, Qin Yi listened as the dean suggested he take a break from teaching for the rest of the semester to focus on recovery. Qin Yi nodded in agreement.","This wasn’t the school being difficult; the incident had caused quite a stir, and it would be hard for everyone to focus if Qin Yi acted like nothing had happened. Qin Yi had actually come to request leave, so the dean’s suggestion aligned perfectly with his plans.","Then the dean added, \"But starting next semester, aside from your regular teaching duties, would you consider taking on more students?\"","Qin Yi immediately showed resistance.","The dean chuckled awkwardly and said, \"You can’t let one bad experience ruin everything. People like Wan Sitong are rare. There are plenty of talented students who lack financial resources and need someone like you—a teacher who values talent over money—to guide them.\"","The dean couldn’t bear to lose Qin Yi as a free resource and was laying on the flattery thick.","\"It’s such a shame to deny others opportunities just because of Wan Sitong, don’t you think?\" the dean asked, looking at Qin Yi expectantly.","Qin Yi, being kind-hearted, couldn’t refuse. He nodded and said, \"Alright, do you have any candidates in mind?\"","The dean immediately handed over a prepared list.","\"How about taking on a few more? That way, they can keep an eye on each other, and we’ll assess their character beforehand,\" the dean suggested with a smile.","Qin Yi wasn’t so jaded that he’d stop helping students altogether because of Wan Sitong, but he knew his judgment wasn’t the best. It was safer to choose from the dean’s recommendations.","However, because of that dream, his first instinct was to look for Zhou Rushi’s name.","After all, aside from Wan Sitong, Zhou Rushi had been the most outstanding student in her year.","Qin Yi naturally assumed her name would be on the list.","But after scanning it once, he didn’t see it. He checked again, only to confirm that her name was indeed missing.","\"Why isn’t Zhou Rushi’s name on the list?\" After having that dream, Qin Yi should have avoided her to prevent awkwardness, but seeing her name absent, he instinctively felt the need to defend her rights. She deserved to be on that list.","After he asked, the dean sighed and shook his head.","Qin Yi’s heart sank. Since the dean had curated the list, did that mean... did that mean...","Qin Yi couldn’t help but overthink. After the Wan Sitong incident, he had started to suspect that some students might have ulterior motives.","So... was Zhou Rushi one of them? Is that why the dean had excluded her in advance?","As Qin Yi was lost in these thoughts, the dean spoke up. \"Ah, Zhou Rushi recently applied for an exchange program to study at a music conservatory abroad. She passed the assessment and will be leaving in a couple of days. I did mention this opportunity to her, since studying under you would provide her with better guidance, but she declined.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yi’s heart sank even further.","Why... did she refuse?"]},{"number":353,"title":"Chapter 353: I Don't Need You to Take Responsibility","paragraphs":["Qin Zhao and Qin Rong went to the office to inquire briefly and, after receiving an answer, were left utterly puzzled.","Are they really leaving?","They had previously heard from Ji Fei about the incident between the two, and although it was rumored that Zhou Rushi had no intention of acknowledging it, given that Zhou Rushi liked Qin Yi, they felt there might still be some chemistry between them. Today, with Qin Yi possibly regaining his memory, they were sure this drama was far from over.","[Wow?! This girl... she’s quite decisive. Studying abroad was her initial choice, but now that she has the chance to become Qin Yi’s apprentice, which seems like a better opportunity, she’s sticking to her original decision. If it weren’t for the fact that she genuinely likes Qin Yi, I’d think she didn’t care for him at all!]","Hearing Ji Fei’s inner thoughts, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were filled with confusion about the current situation.","Not long after, Qin Yi came out, looking somewhat dazed.","Eager for more gossip, Qin Zhao immediately asked, “Cousin, did something happen?”","“Nothing much. The dean gave me a break.”","“Huh? Did it still affect you?” Qin Rong asked worriedly.","Qin Yi shook his head. “No, it’s just a simple break. Next semester, I’ll be taking on an apprentice.”","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong exchanged glances. So, this was what Ji Fei’s inner thoughts were referring to?","Cousin Qin Yi might take on an apprentice, but Zhou Rushi had already turned down the opportunity? What’s going on here?","[Seriously, cousin... why doesn’t he just ask Zhou Rushi why she refused? Is that it? Is it over just like that?]","Indeed, it seemed to be over. In Qin Yi’s current mindset, he was just confused and wouldn’t bring up Zhou Rushi, especially since she was the one who had declined. He couldn’t exactly chase after her to be her teacher, not to mention the embarrassing dream he’d had. Facing this student would just be awkward.","Avoiding her was probably for the best.","Ignoring the expressions of the three around him, Qin Yi went to gather his things.","Some of his belongings were still in the building where the incident had occurred, as he had been mentoring Wan Sitong there.","As they walked down the corridor, Qin Zhao couldn’t resist gossiping with Qin Rong, especially since Qin Rong hadn’t been there that night. Qin Zhao pointed out the scene of the incident.","“If Wan Sitong had chased after him that night and found out cousin hadn’t gone far, he might have been in big trouble,” Qin Zhao said carelessly, pointing to the room where Qin Yi had hidden that night.","Qin Rong quickly hushed Qin Zhao, reminding him that gossiping about their cousin so loudly was a bit much.","Ji Fei, smirking, listened to the two behind her. Up ahead was the rehearsal room, and Ji Fei couldn’t help but glance at Qin Yi out of the corner of her eye.","She expected Qin Yi to react with embarrassment or annoyance, but instead, he looked stunned, his gaze fixed on the rehearsal room.","Just as Ji Fei was wondering what was going on, the door to the rehearsal room suddenly opened from the inside.","For a moment, all four of them froze.","[Oh my god, oh my god, oh my god! What a fateful encounter!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong nearly screamed when they saw Zhou Rushi step out. It was all so dramatic, but they managed to hold it in, their eyes darting back and forth between the two.","Zhou Rushi was equally shocked by the unexpected encounter. She hesitated, unsure whether to step out or retreat back inside, her expression visibly uneasy.","Qin Yi, meanwhile, was completely frozen. His mind went blank at first, but then vivid images flashed through his memory, gradually piecing themselves together. His body trembled, overwhelmed by shame and regret, until a deep blush spread across his pale face.","He couldn’t bring himself to look at Zhou Rushi.","The redness of his cheeks was so obvious that the other three immediately noticed.","[Wow, his memory’s back already?! Just like that?! Well, it makes sense. After all, this is the first time he’s been back at the scene since he was rescued. It’s natural for it to come back to him. Hahaha, this is getting good. Good thing I tagged along today. This kind of drama isn’t something just anyone gets to witness.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong had also figured it out by now, their eyes wide with excitement, their hearts pounding.","Zhou Rushi had initially composed herself, planning to face Qin Yi with the polite demeanor one would use with a teacher.","But then she was met with Qin Yi’s utterly distraught expression, his face alternating between pale and flushed.","In that moment, someone as perceptive as her couldn’t miss what was happening. Her face turned pale.","The silence was heavy and awkward for a while before Zhou Rushi, as if jolted awake, quickly grabbed her books and tried to leave.","But before she could escape, Qin Yi spoke up. “Zhou Rushi, I need to talk to you.”","Although the sudden return of his memories left him devastated, Qin Yi wasn’t a young man anymore. He knew he had to face this. He had wronged her.","He remembered everything now.","That night, the rehearsal room he had stumbled into in his desperate state hadn’t been empty. Zhou Rushi had been practicing inside. Seeing him burst in, disheveled and in distress, she had assumed something was wrong and approached him, concerned, trying to help him up.","But with that one touch, Qin Yi, completely out of control, had pushed her down.","Zhou Rushi had struggled, cried out, resisted, but the room’s soundproofing was too good. No one could have heard her in time, and Qin Yi had been completely unaware of his actions.","As things unfolded, Zhou Rushi realized Qin Yi had been drugged and had no choice but to endure.","Qin Yi felt it was all his fault, and the fact that he had forgotten made it even worse. He owed Zhou Rushi an apology.","So, after asking Zhou Rushi to stay behind and returning to the rehearsal room, Qin Yi bowed deeply to her, offering a sincere apology.","Zhou Rushi waved her hands frantically. “No... no, it’s fine... Teacher Qin, you don’t have to do this. I know it wasn’t your fault. It was all Wan Sitong’s scheme. You were a victim too.”","Hearing her say this only made Qin Yi feel worse.","“Don’t forgive me so easily. No matter the cause, I hurt you. You can vent your anger on me, or demand compensation. Anything you ask, I’ll do my best to fulfill. If you want... I’m willing to take responsibility for the rest of my life,” Qin Yi said earnestly.","But as soon as he finished, Zhou Rushi’s eyes welled up with tears.","Qin Yi panicked. “Don’t... don’t cry. I’m sorry, it’s all my fault. I’m not saying you have to marry me. I’m just saying the choice is yours. If you want, I’ll... I’ll take care of you for the rest of my life.”","Zhou Rushi wiped her eyes and smiled. “Teacher, I don’t need you to take responsibility, really. If I ever marry, it’ll be to someone I truly love. I know you’re a lifelong bachelor, devoted to your music and art. You don’t have to let this one incident derail your life. Forcing ourselves together would only ruin both of us.”"]},{"number":354,"title":"Chapter 354: This thing never does anything productive all day.","paragraphs":["Qin Yi was stunned, feeling extremely awkward. His mind was in a muddle, and he didn’t fully process Zhou Rushi’s words.","But Ji Fei had already caught on.","[It’s obvious that Zhou Rushi likes Qin Yi, but she knows Qin Yi doesn’t feel the same way. He only wants to marry her out of a sense of duty, and she doesn’t want their relationship to be like that, which is why she’s refusing. This is also why Zhou Rushi pretended nothing happened—she never intended to use her kindness as leverage to win over the person she admires.]","Meanwhile, outside the door, the two who couldn’t hear anything and relied on Ji Fei’s mental commentary were scratching their heads in frustration.","“Then let me compensate you in other ways—money, a house, or connections. Of course, this isn’t meant to insult you, it’s just...” Qin Yi genuinely felt guilty and wanted to make amends.","“I don’t need any compensation. Please don’t worry about it, Professor,” Zhou Rushi insisted.","[Why refuse compensation? Even if you don’t want a loveless marriage, at least take the money! He’s the Qin family’s young master—a snap of his fingers could set you up for life! What are you thinking, girl? You helped Qin Yi, and you’re the victim here. This isn’t some idol drama! Don’t feel like accepting compensation hurts your pride!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, whose way of thinking had already been influenced by Ji Fei, agreed with her perspective. If you can’t have the person, at least take the money. Why make things harder for yourself?","[Alright, I underestimated you. So this is how you see it—hahaha! You think this whole situation is like accidentally getting to sleep with the guy you’ve had a crush on for ages, like you hit the jackpot. Something you never even dared to dream about happened, and even if you two can’t be together in this lifetime, at least you got to fulfill a dream. You’re not being greedy. Girl, you’ve got a clear head, hahaha!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong struggled to hold back their laughter. From a certain perspective, it made perfect sense!","So Zhou Rushi even felt like she was the one who had gained something and kept reminding herself not to push her luck.","“But...” Qin Yi frowned, clearly distressed by the sense of indebtedness.","Seeing the person she liked in such a difficult position, Zhou Rushi worried he might misunderstand her intentions. After some thought, she decided to voice a small hope. “Then... could you write me a recommendation letter? I’m applying to be an exchange student at XX. I remember your mentor is there. Could you recommend me? Even if it’s not as a direct disciple, I’d like to receive guidance from them.”","Qin Yi’s mentor was, of course, someone of extraordinary status, and not just anyone could get such an opportunity.","Hearing this request, Qin Yi let out a sigh of relief, though he still felt it was hardly enough compared to what Zhou Rushi had gone through. But since she had asked, he would definitely make it happen.","“That’s no problem at all. You can count on me...” Qin Yi paused, then added, “You... refused to become my disciple because of this, didn’t you? I really owe you.”","Zhou Rushi was taken aback, realizing Qin Yi must have heard something from the dean. After a moment’s hesitation, she decided to be honest. “So you did consider taking me as your disciple. That means my abilities were recognized by you after all. But I couldn’t have become your disciple, whether or not this incident happened.”","Qin Yi looked up at her, confused.","Outside the door, Ji Fei was practically vibrating with excitement, grabbing Qin Zhao and Qin Rong by the arms.","[Is she going to confess?! That’s the spirit! Even if you know it won’t work out, it’s better to express your feelings and leave no regrets!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong couldn’t resist anymore. Though it was unethical, who could resist such a moment? They quietly peeked through the door crack—hearing it live was far more exciting than relying on Ji Fei’s commentary.","“Why? Is there something wrong with my teaching, or...”","“No, Qin... Qin Yi, I’ve actually had a crush on you for a long time,” Zhou Rushi admitted, still unable to look him in the eye. She kept her head down as she spoke. “I like you, but I also love singing. If I became your disciple, I wouldn’t be able to focus on my studies. I’d be constantly thinking about you. That’s why I decided long ago to leave. I know you could never feel the same way about me, so I don’t have any other expectations. I’m sorry, Professor, for betraying your trust. But since I’m leaving soon, I wanted to tell you. You’re a really wonderful person. As a student, falling for you might not be appropriate, but feelings are hard to control. I hope everything goes well for you in the future.”","Qin Yi was stunned.","Zhou Rushi, however, smiled in relief after saying her piece. She bowed to Qin Yi as a final farewell between teacher and student, then left the rehearsal room.","When the three entered the room later, Qin Yi was still in a daze.","Even after being brought back to the family home, he remained withdrawn.","Naturally, everyone downstairs gathered to gossip about the juicy drama. Thanks to Qin Zhao and Qin Rong’s eavesdropping, the discussion flowed effortlessly.","Qin Wenqiang, upon hearing about the situation, even considered playing matchmaker for her brother and Zhou Rushi. After all, Zhou Rushi had feelings for him, and there was already a connection between them. Qin Wenqiang thought her perpetually single brother might finally have a chance at companionship.","But the others didn’t agree.","This was Zhou Rushi’s choice. Her view of love was that it had to be mutual. She wasn’t insecure—she just had a clear understanding of herself. She believed Qin Yi might treat her well but would never fall in love with her, so she chose to pursue her dreams instead.","As for Qin Yi’s withdrawal, it wasn’t because he was agonizing over whether he could love Zhou Rushi. In the future, he would ask people in the industry to look out for her, but if he couldn’t love her, he wouldn’t disrupt her life. At most, he’d step in if she ever faced difficulties.","What bothered him most was that two female students had developed feelings for him. Was there something wrong with his teaching? He needed to reflect deeply before considering taking on another disciple.","A few days later, Zhou Rushi went abroad, and Qin Yi kept his promise by reaching out to his mentor, who accepted her as a new disciple.","When Ji Fei heard the news, she laughed.","[I thought they’d be teacher and student, but now they’re just fellow disciples. Haha!]","After resolving this matter, Ji Fei remembered her promise to visit Qin Jiaxi’s School. She had planned to go that day, but Qin Jiaxi had come home late the previous night and left early in the morning, so they hadn’t finalized the arrangements.","When Ji Fei woke up, she chatted with the others in the living room about it.","Just then, a servant came in and said, “Miss Jiaxi is injured...” The servant meant to say that Qin Jiaxi was hurt, so it might not be appropriate for others to visit her.","But as soon as the servant spoke, everyone was alarmed.","“Injured? What happened?”","The servant only knew what Qin Jiaxi had told her—that she had fallen and gotten some bruises, and she had asked for ointment.","But Ji Fei’s expression changed immediately.","[Dammit! That scumbag Qin Han! He’s always up to no good, bullying his own sister! Did he really go to her school to pick on her?!]"]},{"number":355,"title":"Chapter 355: Severely Bullied","paragraphs":["Ji Fei's inner thoughts exploded in her mind.","Before Qin Second's family could react, they heard Ji Fei venting her frustrations.","[\"What business is it of yours that I gave Jiaxi a bracelet? Just because Yu Xin said something, you have the nerve to go and demand that Jiaxi give the bracelet to Yu Xin? Who do you think you are!\"]","[\"And you say that Yu Xin will eventually be a daughter of the Qin family, so it's only fair to give it to her? As an apology for Jiaxi not helping to plead her case? Are you even listening to yourself? Is your brain full of crap?\"]","[\"Jiaxi finally stood her ground and said what I told her. Yes, it was me who said it—only the girls with Qin family blood get one! And only those present at the time! That's the decision of the matriarch of the family, so what? I won't give it to your precious Yu Xin! If you're not happy, are you going to snatch it?\"]","[\"I'm so done with this. You still have some respect for Qin Xian, so you didn't dare to take it by force. But when you couldn't get it, you took your anger out on your own sister and pushed her down? Are you out of your mind? If Third Uncle ever makes you the heir, I'll have my husband strip you of your position! Let you taste what it's like to be bullied and ostracized by your siblings!\"]","At the moment, only Qin Yi at home couldn't hear any of this. After hearing the servants' account, he didn't think much of it at first, but suddenly he felt a murderous aura surrounding him.","He glanced around and saw Ji Fei, Qin Zhao, and Qin Rong all looking furious.","Qin Yi: ?","Ji Fei grew angrier the more she thought about it and immediately took out her phone to message Qin Xian.","\"Husband, I found out that Jiaxi is hurt, and it might be related to her brother. That guy bullied his sister. Teach him a lesson!\"","Ji Fei's guard around Qin Xian had been lowering more and more lately. Sometimes, she didn't even care about the risk of exposing herself. After all, Qin Xian never questioned her words, so she felt free to speak her mind.","\"He's not at the company today, but there are other ways.\"","Seeing Qin Xian's reply, Ji Fei smiled.","Qin Xian had taken her words to heart and was planning to teach the guy a lesson directly, but since he wasn't around, he would have to do it indirectly.","However, during this period, Qin Xian had been working with Fourth Uncle's family to audit the Qin family's businesses in Y City. Qin Han had been following them most of the time, as if he were afraid someone would steal his future power. After all, under normal circumstances, Qin Xian was based in the mainland, while Fourth Uncle's family was in G City, so they wouldn't take over his side of the business.","But if Qin Xian discovered something that needed adjustment during the audit, he might just swallow up what Qin Han was supposed to inherit in the future. Qin Han was on high alert because of this.","So it was strange that he wasn't around today.","[Could he be at the school bullying someone again? Let me check... Damn! He really is at the school, but not to snatch the bracelet. He's there as a guest speaker, replacing Third Uncle to give a speech at the university. Is he trying to show off?]","When Ji Fei found this out, a sly smile crept onto her face. She immediately sent a message to Qin Xian.","Then she turned to the others and said, \"The weather is nice today. Why don't we go to the school and surprise Jiaxi? If she's not feeling well, we can take care of her!\"","[The school doesn't know Jiaxi's identity, right? We need to go and back her up!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were already in sync with Ji Fei. They knew she was planning to stir up trouble and couldn't help but grin mischievously.","Qin Yi felt something was off, but as their guide, he had no choice but to take them there.","Soon, the four of them arrived at the university campus where Qin Jiaxi was studying.","Ji Fei used her gossip system to check and found that Qin Jiaxi was in class at the moment, so she didn't want to disturb her. Instead, they decided to explore the campus.","The campus was beautifully landscaped.","As they passed through a grove of trees, they suddenly heard voices. Since it was class time, there were few students wandering around, so the grove was quiet, and the voices were clear.","\"You know I'm doing this to protect you. Otherwise, my parents would tear us apart, and others would target you. I'm doing this for your own good,\" a male voice said.","\"But... I still feel so wronged,\" a delicate female voice replied.","\"Baby, you know I only love you. Once the plan succeeds, my family won't oppose us anymore.\"","Hearing this conversation, Ji Fei and the others exchanged glances, feeling like they had stumbled upon some juicy gossip.","At the moment, they thought it was just a young couple facing disapproval from those around them. Nothing seemed out of the ordinary, but it was still intriguing.","However, when they looked over, they saw a young couple embracing. The boy was passionately kissing the girl. Both were good-looking and well-dressed, so it didn't seem like a case of mismatched social status.","The group couldn't make sense of it, but running into such a scene was awkward, so they quickly walked away.","Once they left the grove, they couldn't help but sigh about the joys of youth.","Just then, the school bell rang.","Ji Fei couldn't very well use her gossip system to lead everyone to Qin Jiaxi's classroom, so she decided to call her instead.","Qin Jiaxi immediately answered the call, sounding thrilled that they had come. When she heard they wanted to pick her up, she insisted it wasn't necessary.","So they agreed to meet at a central landmark on campus.","However, after waiting for a while, Qin Jiaxi still hadn't shown up.","Ji Fei grew worried and decided to check on her.","When she did, her expression changed, and she immediately started walking, making up an excuse as she went, \"She's taking so long. Maybe her legs are still hurting? Let's go and get her.\"","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong only heard a string of curses in Ji Fei's mind and immediately followed without question.","Seeing the three of them marching forward with determination, Qin Yi was once again filled with confusion.","Soon, they arrived at a plaza with a fountain. A crowd had gathered around it, watching something.","\"What are they doing around the fountain? Making wishes?\" Qin Yi asked curiously.","No one answered him. Instead, they saw Ji Fei quicken her pace and head straight for the fountain.","When they got closer, they saw someone bending over in the fountain, picking something up from the water.","Qin Yi took a closer look and was stunned.","It was Qin Jiaxi.","Qin Jiaxi's clothes were soaked, and she looked utterly disheveled. Her eyes were red, but she stubbornly refused to cry.","In her hands, she held a few beads.","Qin Yi vaguely remembered that they looked like the beads from the bracelet Ji Fei had given Qin Jiaxi.","Nearby, a group of girls was taunting her.","\"Qin Jiaxi, this is all your fault. If you had just handed it over, it wouldn't have been torn. So don't blame me later.\"","\"Better collect them all. If you don't, Yu Xin might make you pay for it, and you can't afford that.\"","\"How dare you be Su Ze's girlfriend? You're such an embarrassment to him. You can't just steal things because you're jealous!\"","\"Thief and liar. I don't know what Su Ze sees in you.\"","\"Let's not hold back. We should just report her to the school and get her expelled.\"","The girls at the edge of the fountain laughed mockingly.","Meanwhile, some boys nearby were leering at Qin Jiaxi, their eyes lingering on her wet clothes."]},{"number":356,"title":"Chapter 356: It Was Sent by My Family","paragraphs":["Seeing this scene, Ji Fei and the other three collectively felt their blood pressure rise.","Except for Ji Fei, the other three immediately rushed forward.","Ji Fei, however, held her phone calmly, recording everything that had just happened. She wasn’t going to let any of them off the hook.","Qin Jiaxi kept her head down, searching desperately. After all, it was the most heartfelt gift she had received in a long time, and she cherished it deeply. She had managed to avoid her brother’s attempts to take it, but now it seemed she couldn’t escape others.","She needed to hurry; she didn’t want to keep everyone waiting for too long.","But the disgusting words being thrown at her made her whole body tremble.","Bullying had become a habit. No matter what she said in the past, no one would believe her. Su Ze would even tell her not to cause trouble or that she was in the wrong. Gradually, she had stopped bothering to explain herself.","But now, holding those beads in her hand, she couldn’t hold back anymore.","“It’s not my fault! You’re the ones bullying me! I’ll report this to the school! I’ll even call the police! You’re stealing my bracelet!”","“The bracelet is mine! It’s not Yu Xin’s! I don’t know why Yu Xin has a similar one, but mine is mine! It was a gift from my family! Her losing her things has nothing to do with me! I’m not a thief, and I’m not a liar! You’re the ones spreading rumors and bullying me! You’re in the wrong!”","Perhaps they hadn’t expected Qin Jiaxi to fight back, and it instantly ignited their anger.","“You still won’t admit it? The first time we saw it, Yu Xin was wearing it! You’re just jealous because Yu Xin has a beautiful bracelet, so you stole it! A gift from your family? Can your family even afford it? At most, Su Ze bought it for you, but we asked him, and he said he never gave you anything!”","Qin Jiaxi froze, her hand stopping mid-air as she picked up the beads.","It felt like an electric shock had struck her mind.","At that moment, a boy deliberately decided to cause trouble. Using the excuse of punishing a thief, he scooped up water from the pool, intending to splash it on Qin Jiaxi. His smug expression made it clear he was just messing with her.","“Let’s teach you a lesson...”","They weren’t worried. Even if Qin Jiaxi was Su Ze’s girlfriend, they knew bullying her wouldn’t anger him.","But just as he was about to throw the water, a figure quickly approached, grabbing his wrist.","Before anyone could react, the boy was thrown into the pool with a swift shoulder toss by Qin Zhao.","The splash of water instantly drenched the onlookers.","Meanwhile, Qin Yi and Qin Rong had already appeared in front of Qin Jiaxi, urging her to come out quickly.","Qin Jiaxi was too stunned to react, simply obeying their instructions. Qin Rong took her hand, her face filled with concern.","Qin Yi had already taken off his coat and draped it over Qin Jiaxi’s shoulders.","The sudden turn of events left everyone in shock.","Not only because of the group’s striking appearances, but also because of Qin Yi’s identity. He was somewhat famous, and everyone knew him.","They also knew his background—he was from the Qin Corporation. But no one could understand why he was here, protecting Qin Jiaxi.","The boy who had been thrown into the pool stood up, furious. “What do you think you’re doing?!”","“Stay there. Don’t come out, or I’ll smash your head!” Qin Zhao said coldly.","Though he didn’t know Qin Zhao’s identity, the boy was intimidated by his menacing aura and didn’t know how to respond.","“You’re... Teacher Qin? Why are you...” someone stammered in surprise.","Qin Yi glared at the crowd, his expression icy. “You’re bullying a classmate!”","The ringleaders were startled and quickly tried to play innocent. “We weren’t! We were just teaching a bad student a lesson!”","“Teacher Qin, you don’t understand. This girl is terrible—she steals things!”","“We were just making her return what she took!”","“You... What evidence do you have?” Qin Rong was so angry she could barely speak.","“One of our classmates lost an identical bracelet...”","Before they could finish, a voice called out from a distance, “Jiaxi, what’s going on?”","Everyone immediately fell silent, turning to see a boy walking over with a cold expression.","Someone whispered, “Su Ze is here. He’s probably not here to back Qin Jiaxi up.”","At that moment, Ji Fei and the others saw the newcomer and heard the whispers around them. Their eyes widened in disbelief.","Wasn’t that the guy who had been passionately kissing someone in the woods earlier?","Ji Fei’s mind raced.","[Su Ze... So the person with him was Yu Xin!]","[Damn! They came together. Knowing Qin Yi’s identity, they were worried things would get out of hand, so Su Ze rushed out, but Yu Xin is watching from a distance!]","[So the bracelet situation is definitely...]","Before Ji Fei could investigate further, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong had already caught on, their eyes narrowing dangerously as they stared at Su Ze.","Su Ze didn’t know Qin Zhao or Qin Rong, but as someone from Y City’s elite circles, he naturally recognized Qin Yi. The two had even met before.","Originally, Qin Yi might have trusted him more, knowing he was Qin Jiaxi’s boyfriend.","But now, Su Ze’s image had completely crumbled in Qin Yi’s eyes—not just because of his affair, but also because of what these people had said and done.","Qin Yi couldn’t understand why a young lady from the Qin family was being bullied at school, and why her supposedly well-matched boyfriend hadn’t done anything to protect her.","Given their statuses, dominating the school shouldn’t have been a joke.","Su Ze, ever the show-off, stepped forward and nodded at Qin Yi. “Brother Qin Yi, you’re here too. Thanks for looking out for her.”","With that, he tried to pull Qin Jiaxi away from Qin Yi and Qin Rong.","His movements were far from gentle, even a bit rough.","As he pulled her, he said, “Causing trouble again? Can’t you just behave? Why do you always stir things up? Look at the mess you’re in. Let’s go.”","He seemed intent on taking her away.","“Hold it! Since when is it your place to take Jiaxi away?”","Ji Fei put her phone away and slowly walked through the crowd. With a swift chop, she struck Su Ze’s arm, forcing him to let go.","Given Ji Fei’s strength, it shouldn’t have hurt, but Su Ze froze, completely stunned. This was the first time anyone in Y City had dared to treat him like this.","He looked at Ji Fei in disbelief. “Are you insane?!”","“Good. I’ll be sure to tell my husband about this,” Ji Fei said with a cold smile.","Su Ze paused, a bad feeling creeping over him. After all, this person was defending Qin Jiaxi, and while others might not know Qin Jiaxi’s background, he did. But he wasn’t one to back down easily. “I don’t care who you are! My girlfriend needs to change her clothes. I’m taking her with me. What business is it of yours? Jiaxi, are you coming or not?”","Qin Jiaxi, however, didn’t respond, as if lost in thought.","Ji Fei took Qin Jiaxi’s hand and said to Su Ze, “Since you’re Jiaxi’s boyfriend, you handle this. These people were just bullying her, claiming she stole someone else’s bracelet. They even tore her bracelet apart. What are you going to do about it?”"]},{"number":357,"title":"Chapter 357: Don't Want to Be Exposed","paragraphs":["Because of Ji Fei's interference, Su Ze's expression turned grim. \"If there's any issue, we can discuss it later. Jiaxi needs to change her clothes now.\"","After speaking, he shot a sharp glance at Qin Jiaxi.","In the past, whenever Su Ze wore a cold expression, Qin Jiaxi would obediently comply. But this time, she remained unmoved.","[Heh, the scumbag is panicking. He’s only trying to take Jiaxi away quickly because Qin Yi is here. Is he really that afraid of others finding out that Jiaxi is a member of the Qin family? So, it wasn’t just Qin Han’s request to keep Jiaxi’s identity hidden on campus—you were in on it too. I always wondered why, as her boyfriend, you allowed others to bully her like this. Turns out, it was all by design. You two hid her identity from the public and watched her get bullied. What a brilliant move!]","Ji Fei’s internal monologue was seething with anger.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong finally understood. Su Ze’s urgency to take Jiaxi away wasn’t simply about not standing up for his girlfriend—it was about preventing her identity from being exposed.","Earlier, when he thanked Qin Yi for looking out for her, he was deliberately vague, making it seem like Qin Yi’s intervention was out of respect for Su Ze, not because of any connection to Jiaxi.","What a bold move! How dare he bully the Qin family’s daughter? He’s got quite the nerve!","\"This is no small matter. This bracelet is priceless and holds significant meaning,\" Qin Zhao said with a cold laugh. \"What? Is the young master of the Su family so generous that he won’t even seek justice for his own girlfriend?\"","Though Qin Zhao didn’t work for the Qin Corporation, his celebrity status carried a commanding presence.","Su Ze’s face darkened. \"It’s just a small matter. Jiaxi won’t make a fuss about it.\"","\"No, it’s not a small matter. I care about it,\" Qin Jiaxi suddenly spoke up, breaking her silence.","Qin Jiaxi raised her head, tears welling in her eyes. She stared directly at Su Ze, as if the fog had finally lifted. \"Do you always try to downplay things and make me endure in silence? Why is it that every time I’m wronged, you act like this? Aren’t you my boyfriend? I don’t expect you to fight for me, but why won’t you even give me fairness?\"","When the signs of something being off became too obvious to ignore, the grievances she had long suppressed finally erupted.","Qin Jiaxi’s trembling voice and pointed questions made Su Ze flush with anger. \"Jiaxi, stop making a scene. If you’re too unreasonable, I’ll have to ignore you!\"","Ji Fei and the others nearly laughed in disbelief.","Qin Yi frowned and retorted, \"Are you out of your mind? Who’s making a scene here?\"","Su Ze’s face turned a kaleidoscope of colors after being directly confronted by Qin Yi.","The surrounding students couldn’t help but start whispering among themselves.","\"Su Ze probably doesn’t want his girlfriend’s scandal to blow up. That’s why he’s acting like this. Qin Jiaxi is being ungrateful.\"","\"Exactly. Qin Jiaxi stole Yu Xin’s things. Su Ze is just trying to protect her. I don’t think Teacher Qin knows the full story.\"","\"He probably doesn’t. If he did, given his status, he wouldn’t be defending a thief.\"","Qin Yi naturally overheard the murmurs and was utterly baffled.","What on earth? Who’s Yu Xin?","Just as Qin Yi was about to ask, Su Ze, seemingly realizing something, hastily interrupted.","\"Jiaxi, I’ll ask you one more time—are you coming or not? My patience has its limits.\"","Before Ji Fei and the others could react, Qin Jiaxi suddenly asked with seriousness, \"I have a question. You knew this bracelet was a gift from my family, right? So why didn’t you say that when they asked you? Instead, you just said it wasn’t something you bought. Were you trying to lead everyone to believe that my bracelet was obtained through shady means?\"","Her words instantly silenced the room.","[Well done, sister! You’ve finally woken up. Yes, that’s exactly what he was doing! He wanted to stand up for Yu Xin because, in truth, he has feelings for her!]","Though Qin Zhao and Qin Rong had already guessed as much after piecing together the clues, hearing it out loud still infuriated them.","The only silver lining was that Qin Jiaxi wasn’t a lovesick fool. She had finally seen through the scumbag’s intentions.","Perhaps flustered by being exposed, Su Ze grew even angrier, as if Qin Jiaxi had insulted him.","\"Qin Jiaxi, you’d better think carefully before you speak,\" Su Ze said coldly, his tone laced with warning and his attitude still dripping with arrogance. \"Why would I do such a thing? Do you still consider me your boyfriend?\"","Qin Jiaxi froze, instinctively shrinking back.","Su Ze had meant the world to her. When she was drowning in misery, he had appeared like a beam of light in her life. His public confession had given her, who had always doubted herself, a sense of validation.","To her, it had been salvation.","When she learned that she could one day marry Su Ze, she had been overjoyed. She thought that marrying him would allow her to escape her suffocating family. Even if her mother and brother didn’t love her, at least she had a boyfriend who did.","So, Su Ze was her lifeline. Even if that lifeline was covered in thorns that silently wounded her, she didn’t dare let go.","But after this family gathering, something felt off—very off.","Su Ze had been cold toward her, showing almost no concern. Aside from publicly acknowledging their relationship, he had never stood up for her or protected her. Whenever she clashed with someone, Su Ze always took the opposing side, criticizing her. It wasn’t the complete rejection and scolding she got from her mother and brother, but it was still heartless.","Everything felt wrong.","\"I’m starting to wonder—are you really my boyfriend?\" Qin Jiaxi murmured softly.","Su Ze’s expression changed, his eyes widening in disbelief.","Just then, a delicate-looking girl rushed over.","\"What’s going on? Jiaxi, are you arguing with Su Ze?\"","[Oh ho ho, the scheming saint has made her grand entrance. She’s been watching from the sidelines all along, hasn’t she? Is she worried the show’s about to fall apart?]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong immediately fixed their gazes on the newcomer. This was Yu Xin.","When Su Ze saw Yu Xin, his expression softened noticeably. His attitude was completely different now.","\"We’re not arguing. Jiaxi’s just being unreasonable. I wanted to take her to change her clothes, but she’s being stubborn,\" Su Ze explained.","Yu Xin immediately turned to Qin Jiaxi with disapproval. \"Look at you, you’re soaked. Come back to the dorm with me and change before you catch a cold.\"","\"Yu Xin, why are you being so nice to her? Look at what she’s holding,\" one of the girls who had previously bullied Jiaxi interjected, clearly confused.","Yu Xin’s expression shifted slightly. \"We’re good sisters. What does it matter if I’m nice to her? Nothing else is important. Please step aside.\"","[Another master of ambiguity, trying to wrap this up without clarity. Not happening!]","\"Oh, so you’re Yu Xin? Perfect timing. Let’s settle this face-to-face. They’re saying Jiaxi stole your bracelet. Is the one Jiaxi’s holding the same as yours?\""]},{"number":358,"title":"Chapter 358: Everyone Roll In to Pick Up Beads, If One is Missing, We Will Call the Police","paragraphs":["Ji Fei cut straight to the point, causing Yu Xin's expression to stiffen. However, Yu Xin quickly adjusted herself and said, \"Oh, sister, it’s fine. I don’t mind anymore. If it’s lost, it’s lost. No big deal.\"","[Is she trying to continue smearing Qin Jiaxi’s name, making it impossible for her to defend herself?]","\"Wow, that sounds so generous of you. You don’t mind, so you’re letting everyone assume Qin Jiaxi stole it, but you’re just choosing not to pursue it, right?\" Ji Fei directly exposed Yu Xin’s little scheme.","Yu Xin’s face changed, and Qin Jiaxi finally caught on. Judging by the expressions of those around them, it seemed like everyone had already assumed that Yu Xin was magnanimously letting Qin Jiaxi off the hook for being a thief.","Qin Jiaxi seemed to finally understand why she had always been left speechless when dealing with Yu Xin in the past. Even though Yu Xin never directly attacked her with words, she always managed to make everyone despise her. Qin Jiaxi had thought she was just inherently unlikeable, but now...","She immediately glared at Yu Xin and said, \"You know perfectly well that the bracelet is mine! I would never steal your things. You did this on purpose!\"","\"Qin Jiaxi, what are you doing? How can you have such a malicious mind and judge others like that?\" Su Ze snapped angrily.","Qin Jiaxi was stunned by his harsh tone. She looked at Su Ze’s furious expression, then at Yu Xin, her eyes flickering before she let out a bitter laugh.","\"You’re right. Someone who does this on purpose is truly malicious!\" Ji Fei said with a smile, turning her gaze to Yu Xin.","Su Ze was momentarily taken aback, while Yu Xin was on the verge of hyperventilating from being cornered. Still, she managed to say in a pitiful tone, \"I just wanted to say that I don’t care about the bracelet being lost. I really didn’t mean anything else by it.\"","\"You don’t care, but I do. After all, I was the one who personally gave that bracelet to Jiaxi. Are you suggesting I stole it from you and then gave it to her?\" Ji Fei’s expression turned cold.","This statement immediately revealed Ji Fei’s identity—the current matriarch of the Qin Family!","Yu Xin panicked, her eyes darting around as if searching for a way to defend herself. But Ji Fei was already losing patience.","\"Cat got your tongue? Open your eyes and take a good look. Are the beads on this bracelet the same as yours? If you say they are, I’ll call a jewelry appraiser right now to examine them in front of everyone! I’d love to see how an antique bracelet somehow became your new one!\"","Not daring to go up against a member of the Qin Family, Yu Xin could only try to save face by saying, \"I never said Jiaxi stole it. I just said my bracelet was lost.\"","Qin Zhao snorted coldly and said, \"So you’re saying you and Qin Jiaxi have identical bracelets, but yours got lost, so everyone just assumed it was hers and tried to take it from her to give to you?\"","Yu Xin was at a loss for words.","Qin Rong chimed in, \"Damaging someone else’s property beyond a certain value can land you in jail. That’s an antique bracelet my sister-in-law gave her. If we’re talking market value, it’s worth at least ten million. And you all broke it.\"","The moment these words were spoken, the room erupted in chaos.","\"What? I thought the most expensive version of that bracelet was only worth a million!\"","\"That can’t be true. Why would Qin Jiaxi have a bracelet worth ten million? What’s going on here?\"","Seeing everyone still trying to shift the blame, Qin Yi couldn’t help but add, \"The bracelets in the same series look similar, but the most expensive one is only worth a million. Jiaxi’s is an antique, one of a kind in the world. And now the beads are missing... Should I call the police right now?\"","Finally, someone couldn’t take it anymore and said, \"Yu Xin, that bracelet is yours, right?\"","\"Earlier, you were crying about how your brother gave you that bracelet and it went missing. When we said we saw a similar one on Qin Jiaxi, you didn’t deny it!\"","\"Young Master Su, when we asked you about the bracelet earlier, we even mentioned whether Qin Jiaxi had taken Yu Xin’s. You didn’t explain anything, so we misunderstood!\"","\"This isn’t our fault!\"","Afraid of being held responsible, everyone started exposing the misleading actions of the two. After all, if they knew Qin Jiaxi already had the bracelet but still made those ambiguous statements, weren’t they deliberately misleading everyone?","They might not be afraid of offending Qin Jiaxi, but if the bracelet was really that valuable, how many of them could afford to pay for it? They didn’t want to be arrested.","This left Su Ze and Yu Xin looking extremely uncomfortable. Since they had indeed done these things, they had no way to defend themselves.","[See, some things just can’t withstand scrutiny. But Yu Xin is truly a master at manipulating people. She deliberately played the victim so Qin Han would give her a bracelet from the same series. Once she received it, she started scheming. Since Qin Jiaxi had always worn the bracelet discreetly, no one had seen it before. So everyone assumed Yu Xin was the first to wear it, and when it went missing, Qin Jiaxi started wearing it. Add to that her affair with Su Ze, knowing that even if Su Ze didn’t understand what she was doing, he would never defend Qin Jiaxi. This way, Yu Xin could once again use her classmates to bully Qin Jiaxi and vent her frustration. If she couldn’t have the bracelet, she might as well destroy it.]","[It seems like she’s done this many times before, and it’s always worked. Of course, Su Ze and Qin Han are also complicit in this.]","Finally, Su Ze couldn’t take it anymore. \"Shut up, all of you! What did Yu Xin and I ever say? You’re the ones who jumped to conclusions! What does this have to do with us?\"","Yu Xin also put on a pitiful expression, even hiding behind Su Ze. \"I don’t know how things turned out this way. I really didn’t know anything. The bracelets just happened to look similar, that’s all.\"","At this point, everyone understood—they had wronged Qin Jiaxi.","In the past, it might have been brushed off, but now that the bracelet was so valuable...","\"It was her who pulled it off! We just said a few words!\" someone pointed at the female classmate who had led the bullying against Qin Jiaxi.","The female classmate, who seemed to have some status, was flushed with embarrassment from Yu Xin’s betrayal but still stubbornly said, \"I was just being reasonable. If Qin Jiaxi had shown us the bracelet for verification, there wouldn’t have been any misunderstanding, and the bracelet wouldn’t have broken.\"","\"Quite the master of twisting words. Cousin, call the police,\" Ji Fei said bluntly.","Everyone immediately panicked and started trying to persuade the female classmate.","\"You... you’re going too far!\" the female classmate said, looking nervously at Su Ze, as if hoping he would speak up for her.","But Su Ze just glared at everyone, not bothering to help her.","\"Haha, you didn’t think about the consequences when you were bullying her, did you?\" Qin Zhao sneered. Then, after a moment of thought, he whispered to Ji Fei, \"Sister-in-law, calling the police might not be enough. How about we try something else?\"","Ji Fei shrugged indifferently. As long as Qin Jiaxi got justice, she didn’t care how.","Qin Zhao took the beads Qin Jiaxi had just picked up and suddenly tossed them into the pool. \"Fine, we won’t call the police. But you, you, you, and you...\"","He pointed at everyone who had bullied Qin Jiaxi. \"Go fish out the beads. If even one is missing, we’ll call the police. Consider this your only chance.\"","Instantly, the faces of those named turned ashen.","Ji Fei, sharp-eyed, noticed Qin Zhao had secretly pocketed one of the beads. Well, good luck to them trying to find all of them now."]},{"number":359,"title":"Chapter 359: Aren't You Two Inseparable","paragraphs":["When they bullied Qin Jiaxi, they felt nothing, but now they were overwhelmed with a deep sense of shame.","They wanted to fight back; how could they accept being treated like this?","But Qin Zhao directly said, \"Damaging someone else's property, combined with the collective bullying just now, I think it’s negotiable to request your school to expel you. I advise you to know when to stop. Right now, we can still settle this matter quietly. Later, we might not be so kind.\"","Finally, the boy who had been hiding in the pool, unable to withstand Qin Zhao's piercing gaze, couldn't hold back anymore and shouted, \"Why don’t you all just come in? We were the ones who wronged her in the first place. I don’t want to be dragged down any further. What if this gets reported to the school...\"","The others weren’t fools either. Hearing their companion’s words, they immediately backed down.","They had dared to bully Qin Jiaxi so brazenly before because no one had stood up for her. After all, in everyone’s eyes, Qin Jiaxi’s biggest supporter was her boyfriend, Su Ze. But now, it was clear that Su Ze was completely subdued.","What was most baffling was that the people who came with Qin Zhao also seemed to be from the Qin family. Instead of siding with Yu Xin, they were supporting Qin Jiaxi? Perhaps they were siding with justice rather than family ties, or maybe it was some internal power struggle within the wealthy families. They didn’t want to become collateral damage, so they took the opportunity to step back gracefully.","It could only be said that these people were deeply brainwashed, as they still hadn’t realized the issue of their identities.","In the end, only the ringleader, the female classmate, didn’t step back. Instead, she glared at Qin Jiaxi with red eyes, her entire body trembling.","\"You seem to be the main culprit. It looks like your family is quite wealthy, so you can afford to pay for this bracelet,\" Ji Fei said with a smile, though it was clear she had already figured out that, judging by the female classmate’s attire, she was also a wealthy heiress.","Being called a criminal made the female classmate even angrier.","Meanwhile, her companions, who were picking up items in the pool, called out her name, trying to calm her down.","This gave Ji Fei the chance to learn the female classmate’s name.","Ji Fei wanted to know why this girl was so fixated on targeting Qin Jiaxi.","[Ah? So this is the girl who’s been actively leading the bullying against Qin Jiaxi. Let me see... She’s been in the same school as Su Ze, and her family does business with the Su family. She’s been infatuated with Su Ze since childhood and has been jokingly called the \"Captain of the School Hunk Protection Squad.\" She’s always driven away any girls who got close to Su Ze. Anyone who got too close to Su Ze, as long as their status wasn’t as high as hers, would be bullied by her little clique. Qin Jiaxi wasn’t the first, but because she felt Qin Jiaxi wasn’t worthy of being Su Ze’s girlfriend, she’s been targeting her for over a year... Wait... let me see more!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were listening, growing increasingly furious, when suddenly the narrative was cut off, leaving them curious. What had their sister-in-law discovered now?","Ji Fei suddenly turned her gaze to Su Ze, her expression changing several times.","[Good, I had a feeling this was the case. That scoundrel!]","Before Ji Fei’s inner thoughts could explode, she addressed the female classmate directly, \"I’m curious, why do you hate Qin Jiaxi so much? Has she ever done anything to hurt you?\"","The female classmate was caught off guard by the question and froze for a moment. Her eyes, however, involuntarily drifted toward Su Ze.","Qin Jiaxi, naturally, knew the reason. She was sensitive enough to understand that it was because of Su Ze. In the past, she hadn’t wanted to confront the issue, not wanting to attack another girl in this way. But now, she realized how foolish she had been. The other girl had bullied her relentlessly; why shouldn’t she fight back? She should be like her siblings.","So Qin Jiaxi spoke up directly, \"She hates me because she likes Su Ze.\"","These words immediately made the female classmate’s face flush with embarrassment, and Su Ze’s expression darkened instantly. \"Qin Jiaxi!\"","His shout made Qin Yi shiver. He hadn’t expected Su Ze to dare shout at Qin Jiaxi so boldly in this situation. His face turned cold. \"Are you shouting at Jiaxi? What right do you have? It seems I need to have a serious talk with your family about your manners!\"","Su Ze’s face paled, but he didn’t dare retort to Qin Yi. He could only say coldly, \"Jiaxi, proving your innocence is enough. Do you have to make things so awkward for everyone? What are you doing now? Gossiping? How have you become like this?\"","\"That’s right, Jiaxi. It’s not good to gossip like this. Once we retrieve the bracelet beads, let’s just drop it, okay?\" Yu Xin chimed in softly from behind, trying to mediate.","Ji Fei, however, chuckled lightly and said to the female classmate, \"You’ve been targeting Qin Jiaxi because she’s Su Ze’s girlfriend, but I think you might need to get your eyes checked. Maybe you should visit an ophthalmologist.\"","The female classmate was stunned by Ji Fei’s words and was about to lose her temper when Ji Fei took a step to the side, giving the girl a clear view.","Ji Fei pointed in the direction of Su Ze and Yu Xin and said, \"Anyone who isn’t blind can see who Su Ze truly cares about. The nominal girlfriend or the one he truly loves—are you targeting the wrong person? Don’t be so proud of being used as a pawn. They probably think you’re an idiot.\"","With Ji Fei’s earth-shattering words and her gaze directed toward them, only two people stood there, clearly separated from the rest.","Su Ze stood in front, while Yu Xin seemed to be hiding behind him, seeking protection.","They stood closer to each other than anyone else.","In contrast, Qin Jiaxi, the so-called girlfriend of Su Ze, stood completely on the opposite side.","In an instant, it was as if the fog had lifted.","The people picking up the beads froze, staring in this direction, struck by the revelation.","Qin Jiaxi, who had always had a vague sense of what was happening, finally realized the truth. She had been too close to the situation to see it clearly, while others had figured it out at a glance.","She truly had been a fool.","Meanwhile, Su Ze and Yu Xin, now exposed, couldn’t hold back their anger.","\"What nonsense are you spouting!\"","\"Big sister, how could you accuse me like this? I would never... Jiaxi and I are good friends. I’m not...\" Yu Xin’s eyes welled up with tears, looking as if she were about to cry.","\"You’re just a shameless homewrecker,\" Qin Rong, who rarely engaged in arguments, couldn’t hold back anymore. \"We saw it all when we arrived!\"","Qin Yi also couldn’t contain himself. He had held back earlier due to a lack of evidence, but now he spoke up, \"Earlier in the woods, weren’t you two kissing like there was no tomorrow? The four of us aren’t blind!\"","Qin Yi grew angrier the more he thought about it. They should have caught them red-handed earlier in the woods, but at the time, they had only seen their profiles. Although he had attended wealthy family gatherings and seen Su Ze a few times, they weren’t in the same age group and had never interacted. So, he hadn’t recognized him at first.","It wasn’t until he saw Su Ze’s face clearly that he realized who this scoundrel was. He couldn’t understand why his uncle had allowed such a person to be his younger sister’s boyfriend.","Now, Su Ze and Yu Xin were truly stunned. They had never expected that their earlier actions had been witnessed. No wonder the Qin family had treated them this way. Had Qin Jiaxi heard about it, which was why she had acted so coldly toward him earlier?"]},{"number":360,"title":"Chapter 360: Could it be that Qin Han has done something utterly despicable again","paragraphs":["Su Ze subconsciously believed that Qin Jiaxi was deeply in love with him, so much so that she couldn’t live without him. It was only because she had been hurt that she was treating him this way.","Moreover, he remembered that there had been no one around earlier. Even if someone had seen them, it was from a distance. So, without thinking, he refuted the accusation and took two steps forward, trying to grab Qin Jiaxi’s hand. “I didn’t do anything wrong. I was with Yu Xin earlier, but we were only discussing your bracelet. Yu Xin just tripped, and I helped her up. It must have been a misunderstanding.”","Now was not the time to expose his relationship with Yu Xin. He had to suppress it.","Yu Xin also knew how serious the situation was. If it had been someone else who saw them, they might have been able to argue that it wasn’t them. But the person who saw them was from the Qin family! There was no way they could argue their way out of this. Su Ze’s explanation was the only thing that could barely save face.","“That’s right, you must have seen it wrong. We were just...” Yu Xin tried to chime in.","But Ji Fei didn’t give her a chance to finish, cutting her off sharply. “Are you sure your lips didn’t collide when you ‘fell’ together?”","What kind of explanation was that? Both of them vehemently denied it.","“Hmph, why don’t you wipe off the messy lipstick stains on your mouths before you try to explain?”","As soon as Ji Fei said this, everyone’s eyes immediately focused on their lips.","Although Yu Xin had been wearing a light shade of lipstick, close to her natural lip color, the smudged traces at the corners of her mouth were still visible. As for Su Ze, if you looked closely, you could clearly see the remnants of lipstick on his lips.","It was obvious that they had been kissing passionately earlier, leaving each other’s lipstick behind.","Qin Zhao laughed. “Can’t you even cheat properly? You didn’t even bother to clean up after yourselves.”","The Qin family members couldn’t help but chuckle.","Su Ze and Yu Xin were truly at a loss for words now. They instinctively tried to wipe their mouths, which only confirmed everyone’s suspicions.","In an instant, the way everyone looked at them changed. It was hard to believe because, in their eyes, Su Ze was the eldest son of the Su family! Why would he need to sneak around and cheat? It was simply unbelievable.","Ji Fei added, “At least they’re professionals when it comes to lying through their teeth. They don’t even blush or feel guilty. It seems they’ve been deceiving Jiaxi for a long time.”","The turn of events was quite unexpected. Without much thought, they had exposed the cheating couple on the spot. Although Ji Fei was worried about whether Qin Jiaxi could handle it, she couldn’t let it continue. After all, as the matriarch of the family, she had to protect the younger ones.","So, it was better to end the pain quickly.","Ji Fei turned directly to Qin Jiaxi and said, “Do you see now? You’ve been deceived.”","Qin Jiaxi didn’t cry, though her eyes were red. With a cold expression, she nodded. “I know. I’ve been deceived from the very beginning. Su Ze never liked me. He’s always liked... Yu Xin. That’s why he kept choosing to help Yu Xin and hurt me, time and time again.”","Qin Jiaxi spoke everything out loud, as if she were tearing open her own heart, forcing herself to see the truth. All the sweet memories she had cherished were fake, just illusions she had painted over in her mind.","“Jiaxi, you...” Su Ze panicked. “How can you deny my feelings for you? This can all be explained, I...”","“Su Ze, from the first time you stood by Yu Xin’s side without reason and made me suffer, I should have seen it clearly. I’ve been deceiving myself all along, giving you the chance to hurt me. From now on, we’re no longer in a relationship. You’re free to be with whoever you want.” After saying this, Qin Jiaxi lowered her eyes and fell silent. It wasn’t a dramatic breakup, just a quiet, matter-of-fact ending.","“You... you’re breaking up with me?” Su Ze couldn’t believe it. “Don’t forget, it was you who liked me. I was the one who gave you the chance to be my girlfriend!”","Even now, Su Ze still had the audacity to act as if he had done Qin Jiaxi a favor by letting her be his girlfriend.","It was truly disgusting.","For a moment, Qin Jiaxi wanted to retort, to remind him that it was Su Ze who had pursued her first, who had confessed his feelings and made her fall for him.","But suddenly, it all felt pointless.","Let him say whatever he wanted. She had indeed loved him once, so she couldn’t deny that. But since they were breaking up now, arguing about it would only drag things out.","Because of Qin Jiaxi’s gentle nature, she didn’t argue back, and Ji Fei missed the chance to dig deeper into the matter.","“Consider me blind,” Qin Jiaxi said coldly.","Qin Rong, feeling heartbroken, hugged Qin Jiaxi tightly.","Su Ze was furious and wanted to yell at her, but Ji Fei interrupted him.","Ji Fei asked, “Aren’t you going to ask him why he did this? If he likes Yu Xin, why didn’t he just date her openly? Why did he have to make a grand confession to you, date you in name, and then secretly be with Yu Xin?”","Ji Fei already knew the answer, but she couldn’t say it herself. She wanted Qin Jiaxi to force it out of him, to completely sever their relationship.","Su Ze’s anger instantly deflated, and his eyes darted around nervously.","But Qin Jiaxi seemed to have already accepted it. After all, her mother and brother had also chosen Yu Xin over her without reason, so she had long since stopped questioning why.","Seeing Qin Jiaxi’s emotionless expression, Ji Fei felt both heartbroken and helpless. She was about to think of a way to expose Su Ze even further when suddenly, a female classmate who had been silent all along finally exploded.","Whether it was seeing the two of them standing together earlier, the lipstick stains, or Qin Jiaxi’s revelations, there had been a voice in her heart telling her that it was all true. Su Ze’s attitude toward Qin Jiaxi had always been strange. He never stood up for her when she was being bullied, and whenever there was a conflict between Qin Jiaxi and Yu Xin, he would always side with Yu Xin, watching Qin Jiaxi suffer without a care.","Back then, she had felt smug, enjoying the fact that Su Ze’s girlfriend wasn’t happy. But now, she felt a chill run down her spine.","And what Ji Fei had said earlier—had she been used as a pawn?","No, that couldn’t be. She had to find a reasonable explanation. How could Su Ze like Yu Xin? What did that make Qin Jiaxi? And what did all their actions against Qin Jiaxi mean?","“No, that’s not possible... Su Ze only takes care of Yu Xin because she’s his good friend’s sister, that’s all...” The female classmate seemed deeply shaken but still tried to argue based on her preconceived notions.","But when she saw the lipstick stains that were hard to wipe off, her lips trembled.","The Qin family members were also confused. They had heard something about a brother and sister before.","But wasn’t Yu Xin from an orphanage? Where did she get a brother?","It was only then that Ji Fei remembered something.","She had heard before that Qin Han, in order to protect Yu Xin’s pride, had forced Qin Jiaxi to hide her identity at school.","And these people, who were usually so snobbish, had treated Yu Xin so well. If it wasn’t because of her status, it would have been very strange.","[Could it be that Qin Han had done something despicable again?]"]},{"number":361,"title":"Chapter 361: You Treat Qin Jiaxi as a Target","paragraphs":["“What brother? Who is her brother?” Qin Yi immediately sensed something was off and asked.","The female classmate seemed to have grabbed onto a lifeline, as if proving Yu Xin’s extraordinary status could somehow serve as an excuse to explain everything.","At that moment, Yu Xin felt as though she had been cornered, her guilty conscience making her want to interrupt immediately.","But the female classmate was quicker, turning to Qin Yi and saying, “Don’t you know? She’s Qin Han’s younger sister! Because Qin Han and Su Ze are close friends, he asked Su Ze to take care of Yu Xin!”","The Qin Family was stunned.","Ji Fei let out a cold laugh, glaring at Yu Xin.","Yu Xin was already drenched in sweat.","Su Ze, on the other hand, was at a loss for words.","At this point, Qin Yi still didn’t think Qin Han was being outrageous. After all, Qin Han had always wanted the family to adopt a daughter, and he seemed to have a good relationship with Yu Xin. So, Qin Yi simply assumed that Qin Han treated Yu Xin like a younger sister and referred to her as such when talking to others. It wasn’t much different from saying, “This is a younger sister I’m close with.”","So, he just muttered, “He’s never shown much care for his actual younger sister, but he treats an outsider like a treasure? And he even asked his actual younger sister’s boyfriend to take care of her? Is he out of his mind?”","This casual remark struck like a thunderbolt, silencing everyone in the room.","“What did you say?” the female classmate exclaimed, her eyes wide with shock.","Qin Yi was taken aback, not understanding why she was reacting so strongly.","“Isn’t Qin Han’s actual younger sister Yu Xin?” the female classmate shouted, no longer holding back. “What are you saying? Who is Qin Han’s actual younger sister?”","If Yu Xin wasn’t his actual sister, then Su Ze’s so-called “taking care of a friend’s younger sister” was utterly ridiculous.","If she was his actual sister, then why would Qin Han allow Su Ze to treat his own sister like that?","Qin Yi was stunned for a moment before replying incredulously, “What do you mean? Did you all think Yu Xin was Qin Han’s actual younger sister? She doesn’t even share our surname. Qin Han’s actual younger sister is Qin Jiaxi. She shares our surname—how could you not tell?”","Qin Yi then turned to Qin Jiaxi, “Jiaxi? What’s going on? Didn’t everyone know you’re the Qin Family’s eldest daughter?”","Previously, Qin Yi had thought that perhaps Qin Jiaxi was just keeping a low profile at school or that her personality made her an easy target for bullying.","But how could someone else pretend to be Qin Han’s actual younger sister while the real one was treated like an impostor?","Qin Jiaxi seemed to have realized something, her heart trembling as she said, “My brother told me not to reveal my identity at school...” Her gaze then shifted to Yu Xin, the apparent beneficiary of this situation.","Yu Xin’s face had turned ashen.","“My brother usually comes to school to visit Yu Xin. I didn’t know...” Qin Jiaxi’s voice trailed off, her pupils shaking with disbelief. She couldn’t even bring herself to voice her suspicions.","She had always known her brother favored others, but if her suspicions were true, just how much did he despise her to do something like this?","“No, no! Qin Han himself said that Yu Xin is his actual younger sister!” someone from the crowd couldn’t help but shout.","They weren’t stupid enough to mistake someone with a different surname for his sister. It was because Qin Han himself had told them to take care of his younger sister that they had believed Yu Xin was his actual sister!","“You... Su Ze, we’ve talked about this in front of you, and you never corrected us! That’s why we thought we were taking care of a friend’s sister! You lied too!” another person shouted.","At this point, both Su Ze and Yu Xin were visibly shaken.","Su Ze clenched his teeth, his face alternating between green and purple.","Yu Xin was utterly humiliated.","The revelation of the truth left Qin Jiaxi almost unable to stand.","Her heart felt as though it had been torn apart.","She had already resigned herself to the fact that her brother and her boyfriend both preferred Yu Xin over her.","But why were they so cruel as to strip away her identity too? Was she really that detestable?","Qin Jiaxi’s expression went blank, the cruelty of it all too much for her to bear.","She felt as though she had been plunged into an icy abyss.","But in the next moment, warmth surrounded her.","When she came to her senses, she saw Qin Rong holding her tightly, her face full of concern, while Ji Fei also moved closer, gently patting her head.","Standing beside her were her brothers, Qin Yi and Qin Zhao.","Tears welled up in Qin Jiaxi’s eyes.","“I... am Qin Jiaxi... of the Qin Family of Y City!” Qin Jiaxi’s voice, neither too loud nor too soft, reached everyone around her. She turned to Yu Xin, “Just how much more do you plan to take from me?”","Yu Xin, as if her tail had been stepped on, immediately defended herself, “Jiaxi, how can you say that? When have I ever taken anything from you? Qin Han does treat me like a younger sister. What he says to others and how they interpret it—how is that my fault? Should I have ignored his care just because of you?”","“Here we go again, passing the blame. Were you a chef in your past life? You’re so good at tossing blame around,” Ji Fei sneered. “Yes, yes, it’s always someone else’s fault, never yours. It’s always others who misunderstood.”","Yu Xin was left speechless, never having encountered a noblewoman like Ji Fei before. She could only look at Ji Fei with feigned grievance, \"If you don’t believe me, you can contact Qin Han.\"","After all, Yu Xin knew Qin Han would back her up.","Ji Fei narrowed her eyes at Yu Xin, “Oh, we’ll definitely have a good talk with him.”","[Interesting... a “sister” in name only. Yu Xin is truly something. It seems neither Qin Han nor Su Ze are aware of each other’s true relationship with Yu Xin.]","Earlier, while observing the drama, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong had suspected that Qin Han and Yu Xin’s relationship wasn’t purely platonic. Now, seeing that Yu Xin seemed to have something going on with Su Ze as well... Wait, is she playing both of them?!","Of course, now wasn’t the time to dwell on that.","The female classmate’s world had completely crumbled with the revelation of the truth.","She suddenly lunged at Su Ze, grabbing his collar and shouting, “It’s all a lie! You lied to me! You used me!”","Su Ze, who had never been treated like this before, roughly pushed her away, causing her to fall to the ground in a pitiful state.","“What nonsense are you spouting? This... this is all just a misunderstanding,” Su Ze refused to admit the truth. How could he possibly admit to being so despicable?","But the female classmate burst into bitter laughter, tears streaming down her face as she pointed at Su Ze, “Do you think I’m an idiot? I get it now. That’s why you made such a grand show of confessing to Qin Jiaxi. It was all fake! You used her as a shield, knowing we’d target your girlfriend if her status wasn’t up to par. You made Qin Jiaxi the target, refusing to acknowledge her identity, just so you could secretly date Yu Xin behind the scenes!”"]},{"number":362,"title":"Chapter 362: Where Does Our Little Sister Need to Strive So Hard","paragraphs":["It was one thing to feel unworthy of someone, but to discover that the man she had admired for years was so despicable and shameless was like swallowing a fly—utterly disgusting. What made it worse was that he had schemed against an innocent girl just to protect the woman he loved. Such behavior was something even she found contemptible.","The female classmate angrily pointed at the two of them. \"You couldn't bear to let your precious one get hurt, so you pushed Qin Jiaxi to the forefront as a scapegoat! Su Ze, you have such a cruel heart, so vile. How could you be this kind of person? You knew perfectly well that Qin Han deceived everyone, making people misunderstand their identities, yet you still went along with it. Aren't you afraid we might ruin Qin Jiaxi's life?\"","Yes, if it were just about identity issues, Su Ze's reluctance to openly date Yu Xin and instead choose someone of higher status as a shield wouldn't be so despicable.","But because of Qin Han's underhanded tactics, the identities of the two girls had been completely reversed in everyone's eyes. Yet Su Ze still went ahead with his plan, showing no regard for Qin Jiaxi's well-being. Such behavior was worse than that of an animal.","The Qin Family members trembled with rage upon hearing this.","This was simply too much bullying.","Su Ze hadn't expected his hidden motives to be completely exposed. His face flushed with shame and anger. \"You're talking nonsense! Shut up!\"","\"Su Ze, do you still think we're fools?\" the female classmate roared. \"You thought right—I will target the person you love. As you wish, from now on, Yu Xin can wait for it! If you dare play me like this, even if I can't touch you, I can certainly make her suffer!\"","\"You...\" Su Ze was furious and was about to issue a warning when he heard Qin Jiaxi's voice.","Guilt and fear gripped him, and he couldn't help but shudder at the sound of her soft voice.","“Why me? What have I ever done to you to deserve this?” Qin Jiaxi finally couldn't hold back her question.","Facing Qin Jiaxi, Su Ze wanted to deny everything, but he was truly at a loss for words. After all, his secrets had been completely laid bare. He had never felt so humiliated before, and this situation was driving him to the brink of madness.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei felt something flash through her mind, but with so much drama unfolding, she couldn't spare the mental energy to dig deeper. In response to Qin Jiaxi's question, Ji Fei gave the most straightforward answer.","\"It's laughable, but it's probably because you're from the Qin Family,\" Ji Fei said.","\"Because the Su Family wants to arrange a marriage alliance with the Qin Family?\" Qin Yi interjected.","Qin Zhao sneered, \"Oh, I see. People at school might not know, but those in our circle are well aware of who's the pearl and who's the fake. He had to put on a show for his family, lest they find out he's messing around with a fake and take action against her. What a devoted lover, protecting the fake in every way.\"","Choosing Qin Jiaxi was probably Su Ze's only option, but it was still a cruel and heartless move.","So, what was said in the woods was likely about waiting until the fake became the real deal, then switching girlfriends. By then, the Su Family would also assess who held a higher position in the Qin Family. If Qin Han took over the power of the Qin Family's third branch, Yu Xin might actually surpass Qin Jiaxi, and the fake would outshine the real pearl.","With every word they spoke, Su Ze felt as though another layer of his dignity was being stripped away.","His thoughts were laid bare for everyone to mock, and he couldn't stay any longer.","\"Think whatever you want. I... I know I'm innocent,\" Su Ze said stiffly. \"If you don't believe me, then let's just break up.\"","Yu Xin, who had been called a fake, couldn't contain her resentment. She had hoped Su Ze would at least admit something to salvage a bit of dignity, but she was disappointed. She knew Su Ze wanted to figure things out later, as today's events had caught them off guard. They could only retreat for now and come up with a plan later.","But when Su Ze said that, Ji Fei and the others burst into laughter.","The mocking laughter felt like a series of slaps to their faces.","Su Ze turned to leave, but then he heard Qin Jiaxi call out, \"Wait.\"","Su Ze's heart stirred, thinking Qin Jiaxi might still have feelings for him.","But as soon as he turned around, a harsh slap landed on his face.","Su Ze's head snapped to the side, and after the initial shock came anger. He turned back, only to see the usually meek Qin Jiaxi raise her other hand and deliver a slap to Yu Xin, who was standing beside him.","Yu Xin was stunned. After all, she was usually the one bullying Qin Jiaxi, never the other way around.","Even though she had falsely accused Qin Jiaxi of hitting her before, she had never actually been struck!","Qin Jiaxi's actions left Su Ze momentarily dazed, but before he could react, he received a second slap from her.","Yu Xin, who was about to retaliate, saw Su Ze get hit again and froze, giving Qin Jiaxi the chance to deliver a second slap to her as well.","The sound of these four slaps drowned out all other conversations.","Everyone stared in shock at the usually timid Qin Jiaxi.","Qin Jiaxi, who had never done anything like this before, was left panting after delivering the four slaps.","Ji Fei shook her head and tutted, \"Tsk tsk tsk, that's not enough!\"","Qin Jiaxi had tears in her eyes as she delivered the slaps, but once she caught her breath, she exhaled deeply, feeling as though a weight had been lifted.","\"You... you dare hit me!\" Su Ze finally reacted, looking as though he was about to charge at her.","Yu Xin also covered her face, glaring venomously at Qin Jiaxi.","Qin Jiaxi glared back. \"You've treated me like this, so what's wrong with me hitting you? If you dare bully me again, I... I'll fight back with everything I've got!\"","Perhaps it was the lack of someone to protect her that made Qin Jiaxi instinctively think of fighting back with her life.","\"Our little sister doesn't need to risk her life for this,\" Qin Yi said with a smile, stepping forward. Before Su Ze could react, Qin Yi punched him, sending him staggering. Qin Yi shook his hand, which hurt from the impact. \"Bullying the Qin Family's young lady—do you think we're dead or something?\"","\"If our sister has to fight back on her own, doesn't that make us, her brothers, look like useless scum?\" Qin Zhao said pointedly. Without waiting for Su Ze to recover from the punch, he kicked Su Ze squarely in the stomach.","Su Ze was sent flying backward, landing hard on the ground.","He was completely dazed, unable to react for a moment. When he looked up, he saw the two brothers standing protectively in front of Qin Jiaxi, as if saying, \"You think you can bully our sister and get away with just a couple of slaps? We're the Qin Corporation of Y City. Do you think we need to think twice before beating you up?\"","It seemed that Qin Han had given him the illusion that he could mistreat a girl from the Qin Family without facing any consequences.","But at this moment, Su Ze didn't dare fight back. Deep down, he knew that if he clashed with the Qin Family, his parents would tear him apart."]},{"number":363,"title":"Chapter 363: Crazy Accusations","paragraphs":["It was also the illusion given by Qin Han and his mother that made Yu Xin never expect someone would protect Qin Jiaxi to such an extent.","At this moment, Yu Xin felt guilty and couldn't help but want to retreat.","Although Qin Zhao and Qin Yi didn’t hit women, and Qin Rong wasn’t good at physical confrontations, Ji Fei had quite a reputation for slapping people. And she had been itching to do it for a while.","But before Ji Fei could act, a female classmate took matters into her own hands, true to her word.","She slapped Yu Xin to the ground, pinned her down, and kept slapping her repeatedly.","Yu Xin’s cheeks visibly swelled up.","Yu Xin screamed incessantly, trying to fight back, but only ended up getting beaten worse.","Normally, someone might have stepped in to help, but this time everyone just watched the spectacle. Qin Zhao, however, still remembered their task and shouted at the people in the pool, “Don’t think you’re innocent just because you were deceived. The bullying and stealing of the bracelet aren’t over yet. Hurry up and pick them up!”","And so, the people in the pool continued to miserably pick up the beads, too busy to even glance at the fight.","But even after collecting all the beads, one was still missing. They were frantic, worried it might have fallen into the drain. One after another, they dove down to check, looking disheveled and anxious, almost on the verge of tears.","Because of the chaos, more and more onlookers gathered.","Ji Fei and the others didn’t want to be surrounded by a crowd. They had done all they could, so it was better to take Qin Jiaxi to change her clothes first.","Qin Zhao stepped forward, pretending he had found the last bead, and issued a few more threats before leaving with the group.","What they didn’t know was that after they left, Su Ze immediately went to rescue Yu Xin. After all, she was his beloved, and he couldn’t bear to see her hurt. He then lashed out at the bystanders with a warning.","“If any of you dare to spread word of what happened today, don’t blame me for being ruthless.”","Of course, such things could never truly be kept under wraps—it was only a matter of time.","But both Su Ze and Yu Xin knew that as long as they adamantly denied it and no one publicly exposed them, they could twist the truth. After all, Qin Han would never admit at school that Qin Jiaxi was his sister.","Anything others said would just be dismissed as rumors.","But they were too naive.","The female classmate who had struck Yu Xin had already decided to go all out.","Even if she didn’t have concrete evidence, there were always nosy people around secretly recording.","After the female classmate stormed off in tears, she began offering a reward for the video. Those who had secretly recorded it, though too intimidated by Su Ze to show it off publicly, were willing to sell it to her.","And so, a scandal that could ruin reputations was about to erupt on the university’s exclusive forum.","Of course, the female classmate also knew that the people involved today were not to be trifled with, and she didn’t want her own disgrace exposed. So, she only released a segment exposing the affair between those two, along with the backstory of Qin Han’s fake sister, and even thoughtfully blurred out Ji Fei and the others.","Meanwhile, Yu Xin had already discussed with Su Ze to deny everything publicly. She then called Qin Han, who was about to give a speech at the school, crying about how she had been bullied and beaten over the bracelet incident.","When it came to tarnishing Qin Jiaxi’s reputation, Yu Xin was a natural. She also accused the other Qin family members, having shrewdly noticed that Qin Han disliked those relatives. So, she had no qualms about slandering them, even claiming that they had deliberately suppressed her because they didn’t want to adopt her.","When Qin Han saw the photos Yu Xin sent of her swollen, slapped face, he was furious.","He thought Qin Jiaxi had grown too bold, using the presence of other relatives to back her up and turning against her own family. She didn’t even respect him as her older brother anymore—it was like she was siding with outsiders.","Qin Han cursed and tried to call Qin Jiaxi, but no one answered.","At that moment, Ji Fei and Qin Yi were accompanying Qin Jiaxi to the girls’ bathroom, while Qin Zhao and Qin Rong had gone out to buy her some clothes.","When Qin Zhao and Qin Rong returned with the clothes, they overheard Qin Yi on the phone with Third Uncle Qin, lodging a complaint.","As the eldest among the siblings, Qin Yi felt it was his duty to take the lead in this matter.","Speaking to his elder, Qin Yi’s tone was far from polite as he recounted everything Qin Han and Su Ze had done to Qin Jiaxi. He concluded with, “Uncle, if we hadn’t coincidentally come here today, who knows what might have happened to Jiaxi? I always thought she seemed a bit withdrawn, and now I understand why. After all the suffering she’s endured, with no one to stand up for her, how could she not be? Third Uncle, are you really going to let your daughter be treated like this by her brother and boyfriend? Just because she doesn’t say anything, does that mean you’ll pretend not to know? If your family is too busy, I’m here in Y City, the eldest and least busy brother. I’ll take care of Jiaxi from now on. After all, Qin Han doesn’t seem to want to be her brother anymore.”","These words were a slap in the face to Third Uncle Qin.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong couldn’t help but chuckle in satisfaction.","Third Uncle Qin deserved to be scolded. Being reprimanded by a junior was his just desserts. Look at the kind of son he had raised and the mess he had made.","Third Uncle Qin had hoped that Qin Han would follow in Qin Xian’s footsteps, but that was impossible now. Given what Qin Han had done, even if Qin Xian hadn’t explicitly said so, Qin Han was already out of the Qin family’s inner circle. Qin Xian would probably prefer to groom a distant relative over his own cousin.","In the break room at Qin Corporation’s branch office, it was currently rest time.","Except for Qin Zhao, all the Qin family members were present. Third Uncle Qin had been frozen in place since receiving the call.","Qin Yi, usually calm about his own affairs, was unusually loud this time. In the quiet break room, everyone overheard the key details.","Qin Xian had already been briefed on the situation through a conversation with his wife.","He hadn’t expected that these people would treat a Qin family girl like a fool.","Watching the video his wife had sent, he said, “Although they’ve been taught a lesson, they’ve been bullying Jiaxi for over a year, causing her significant psychological harm. We can’t let this go so easily.”","Qin Xian glanced at Third Uncle Qin, whose face grew darker and darker, exuding a low, oppressive aura.","He replied to his wife, “Don’t worry, I’ll leave it to Third Uncle to handle.”","Ji Fei: “Will he?”","Qin Xian: “He will.”","Third Uncle Qin was like the calm before a storm. His anger wasn’t directed at Qin Yi’s disrespect toward him as an elder but at the horrifying things he had just heard.","Even though it involved his own son, Third Uncle Qin immediately believed Qin Yi’s account.","After Qin Yi finished his complaint, Third Uncle Qin finally spoke, his first question being, “How is Jiaxi now?”","Qin Yi paused before answering, “Ji Fei and the others are with her, helping her change. Jiaxi seems... fine now. She ended the relationship decisively and faced it bravely.”","Third Uncle Qin let out a sigh of relief and said, “Thank you all for this. Rest assured, as her father, I won’t let her suffer like this again.”"]},{"number":364,"title":"Chapter 364: This Time, We Must Stand Firm for Our Daughter to the End","paragraphs":["Third Uncle Qin did not try to justify himself by saying that since Qin Jiaxi hadn’t spoken, he knew nothing. He understood that as a father, failing to notice his daughter’s unusual behavior and not taking the initiative to ask about it was a dereliction of duty. Moreover, his other son had led the charge in making his daughter feel wronged, which was a clear sign of his own failure in parenting. When had his son become so unreasonable, unable to distinguish right from wrong, and blurring the lines between family and outsiders?","Originally, he had wanted to have a good talk with his daughter, but knowing she wouldn’t be able to answer the phone anytime soon, he decisively ended the call and instead dialed Qin Han.","In the lounge, Qin Wenqiang and the family of Fourth Uncle Qin were all present. They exchanged glances, eager to gossip but hesitant to interrupt.","Soon, Qin Han answered the call.","“Dad, I was just about to call you. Let me tell you—” Qin Han was about to lodge a complaint when he was cut off by his father’s icy voice.","“Let me ask you something. Was it you who told Jiaxi not to reveal her identity at school? And you went around saying that Yu Xin is your real sister, letting everyone at the university mistake their identities and bully Jiaxi? What? Are you trying to replace your own sister? Did you even think to ask for my permission?”","Third Uncle Qin, who was usually composed and restrained, had never lashed out so fiercely before.","Beside him, Fourth Uncle Qin whispered to the children, “It’s rare to see Third Uncle this angry.”","Everyone’s eyes widened in astonishment.","Qin Wenqiang couldn’t help but ask her younger brother for details. Meanwhile, Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing, who had previously hung out with Ji Fei and the others and were part of a group chat, couldn’t resist seeking the juicy gossip. Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, having some free time, took it upon themselves to fill everyone in on the foolish things Qin Han had done.","Qin Han, however, didn’t think he was in the wrong. Even when confronted by his father, he felt no guilt. Instead, his anger only grew.","“What? She hit someone and still dares to play the victim? Just because I bought Yu Xin a similar bracelet, which led to some classmates misunderstanding and causing trouble for her, does that give her the right to bully Yu Xin in return? Dad, look at this. She’s already bullying others while hiding her identity. If we let her reveal who she is, who knows how much worse she’ll get? I’m only trying to discipline her by making her do this!”","In Qin Han’s eyes, Qin Jiaxi had always been the one bullying Yu Xin. If it weren’t for him and his mother keeping her in check, she would have caused even more trouble.","“Don’t be fooled by her usual act of playing the victim, pretending like everyone’s out to get her. That’s all just an act for us to see. If she didn’t have issues herself, why would so many people target her? As her brother, it’s my duty to keep her in line!”","“As for Yu Xin being my sister, what’s the big deal if I said it? Yu Xin is destined to become part of our family. What’s wrong with me saying she’s my sister ahead of time? If anyone’s to blame, it’s Jiaxi for constantly comparing herself to Yu Xin. Yu Xin is an orphan and already has it hard. Is it so wrong for me to show her a little extra care? Jiaxi’s jealousy and pettiness are the real problems here!”","“What nonsense are you spouting? Don’t you realize that the main reason your sister is being bullied is because of that brat Su Ze? Since Jiaxi’s identity hasn’t been revealed, people look down on her and think she’s not good enough for Su Ze. That’s why they bully her. And the root cause of all this is you, you idiot!”","Qin Han was momentarily stunned. He clearly hadn’t known the full story, but he still refused to believe it. “Dad, you’re really buying into this? I heard that today Jiaxi caused a huge scene, even threatening to break up with Su Ze because he didn’t stand up for her. She even dragged Yu Xin into it, accusing them of having an affair. I only asked Su Ze to look out for Yu Xin, and she’s twisting it into something else. She’s clearly unstable.”","“You!” Third Uncle Qin was so infuriated by his son’s stubbornness that he could barely breathe. Qin Fourth quickly rushed over to pat his back.","“Why are you so cruel to your own sister while being so kind to an outsider?” Third Uncle Qin couldn’t help but ask in confusion.","Qin Han, however, replied as if it were the most natural thing in the world. “I’m just disciplining my sister. If I’m not strict, she might go down the wrong path. And Yu Xin isn’t an outsider. No matter what you or Jiaxi say, Mom and I have already accepted her. We’re definitely going to adopt her. Even if Jiaxi tries to turn the rest of the family against Yu Xin, it won’t work. In fact, it only makes us more determined to adopt her.”","In the past, Third Uncle Qin had been able to keep Qin Han in check, but recently, he had been spending more time with Qin Xian, completely neglecting his son. This had led to Qin Han feeling increasingly resentful. Coupled with Yu Xin’s words of sympathy and support, Qin Han had come to believe that his father was losing his grip on reality and had stopped respecting him altogether.","“You... get back home! We’ll settle this later.” Third Uncle Qin had clearly lost all patience with arguing with Qin Han. For a son who refused to listen, he had no qualms about resorting to more forceful measures.","Moreover, he suspected that his wife might also be part of the problem and was determined to get to the bottom of it once he returned home.","Qin Han, however, was unfazed. After all, Yu Xin had just been through a lot, and if Qin Jiaxi wanted her identity recognized, she’d have to get his approval first.","“Dad, I don’t want to argue with you either. You’re too biased toward Jiaxi. I hope you calm down and think about it. Is it really okay to let Jiaxi continue like this? Our family doesn’t need a young lady with such poor character. It’s embarrassing. I won’t say more. I have things to do and will be home tonight.”","After spouting this nonsense, Qin Han hung up the phone.","This time, Third Uncle Qin was so angry that his vision blurred, and Qin Fourth hurriedly fetched his blood pressure medication.","Third Uncle Qin seemed to deflate all at once.","“How did I raise such a son? Why is this happening?” he murmured to himself.","“Isn’t your son raised by your wife?” Qin Fourth couldn’t help but remark. He had never liked Third Uncle Qin’s wife. His own wife had once said that Third Aunt had a poor character and wasn’t worthy of Third Uncle Qin. She had even predicted that their household would be plagued with strife.","Back then, he hadn’t paid much attention, but now he could see it clearly.","A good son had been turned into such a rebel, and a good daughter had been crushed under the weight of it all.","What a tragedy!","Third Uncle Qin only wallowed in despair for a moment. He knew he would deal with his son later. There was still another matter to attend to.","He turned to Qin Xian and said, “Recently, the Su Family has expressed interest in collaborating with us... I can’t let them treat my daughter like this.”","As the head of the family, Qin Xian’s decisions carried significant weight. If they were to retaliate, the consequences would be substantial. Therefore, Third Uncle Qin felt it necessary to inform him. If Qin Xian or others were unwilling, he was prepared to make concessions. No matter what, he was determined to stand up for his daughter. That scoundrel Su Ze had dared to toy with his daughter’s feelings, and that was absolutely unacceptable.","This time, he would support his daughter to the very end."]},{"number":365,"title":"Chapter 365: Venting Everywhere","paragraphs":["Qin Xian nodded and said, \"Our family naturally cannot be bullied, but there's no need to terminate the cooperation either. Third Uncle, you can contact the current head of the Su family and make it clear that cooperation is possible, but not with Su Ze's branch. If they want to work with us, they must replace him. As long as it's someone from their family, we will never cooperate. This is to stand up for our young lady.\"","Third Uncle Qin was stunned for a moment, while the others instantly admired Qin Xian's approach.","Simply terminating the cooperation would only result in mutual losses, and it might even unite the Su family against them. That way, Su Ze wouldn't receive the harshest lesson.","He remembered that the reason Su Ze was being groomed as the successor was due to the possibility of a marriage alliance with their family.","The Su family was vast, and the internal struggles were fierce. Currently, Su Ze's father held the upper hand because he had a son who was somewhat outstanding and had connections with the Qin family.","If that advantage were lost, the other members of the Su family would surely seize the opportunity and go all out to suppress Su Ze and his father.","Moreover, Su Ze's father had more than one son. If he had to bear such immense pressure and losses because of his son's mistake, one could only imagine what kind of life Su Ze would lead in the Su family from then on.","They wanted Su Ze to understand that Qin Jiaxi was not a girl he could toy with and discard after using her.","If he dared to bully her, he had to be prepared for the consequences.","This also served as a message to the upper echelons of Y City. Everyone knew Qin Jiaxi was somewhat of a background figure, but this time, the Qin family's public display of anger on her behalf made it clear to everyone: although Jiaxi was easygoing and gentle, the Qin family would always be her unwavering support. Anyone who dared to mistreat her in relationships or marriage proposals would face the consequences!","Qin Xian's move effectively paved the way for Qin Jiaxi's future.","Third Uncle Qin quickly understood the reasoning, though he was initially surprised that Qin Xian would go to such lengths for a cousin he wasn't particularly close to.","Previously, the elders had worried that Qin Xian might be too cold and detached. But now, it was clear that he had a warm heart; he just didn't show it often. When he did, the younger generation of the Qin family would see that Qin Xian was their greatest pillar of support.","Indeed, the younger members present looked at Qin Xian with deep admiration and emotion.","Without hesitation, Third Uncle Qin called the Su Family Patriarch.","He directly stated that they would only continue cooperation if the Su family replaced Su Ze. Otherwise, all collaborations would cease. The reason was that Su Ze had not only cheated but also manipulated and toyed with Qin Jiaxi for over a year, something the Qin family could not tolerate. If the Su family refused to replace him, they would find another company to work with.","The Su Family Patriarch was no pushover, but after hearing the full story and sensing the anger from the Qin family, especially with Qin Xian's recent involvement, it was clear that this matter had the approval of the Qin family's leader.","Originally, the Su Family Patriarch had planned to use Qin Xian's presence to arrange an engagement ceremony for Su Ze, hoping to get closer to the young and promising new head of the Qin family. But now, with this scandal, the Su Family Patriarch was furious with his wayward descendant.","\"Don't worry, we will definitely give your Jiaxi a proper explanation,\" the Su Family Patriarch assured.","\"We are old acquaintances, so we haven't completely severed ties. Maintaining the cooperation is out of respect for you. We don't need any explanation; just make sure Su Ze and his mistress stay far away from our Jiaxi!\" Third Uncle Qin said bluntly.","The Su Family Patriarch had no choice but to swallow his pride and apologize. After hanging up, he immediately summoned Su Ze's father and gave him a stern reprimand.","Su Ze's father was left red-faced and seething, silently cursing his son.","He wanted to apologize to Third Uncle Qin right away, but the Su Family Patriarch stopped him. \"The fact that they contacted me directly shows they don't want to deal with you anymore. Even if their daughter seems insignificant, you can't humiliate her like this. The Qin family is different from us; their direct relatives are tightly united and fiercely protective! You better discipline your son properly. If he causes any more scandals, the Su family won't be able to handle the fallout. We'll send a formal apology on behalf of the family. You stay out of it.\"","As long as the cooperation wasn't severed, the Su Family Patriarch didn't care who took over. It was never about Su Ze's branch specifically, so he had no intention of letting them cause further trouble.","But to Su Ze's father, these arrangements felt like the stripping of a crown prince's title.","Devastated, he left the office and immediately called Su Ze, unleashing a torrent of curses.","Su Ze, who had been comforting Yu Xin, turned pale upon hearing his father's voice. It seemed he had grown so accustomed to ignoring Qin Jiaxi that he had forgotten the breakup might escalate to the elders.","After all, during their relationship, they never discussed family matters, and over time, Su Ze had forgotten just how much he had benefited from being Qin Jiaxi's boyfriend.","\"Are you out of your mind? How could you do something like this? If you wanted to keep a mistress, you should have at least kept Qin Jiaxi happy! Who do you think you are? How dare you manipulate and use her like that? I never knew you could be so stupid! Now, forget about being the successor—it's over! You've even dragged me down with you. If our family falls, it's all your fault! Get your ass back home now!\"","Su Ze tried to defend himself, but his father hung up before he could finish.","Furious, Su Ze threw his phone. \"She actually complained! After everything, she still went this far. I was already beaten, and now she...\"","Yu Xin, who had just received a message from Qin Han, was also trembling with anger. Qin Jiaxi had never complained before, but now she had the nerve to do so.","At least Qin Han was still on her side.","Yu Xin grabbed Su Ze's sleeve and tearfully said, \"How could Jiaxi do this? Just because she likes you and can't have you, she wants to ruin you?\"","Su Ze gritted his teeth and snapped, \"I underestimated her. She's trying to control me with this! I was planning to win her back and use her a little longer, but now I won't bother. Let's see if she really has the guts to let me go. She was so infatuated with me, so dependent on me. If she doesn't come begging for my forgiveness and doesn't get her father to smooth things over with our family, I'll never forgive her!\"","Yu Xin's expression shifted slightly. Although she knew Su Ze wouldn't acknowledge her so quickly and that she shouldn't openly be with him yet—especially since she was still deceiving Qin Han—she couldn't help but feel deeply uncomfortable.","Meanwhile, after dealing with the Su family, Third Uncle Qin received videos from Qin Xian that identified those who had bullied his daughter. He intended to handle each of them.","Seeing his daughter standing drenched in the fountain pool, his blood pressure spiked again.","Third Uncle Qin was grateful for everything everyone had done for Jiaxi. Since he didn't have much to do in the afternoon, he decided to personally pick up Jiaxi, apologize to her, and then treat everyone to a meal."]},{"number":366,"title":"Chapter 366: Hehe, is this how you play","paragraphs":["Qin Jiaxi had regained her spirits and led everyone to savor the youthful flavors of the campus snack street.","In truth, Qin Jiaxi's eyes were swollen, like walnuts, likely from crying her heart out in the shower. Now, her smile was pure and clear, indicating that she had partly let go of her burdens. She couldn't say she was completely carefree, but having found some courage, she no longer felt so downcast.","After finishing their desserts, Qin Yi asked, \"Where are we going this afternoon? Still exploring the campus?\"","Qin Rong replied, \"We'll follow Jiaxi's lead.\"","Qin Jiaxi hesitated, remembering that she had something scheduled for the afternoon.","Qin Han was coming to their college to give a speech. As an outstanding alumnus and a representative of Qin Corporation, he was there to encourage the students. The lecture was bound to be packed, and while attendance wasn't mandatory, Qin Jiaxi, being a student in the direct department, had been instructed by her advisor to attend.","However, she didn't want to face Qin Han at all. Judging by the barrage of missed calls and messages, it was clear that he had already heard Yu Xin's complaints.","She didn't want to be scolded. While she could stand up to Su Ze, facing Qin Han was a different matter. After all, he was her older brother, someone she had grown up with, and his authority carried more weight. She wasn't ready to confront the reality that her own brother might not love her as much as he seemed to favor Yu Xin as his sister.","For now, she chose to avoid the situation.","As she contemplated quietly taking leave and pretending nothing was wrong, she overheard two female classmates engaged in an animated discussion.","\"It's confirmed! Qin Han, the eldest son of the Qin family, is coming to give a speech this afternoon!\"","\"He's so handsome and capable. He was a campus heartthrob back in the day. It's a shame he graduated before I enrolled, or I would have definitely pursued him!\"","\"I heard he's still single!\"","\"He's a total doting brother, you know.\"","\"Oh, you mean Yu Xin, right? I often see Qin Han picking her up. I'm so jealous! I wish I could be his sister too!\"","\"Miss Yu Xin is also very down-to-earth and easy to get along with.\"","\"Today, we might even get to see the siblings together!\"","Listening to this gossip, Ji Fei and the others at the table felt like they were about to vomit.","Qin Han was such a hypocrite, keeping Qin Jiaxi's identity under wraps while flaunting his relationship with his fake sister. And yet, such a scoundrel still managed to attract so many admirers. It was clear that people didn't know his true colors.","\"Why hasn't the news spread yet?\" Qin Zhao wondered aloud.","Qin Yi asked, \"Are you talking about what happened earlier?\"","Qin Zhao nodded.","\"I'm also curious. Aren't your university classmates into gossip? This is such a big deal,\" Ji Fei said, glancing at Qin Jiaxi with a hint of frustration.","Qin Jiaxi, who had been feeling uneasy, was now at a loss for words. She didn't know either. Would something like this spread quickly?","Ji Fei's eyes lit up. This was perfect. Earlier, she had been worried that Qin Jiaxi might not want to take them along.","\"I can't stand seeing bad people show off. How about this? Let's go and see. If Qin Han dares to appear with Yu Xin and let others continue misunderstanding, then we'll...\" Ji Fei made a slashing motion with her hand.","Qin Zhao chimed in, \"Clean house!\"","Even Qin Yi and Qin Rong were infected by the excitement and chuckled along.","Qin Jiaxi widened her eyes in confusion. She had always been taught by her mother to keep family matters private and resolve issues at home, without even troubling her father, as her problems were considered minor.","Why was everyone around her so... excited?","This was a public event. Surely, they couldn't cause a scene and embarrass Qin Corporation, could they?","Qin Jiaxi, being soft-spoken, instinctively went along with the group's decision.","Soon, they relocated to the grand auditorium.","As expected, the place was packed, with people already lining up.","Ji Fei was annoyed. Why did they have to queue just to see Qin Han? It felt like they were giving him too much credit.","She complained to her husband.","Qin Xian replied, \"You might enjoy watching the show from the audience seats.\"","Ji Fei perked up. \"They're here?\"","Qin Xian confirmed, \"Everyone's here.\"","Ji Fei grinned. \"Well, humans are naturally drawn to drama. I'll make sure to grab a good seat.\"","Indeed, Ji Fei had sent Qin Xian a message as soon as she found out Qin Han was coming to show off. She didn't want to give him the chance and thought it would be a good opportunity for Qin Jiaxi to assert her identity. So, she had arranged for others to take Qin Han's place.","Qin Xian, being the supportive husband, had ensured her plan would succeed.","Coincidentally, the events of the morning had exposed everything. Qin Jiaxi's uncle was coming to pick her up, and now everything was converging.","Ji Fei couldn't be more thrilled.","Sitting in the back row, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, having caught wind of what might happen, were equally excited.","Qin Yi, not quite on the same wavelength, was curious about whether the family was planning something big.","Lately, hanging out with this group had made Qin Yi feel less composed, always eager for drama and mischief.","Only Qin Jiaxi was lost in her thoughts, her mind wandering.","Qin Han certainly kept everyone waiting.","An hour later, the host finally took the stage to introduce the event, urging everyone to give a warm round of applause to welcome Qin Han.","As Qin Han walked in with confident strides, appearing completely at ease, it was clear he had no idea that everyone else had arrived.","Ji Fei took a quick look and was instantly disgusted.","[Ugh, Su Ze isn't here. Seems like his family called him home. So Yu Xin dares to cozy up to Qin Han now? What a time management master! She arrived early backstage, crying to Qin Han, who immediately comforted her, even... sharing a kiss. Disgusting.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong felt like they were about to vomit but held it in. Did these two men know they were sharing the same woman?","[Qin Han even promised to let Yu Xin present flowers later and help solidify her position... Oh, so that's how they're playing it? The girl who hit her earlier wasn't strong enough. Why didn't she leave a mark? Now we have to endure this eyesore.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong expressed their disappointment.","[Wait, the girl... she's doing what? Oh?! This is getting juicy!] Ji Fei's thoughts jumped around.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong struggled to keep up, unable to hear the details, and watched as Ji Fei suddenly asked Qin Jiaxi for the university forum's website.","It was the same forum where Qin Yi's gossip had previously surfaced, widely used by students in Y City.","The two men, no longer interested in Qin Han's speech, quietly searched and refreshed the page, waiting for updates.","Suddenly, a post with familiar names appeared.","#Su Ze Cheats, Qin Han Lies!#"]},{"number":367,"title":"Chapter 367: Who Are You, This Female Classmate","paragraphs":["The title was simple and straightforward, but due to the high popularity of the two individuals involved, it instantly became a trending post.","There was no explanation inside, just a video.","At first, there was some concern, but after watching the silent video, it was clear that their faces were hardly shown, and there were no scenes of violence. This brought temporary relief, as while they were bold enough to take responsibility, they didn’t want to be scrutinized online.","Upon watching the video again, it was amusing—Qin Han had failed before even achieving anything!","Although most people in the auditorium were attentively listening to Qin Han’s speech, not many were distracted by their phones. However, once such explosive news was revealed, it would spread quickly, especially since everyone knew Qin Han was currently giving a speech there.","Sure enough, it didn’t take long before students in the auditorium started glancing at their phones. Occasionally, there were even noises as people watched the video.","Qin Han, who was speaking on stage, seemed to notice some people below openly playing with their phones. He was visibly annoyed and considered ending his speech early to express his displeasure and teach them a lesson.","However, the host suddenly signaled him to wrap up his speech quickly.","Qin Han was immediately puzzled—how had the other party beaten him to it?","Since he was already frustrated, he decided to just go with it and hastily concluded his speech. When the applause came, it was scattered and lukewarm, completely different from the enthusiastic response he had received before. This only fueled his anger.","Qin Jiaxi also noticed that everyone around her was looking at their phones, and she could feel the occasional glances directed her way. No one seemed to notice that the speech had ended. She had always been sensitive to such stares, and this made her extremely uncomfortable. She nervously glanced at her family members beside her, only to find that they, too, were engrossed in their phones. When she took a closer look, her eyes widened in shock, and she quickly pulled out her own phone to check. What she saw left her stunned.","Meanwhile, Yu Xin, who was waiting anxiously at the side of the stage with a bouquet of flowers, hadn’t realized that something was amiss. Right on cue, she rushed up to the stage to present the flowers to Qin Han.","Seeing Yu Xin approach, Qin Han’s anger subsided slightly.","He accepted the bouquet and then signaled the host with his eyes to start the Q&A session.","Before coming on stage, they had already arranged with the host to casually bring up their relationship.","However, the host was distracted. He had just received a prompt through his earpiece that a heavyweight guest was about to make an appearance, so he needed to quickly wrap up Qin Han’s segment and move on to the next part. He was brainstorming how to transition smoothly.","If it weren’t for Qin Han’s obvious glare, the host might have remained distracted.","The host turned his head, noticing Qin Han’s displeased expression and Yu Xin’s awkward demeanor, and finally remembered the small task at hand. He quickly improvised.","“Hmm, the two of you seem quite close. Could she be your girlfriend?”","Qin Han then smiled, wrapped his arm around Yu Xin’s shoulders, and declared boldly in front of the entire audience, “Don’t misunderstand, everyone. Yu Xin is my sister! She’s my one and only precious little sister. I hope you’ll all take good care of her at school.”","Yu Xin instantly breathed a sigh of relief and stood tall. She knew that, despite the earlier conflict, as long as Qin Han publicly acknowledged her, Qin Jiaxi’s efforts would be in vain. After all, Qin Han was her biological brother.","However, the applause and gasps they expected didn’t come. Instead, the crowd began murmuring and whispering, completely contrary to what they had anticipated.","“What a shameless guy. He’s full of nonsense,” Ji Fei couldn’t help but curse under his breath.","Qin Jiaxi, standing nearby, had a calm expression, but her eyes were cold. Although she had anticipated this, hearing her own brother acknowledge only Yu Xin still left her heart aching.","“His one and only precious sister? How could he say that?” she thought.","“Am I really that detestable to him?”","“You two were never meant to be siblings. It’s his loss,” Qin Yi said.","Qin Zhao chimed in with a smile, “We don’t consider him family either.”","Qin Rong nodded in agreement. “That’s right. You’re the only sister we recognize.”","Ji Fei chuckled and said, “Don’t be disheartened. Let’s keep watching.”","Meanwhile, the two on stage were starting to feel that something was off.","At that moment, the host announced, “By the way, we have a special surprise for everyone today. An even more distinguished guest has come to share their wisdom with us. Please welcome the current President of Qin International’s Y City branch, President Qin!”","The entire auditorium erupted in shock.","“Isn’t President Qin Qin Han’s father? The wealthiest man in Y City?”","“Why are both father and son appearing together today?”","“Look at Qin Han and Yu Xin’s surprised expressions. It doesn’t seem like they knew about this beforehand.”","“Hey, have you seen the post on the forum? I think President Qin’s appearance might be related to that!”","“Why do I feel like something juicy is about to happen?”","“A real versus fake heiress?!!!! Is this drama really unfolding right before my eyes?”","“Honestly, just based on the surname, I’d believe Qin Jiaxi!”","“And when I look at Qin Han and Yu Xin, they don’t seem like they’re just siblings.”","“Nonsense! Yu Xin is clearly involved with Su Ze!”","“Oh? Watson, you’ve spotted something!”","Ji Fei raised an eyebrow in surprise. The original plan was for Qin Xian to take the stage, but it turned out to be Third Uncle Qin instead!","Well, it was better this way. Let him personally teach his foolish son a lesson.","Qin Jiaxi, standing nearby, was utterly stunned, even beginning to doubt whether she had heard correctly.","It wasn’t until the familiar, towering figure walked onto the stage that she snapped out of it.","The other members of the Qin family were already buzzing with excitement. This turn of events was simply too thrilling.","Their elders were finally seeing for themselves what kind of person their son was outside.","Qin Han’s earlier statement, to put it bluntly, was an attempt to confuse the Qin family’s bloodline and swap the real and fake heiresses.","If Qin Han had succeeded, Yu Xin could have used the Qin family’s name to do who knows what, tarnishing the family’s reputation in the process.","As members of the Qin family, they naturally bore the responsibility of upholding the family’s honor. Qin Han, in his foolishness, thought he could grant anyone the status of a Qin family member. It was utterly ridiculous.","Meanwhile, Qin Han, seeing his father walking towards him with a calm expression, began to tremble.","He wasn’t stupid. He knew his father had heard everything he had just said. He had already been scolded over the phone about this matter, and now he had gone and said it again in front of his father. This was bound to provoke his father’s anger.","But the fact that his father showed no outward signs of anger only made him more anxious.","He had no idea what kind of storm was brewing beneath that calm exterior.","He could only hope that his father would prioritize the family’s image and not embarrass them in public. Even if his father didn’t support him, he wouldn’t openly contradict him, as that would only help Yu Xin. At worst, he’d get a scolding once they returned home.","Yu Xin, on the other hand, was already panicking. Such a blatant lie being exposed in front of Third Uncle Qin could reveal her scheme of pretending to be his daughter. This would only make it harder for her to enter the Qin family. She forced a smile, trying to keep things under control.","But the moment Third Uncle Qin took the microphone, the situation began to spiral out of control.","Third Uncle Qin’s hand holding the microphone trembled slightly with anger, though he maintained a composed exterior.","He directly addressed Yu Xin, “Young lady, who are you?”","His words struck like lightning, shocking the entire auditorium.","Gasps and murmurs filled the room.","Qin Han’s face twisted in panic. “Dad, what are you saying?” he exclaimed, desperately trying to signal his father to maintain decorum.","But Third Uncle Qin continued, “Why does my son say you’re his sister? I don’t know you. Since when did our Qin family have a daughter like you?”","All eyes were now fixed on Yu Xin, making her feel as though she were being roasted over a fire.","Tears welled up in her eyes—this time, they were genuine."]},{"number":368,"title":"Chapter 368: You rebellious child","paragraphs":["The host was also stunned. He truly hadn't expected so many twists and turns during a single speech.","Wasn’t Yu Xin Qin Han’s sister? Then why had Qin Han asked him to do this earlier?","The poor host, having been busy with preparations, hadn’t had time to catch up on the latest gossip.","In the heat of the moment, he instinctively blurted out, “Mr. Qin, isn’t Yu Xin your daughter?”","Third Uncle Qin let out a scoff. “What? Do you think I wouldn’t recognize my own daughter? Qin Han, tell me, who is she? Why did you claim she’s your one and only precious sister? Have you forgotten what your own sister looks like? If you’re mentally unwell, perhaps you should see a psychiatrist.”","[Pfft, hahaha, who knew Third Uncle Qin could be so savage?]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong couldn’t help but burst into laughter.","Qin Yi chimed in with a smirk, “He’s right. Only someone with a mental disorder would pull something like this.”","Meanwhile, Qin Jiaxi stared blankly at her father on stage, feeling for the first time as though a protective umbrella had been held over her head in the midst of a storm.","Qin Han, on the other hand, was utterly dumbfounded. He even started to feel a pang of grievance, unable to believe what was happening. “Dad?”","He had expected his father to be angry, but he never imagined he would humiliate him so publicly, slapping him in the face—metaphorically speaking—so hard that his cheeks burned as if he’d been struck repeatedly.","Qin Han had always been proud and arrogant, a top graduate of the school and a legend among his juniors.","Now, his father had just told his admirers that he needed to see a psychiatrist. What kind of message did that send? He couldn’t even begin to imagine how the internet would react.","How could his father be so ruthless? How could he do this to him?","“Dad, stop joking around with me. Don’t be mad at your son,” Qin Han said, desperately trying to salvage his shattered pride.","“As my son and an employee of Qin Corporation, I hope you’ll be more careful with your words in the future. No more nonsense,” Third Uncle Qin stated bluntly.","Qin Han was on the verge of losing his mind. If these words got out, how could he ever manage the company or move in elite circles again?","Yu Xin, meanwhile, was already tearing up, as if she were the one who had suffered a great injustice.","She and Qin Han now felt like clowns on display, wishing they could vanish into thin air.","But Third Uncle Qin wasn’t done. After reprimanding his son, he turned to Yu Xin. “I don’t care what your relationship with my son is, but falsely claiming family ties is unacceptable. I hope you’ll correct your behavior.”","With those words, Yu Xin was cast into hell. Accused of having poor character, how could she ever maintain her “school goddess” image? Everyone would despise her now.","Yu Xin felt like she was about to faint.","Just moments ago, the two of them had been smug, thinking they had resolved their troubles. Now, they felt utterly exposed, humiliated and ridiculed before everyone.","The murmurs in the auditorium grew louder.","Finally, someone gathered the courage to shout, “Mr. Qin, who is your daughter, then?”","Third Uncle Qin smiled and seized the opportunity. “Indeed, I have a precious daughter who’s currently studying at this university. She’s probably here today.”","The auditorium erupted in excitement.","Those who had seen the posts already knew, and those who hadn’t were quickly filled in.","Then, Third Uncle Qin called out, “Jiaxi, are you here? Come up to the stage and join me for the speech.”","Before Qin Jiaxi could react, her relatives eagerly responded on her behalf.","“She’s here! Over here!”","What followed felt like a dream to Qin Jiaxi. Every step felt unreal, as though she were floating.","Qin Han and Yu Xin were escorted off the stage by staff.","Third Uncle Qin softened his demeanor, showering his daughter with warmth as he brought her on stage.","He seamlessly integrated questions about Qin Jiaxi’s studies with the interview, cooperating fully.","When the speech ended, Third Uncle Qin took Qin Jiaxi’s hand and placed it on his arm.","Father and daughter stood together, receiving applause from the audience. They then posed for photos with the school leaders, with Third Uncle Qin proudly introducing, “This is my daughter, Qin Jiaxi. Please take good care of her in the future.”","The leaders enthusiastically greeted her, practically engraving Qin Jiaxi’s name and face into their memories.","As the students left the auditorium, the buzz of gossip was loud enough to echo across the campus.","The previously skeptical posts were instantly flooded with replies, leaving no room for doubt. The evidence was now undeniable.","Finally, everyone believed the almost absurd video.","Qin Han had disowned his real sister, embraced a fake one, and allowed the imposter to bully his biological sister at school.","Su Ze was equally laughable. To secretly date the fake heiress, he had deceived the real one, manipulated her into being a scapegoat, and subjected her to constant emotional abuse and neglect, letting the bullying he caused fall on her shoulders.","Of course, no one forgot Yu Xin, who seemed to do nothing but benefit from everyone else’s actions behind the scenes.","Yu Xin’s reputation as a scheming, manipulative “white lotus” was now set in stone. How could she have charmed both the real brother and the boyfriend into orbiting around her, shamelessly refusing to deny her false identity? Did she really think everyone was blind to her antics?","In the end, the one who suffered the most was Qin Jiaxi—a true victim of circumstance.","People sympathized with the young heiress, even starting to feel protective of her. After all, for a young lady to end up in such a state, it was clear how easily she could be taken advantage of. Everyone felt she deserved to be shielded and cared for.","Unbeknownst to her, Qin Jiaxi had quietly gained a group of protectors.","But for now, Qin Jiaxi was still in a daze.","It wasn’t until she heard her brother’s furious accusations backstage that reality snapped back into place.","“Was it you? Did you make Dad come here? You’re so calculating! You bullied Yu Xin this morning, and now you’re trying to ruin both of us. How can you be so vicious? You—”","As Qin Han lunged toward her, Qin Jiaxi froze, instinctively covering her head instead of dodging.","This reflexive reaction ignited Third Uncle Qin’s fury.","He kicked out, sending Qin Han flying.","“You ungrateful brat!”"]},{"number":369,"title":"Chapter 369: Appropriating Others' Labor Achievements is the Most Disgusting","paragraphs":["Qin Han's fall sent the backstage clutter tumbling, accompanied by his cries of pain. Yu Xin, standing nearby, was utterly stunned. Ji Fei and the others had also arrived backstage with Qin Xian. Strangely, no one stepped forward to intervene or mediate; they all seemed content to watch the drama unfold.","Fourth Uncle Qin clicked his tongue and remarked, \"Third Uncle Qin may be fierce, but he rarely resorts to physical violence. Qin Han has really gone too far this time.\"","\"Not just this time,\" the twins chimed in, complaining to their father.","Qin Xian, with Ji Fei by his side, quietly filled her in on Third Uncle Qin's subsequent plans, satisfying her appetite for gossip. Ji Fei listened with great satisfaction. This was exactly how it should be—let Su Ze, who had always been so self-important, get a taste of his own medicine.","[Heh, now Su Ze is also getting a beating. It seems he and Qin Han are truly brothers in both fortune and misfortune.]","After finishing his tirade against Qin Han, Third Uncle Qin was left panting with anger. He stepped forward and coldly addressed his son, \"Is this how you behave as an older brother? What has gotten into you? Today, we’re going to settle this once and for all. What exactly are you trying to achieve?\"","Originally, he had planned to deal with the matter gradually at home, but after witnessing his foolish son’s antics today, he could no longer tolerate it.","Qin Han, who had never been beaten by his father before, was left dazed. Yu Xin quickly stepped forward to help him up and then turned to Third Uncle Qin. \"Uncle, this is all a misunderstanding. Qin Han only sees me as a younger sister. We didn’t bully Jiaxi. I don’t know what she told you, but I’ve always admired you deeply. As an orphan with no parents, I’ve long considered you and Auntie as my own...\"","\"Yu Xin, this is a family matter and has nothing to do with you. Keep your intentions to yourself. Let me make this clear today: the Qin family will never adopt a girl with ulterior motives like you. I already have a daughter; I don’t need another one,\" Third Uncle Qin interrupted coldly.","Yu Xin’s face instantly turned pale.","\"Dad, how can you say that? Qin Jiaxi is selfish and spiteful. Just because Mom and I were kind to Yu Xin, she lashed out at her. With such a character, you’re still indulging her instead of addressing her behavior,\" Qin Han retorted, jumping to Yu Xin’s defense the moment his father dismissed her.","[What’s wrong with Qin Han? It’s like a reflex—he stays silent when criticized but leaps to Yu Xin’s defense the moment she’s mentioned. Oh, I get it now. He’s been conditioned by that mysterious Third Aunt since childhood to protect Yu Xin at all costs. No wonder he’s acting so ridiculously. In Qin Han’s memory, Yu Xin is thoughtful and considerate, while his own sister is dull and uninteresting. But did he ever give Jiaxi a chance to be interesting?]","Third Uncle Qin couldn’t help but laugh bitterly. \"You say Jiaxi is selfish and spiteful in front of you, but have you ever asked yourselves why? Have you ever treated her with genuine kindness? Have you ever shown her a warm expression? Reflect on your own actions! You treat Yu Xin better than your own sister, and you expect Jiaxi not to feel upset?\"","\"Moreover, your judgment is completely skewed. How much of what you say is even true? I never thought you’d become so blind to reason. Is your brain filled with mush? Let me make this clear: not only am I rejecting your idea of adoption, but from now on, no one in our family is allowed to associate with this girl.\"","Yu Xin nearly stumbled, and Qin Han’s eyes widened in shock.","\"Between Jiaxi and Yu Xin, you can only choose one. Let’s see if you’ve truly lost your mind to the point of abandoning your own family!\" Third Uncle Qin snorted coldly.","\"Dad, how can you be so heartless? Don’t you remember when you, Mom, and I were unwell? It was Yu Xin who went to great lengths to prepare medicinal dishes to help us recover. She cared for us every day, while Qin Jiaxi was like a mute, completely indifferent to the family. She’s been more filial to us than Jiaxi. Are you favoring Jiaxi just because of blood ties? You must be losing your mind.\"","Third Uncle Qin was so furious he nearly had a heart attack. He did remember the medicinal dishes. It was because of that incident that he allowed Yu Xin to frequent their home, thinking it would make his wife and son happy. But in doing so, he had gradually neglected Jiaxi’s feelings.","He had been truly foolish, failing to see Yu Xin’s true intentions. She had been trying to subtly replace his precious daughter all along. As the saying goes, excessive kindness often hides ulterior motives.","Looking back, giving Yu Xin a gift in return had been a wise decision. Otherwise, she might have used it as leverage now.","[Medicinal dishes, health remedies...]","Ji Fei, hearing this, noticed Qin Jiaxi’s hesitant expression and immediately sensed something was amiss.","[Let me investigate.]","The Qin Second family perked up, wondering if there was another twist. But if there was, why hadn’t Jiaxi spoken up? With Third Uncle Qin now on her side, was she still so insecure?","Just as everyone was growing curious, Ji Fei uncovered the truth.","[I want to curse. Who knows how many times this shameless Yu Xin has pulled such stunts? The medicinal recipes were actually collected by Jiaxi after consulting numerous traditional Chinese doctors. She compiled the information into a document, which Yu Xin secretly copied and presented as her own. Jiaxi thought they had both gathered the information and that she had simply been a step behind. Seeing the family praise Yu Xin, Jiaxi felt too embarrassed to present her own work, fearing it would seem like she was seeking credit. That’s why she didn’t speak up—she genuinely didn’t know Yu Xin had stolen her efforts.]","The Qin Second family was outraged. How could someone be so despicable?","Stealing someone else’s hard work is utterly vile.","But how could they refute this now?","Qin Xian’s eyes flickered, and he suddenly interrupted the tense atmosphere. \"Medicinal dishes? Were they for Third Uncle Qin’s stomach issues?\"","Third Uncle Qin, still seething, was momentarily taken aback. He hadn’t expected Qin Xian, who didn’t live with them, to know about his stomach problems. This once again impressed him.","The others also looked at Qin Xian in surprise.","Third Uncle Qin nodded. \"Indeed, the medicinal dishes were very effective. Not only did they help my stomach, but they also alleviated my wife’s cold constitution and Qin Han’s headaches. That’s why I rewarded the girl with housing.\"","\"Dad, you’re joking, right? Can sincerity be bought with money?\" Qin Han retorted.","Qin Xian suddenly turned to Yu Xin. \"You put a lot of effort into finding these medicinal recipes?\"","Yu Xin, tears in her eyes, nodded timidly. She glanced shyly at Qin Xian, surprised to find that the family head Qin Han had spoken of was such a young and handsome man. She couldn’t help but blush nervously.","Unfortunately, this man was already married, and to a wife who didn’t care about her appearance. Remembering the humiliation she had endured earlier that morning, Yu Xin immediately adopted a more pitiful demeanor, instinctively trying to attract his attention and sympathy.","\"Since I need them too, why don’t you recite the recipes for me now?\" Qin Xian said directly.","Yu Xin was stunned, momentarily speechless."]},{"number":370,"title":"Chapter 370: How Innocent She Is, Innocent to Death","paragraphs":["Qin Xian spoke indifferently, \"What? Can't recite it? Even one sheet will do, or just a part of it. Wasn't it something you painstakingly collected?\"","Yu Xin's face began to show panic.","\"Or perhaps you could tell us which book or which old Chinese medicine practitioner you got it from?\" Qin Xian continued mercilessly.","By this point, Ji Fei and Qin Second's family had completely understood Qin Xian's intention.","Ji Fei leaned into Qin Xian's arms, her heart filled with excitement and joy.","[Wow, my husband is amazing! I love him so much. He's so clever! He’s going to expose this fraud so thoroughly.]","Qin Xian's lips curled into a smile as he casually pulled his wife closer, not caring about appearances.","With his wife in his arms, it was as if he had absorbed some comforting energy, and his tone became slightly lazy.","\"What? Can't say anything? It seems you didn't put much effort into it after all,\" Qin Xian said lightly.","\"No, I... I...\" Yu Xin tried to gather her thoughts and defend herself.","\"Can't even name a single herb? Three recipes, and you don't remember a single one? How... heartfelt,\" Ji Fei added sarcastically.","Qin Han tugged at Yu Xin, confused as to why she wasn't speaking up.","[Hahaha, Qin Han actually seems clueless. I thought they were in cahoots. It seems that in the beginning, Qin Han wasn't so blinded and irrational. Did he lose his mind later when his sister became his lover? I wonder if he’ll still be so self-righteous once he finds out the truth!]","Meanwhile, Third Uncle Qin thought that perhaps Yu Xin had just randomly picked up the recipes and hadn’t bothered to memorize them, despite her earlier grand claims. Now that it was clear the girl had ulterior motives, nothing else mattered.","Just as the topic seemed to be winding down, his daughter, Qin Jiaxi, began softly reciting the names of the herbs.","Third Uncle Qin was startled and turned to look at Qin Jiaxi.","Qin Jiaxi looked dazed, as if she were reciting something she knew by heart, flawlessly listing the ingredients of the three medicinal recipes.","The room fell silent.","Qin Jiaxi stared blankly at her father.","Third Uncle Qin, being sharp, instantly guessed what might have happened. His voice trembled as he asked, \"Jiaxi, how do you know these? Tell me, I’m listening.\"","Qin Jiaxi seemed to realize the implications of what she had just done, which was why she had absentmindedly recited the recipes.","\"I... I also collected medicinal recipes during that time. These three were among them. I had prepared them to give to you, but... the next day, Yu Xin presented the same recipes. So, I didn’t bring them up. I...\" Qin Jiaxi's voice shook.","\"No way! You can recite them, but she can’t even stammer out a single word and looks so guilty. Doesn’t that prove she stole your recipes and took credit for your work?\" Qin Xiaoyu exclaimed in shock.","Qin Jing couldn’t help but say to Qin Han, \"Qin Han, it turns out your headaches were cured by your sister.\"","Qin Han was stunned for a moment before quickly reacting, \"No way! Yu Xin would never steal from her. She must have secretly memorized them out of spite and is now using them to frame Yu Xin.\"","Qin Yi shook his head at this and muttered, \"Hopeless.\"","Qin Han, of course, noticed their mockery and flushed red. He turned to Yu Xin and said, \"Yu Xin, don’t worry. I’ll stand by you. Prove them wrong!\"","But how could Yu Xin prove anything? She knew that if she tried, others would speak up for her, and Qin Jiaxi wouldn’t question her. She had never put in any real effort, leaving everything to the butler to handle.","\"Proving it is simple. We just need to trace the origins of the recipes. We have plenty of time today, and we don’t mind unraveling all your past misunderstandings,\" Qin Zhao said mockingly.","Qin Rong chimed in, \"Yes, we’ll be witnesses to make sure no one slanders Jiaxi again.\"","Third Uncle Qin didn’t need any more proof. He was already furious, glaring at Qin Han and Yu Xin. \"Fine, very well! Will you admit it yourself, or shall I investigate? If I find out you’ve lied and taken credit for my daughter’s work...\"","He didn’t finish his sentence, but the threat was clear.","Yu Xin was completely at a loss and even considered fainting to escape the situation.","But before she could act, Ji Fei suddenly spoke up, \"Don’t even think about fainting now. Even if you do, we’ll call our private doctor. Today, we’ll get to the bottom of this, even if we have to hook you up to an oxygen tank!\"","Yu Xin froze, feeling utterly desperate. Finally, she stammered, \"I... I was wrong. I’m sorry. I... I saw the recipes on Jiaxi’s computer. I thought she didn’t want to share them because she seemed distant from the family, so I took it upon myself... I wanted to help her improve her relationship with everyone. But then Auntie and Qin Han misunderstood, thinking it was my work. I just... I just wanted to be closer to everyone. I wanted them to like me. When Jiaxi didn’t say anything, I thought she didn’t care or didn’t want to share them. So I... It’s all my fault. I was greedy. Waaah!\"","Ji Fei couldn’t help but admire Yu Xin’s audacity. Even in such a dire situation, she could come up with such a flimsy excuse and even try to shift the blame.","And, unbelievably, someone actually believed her!","Ji Fei was stunned, watching Qin Han’s expression of helplessness and pity. She almost laughed out loud.","\"So it’s all Jiaxi’s fault, huh? It’s her fault for not sharing the recipes immediately, giving you the chance to steal them. It’s her fault for not suspecting your deceitful actions and exposing you. It’s her fault for not fighting back when you stole the family’s affection. Oh my, how innocent you are! It’s all Jiaxi’s fault for not being more accommodating.\"","As soon as Ji Fei finished speaking, the rest of the Qin family burst into laughter.","\"Exactly, she’s so innocent. Poor thing.\"","\"Does she really think anyone would believe such a ridiculous excuse? Only an idiot would fall for that.\"","\"Maybe there is an idiot, considering how convincingly she’s acting.\"","\"She’s really something. In her version, Jiaxi, the victim, is the one at fault.\"","The family’s mockery left Qin Han and Yu Xin both humiliated and frustrated. Their usual tactics seemed utterly ineffective against this family.","Third Uncle Qin had no patience left for their act. He pulled Qin Jiaxi close and said, \"I’m sorry, Jiaxi. This is all my fault. I failed to see the truth.\"","\"No, it’s not your fault. It’s mine. I was too naive, too easily taken advantage of,\" Qin Jiaxi said, tears finally spilling over. She had only ever wanted to do something good for her family, never seeking recognition. She never imagined someone would exploit her kindness. She felt so foolish.","Third Uncle Qin wiped away his daughter’s tears and glared coldly at Yu Xin. \"The house we gave you—be out by 6 PM today. I’ll have the lawyer handle the transfer. If you’re not gone by then, I’ll sue you for fraud.\""]},{"number":371,"title":"Chapter 371: It's Not That I'm Not Good, It's That You're Not Good","paragraphs":["Third Uncle Qin's methods were relatively lenient, as he still remembered the life-saving favor Yu Xin had done for his wife and the child in her womb. So, he only publicly reclaimed the house and privately restricted his family members from interacting with her further. Additionally, he banned her from working within the Qin Corporation. So far, this was fairly merciful.","At one point, Third Uncle Qin wondered if the car accident rescue was also something Yu Xin had falsely claimed, taking credit from his Jiaxi. But he knew Jiaxi couldn't have been at the scene at the time, so it must have been genuine. The video footage was also very clear. Third Uncle Qin had never imagined his wife would take such risks to help an outsider, so his doubts and speculations only went so far.","At this moment, Yu Xin was stunned by Third Uncle Qin's words. It was her bachelor apartment, located near the school, and it was expensive. There was no way she could bear to give it up. She hadn't expected him to be so ruthless, taking away her biggest asset in one fell swoop.","This was truly too much to bear, and she swayed unsteadily, looking as if she might faint. Qin Han immediately grasped Yu Xin's arm, furious, \"Dad, how can you do this... Yu Xin already said she didn't mean it.","She just wanted a family, what's wrong with that! Besides, it's so embarrassing to take back something once it's given away.\"","\"You want to be a fool, but I don't! What right does she have to keep something she deceived? Qin Han, do you even have a conscience? Your headaches improved because of who? Don't you owe your sister an apology, a thank you? You just said she doesn't care about you!\" Third Uncle Qin coldly retorted.","Qin Han, however, felt no guilt and instead glared viciously at Qin Jiaxi. \"Overreacting, aren't you? So eager to show off your achievements, are you? Are you satisfied now?\"","“You!”","If this happened a few more times, Third Uncle Qin might really end up seriously ill from anger.","Suddenly, Qin Jiaxi spoke up, \"Not satisfied.\"","Qin Han was stunned, and those around were also astonished. After all, this was the first time Qin Jiaxi had directly confronted her brother in front of everyone with harsh words.","I hope you won't eat the medicinal meal made from the prescription I gave you anymore. I don't want to feed you. I regret helping you find the prescription. No matter how well I treat you, you never see it. Before, I didn't understand, thinking it was my fault. Now I finally get it.","Qin Jiaxi looked around and then suddenly understood, \"It's not me who's wrong; it's you. You ungrateful wretch, you have a heart of a wolf. You... don't deserve my brotherly affection. You only have her as your sister, so I’m not your sister anymore. I have other brothers and sisters who care about me, so I don’t need you.\"","It seemed that the so-called \"brother\" had truly broken her heart, and Qin Jiaxi suddenly realized/understood.","Just moments ago, she had held a shred of hope, always fantasizing that maybe her brother was misled by expectations, misunderstanding her and siding with Yu Xin against her. But now that it had been proven so clearly, her brother still stood against her, criticizing her. She had been such a fool, so desperate for his approval that she had been degrading herself, indulging in such brotherly affection. Her sincerity had been wasted.","Now, it didn't matter anymore; at least her dad was genuinely on her side, willing to listen to her grievances.","She was truly exhausted, no longer wanting this brother.","As for her mother, that was another matter.","Qin Han was dumbfounded. How dared his timid sister, Qin Jiaxi, speak to him like that?","She actually said she didn't want him, and even insulted him?","This wasn’t supposed to be his role – Qin Jiaxi was expected to act like a devoted little sister, always trying to grab his attention. She must be out of her mind! How could she give up on him, her brother!","Qin Han seemed incapable of accepting the situation, feeling an indescribable ache in his chest.","As for his daughter's outburst, Third Uncle Qin had no reservations.","He wouldn't preach about keeping the family harmonious, hoping for a chance for the siblings to reconcile later. He wouldn't ask the wronged Qin Jiaxi to be forgiving.","He only knew that his daughter had suffered enough, and from now on, she could do whatever she wanted. If she didn't want to acknowledge her brother, so be it. As Qin Jiaxi said, she had other siblings who would unconditionally support her.","Third Uncle Qin smiled, took his daughter's hand, and addressed Qin Han, \"Go reflect, and tell your mother clearly about cutting ties with her. What I just said, you'd better listen to, unless you also want to find yourself a new dad.\"","Qin Han's face paled.","Third Uncle Qin finished speaking and ushered everyone to leave.","Today marked Qin Jiaxi's new beginning, really reclaiming her dignity and avenging past wrongs.","Third Uncle Qin took everyone straight to the best hotel in Y City to celebrate Qin Jiaxi.","The revolving restaurant on the top floor of the hotel had a great view. Qin Xian directly stole away his wife for a private date, the two enjoying the beautiful scenery and sweetness.","Everything was going well. Ji Fei, gazing at Qin Xian under the night sky, felt her heart flutter, wanting to lean over to kiss her husband. But then she heard footsteps.","\"Second Sister-in-law, new update – Yu Xin is really refusing to leave. Qin Han, that idiot, is still helping her, but the lawyers and security have forcibly evicted them, tossing them out. She even faked a faint, but the lawyer just sent her straight to the police station. Before even entering, she panicked and signed the agreement, losing the house for good.\"","\"Qin Han was furious and wanted to take Yu Xin home, but Third Uncle Qin had already warned the security, so they wouldn’t let Yu Xin in.\"","\"In the end, Qin Han had to arrange a hotel for her, and things finally calmed down.\"","\"But Third Aunt’s call has already come through. Third Uncle Qin will likely have a tough time when he gets back.\"","Third Uncle Qin entrusted Jiaxi to me, asking us to take her back to the ancestral home. He’s worried Jiaxi might get mistreated.","Somehow, a gossip circle centered around Ji Fei had gradually formed. So, as soon as someone heard any news, Qin Second's family rushed over to report, and others followed suit, eager to join in.","When the crowd rushed up to the observation deck, they saw their head of the family, deeply gazing into his wife's eyes, hugging her... and the lady already had her arms around his neck, tiptoeing, ready for a kiss.","Everyone was shocked...","\"Sorry to interrupt!\"","Before anyone could leave, Ji Fei had already gotten interested.\"What? Really? Third Uncle Qin will have a tough battle when he gets home!\"","She abandoned her husband and turned towards the crowd...","Everyone looked over cautiously and saw Qin Xian's face darken, staring coldly at them with no emotion.","Everyone: Will we be in trouble later...?!!","It was mainly that Qin Xian's image was too restrained, making them always forget to be discreet. Boohoo.","After returning to the ancestral home, everyone gathered to gossip some more.","While Ji Fei was enjoying the ongoing \"eating melon\" act and live real-time updates.","\"Wow, Qin Han just left, and Su Ze is already seeking comfort.\"","“Hehe, Third Aunt is really pulling out the 'cry, make a scene, threaten to faint' routine! Oh, she's claiming a 'dong tai qi' threatened miscarriage now? I’m not being unkind here, but trying to force Third Uncle Qin to agree to adoption at a time like this is just too fake. Fortunately, Third Uncle Qin stuck to his guns and sent her straight to the hospital.”","\"Qin Han is still so stubborn, always thinking Yu Xin is good and Jiaxi is bad... Oh? He seems to still not know about Su Ze and Yu Xin’s affair. If we could get evidence...\""]},{"number":372,"title":"Chapter 372: Ambiguous Financial Relationships","paragraphs":["Qin Xian naturally arranged everything for his wife's little whims without question, treating it as a small surprise for her.","However, the subsequent developments left Qin Xian momentarily unable to produce the evidence he had gathered.","The campus speech incident had caused quite a stir, and Qin Han and Su Ze frequently made headlines in the entertainment news.","Fortunately, Third Uncle Qin's support for his daughter prevented any damage to the Qin Family's reputation.","It seemed that Third Uncle Qin had even disciplined Qin Han, who ended up hospitalized and unable to return to work.","Yu Xin also went quiet for a while.","Just when it seemed like the matter had blown over, Third Uncle Qin suddenly announced that he would be hosting a birthday party for Third Aunt.","Third Aunt's birthday was indeed around this time, but due to her unstable pregnancy and the proximity to the Old Master's grand birthday celebration, they had originally decided not to hold a party.","Now, however, they changed their minds, citing the need to avoid speculation about the family's internal relationships.","After all, family discord could negatively impact Qin Corporation's business in Y City.","Maintaining appearances was essential in their social circle.","Third Uncle Qin discussed this with Qin Jiaxi, as she had been staying at the family estate and hadn't returned home since the incident.","\"Your mother has calmed down recently. Although she hasn't said it outright, I think she wants to reconcile with you,\" he said.","Since Third Aunt had never directly clashed with Qin Jiaxi, Third Uncle Qin held some hope that his wife wouldn't be as stubborn as their son. After all, Jiaxi was her biological daughter.","Although Qin Jiaxi had given up on her brother, she still held a sliver of hope for her mother.","Qin Jiaxi nodded. \"I also want to see how Mom feels. If she still doesn't welcome me, I don't want to put you in a difficult position, Dad. I plan to stay at the estate for the long term, and Grandpa has already agreed.\"","Third Uncle Qin, usually cold and stern, felt his eyes well up with tears. He didn't try to defend anyone.","While he loved his wife, he also loved his daughter. If his wife refused to change, he wouldn't hesitate to divorce her and raise his daughter alone, leaving his son with his wife.","Thinking back to the arguments when he first returned home, he sometimes wondered if he truly loved such an unreasonable woman.","But for the sake of the family, he had to make an effort.","For Third Aunt's birthday, the rest of the Qin Family naturally had to attend.","Third Uncle Qin informed Qin Xian about the party. Although the guest list was limited, many attendees would likely be there to see Qin Xian.","Qin Xian acknowledged this but noticed that Third Uncle Qin seemed unusually eager.","Qin Xian wasn't the type to spare someone's feelings just because they were happy.","In case of any conflicts, he wanted his uncle to be fully aware of the situation, so he laid out all the evidence he had gathered so far.","Of course, he wasn't foolish enough to admit he was investigating Third Aunt directly.","Instead, he said, \"I had someone look into Yu Xin's background because of your previous interest in adopting her.\"","Third Uncle Qin assumed Qin Xian was simply vetting the candidate.","\"Since we're not adopting her anymore, there's no need to worry about it,\" he replied.","But Qin Xian handed over the documents anyway. \"You should take a look.\"","The documents contained a lot of information about Third Aunt.","Third Uncle Qin knew that his wife had known Yu Xin for a long time, so it made sense that investigating Yu Xin would involve his wife. His wife had been involved in charity work, and Yu Xin was from the same orphanage she supported. Since she often brought their son along, Third Uncle Qin had never suspected anything.","Looking back, it was no wonder his son and Yu Xin were so close—they had known each other since childhood.","However, when Third Uncle Qin reviewed the documents, he frowned.","His wife had indeed been donating to charity, and the records were clear, with substantial amounts listed. But upon closer inspection, the funds almost entirely ended up in Yu Xin's personal account.","If this had been going on for years, Yu Xin should have been extremely wealthy by now and wouldn't have cared about her modest living situation.","Yet Yu Xin didn't seem to have much money, as the funds in her account were regularly transferred to another account.","The account holder's name was unfamiliar, but the location was clear—it was from another city.","This city was significant because Third Aunt's ex-boyfriend, whom she had dated before marrying Third Uncle Qin, was from there.","Though they had broken up before the families arranged their marriage, and the man had long since left Y City, Third Uncle Qin had never suspected anything. But now, the coincidence was too glaring to ignore.","It was impossible for Yu Xin to have orchestrated this on her own, as the funds were willingly given by his wife.","Qin Xian couldn't investigate Third Aunt's accounts directly, so Third Uncle Qin realized he would have to look into it himself. He needed to find out how the financial manager handling his wife's charity accounts had been operating.","Pride kept Third Uncle Qin from delving deeper into the matter just yet. He thanked Qin Xian, took the documents, and left.","When Qin Xian stepped out, he saw Ji Fei and his siblings buzzing with excitement.","Among them, Ji Fei was the only one who hadn't met Third Aunt yet.","Ji Fei had a strong intuition that Third Aunt was hiding something.","Meanwhile, Qin Second's family had a feeling that the birthday party would be eventful once Ji Fei met Third Aunt. After all, Ji Fei was known as the \"Melon King\" of high society for a reason!","Soon, the day of the birthday party arrived. Aside from the Old Master and his wife, the rest of the family arrived in full force at Third Uncle Qin's house, making quite the grand entrance.","Third Aunt's previous absence from family gatherings had left many feeling slighted, as if she didn't respect Qin Second and Qin Fourth's families.","But given her status as an older expectant mother, everyone had refrained from commenting. Now that the elders were willing to attend, it was a gesture of goodwill. If she still didn't appreciate it, they might as well cut ties.","Qin Jiaxi walked in with Qin Rong, as the two were close in age and got along well.","As they approached the house, Qin Jiaxi felt a wave of nervousness—it had been so long since she'd been home.","When they arrived at the entrance, they saw Qin Han, who greeted everyone with a smile, maintaining a polite facade. However, his expression faltered momentarily when he saw them, though he quickly forced another smile.","Ji Fei got out of the car just in time to catch Qin Han's change in expression.","[Oh ho~ Let me see what you're up to, you little schemer. Are you planning to force Third Uncle Qin to adopt Yu Xin today? Is Yu Xin even hiding in your room? Are you out of your mind?]","Qin Second's family nearly stumbled. They knew something juicy was about to go down!"]},{"number":373,"title":"Chapter 373: Poisonous Woman, Poisonous Woman, Poisonous Woman","paragraphs":["Upon hearing such juicy gossip, Ji Fei naturally wouldn’t expose it right away. Even if Yu Xin were to be driven away now, who knows what schemes they might come up with later to force Third Uncle Qin and Qin Jiaxi into submission.","The best approach was to let them play their cards and have Third Uncle Qin reject them outright in front of everyone, making his stance clear and putting an end to their delusions once and for all.","[Let’s see what Third Uncle Qin does. I believe he won’t let Qin Jiaxi down.]","The Qin Second family also thought it best to stay on the sidelines.","However, as they passed by Qin Han, none of them gave him a friendly look—it was almost as if they were all rolling their eyes.","Qin Jiaxi initially planned to ignore Qin Han completely, but just then, Third Uncle Qin hurried out, smiling warmly to welcome them.","In truth, Third Uncle Qin didn’t need to greet guests at the door, but he had known in advance that his daughter had returned and was worried she might be treated unfairly, so he came out to meet her.","He even kept Qin Jiaxi by his side, personally guiding her to greet the remaining guests.","This sent a subtle but clear message: his precious daughter, Qin Jiaxi, was the true lady of the Qin Family, no matter what his wife and son might say about her to outsiders.","In the past, Qin Jiaxi would always hide in the corners of the house, trying to make herself as invisible as possible.","This was the first time she had been so openly involved in receiving guests. She was extremely nervous, but with her father by her side, she gradually found her footing.","Meanwhile, Qin Han kept shooting her ambiguous glances from the side.","Qin Han had glanced over several times, but his sister didn’t come over to bow her head as she usually would. Her completely different attitude left him somewhat flustered.","He didn’t reflect on his own mistakes, though. Instead, he grew even angrier at Qin Jiaxi, thinking she was being disrespectful by defying him, her elder brother. How ungrateful!","Looking at his father’s attitude, Qin Han couldn’t help but feel a twinge of doubt.","Could it really be as Yu Xin had said? Was his father planning to fully support Qin Jiaxi and pit her against him?!","Moreover, Qin Xian had a much better relationship with Qin Jiaxi than with him. If Qin Xian supported Qin Jiaxi... the Qin Family had no tradition of favoring sons over daughters.","Qin Han had never taken his useless sister seriously before, but now he was genuinely starting to feel a sense of crisis.","However, this sense of crisis was fleeting. He still looked down on Qin Jiaxi, confident that he could continue to belittle and dismiss her.","But the guests at the birthday banquet were watching with mixed expressions. Having just heard the gossip about the family, they couldn’t help but read into Third Uncle Qin’s actions.","The rest of the Qin Family was led by the butler to the garden, where the main seats were arranged.","As they entered, they saw a group of noble ladies gathered around a beautiful, slightly pregnant woman.","The woman appeared gentle and serene, the very picture of a virtuous wife and mother. Yet, she was anything but—she was someone who showed blatant favoritism toward her own daughter.","When the Qin Family arrived, Third Aunt Qin didn’t act presumptuously. She slowly stood up, despite her apparent discomfort, and greeted each of them politely. Her manners were impeccable.","But then she added, “I’m afraid Jiaxi has caused everyone some trouble recently. My daughter has a rather peculiar personality, which has led to many misunderstandings. I’ll make sure to educate her properly from now on.”","As soon as these words left her mouth, the Qin Family’s expressions darkened.","How audacious! She was subtly implying, in front of the guests, that the recent gossip was all Qin Jiaxi’s fault, not Qin Han’s or Yu Xin’s.","It was truly shocking to see such blatant favoritism. Did she think the Qin Family would hold back out of politeness and not call her out on Qin Han’s misbehavior?","Well, she clearly didn’t understand the Qin Family’s temperament.","“Jiaxi is such a wonderful girl. There’s no need to educate her. If anything, Third Sister-in-law, you should focus on educating Qin Han. He’s old enough to know better, yet he’s still acting so immaturely, making a fool of himself in front of everyone,” Qin's Mom retorted sharply. “Oh, wait—I heard Qin Han has always been under your guidance. Then I suppose it’s Third Uncle’s fault for not stepping in to discipline him properly. Yes, it’s all Third Uncle’s fault.”","Third Aunt Qin’s face immediately changed color. She stared at Qin's Mom in disbelief, clearly not expecting her to be so bold as to openly challenge her in front of everyone.","The onlookers’ eyes widened in excitement, eagerly watching the confrontation between the sisters-in-law.","After all, it was widely believed that the Qin Family was as tight-knit as a drum, with harmonious relationships. No one had expected such drama to unfold.","“Second Sister-in-law, how we raise our children...” Third Aunt Qin’s temper was not as gentle as her appearance suggested.","But Qin's Father cut her off, firmly supporting his wife. “I heard Third Uncle gave Qin Han a good beating recently. I saw him greeting guests earlier—has he fully recovered? But then again, he deserved it for his mistakes. It’s only natural.”","Fourth Uncle Qin chimed in with a smile, “Third Sister-in-law, you shouldn’t stand for too long. Weren’t you just at the hospital not long ago?”","These remarks only confirmed the earlier gossip, leaving Third Aunt Qin’s face a kaleidoscope of emotions.","She couldn’t tell whether these people were genuinely displeased with her or simply standing up for Qin Jiaxi.","What was so special about that useless, unlikable girl that they would go out of their way to defend her?","Knowing she was at a disadvantage, Third Aunt Qin swallowed her pride for the sake of the bigger picture.","The younger members of the Qin Family struggled to hold back their laughter. It was satisfying to see their elders handle the situation so effectively, as they themselves couldn’t openly challenge their elders.","Meanwhile, Qin Xian was carefully helping Ji Fei sit down, treating her like a delicate doll.","Ever since she had seen Third Aunt Qin, Ji Fei had been in a daze.","The Qin Second family had been stealing glances at her, puzzled by her unusual silence.","But seeing Ji Fei lost in thought, they began to feel uneasy.","This had happened before, and every time it did, it meant there was some earth-shattering gossip waiting to be revealed.","Ji Fei was overwhelmed, stunned, and utterly shaken.","There was so much information to process that she could barely keep up with the first few pieces. She hadn’t even had time to read the rest before her urge to comment took over.","Unbeknownst to her, in her excitement, she had been gripping Qin Xian’s hand so tightly that she was on the verge of bruising it.","[What a vile woman! I’ve seen shameless, despicable women before, but Third Aunt Qin takes the cake! How can she live with herself after doing all this?]","The Qin Second family was already trembling with dread. While they didn’t particularly like this woman, she had been Third Uncle Qin’s wife for over twenty years and was considered part of the Qin Family. They could tolerate her being foolish or misguided, but they truly hoped she didn’t have any major skeletons in her closet.","Yet, it was rare to hear Ji Fei speak so harshly.","They braced themselves for the worst.","And Ji Fei didn’t disappoint, dropping a bombshell right from the start.","[What “advanced maternal age,” needing Third Uncle’s care and attention? You’re carrying someone else’s child!]","The Qin Second family: !!!!!!","[You’ve been keeping your old lover in an apartment in the neighboring complex, cheating on Third Uncle for the past six months!]","The Qin Second family was now shaking uncontrollably.","[No wonder you wanted to adopt Yu Xin—she’s your old lover’s daughter! You’re trying to let your old lover’s daughter leech off the Qin Family!]","The Qin Second family could no longer hold back their furious glances toward Third Aunt Qin.","[Wait, the leeching has already started?! All these years of charity work were just a front to funnel money to your old lover in another city! How dare you! Third Uncle works so hard to earn money, and you’re spending it like this! I’m furious, furious, furious!]","The Qin Second family was now taking deep breaths, trying to restrain their urge to lash out.","What kind of vile woman had they let into the Qin Family?!"]},{"number":374,"title":"Chapter 374: Yu Xin is indeed more suited to Su Ze than you.","paragraphs":["According to Ji Fei's system, everyone now understands the full story.","Originally, the two were college sweethearts, but the old flame was just a gold-digger. Since Third Aunt Qin's family was wealthy, they naturally wouldn't consent to her being with him. They offered him money to leave, and the two indeed broke up. Later, through a marriage of convenience, Third Uncle Qin took a liking to Third Aunt Qin, and they got together smoothly.","Initially, everything was fine, but when Qin Jiaxi was about three years old, the old flame returned, contacting Third Aunt Qin to borrow money to pay off debts using various methods.","Third Aunt Qin secretly met with the old flame, gave him the money, and learned that he had already divorced. They almost rekindled their romance, but since Qin Jiaxi was still young and needed her mother, Third Aunt Qin had no time for secret meetings. The old flame, not daring to push too hard, decided to take the money and leave for another city.","However, before leaving, he abandoned his daughter from his previous marriage, Yu Xin, at an orphanage.","In fact, he never asked Third Aunt Qin to take care of Yu Xin; she did it on her own to appear virtuous and devoted to the man, demonstrating her willingness to sacrifice for him. Love begets love, and so she took care of Yu Xin.","The old flame, upon learning about his daughter being taken care of, used this connection to ask for more money, maintaining their relationship through this method.","Eventually, in the past half year, the man arrived here fleeing debts. Unable to pay off the large debt, Third Aunt Qin couldn't help him without fear of being discovered. She came up with the idea of adopting Yu Xin, as being a foster daughter of the Qin family would entitle her to some benefits. With those benefits, the Qin family wouldn't interfere much.","Moreover, if Yu Xin became a foster daughter and won Third Uncle Qin's affection, Third Aunt Qin could continue to funnel money to the man in the future.","This is why they relentlessly squeezed Qin Jiaxi's living space, gradually replacing her position with Yu Xin, aiming for a bright financial future.","[During this process, Third Aunt Qin and the old flame finally rekindled their affair, leading to an unexpected pregnancy. Unable to bear the thought of aborting, Third Aunt Qin deceived Third Uncle Qin to register the child. Later, she lied to Third Uncle Qin about being pregnant, using her advanced maternal age as an excuse to manipulate him into giving in to her every whim. How shameless can one be? Ugh, I almost feel disgusted on Third Uncle Qin's behalf. If you love the old flame so much, why not divorce? It's obvious she doesn't want to let go of her wealthy husband's identity, all while craving both love and money. Does she plan to have Third Uncle Qin support their entire family in the future? Ridiculous!]","Qin Second and his family now deeply understand the risks of being caught up in gossip, as they can barely control their rising blood pressure.","They feel utterly nauseated.","What a tragic family misfortune! They must cleanse the family!","If not for too many concerns, they would leap out immediately, pointing their fingers at Third Aunt Qin's face, shouting how shameless she is in front of everyone!","Although the marriage is definitely over, everything must first be discussed with Third Uncle Qin.","And they can't just accuse without proper arrangement.","They all looked at Qin Xian.","Qin Xian's eyes were already icy. However, he didn't immediately offer a solution, as he wanted to rely on the half-investigated information he previously gathered to give to Third Uncle Qin. Third Uncle Qin should investigate the old flame, and then... many things would be suspicious.","At this time, the guests had been welcomed in, and Third Uncle Qin led Qin Han and Qin Jiaxi inside.","Ji Fei was interrupted and looked at them.","[So, the reason for liking Qin Han but not Qin Jiaxi is because she was delayed in her extramarital affairs when Qin Jiaxi was young? Every time she wanted to go out, Qin Jiaxi's presence hindered her, gradually making her despise and become irritable, feeling her freedom and life were being restrained?]","[Not entirely. It's also because she took Qin Han to the orphanage, wanting her son to be her successor who would treat Yu Xin well. Plus, Qin Han would inherit the family business, ensuring their future security. That's why she didn't resent her son. She had already decided to treat Yu Xin as her own daughter, so she didn't want to love Qin Jiaxi anymore, fearing it would make her feel she was betraying her love.]","[This is truly sick. Preferring to be nice to someone else's child over her own?]","[Even funnier is that Qin Han is simply deluded and manipulated by Yu Xin. He has no idea his mother has cheated and brought him a half-sibling.]","[Tsk tsk tsk, this gossip is giving me a headache. I must find a way to let Qin Xian know and uncover their true faces!]","After Qin Jiaxi entered, Third Aunt Qin actually gave her a somewhat forced friendly face, not going off the rails immediately but instead inviting her to sit closer.","Around them, guests moved about, toasting and socializing amicably.","Many approached Qin Xian.","To get closer to the gossip and keep a close eye on Third Aunt Qin, preventing her from mistreating Qin Jiaxi, Ji Fei decisively abandoned her husband and sat near Qin Jiaxi.","Qin Yi, Qin Zhao, and Qin Rong, who didn't need much socializing, quickly followed suit.","This made it difficult for Third Aunt Qin, who wanted to take the opportunity to scold her daughter a few words while Third Uncle Qin was away, to say anything.","\"I heard you broke up with the Su Family's young master.\" Third Aunt Qin chose an appropriate topic.","Qin Jiaxi, however, wasn't used to interacting with her mother, so she simply replied, \"Mom must have seen the news. He and Yu Xin are actually together, so we broke up.\"","Third Aunt Qin frowned slightly and said, \"Well, it's because you didn't have the foresight. Yu Xin is indeed more suited to Su Ze. Don't hold a grudge against Yu Xin because of this. Get along well in the future.\"","Qin Jiaxi showed no reaction, as compared to her mother's usual remarks, this was relatively polite.","But those who hadn't been hurt by her words were dumbfounded.","They had also noticed that, because of their presence, Third Aunt Qin couldn't say much, expecting her to behave, but instead, she opened her mouth.","[Clearly, it's not intentional. This is just her habit! She didn't even realize how harsh she was being to Qin Jiaxi! Her words were relatively mild, and I can't imagine what kind of life Qin Jiaxi had under her mother's control. No wonder she showed no reaction to such insulting words. She's immune!]"]},{"number":375,"title":"Chapter 375: She's Not the Kind of Person Who Cares Seriously About Her Daughter.","paragraphs":["Qin Dynasty Qin Rong: \"We don't have immunity; we've been poisoned.\"","Qin Yi didn't hear Ji Fei's thoughts but could empathize with her. Being slightly older, he spoke without much concern, \"Third Aunt, that's not quite right. How is that person more suited than Jiaxi? Your daughter is the victim here.\"","Third Aunt Qin frowned, feeling extremely annoyed. She was talking to her own daughter, so why did outsiders always feel the need to butt in?","Just as she was about to refute, she suddenly heard Ji Fei speak up.","\"Brother, why are you saying that? Yu Xin and Su Ze are indeed a perfect match. Jiaxi isn't suited for him.\"","Unaccustomed to Ji Fei's approach, both Qin Yi and Qin Jiaxi were stunned. But their instincts told them there was more to this. If someone else had said this, Jiaxi might have felt hurt, but since it was Ji Fei, Jiaxi instantly wanted to hear the rest of the explanation.","Third Aunt Qin, however, suddenly felt that there was at least one normal person among them who could read the room. She was about to speak in agreement when Ji Fei laughed and said, \"How could Jiaxi, a normal person, be a match for Su Ze? Su Ze and Yu Xin are truly made for each other. As the saying goes, 'A scumbag and a slut make a perfect pair; together, they can last forever!'\"","Those words instantly silenced Third Aunt Qin, and her nose nearly twisted in anger.","She wanted to get furious, but the group burst out laughing.","She tried to refute, but everyone was giving Ji Fei thumbs up, saying, \"You're absolutely right!\"","When she attempted to defend herself, Ji Fei added with a smile, \"Third Aunt, you're so wise. You know that a cheating scumbag like that isn't worthy of your daughter. Only someone like that little third wheel is a match. Don't worry, Jiaxi won't hold a grudge against them. After all, Third Uncle has already thoroughly avenged Jiaxi, so if she still held a grudge, it would just seem petty.\"","After saying that, Ji Fei turned to Jiaxi, who had a glint of amusement in her eyes, and continued, \"Jiaxi, listen to your mother's advice. The next time you see Yu Xin, remind her to behave better in the future and not act like a fool in front of the Qin family's eldest daughter. Otherwise, we know how to use our position to bully others.\"","By the last sentence, Ji Fei's tone had lowered, and her gaze turned icy as she stared at Third Aunt Qin.","In that moment, the aura she exuded was strikingly similar to Qin Xian.","Third Aunt Qin didn't expect to be stunned by this young girl in front of her, and in the end, she couldn't muster a single word of resistance.","When she finally came to her senses, she was so furious that her face turned pale.","What was even more infuriating was that her daughter actually agreed.","Third Aunt Qin couldn't help but turn her sharp gaze toward Qin Jiaxi.","Today, Qin Jiaxi felt entirely unfamiliar to her. The once meek little girl who had always tried to please her seemed to have vanished. Now, even when faced with her, Jiaxi wore a cold expression.","But when talking to others, she could smile.","That kind of smile was completely alien to Third Aunt Qin. It was as if there was no memory in her mind of Jiaxi ever smiling like that.","Third Aunt Qin didn't reflect on her own behavior. Instead, she thought Jiaxi was ungrateful and pathetic, a lapdog who tried to please other members of the Qin family. She had always been a nuisance since she was young. Yu Xin, on the other hand, was well-behaved and obedient.","Thinking about the upcoming plans, Third Aunt Qin knew she had to take a bold gamble. So, before that...","She swallowed her anger and pretended not to have been ridiculed, continuing, \"If it's a breakup, then so be it. By the way, a son of a friend of mine is doing business here and doesn't know his way around. You should help him out and make some friends.\"","Before Qin Jiaxi could react, she waved her hand toward the distance, and her smile was as bright as a flower, a level of friendliness she rarely showed to any member of the Qin family.","Her intent was clear: she was going to introduce another man to Qin Jiaxi.","But had Third Uncle Qin even mentioned this?","Seeing Qin Jiaxi's reluctance, it was obvious she disliked this kind of arrangement.","She had just come out of a failed relationship.","Ji Fei, on the other hand, had a simple thought:","[It's strange. She's not the type to genuinely consider her daughter's well-being. Could it be that she's worried Qin Jiaxi's single status might interfere with her precious Yu Xin and Su Ze's relationship? After all, the Su family wanted to arrange a marriage with Jiaxi, not Yu Xin.]","The others, however, were more curious about what kind of man Third Aunt Qin would introduce to Qin Jiaxi.","Then they saw a fat man walking quickly over, gasping for breath. His face was filled with smiles, his head and ears plump, and his face covered in pockmarks, which could completely ruin one's appetite.","Not all wealthy people are handsome, but the rich tend to take better care of themselves. Yet this man was completely out of place in this setting.","Was this the man Third Aunt Qin wanted to introduce?","The Qin family members were all wide-eyed with disbelief, and Qin Jiaxi's face turned pale.","So, in her mother's eyes, this is what she was worth?","Instinct told them not to judge by appearances, but the next second, both Ji Fei and Qin Rong felt an uncomfortable, greasy gaze scanning them, especially Ji Fei.","\"You look very familiar,\" the fat man said with a smile. \"You look like a celebrity.\"","Instead of introducing himself, he started by talking to Ji Fei.","Ji Fei's expression immediately darkened as she coldly glanced at Third Aunt Qin.","But Third Aunt Qin was beaming with affection at the fat man.","Qin Zhao was already furious. He directly said coldly to the fat man, \"If you look over here again, I'll gouge your eyes out.\" Then, taking a fork from the dessert tray, he slammed it into the cake, making the fat man flinch and quickly look away.","Third Aunt Qin, however, was like a blind person who couldn't see the offense. She was displeased and said, \"Qin Zhao, what are you doing? This is my friend's son. People of the same age should get along well.\"","\"Ha. I dislike ugly people,\" Qin Zhao declared proudly.","This made the fat man's expression turn awkward, though he didn't dare to cause trouble.","Third Aunt Qin was incensed but knew Qin Zhao wasn't the type to be reasoned with. So, she ignored him and directly addressed the fat man, \"Chang, come over. Let me introduce you to my daughter, Qin Jiaxi. In the future, if you need anything, just ask her for help. Think of her as family and get along well.\"","Saying that, she actually signaled for the fat man to sit next to Qin Jiaxi.","The fat man looked Qin Jiaxi over and seemed disappointed. Jiaxi was actually quite pretty, but compared to Ji Fei and Qin Rong, she paled in comparison. The fat man had initially assumed one of the two prettier girls would be his match, so upon seeing Jiaxi, he felt a deep sense of regret.","Ji Fei, seeing the fat man still looking regretful but eager to sit next to Jiaxi, felt like vomiting.","\"Jiaxi, come here,\" Ji Fei said directly."]},{"number":376,"title":"Chapter 376: Double Insurance for His Old Flame","paragraphs":["Ji Fei had already been preparing to get up, and as soon as Ji Fei provided a reason, Qin Jiaxi practically leaped to her feet and moved over to Ji Fei's side.","Qin Rong quickly shifted her position to make room for Qin Jiaxi to sit between them.","Third Aunt Qin immediately frowned, \"What are you doing? They should get to know each other properly.\"","【I really want to curse out loud. Does she even realize what she looks like right now? It's like a brothel madam introducing her girls to customers. Does she hate her own daughter so much that she has to set her up with such a piece of work? This guy doesn't need any deep investigation; just his behavior a moment ago shows what a shady character he is. Third Aunt Qin is really pushing the limits. I'm curious to see what kind of person this is!】","At that moment, Qin Yi and Qin Zhao spoke up.","\"Yes, they should get to know each other better. I wonder what business this gentleman's family is in,\" Qin Yi said. \"Although I don't handle the family business, I'm familiar with the circles in Y City.\"","\"Exactly, let's get to know each other. I wonder which school you graduated from and what you studied? What do you primarily focus on now?\" Qin Zhao sneered.","Faced with these inquiries, the overweight man stumbled and evaded the questions, offering no useful information.","Qin Zhao chuckled directly, \"Could he be a scammer?\"","\"What are you talking about?\" The man grew anxious and even tugged at Third Aunt Qin's sleeve, seeking help.","Third Aunt Qin quickly defended him, \"Of course not. His father is a friend of mine.\"","\"Oh, who is his father? And how is he friends with Third Aunt Qin? Does Third Uncle Qin know about this friendship?\" Ji Fei suddenly interjected.","Her tone was a first for her, cold and cutting, as if she were interrogating and mocking at the same time.","Third Aunt Qin became visibly displeased, \"You're questioning your elder here. Do you think I would harm my own daughter?\"","\"That's not guaranteed,\" Qin Rong muttered softly.","\"You... how dare you disrespect your elders!\" Third Aunt Qin grew anxious, her voice rising.","Naturally, people around them began to notice.","Ji Fei, however, wasn't going to give her any face. She directly pulled Qin Jiaxi to her feet and warned Third Aunt Qin, \"I don't think this man is suitable. You'd better keep him away and out of sight. The Qins don't buy into the whole 'obedience to parents' act. If you want to introduce someone to Jiaxi, I'll make sure to have a thorough background check done with Third Uncle Qin. Every single person must be vetted to see if they're worthy of the Qin family's dignity. If anyone tries to pull a fast one, the Qins will make sure they face the consequences of coveting what isn't theirs.\"","As Ji Fei spoke, her icy gaze swept over Third Aunt Qin and finally settled on the overweight man, her threat clear, causing him to tremble all over.","Without another word, Ji Fei led Qin Jiaxi away, finding the atmosphere utterly repulsive.","Qin Jiaxi and Qin Yi were a bit bewildered. While the situation was indeed disgusting, Ji Fei's outburst was much larger than expected. It was as if she had just publicly torn into Third Aunt Qin, and many people were watching.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, however, began to suspect that their sister-in-law might have discovered something.","Qin Xian, naturally keeping an eye on his wife, noticed her sudden anger and excused himself from the people trying to talk to him. He immediately went to Ji Fei.","As soon as Ji Fei sat down, Qin Xian arrived. She leaned on him as if seeking a lifeline, not caring about the others present. Qin Xian embraced her openly and asked, \"What's wrong?\"","\"That woman introduced a disgusting man to Jiaxi,\" Ji Fei explained.","Meanwhile, Jiaxi had been brought over to sit with them. \"Sister-in-law, I'm fine. Just ignore it.\"","Ji Fei hesitated, wanting to say more.","Qin Zhao, however, quickly filled everyone in on what had happened. Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing, who had just freed themselves from other duties, also heard the story and were equally shocked.","\"Could that man be incredibly powerful? Why else would Third Aunt Qin overlook his appearance?\" Qin Jing wondered.","\"Pfft, he's a fraud,\" Qin Zhao replied. \"And a sleazy one at that. Qin Xiaoyu, you should stay far away from him. He was eyeing my sister-in-law and sister like they were his next meal.\"","Qin Xian's expression turned icy, and he drew Ji Fei even closer to him, his eyes dark with displeasure.","Qin Yi sighed, \"I wonder what she's thinking. Sigh.\"","【Heh, what could she be thinking? Double insurance for her old flame, that's what. That fat guy actually followed his father here. He's Yu Xin's brother. When their parents divorced, their mother took him away. Later, the old flame returned to their hometown and reconnected with her son. This woman is really ruthless. In her eyes, even a degenerate raised by a gambler is a treasure. Marrying Jiaxi off to him would make him part of the Qin family. That way, Jiaxi could take care of her old flame's family. Does this woman have holes in her head? How can she think this is reasonable and even a good match? How does she see her own daughter? Does she not feel content unless she ruins her own child?】","Ji Fei vented her frustration in one long rant, feeling utterly tainted by it all. She clung to her husband, needing a moment to recover.","Meanwhile, the others who could hear her thoughts were left in complete shock.","Initially, they thought Third Aunt Qin hated her own daughter. She was merely forcing a miserable match to punish her or perhaps out of stupidity, duped by someone. But they never imagined that she wasn't stupid at all—she was sharp, just sharp in favor of someone else's family.","It was astonishing how she managed to manipulate the entire household of Third Uncle Qin like this.","Thankfully, they found out—otherwise, who knows what kind of mess would have unfolded.","Those who couldn't hear Ji Fei's thoughts merely felt the ominous atmosphere around them.","Soon, the fat man disappeared, though no one knew if he had left.","When Third Uncle Qin arrived, he didn't see the man and only asked Third Aunt Qin what the commotion was about. In his mind, it must have been Third Aunt Qin causing trouble again, bullying Qin Jiaxi, which angered Ji Fei.","Third Aunt Qin tried to defend herself with a few words before covering her stomach, looking distressed.","Seeing that it was almost time, Third Uncle Qin didn't press further. It was time for the toast and cake-cutting.","Soon, a giant cake was wheeled out.","Everyone stood up and gathered around.","Third Uncle Qin helped his wife stand on the steps built beside the pool.","As Third Uncle Qin spoke, someone near Ji Fei suddenly asked, \"Odd, where is Qin Han?\"","Ji Fei thought to herself, 【He's bringing Yu Xin here, of course. They're about to... holy crap... such audacity!】","The thought had barely passed when there was a gasp.","Third Aunt Qin suddenly plunged from the edge of the steps toward the right side, where no one was standing. If she fell, the consequences would be dire."]},{"number":377,"title":"Chapter 377: So We Can Get a Divorce","paragraphs":["Because Third Aunt Qin was pregnant, she was wearing flat shoes today. The stage she was on was very stable, with no reason for her to fall.","And everyone just witnessed this miraculous fall. Most of them were left in a state of shock, unable to react.","Third Uncle Qin was talking when he felt his wife suddenly move beside him. By the time he tried to reach out, it was already too late.","\"Zixuan!\" Third Uncle Qin was genuinely worried, almost wanting to rush over to save his wife.","Even Qin Jiaxi, standing at the bottom of the stage, dashed over in a trance. Even though she was far away and couldn’t reach her, she still ran over. She was so hasty that she tripped over the steps, but after falling, she scrambled back up.","And at this critical moment, someone darted out from behind the green plant pots closest to Third Aunt Qin. They caught her just in time, with perfect angle and force.","Everyone took a closer look and saw it was Yu Xin.","Third Aunt Qin looked pale with fear, her eyes red, still trembling with dread.","Yu Xin appeared slightly worried and well-behaved, repeatedly comforting Third Aunt Qin. \"Auntie, it's okay, it's okay.\"","\"Yu Xin, why are you here? This time, it’s really thanks to you. I almost got scared to death.\" Third Aunt Qin said tearfully.","Yu Xin replied, \"I knew today was Auntie's birthday. Even though the previous misunderstanding made me... unpopular with Uncle and Jiaxi, I still wanted to come and give Auntie a birthday gift. It's a good thing I came.\"","At this point, Third Uncle Qin had already jumped over to Third Aunt Qin's side, his face still showing traces of fear. He took his wife from Yu Xin’s hands and lowered his head to inquire about her wellbeing.","Qin Han finally appeared, pretending to just arrive and expressing concern for his mother. No one noticed Qin Jiaxi silently getting up; it was only when Qin Rong came over to help her sit down.","\"I'm fine, there’s no need to call a doctor. Honey, if it weren’t for Yu Xin, I... I know you don’t like Yu Xin, but she has saved me and our child twice. So no matter how much you and Jiaxi object, I have to announce this here.\" Third Aunt Qin said, choked up and excited.","Third Uncle Qin’s mind was still in disarray; everything had happened too quickly, leaving him confused. But hearing Third Aunt Qin's words, he knew what she was about to do and immediately frowned, wanting to object. However, Third Aunt Qin had already pushed him aside, taking Yu Xin’s hand.","She announced to everyone, \"Everyone has seen it. Yu Xin has saved me and my child twice. I can’t repay this kindness. I believe Yu Xin and I have an destined bond, so I hereby announce that I have decided to adopt Yu Xin. From now on, Yu Xin will be our family's little princess. I will treat her equally with my other children, and I hope everyone will witness this.\"","The crowd instantly erupted in commotion. Yu Xin’s palms were sweaty, and her face revealed an unmistakable look of ambition and triumph. Qin Han stood beside Yu Xin, beaming with joy, as if he and Yu Xin, along with Third Aunt Qin, were the real family.","Qin Jiaxi sat there, staring blankly at all this, her face showing no emotion. As a child, she should have felt gratitude towards Yu Xin for saving her mother, but instead, her heart ached painfully, leaving her mind blank.","The other members of the Qin family were also caught off guard by how events had unfolded. Yet, listening to Third Aunt Qin’s words, they were filled with discontent.","Equal treatment? Was she joking?","\"Zixuan! Don’t be ridiculous. We haven’t even discussed this. How can you...?\" Third Uncle Qin immediately spoke up, trying to halt this farce.","But Third Aunt Qin immediately turned to him fiercely. \"I must repay this life-saving grace. When did the Qin family become so unappreciative? I’m telling you today, Yu Xin, I must adopt her. If you don’t agree, then we’ll get a divorce.\"","Third Uncle Qin’s eyes widened in shock; for a moment, he couldn’t speak.","\"Dad, it’s just adopting Yu Xin. Do you really have to oppose it so much?\" Qin Han chimed in: \"Don’t you value Mom and the child’s lives?\"","Third Uncle Qin immediately glared at Qin Han angrily. He was certain that Yu Xin’s appearance was orchestrated by Qin Han, but he dared not think that his wife might have used her and their child’s safety to scheme to adopt Yu Xin.","The other Qin family members also harbored suspicions but dared not consider the possibility. After all, few people would go to such lengths.","【That’s really something. Can such a scheme be pulled off twice? Last time it was a fake car accident, and now it’s a sudden fall without any reason. She’s acting right here, doing a fine job, but doesn’t she fear an actual accident? Wait, those steps aren’t that high. With her wearing flat shoes and considering her fall, if Yu Xin hadn’t caught her, it would’ve been like jumping down from the same spot. So she must have ensured she wouldn’t get hurt before orchestrating this. Because Third Uncle Qin had clearly stated he wouldn’t adopt Yu Xin, she had to resort to this double life-saving moral high ground.】","Ji Fei felt helpless. There had been so many drama with Third Aunt Qin before that she was too engrossed in those explosive details to closely investigate how they planned to get the Qin family to adopt Yu Xin today. Otherwise, she might have been able to prevent it... But no, this kind of thing is really hard to guard against, especially since Third Aunt Qin is perceived as a vulnerable party.","What now?","Ji Fei was getting anxious when Qin Xian suddenly patted her shoulder.","\"Don’t worry, trust Third Uncle Qin. He won’t be rash at a time like this.\" Qin Xian calmly said.","Ji Fei looked at him in surprise, \"Really?\"","Qin Xian replied, \"If all else fails, I have another way to stop it.\"","\"What?\" Ji Fei immediately became curious, \"But it’s such an unprovable act of life-saving grace.\"","Qin Xian smiled at her, saying, \"A foster daughter can’t get entangled with a son, right?\"","Ji Fei’s eyes lit up, \"You found evidence?\"","Qin Xian just smiled, indicating she should wait and see.","The scene was buzzing with excitement, with everyone tense as they watched how events would unfold. Just when everyone thought Third Uncle Qin would yield,","Third Uncle Qin suddenly said coldly, \"Yu Xin absolutely cannot enter our Qin family. If you insist on your idea, then we can get a divorce.\"","This statement stunned everyone except Qin Xian, feeling like they had just been struck by lightning.","What? Someone is adopting a little girl out of gratitude for a life-saving act, and it’s escalating to divorce? These two have been married for so long, could they be going through a rebellious phase now?","\"Dad! What are you saying! You want to divorce Mom!\" Qin Han was utterly enraged. He thought everything would naturally fall into place, whether through moral obligation or threat, but they didn’t expect Third Uncle Qin to be so ruthless and decisive.","\"You... you...\" Third Aunt Qin was also dumbfounded, nearly collapsing, her tears streaming down.","Yu Xin quickly supported Third Aunt Qin, her expression completely panicked. After all, whether she could enter the Qin family depended entirely on Third Uncle Qin’s decision."]},{"number":378,"title":"Chapter 378: Who Knows If There Will Be a Third Time","paragraphs":["Third Uncle Qin faced the hostility from his wife and son directly, saying firmly, \"A debt of gratitude can be repaid in other ways, but entering the Qin Family is absolutely impossible. We, the Qin Family, never accept someone who harms their own siblings. I think you're all confused, don't you remember the recent scandal? This woman conspired with another man to deceive our daughter's feelings, leading to our daughter being bullied at school. She even tacitly admitted to usurping our daughter's identity, enjoying the benefits that came with it, while indifferently allowing our daughter to be mistreated, and even guided the situation. What qualifications does someone who bullies our daughter have to join the Qin Family?\"","Third Uncle Qin's words were impactful, causing those around to recall the incident. Indeed, this young lady wasn't someone easy to deal with. They were all shocked to hear that the Qin Family Eldest Miss was bullied at school, let alone the fact that her brother at school didn't acknowledge Qin Jiaxi but instead recognized Yu Xin as his sister.","They didn't believe that Yu Xin had no ill intentions towards Qin Jiaxi.","Hearing this, Qin Jiaxi's tears silently rolled down her cheeks. She gazed at her father's back, no longer able to hold back her emotions. She stood up and declared, \"I also oppose Yu Xin joining our family!\"","\"Shut up!\" Qin Han, unable to refute his father, turned his anger on Qin Jiaxi. \"Are you done yet? Must you distort the facts to be satisfied? Yu Xin and Su Ze were completely innocent; it was all a misunderstanding. Yet you cling to it. The bullying you faced was clearly due to your own personality issues. Blame heaven, blame earth, but why don't you blame...\"","Before Qin Han could finish, Third Uncle Qin grabbed a glass of wine and splashed it onto his face.","Qin Han was stunned. Even though this wasn't the first time, being publicly humiliated in front of their circle of acquaintances was unbearable. Qin Han couldn't hold back anymore.","\"Think about what you just said,\" Third Uncle Qin scolded. \"As an older brother, you fail to protect your own sister and instead blame her at every turn. It seems you don't want to be Jiaxi's brother but only Yu Xin's. Fine, if your mother really wants to divorce me and adopt Yu Xin, you can go with her and be Yu Xin's brother.\"","Qin Han froze, realizing the implications of his father's words. Despite his anger, he instinctively didn't dare to argue further.","Third Aunt Qin glared at Third Uncle Qin with resentment. \"Is it really necessary to go this far over something so trivial? I only want to adopt a daughter. Such a small request, and you can't fulfill it?\"","\"Do you not understand what I'm saying, or do you simply not want to listen? Or perhaps you just don't care about your own daughter's suffering and insist on your own views.\" Third Uncle Qin said wearily.","Third Aunt Qin's lips trembled. \"It's you who is stubborn and biased. Yu Xin is clearly a very good girl.\"","\"Third Aunt really has a selective memory,\" Qin Zhao sneered. \"If stealing a man and bullying weren't enough for you to see, what about the medicinal recipe? Yu Xin herself admitted to stealing Jiaxi's hard work and taking credit for it. You don't stand up for your own daughter, yet you still want to adopt someone with such poor character?\"","\"Not seeing her own daughter's grievances but feeling sorry for someone else. Is this what Third Aunt considers fairness?\" Qin Yi added.","\"Yu Xin is already an adult. I wonder what Third Aunt is thinking, insisting on adopting her?\" Qin Rong muttered.","\"Adopting an adult? Isn't it clearly for the sake of the Qin Family?\" Qin Xiaoyu said bluntly.","Qin Jing quickly chimed in, \"Stop speaking the truth. If she's not after the Qin Family's wealth, does she want to gain another father to honor?\"","\"No, that's not it...\" Yu Xin suddenly panicked and desperately denied it.","Third Aunt Qin's face turned pale. \"You all stop spreading rumors. Jiaxi's grievances were naturally seen by me. Yu Xin also wants to sincerely apologize. She was just momentarily confused. Who doesn't make mistakes in their life? Must you hold onto them and nitpick? And Yu Xin isn't here for the Qin Family. She has a connection with us, and we feel sorry for her, that's all. She also wants to be good to us.\"","It was the first time everyone had truly seen Third Aunt Qin's double standards, and they couldn't help but mutter in disbelief.","\"If it's really so sincere, why insist on the adoption procedure?\" Qin Wenqiang shrewdly pointed out. \"If you don't adopt her, does that mean you won't feel sorry for her? And she won't want to be good to you?\"","The onlookers weren't fools. Hearing this, they found it amusing. What was wrong with Third Aunt Qin, insisting on benefiting someone outside the family?","“It's not important, Auntie. Even if we aren't fated to be mother and daughter, I am willing to always show filial piety to you.” Yu Xin said, appearing utterly humiliated, as if everyone had bullied her.","Third Aunt Qin's face turned completely pale. Unable to argue with so many people, she stubbornly looked at Third Uncle Qin, as if she was determined and expected him to make a decision.","However, when Third Uncle Qin firmly said, \"My answer remains the same. You can think it through yourself,\" Third Aunt Qin was completely at a loss.","Yu Xin, understanding the situation, finally bit her lip and decisively grabbed Third Aunt Qin's hand. \"Auntie, I know you want to be good to me, but don't argue with Uncle over me. It's really unnecessary. After all, it's quite strange for someone my age to be adopted and call others 'parents.' It's fine.\"","There would always be opportunities in the future. For now, she couldn't let the relationship between the couple worsen to the point of breaking apart. Otherwise, there would truly be no chance.","Qin Han, who had been humiliated like a wet chicken earlier, felt deep pain upon hearing Yu Xin's words. He wanted to say something but saw Yu Xin give him a glance.","\"I'm really fine,\" she said, and then politely apologized to Third Uncle Qin and Qin Jiaxi for past events, leaving no flaws in her behavior.","This made many in the crowd feel that the young lady was quite pitiful. She had saved someone, yet she still had to apologize in the end. It felt rather strange.","Some even thought the Qin Family was too harsh.","After taking a deep breath, Third Aunt Qin finally coldly said, \"Anyway, you make all the decisions in this family. What am I? But she did save my life after all. We should properly compensate her.\"","Third Uncle Qin didn't object to this suggestion.","Yu Xin also breathed a sigh of relief.","But then, someone else spoke up.","Ji Fei smiled and said, \"Third Uncle, prepare more than one reward since she's saved a life twice. Who knows if there will be a third time? Consider it an advance payment.\"","Her tone was sarcastic, making everyone feel awkward.","Qin Xian chimed in, \"How could there be a third time? Don't talk nonsense.\"","\"Really? I think it's fate. After all, just after Third Uncle made it clear he wouldn't adopt Yu Xin, today there's another life-saving incident, making it hard not to adopt her. But Third Uncle still refused. Maybe later, Heaven will arrange another one. One after another, if Third Uncle continues to insist on not adopting her, wouldn't that require more rewards?\""]},{"number":379,"title":"Chapter 379: No way We can't let them off like this","paragraphs":["After Ji Fei and Qin Xian finished their amicable conversation, the room fell into an eerie silence. Third Aunt Qin, Yu Xin, and Qin Han all showed fleeting signs of panic, quickly replaced by a mix of embarrassment and fury upon being exposed.","\"What do you mean by that? Are you implying that we're acting?\" Third Aunt Qin's voice suddenly rose several decibels, completely losing the delicate demeanor she had just moments ago.","Seeing her reaction, Third Uncle Qin, who had initially been unbothered, immediately darkened his expression.","Ji Fei chuckled. \"What are you talking about, Third Aunt? I didn't mean anything by it. How could you think that? Such underhanded and shameless schemes to betray one's own family? That definitely couldn't be something you'd do. So, I said it was all just fate.\"","At this, Third Aunt Qin was nearly left gasping for breath, her mind short-circuiting from the blatant insult. Ji Fei hadn’t minced words—she was calling her outright deceitful and shameless.","The murmuring around them started to swell.","\"I think there's something to it.\"","\"Exactly, what are the odds of everything happening so coincidentally?\"","\"That platform—how exactly did someone fall off it? I don't get it.\"","\"Who knows? The purpose is so obvious, it's hard not to speculate.\"","\"I thought even a tiger wouldn't eat its own cub. But to risk her own baby for an outsider? Seeing how she treats her own daughter, I'm not so sure.\"","\"Who is this Yu Xin? Not only does Qin Han defend her, but Qin's mother is out of her mind, defending her to such an extent.\"","\"Don’t tell me she’s a love child~ but she doesn’t look like it.\"","As the speculation spiraled out of control, Third Uncle Qin had no choice but to step in and take charge.","“Enough. My wife has been standing too long and needs to rest,” he said, summoning the butler to escort her away.","Yu Xin, feeling guilty, also fled the scene, pulled away by Qin Han.","The small commotion didn't put a halt to the birthday celebration—after all, such events were rarely about the actual birthday. Music resumed, and although the guests continued to murmur, they quickly seized the opportunity to network with the powerful Qin Family.","But from Third Uncle Qin's handling of the situation, everyone could clearly see that he was now completely devoted to his daughter, Qin Jiaxi. Anyone who threatened her interests, even his own wife or son, would be cut off without hesitation. It was clear that in this branch of the Qin Family, Qin Jiaxi's position was unquestionable.","After settling everyone else, Third Uncle Qin immediately checked on Qin Jiaxi, having noticed her fall earlier.","\"Are you hurt? Does it hurt?\" he asked with genuine concern.","Qin Jiaxi smiled softly but also looked anxious. \"I'm fine, Dad... What about Mom and the others?\"","Third Uncle Qin patted Qin Jiaxi's head. \"Don't worry about them. They've completely lost their minds. If you don't want to stay at home, you can stay at the ancestral villa. You don't need to come back. We won't involve ourselves with them anymore. If they don't change, it'll just be the two of us.\"","Though he spoke lightly, Third Uncle Qin had already been harboring some thoughts, especially after following Qin Xian's leads and uncovering a few things.","He thought they might actually get a divorce.","If Yu Xin turned out to be that man's child, he could never tolerate his wife favoring another man's daughter over their own.","He needed to speed up the investigation.","Qin Jiaxi no longer worried about those people. After all, they were so desperate to replace her with someone else as their daughter and sister. If she still had any expectations, it would truly be pitiful.","Deciding this, Qin Jiaxi began considering when the party ended, she would return to her room to pack and move out.","Meanwhile, the others were busy gossiping about what had just happened, unconcerned about Third Uncle Qin being present. After all, Third Aunt Qin's actions had already severed whatever remaining ties there were between them.","\"Was it all an act?\" Qin Yi asked.","\"I saw it—she did it on purpose,\" Qin Zhao confidently claimed, as if he knew the truth.","\"That's terrifying,\" Qin Jing said.","\"Thank goodness she didn't succeed,\" Qin Xiaoyu added.","\"I’m worried, like Sister-in-law said, that there might be more to it,\" Qin Rong mused.","Everyone turned to Ji Fei. Leaning on Qin Xian, she smiled and said, \"Don’t worry. I already threw some salt on their game. If they try the same trick again, it won’t work. They’re probably raging in their room right now.\"","As she spoke, Ji Fei wanted to check on their current predicament to enjoy the spectacle.","But as soon as she did, her teacup almost slipped from her hand, only to be caught by Qin Xian.","Turning to Ji Fei, Qin Xian noticed her look of coldness.","\"What's wrong?\" Qin Xian gently stroked Ji Fei's tense face with his finger.","Ji Fei's expression was rigid. \"N-nothing... no big deal.\"","[It's fine. As long as Qin Jiaxi stays in everyone’s sight, it’s fine! Damn it! Scumbags! Both that woman and her son are disgusting! They failed the adoption plan, so now they're rushing to execute a son-in-law plan.]","The Qin family, who were chattering away, suddenly fell silent, their eyes uncontrollably drifting toward Qin Jiaxi.","What did that mean? Were they trying to force a romance between them?","No, Ji Fei wouldn’t curse like that over something so trivial.","Could it be...?","[They want to drug them and get them into bed? Are you helping a revolting man to rape his own family member? Damn it... I really want to destroy them!]","The Qin family's faces went ashen. If before it was unintentional harm, indifference, or biased favoritism, now it was outright intentional persecution!","How could they be so heartless?","Or did they think doing this to Qin Jiaxi wasn’t a big deal at all?","It was unbelievable!","Third Aunt Qin, for her old flame, had gone so far as to completely lose her mind over love. But what about Qin Han? Could he really treat his own flesh-and-blood sister this way?","Everyone who heard the news felt their hearts race. Thankfully, Ji Fei had her system, or who knows what could've happened.","[No! We can't let them off the hook like this!]","The Qin family felt the same. But how should they act?","Ji Fei's eyes darted, and she quickly came up with a plan. She turned to Qin Jiaxi beside her. \"Jiaxi, it seems my dress is a bit loose. Can you take me to your room to adjust it?\"","Qin Jiaxi, who had been planning to find a chance to go upstairs and pack her things, immediately agreed and led the way.","Others wanted to follow, but it seemed too abrupt, so in the end, only Qin Xian tagged along.","They overheard Ji Fei's plan.","[While they haven't started yet, I need to record all their crimes.]","The Qin family figured out the general idea and sat back to watch the drama unfold.","Ji Fei and Qin Xian were led to Qin Jiaxi’s room on the second floor of the main building.","Ji Fei didn't want Qin Xian to see what she was up to, so she had him wait outside.","She then came up with various excuses to keep Qin Jiaxi distracted while she took out her phone, turned on the video, and placed it on the highest shelf, making sure it could capture the entire room."]},{"number":380,"title":"Chapter 380: Where are the classic lines","paragraphs":["Wait until it's all done, Qin Jiaxi came over with a pin, and Ji Fei chuckled again: \"No need, I've adjusted it myself, let's go.\"","\"Ah, then Sister-in-law and Second Brother, you two go ahead, I still need to pack up, I won't... be coming back.\"","Ji Fei immediately said: \"We'll help you pack up after the banquet, let's go, downstairs.\"","*[How can we catch the turtle in the jar without vacating the room?!]*","At that moment, Qin Han suddenly opened the door and came out. His room was a distance away from Qin Jiaxi's, but just as he stepped out, he stopped immediately.","In the corridor, Qin Xian, hearing the sound, looked over and could see a man behind Qin Han.","Qin Xian's expression grew even colder.","\"Second Brother, why are you...?\" Qin Han's face was extremely unnatural; his heart was pounding like a drum. Truthfully, doing something like this made him feel guilty and uncertain.","But Yu Xin had no chance left. Father was guarding against her so strictly that if they didn't introduce Yu Xin's brother to Jiaxi and bind them together, Yu Xin's future would be bleak. This was all Qin Jiaxi's fault. It wasn't that they weren't considering Jiaxi, but she wasn't considering them. If only she had taken a step back and let Yu Xin in, they wouldn't have had to set this plan into motion.","Moreover, today, some of the people looked at Qin Jiaxi with a calculating gaze, especially Father's few words, which made Qin Han feel his position as the heir was under threat.","All in all, Qin Jiaxi deserved it, Qin Han thought, and his expression calmed down.","Qin Xian silently observed the changes in Qin Han's expression, already sentencing him in his heart.","“Waiting for my wife,” Qin Xian replied lazily.","\"Ah? Sister-in-law is in Jiaxi's room?\" Qin Han was momentarily unsure of how to handle this situation.","Then, the next second, the door opened, and Ji Fei and Qin Jiaxi came out.","Qin Han's expression changed, \"Why did you come up?\" This was directed at Qin Jiaxi.","Qin Jiaxi coldly said, \"Sister-in-law wanted to see my room, that's all. We're leaving now.\"","She no longer bothered to adjust her words based on Qin Han's expression. After saying that, she led Ji Fei and Qin Xian downstairs.","As they passed by, Ji Fei gave Qin Han a smirk.","Qin Han looked puzzled but also felt relieved. Fortunately, he wasn't caught red-handed.","After the three of them were completely gone, Qin Han waved his hand behind him.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei was inwardly shouting in excitement.","*[Go ahead and perform your little act. Show your true ugliness, let's see how you manage to turn this around!*","Once they were out, the atmosphere at the banquet had returned to normal.","Just as the three were about to return to their seats, they were stopped by someone.","It was Su Ze.","Indeed, there were Su family members present today, but Su Ze's branch hadn't received any invitation.","Who would have thought they'd have the nerve to show up uninvited?","\"You don't have an invitation, please leave,\" Qin Jiaxi had already started to be more assertive.","Su Ze hadn't expected to be met with such an expression from Qin Jiaxi right away. He had assumed that Qin Jiaxi would be heartbroken over him and eventually come crawling back, begging for him to take her back. After all, Qin Jiaxi had once said he was her salvation.","But even up until today, there had been no sign of any reconciliation.","It was only when Su Ze's father had rushed to bring him here.","In reality, they had arrived early and only came out after the adoption matter was settled.","\"Jiaxi, I need to talk to you alone,\" Su Ze felt he had to win Qin Jiaxi back, but he didn't want to lose face in front of others.","\"Say it now, or leave,\" Qin Jiaxi even showed a hint of impatience.","Su Ze was stunned; he knew he couldn't control the situation anymore. Finally, he had to lower his head, \"Jiaxi, I was wrong, I was always wrong. I actually like you, wholeheartedly. It's just... I was misled, until you ignored me, I realized my mind is full of you, I...\"","\"Ugh~\"","Ji Fei let out a perfectly timed, very disruptive sound of disgust, then cooed to her husband, \"Honey, I'm feeling nauseous from this.\"","Qin Xian patted Ji Fei's back, saying, \"Their little drama isn't over yet.\"","And not far away, some people had already noticed the scene and were secretly enjoying the spectacle, expecting a potential \"chase love to the grave\" or \"prodigal son returns\" plot. Only to be interrupted.","Everyone: Are you two considerate? Can't you just silently enjoy the gossip?","The next second, Qin Jiaxi said, \"Your words were so fake that even my sister-in-law felt sick. You better stop now.\"","Everyone: ......","Su Ze, on the other hand, was livid, his composure nearly cracking.","\"I'm curious, if Yu Xin had been successfully adopted, would you still have popped out now?\" Ji Fei continued stirring the pot.","Su Ze immediately froze, staring at Ji Fei in disbelief.","*[Hah, kid, you still think you can fool someone? You and your parents arrived early but didn't approach Jiaxi, didn't you just want to weigh your options? It turned out that Yu Xin had no chance and was out of the game. You realized that if you didn't secure Jiaxi, you wouldn't be able to regain control of the Su family. These days, the embarrassment of losing your crown as Su family heir had made Su Ze suffer enough, unwilling to sacrifice anything for love anymore. That's why you're here pleading again. How laughable! Thinking Jiaxi is just some vegetable you can pick and choose. What a fantasy!]*","Su Ze naturally wouldn't admit it, quickly saying, \"This has nothing to do with whether Yu Xin was adopted or not. I'm here for Jiaxi. I love Jiaxi and want to be with her forever.\"","Qin Jiaxi frowned slightly and looked at Su Ze, bluntly saying, \"If you say more, I might vomit too.\"","\"You don't believe me? Fine, I deserve it. All I'm asking is for one more chance, I'll prove it to you.\" Su Ze appeared desperately in love.","\"No,\" Qin Jiaxi directly said, \"Please leave.\"","Su Ze had probably never seen Qin Jiaxi so unresponsive, staring blankly for a moment before saying, \"Back then, it was you who first fell for me, you made the first move. You can't provoke me and then just abandon me.\"","*[Wow, classic lines indeed! Looks like Su Ze took some time to study his lines meticulously to win Jiaxi back. Too bad, it's useless.]*","Indeed, it was useless. Because Qin Jiaxi was confused. \"When did I first fall for you? What are you talking about? You were the one who suddenly confessed.\"","Why was he insisting it was her first attraction? Obviously not!","Before getting to know Su Ze well, she had already been in a state of self-isolation. Facing someone popular like him, she always kept her distance. Even though she did know of his existence early on, given the family connection.","Then, one day, Su Ze confessed to her. Acting like everyone was in love with her, he deceived her.","Because back then, she desperately needed someone's love to rescue her shattered life. So, she was quickly drawn in.","But who was he to claim she first liked him? What grounds did he have?*"]},{"number":381,"title":"Chapter 381: Can't Be Beaten When One Is Despicably Low","paragraphs":["By the way, Qin Xian also handed over his phone.","\"How can you deny it? It was you... you were the one who first liked me,\" Su Ze suddenly exclaimed anxiously.","[There's something fishy here, let me investigate...]","Qin Jiaxi had already felt something strange due to some of Su Ze's statements before, but at the time, she didn't say much. After all, it was over, and arguing about who fell in love first was meaningless. Throughout the whole ordeal, only she had foolishly fallen in love. Now, she also felt that it wasn't worth pursuing, really not wanting to get entangled.","As a result, Su Ze's parents finally couldn't hold back and came forward, earnestly exhorting Qin Jiaxi.","\"Jiaxi, we've always been in favor of you two. My son was just bewitched by that woman, Yu Xin, really.\"","\"Su Ze has seen through Yu Xin's true colors and promised not to interact with her anymore, you can rest assured. Under any circumstances, that unscrupulous woman will never set foot in our home,\"","As they were speaking, it suddenly became very quiet in one spot. Everyone's gaze was drawn there, and sure enough, Third Aunt Qin had just arrived with Yu Xin.","Yu Xin's face looked terrible at the moment.","And Third Aunt Qin was somewhat displeased. She wasn't sure about the truth of Yu Xin and Su Ze's situation, as Yu Xin had always kept them in the dark. Hearing the Su family speak so disparagingly of Yu Xin made her furious. Originally, she had even planned to marry Yu Xin to Su Ze.","Su Ze also saw Yu Xin and immediately became flustered, not daring to meet her gaze.","Yu Xin's eyes flashed with resentment.","Others were also drawn over. When Qin Second's family arrived, they were watching the drama in confusion. Fortunately, Ji Fei provided an explanation in the next moment.","[So that's how it is. Indeed, people are capable of incredible shamelessness. It turns out that Su Ze and Yu Xin were already together in high school, but they were secretly separated by Su Ze's parents. Back then, the two were truly sincere, even contemplating running away together.]","Qin Second's family was stunned. Could it be true? They didn't run away after all?","[However, by that time, the Su family had already planned for their son to pursue Qin Jiaxi. The two had met at various gatherings twice, according to Qin Jiaxi's memories, they weren't really acquainted, only knowing of each other's existence. Yet, Su Ze, due to his parents constantly mentioning her, grew resentful. From 'I don't like her, I won't be with her' to 'Even if she likes me, I only want Yu Xin,' and finally to 'Let Qin Jiaxi give up on this foolish hope, I will never love her.' In this process, Qin Jiaxi was completely unfamiliar with him, not even meeting him, but he, relying on his extreme self-confidence and arrogance, defined her, believing she wanted to break up his relationship with Yu Xin to be with him, resorting to any underhanded means.]","Not only the others, even Qin Xian was astonished by Su Ze's thought process.","Yet, it felt familiar, as if many scumbags were like this, believing their own delusions and one-sidedly tormenting women.","So, this was what Su Ze meant by \"it was you who first fell in love\"?","It seemed they had seen the truth.","[Huh? So, he thinks their runaway plan failed because of Jiaxi. That night, Su Ze and Yu Xin planned to escape, and they happened to encounter Qin Jiaxi. He believed it was because Qin Jiaxi informed his family, who came to capture him, aiming to get him through nefarious means. But in reality, Qin Jiaxi had no recollection of that night, merely passing by without a glance. It was their family's housekeeper who noticed him running away, leading to the pursuit.]","Qin Second's family was ready to curse upon hearing this.","So, it was this shameless guy, Su Ze, who assumed Qin Jiaxi liked him because of a chance encounter, deciding she was obstructing his path to love.","Everyone suddenly understood the drama at school. Back then, they wondered why Su Ze was so cruel, targeting an innocent girl for love. They couldn't understand his deep resentment towards Qin Jiaxi.","Now they got it. He treated Qin Jiaxi as his enemy!","After meeting Yu Xin again in university, he used Qin Jiaxi while completing his revenge.","[So, at first, he didn't know Yu Xin might become a foster child of the Qin family. He thought of genuinely marrying Qin Jiaxi and keeping Yu Xin on the side. Because he knew his family would oppose it to the end, he could never marry Yu Xin. Thus, he planned to marry Qin Jiaxi and torment her forever, as punishment for not being able to be with his true love.]","Ji Fei fell silent, feeling too drained to mock the disgusting, filthy thoughts of some people.","Qin Second's family burst out laughing on the spot, infuriated.","\"What are you doing?\" Third Uncle Qin finally arrived. He hadn't expected that, just a moment of inattention, and these flies were swarming around his daughter again. \"I've said, don't you dare come near my daughter again.\"","\"Uncle, I am sincere, I...\" Su Ze tried to salvage the situation.","Su Ze's parents also chimed in, while other Su family members attending the event hesitated to publicly disown their relative, deciding to see how the Qin family reacted first.","\"I don't care if you're sincere or not. I won't tolerate someone who has harmed my daughter from harassing her again. Leave now, or don't blame me for being merciless,\" Third Uncle Qin declared firmly, protecting his daughter.","Su Ze's parents panicked and hurriedly pulled on Su Ze, indicating he should kneel.","Even if Su Ze was pragmatic, he couldn't cross the line of his dignity. He stood there stiffly, stubbornly staring at Qin Jiaxi: \"You've liked me for so long. I don't believe you can just let go like that. Step back, give each other a chance, and you might actually have me.\"","\"Having you, this cheating, cold-hearted scumbag, is such a great thing?\" Qin Zhao couldn't help but shout in exasperation: \"Our sister is so well-off, there's plenty of choices. Why would she choose you? We don't have a masochistic gene in our family.\"","Su Ze clenched his teeth in anger, still staring at Qin Jiaxi, hoping she would obediently comply as she used to.","But there was no miracle this time.","\"Having liked you is the biggest regret of my life, a stain on my past,\" Qin Jiaxi declared directly.","Su Ze seemed to lose all strength, staring blankly at the girl who had once been so humble before him, now capable of insulting him.","Su Ze's parents also looked terrible. Finally, at Third Uncle Qin's prompting, they hurriedly pulled Su Ze away in disgrace, afraid of being thrown out by the housekeeper.","Just as they reached the front gate, Su Ze's parents left him behind, slapping him hard twice.","\"You still say you've always had control over Qin Jiaxi, that she's desperate for you?\"","\"You idiot, even if you had taken her sooner and made her pregnant, she wouldn't have left so easily! But you, for another woman, kept yourself pure? Are you sick!\"","\"Is this what you wanted? For the sake of 'true love,' you're really my son, losing the opportunity for the family head's position.\"","\"You're going to ruin our family!\"","After speaking, Su Ze's parents left, deeply disappointed.","Su Ze, who had never experienced such prolonged disapproval and criticism, felt like he was going crazy.","Yes, why didn't he take Qin Jiaxi to bed for Yu Xin's sake back then? If he had slept with her, she would be his woman, definitely more obedient."]},{"number":382,"title":"Chapter 382: They Hugged Each Other","paragraphs":["This side farce ended, the Su Family hurriedly came forward to apologize.","Third Uncle Qin was heartbroken for his daughter, who had been through wave after wave of trouble, so he said, \"If you're tired, let someone else take you back to the old estate. You don't have to stay here the whole time.\"","Qin Jiaxi actually wanted to leave, especially since her mother and Yu Xin were here now. She felt uncomfortable just breathing the same air as those people.","However, she didn’t notice that Third Aunt Qin and Yu Xin were glaring at her like a lamb waiting to be slaughtered.","At this moment, Qin Han appeared and went straight to his mother’s side, whispering something.","Ji Fei raised an eyebrow and knew it was about to begin.","Qin Jiaxi was about to come over and tell everyone she was leaving when she heard Third Aunt Qin calling her.","Qin Jiaxi really didn’t want to go, but she was still technically her mother, so she couldn’t just ignore her.","\"Why are you calling her?\" Third Uncle Qin, now on high alert, directly intercepted.","Third Aunt Qin’s face turned sour. \"It's been so long since I saw my daughter. Can’t I talk to her?\"","\"Ha.\" Third Uncle Qin almost scoffed out loud.","Of course, Third Aunt Qin understood what he meant and awkwardly added, \"I just wanted to ask if she’s staying here tonight.\"","\"No, she’s going back to the old estate,\" Third Uncle Qin replied firmly.","\"Should she take some clothes with her?\" Third Aunt Qin asked casually, trying to sound nonchalant.","Such ordinary dialogue would have gone unnoticed if Ji Fei and the others hadn’t already gotten wind of the scheme.","Third Uncle Qin glanced at Qin Jiaxi, who said, \"I’ll go up and pack in a bit.\"","Third Aunt Qin and the others visibly relaxed.","Qin Han suddenly chimed in, \"Someone’s tired and sleeping in a nearby room. Be quiet when you go up, don’t disturb them.\"","Qin Jiaxi nonchalantly hummed in acknowledgment.","And with that, the conversation came to an end.","[Ohhh, they’re worried we’ll all go together and mess up their plan! They’ve talked so much, it’s time to spring the trap. We’ll definitely go together later and scare the pants off them!]","After that, Qin Jiaxi indeed came to tell everyone she was leaving soon.","Everyone agreed, and Qin Jiaxi was about to go upstairs alone to pack her luggage.","Qin Han quickly sent a secret text.","But when he turned around, he saw a group of people ready to follow Qin Jiaxi, and he got anxious, trying to find an excuse to stop them.","Before he could say much, a man’s shrill scream echoed through the air.","Everyone was startled.","The butler immediately led a group of people rushing up, with Third Uncle Qin right behind them.","[Holy crap, there's a drama! Quick, quick!]","Ji Fei’s thoughts exploded, and she dragged Qin Xian into a mad dash.","The Second Uncle Qin's family certainly wouldn’t miss out on the fresh gossip, even though they didn’t know what was going on. But any drama that could make the gossip queen dash like this had to be explosive.","With a group running like crazy, everyone became curious, and almost all the Qin family members followed, with the boldest ones dashing into the main building. The kids, being mischievous, also snuck around, eager to join the fun.","Meanwhile, Third Aunt Qin and the other two were confused. What was going on? Why was there a man’s voice?","When Ji Fei and the others reached the second floor, they saw the butler had already busted open a door.","It was Qin Jiaxi’s room.","Third Uncle Qin spotted it and was instantly shocked.","Rushing over, his blood pressure shot up as he saw his daughter’s bed occupied by two entangled men.","Screams, gasps, and scuffling noises filled the air.","A fat man, red-faced, was pinning Su Ze down with a similarly flushed expression. Both were disheveled, glaring fiercely at each other, their bodies twisted in an unnatural, bizarre manner.","Clearly, something wasn’t right.","And it was all happening in his daughter’s room.","Third Uncle Qin immediately ordered water to be thrown on them.","Ji Fei and Qin Xian arrived just in time to witness the lively scene. The fat man tried to kiss Su Ze, who desperately resisted but couldn’t help leaning closer to the man.","But soon, Ji Fei’s eyes were covered by Qin Xian. \"Don’t look, it’s gross.\"","\"Oh, I didn’t even get a proper look. Did they... really go all the way?\" Ji Fei’s tone was full of disappointment.","Qin Xian: \"Probably not...\"","\"Ah?\" Ji Fei sounded genuinely regretful.","At the same time, some kids who saw the scene ran downstairs, excitedly telling their parents.","\"A man was kissing the Su family brother!\"","\"They were hugging!\"","\"Shameful, shameful!\"","Those who didn’t witness the scene initially thought it was some kind of accident. Upon hearing this, everyone’s hair stood on end, turning to look at the Su Family members who were still there.","The Su Family’s faces were pale, but even more so were the trio of Third Aunt Qin, Qin Han, and Yu Xin. They had no idea how this could happen.","Before the Su Family could rush up, the household staff had already dragged the two men out like dead dogs from the main building.","The Su Family tried to intervene, but Third Uncle Qin’s dark expression hinted at a full interrogation.","They had already heard it was Qin Jiaxi’s room.","Just moments ago, their Su Ze was rejected, yet here he was, in Qin Jiaxi’s room, entangled with another man. And clearly, both seemed drugged. They knew it couldn’t be Third Uncle Qin’s revenge, since he wouldn’t tarnish his daughter’s room like that. As for other possibilities... they didn’t dare to think further.","Looking at the dragged-out fat man, Third Aunt Qin’s face turned ashen, and she could only clutch her son’s and Yu Xin’s hands tightly.","\"What... what do we do?\"","Qin Han was frustrated. \"How would I know! Why was Su Ze even here!\"","Yu Xin glared sinisterly at Su Ze. She could guess that Su Ze had wanted to take things into his own hands and claim Qin Jiaxi. He must have thought that by doing so, he could win her back.","Men were indeed liars, she thought. What’s with the \"I’ll never touch Qin Jiaxi\" nonsense—it was all fake.","After the cold water dousing, both men regained their senses. The fat man’s face was pale, while Su Ze’s eyes burned with a murderous fury as he glared at the other man. \"What are you doing in Qin Jiaxi’s room? What did you do to me? Who the hell are you!\"","\"I... I should be asking you! Why are you in this room? I... I’m Qin Jiaxi’s future husband,\" the fat man stammered.","Before he could finish, his collar was grabbed. \"What did you say?!\"","The fat man turned and found himself staring into Third Uncle Qin’s eyes, which were filled with a murderous intent. He immediately shrank back. \"It... it was Auntie Li who said I could marry Qin Jiaxi in the future. I just wanted to get to know my future wife early!\"","The Auntie Li he mentioned was none other than Third Aunt Qin, Li Zixuan.","Third Uncle Qin’s eyes nearly popped out of his head. He dropped the fat man and turned to Third Aunt Qin with a demonic glare. \"Is this man yours?\"","\"Yes, she even tried matchmaker at our faces just now!\" Qin Zhao sneered. \"But wasn’t she rejected? So why did this guy sneak into her room? Oh, and wasn’t Su Ze rejected too? Were you discussing tactics in the room together?\"","\"Explain!\" Third Uncle Qin lost control, roaring in anger. He couldn’t even begin to fathom what was happening.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei had already retrieved her phone and happily saved the video, preparing to upload it to the birthday party’s big screen."]},{"number":383,"title":"Chapter 383: A Feeling That Even the Word \"Vicious\" Cannot Describe","paragraphs":["The projection screen for the birthday celebration was located in the garden, where earlier images of Third Aunt Qin had been playing.","Now, since everyone was engrossed in the drama unfolding, no one noticed that the screen had gone dark.","Qin Xian was accompanying Ji Fei by the computer, tinkering with it and even handing over his own phone.","Ji Fei's eyes immediately lit up with excitement.","Meanwhile, other members of the Qin Family were gathered around Qin Jiaxi.","Qin Jiaxi was in a state of complete shock, dumbfoundedly staring at the two men before her, then mechanically turning her head to look at her mother and brother.","Despite Third Uncle Qin’s rage, her mother and brother still attempted to justify their actions.","“It must have been... a mistake,” Third Aunt Qin recovered and quickly recalled the prepared excuse. “He’s indeed a young acquaintance of mine, and I asked him to rest upstairs.”","Qin Han, visibly nervous, nodded in agreement. “That’s right. As for what happened afterward, we had no idea.”","After saying this, Qin Han sent a harsh glare to the overweight man, signaling him.","“Who is he? Why did you introduce him to Jiaxi? What are you scheming?” Third Uncle Qin demanded.","Third Aunt Qin immediately retorted with false confidence, “What could I possibly be scheming? Do you think I’d harm my own daughter? I merely wanted her to make more friends.”","“Then how did they end up drugged and in Jiaxi’s room?! What were they trying to do?!” Third Uncle Qin roared.","Both Third Aunt Qin and Qin Han were now drenched in sweat.","Su Ze quickly interjected, “Uncle, this has nothing to do with me. I had intended to talk privately with Jiaxi, but I found a man hiding in the room. As soon as I entered, something sprayed water into my face, and then my body became weak and uncontrollable. This must be a conspiracy.”","Even though it was clear the overweight man might be connected to Qin Han, given their brotherhood, in times of crisis, each looks out for themselves.","“You’re no better,” Third Uncle Qin snapped, refusing to listen to Su Ze’s excuses. “Sneaking into my daughter’s room, do you really think you’re in the clear?”","However, Third Uncle Qin knew that the primary issue was this mysterious overweight man—no, not mysterious, clearly someone his wife had brought in, likely intended for his daughter...","Third Uncle Qin’s eyes grew increasingly red with anger. He stepped forward and kicked the overweight man to the ground, yelling, “Speak! Who put you up to this?!”","“I... I... I didn’t do anything! It wasn’t me! I...” The overweight man was already cowering, but with Qin Han signaling him, he dared not reveal anything.","At this moment, Qin Han stepped forward and proposed, “Dad, since this concern’s Xiao Mei’s (Little Sister's) honor, let me handle it. We have many guests here right now.”","Third Aunt Qin quickly chimed in, “Yes, I’ll talk to his parents. You shouldn’t get involved in this.”","Suddenly, the microphone emitted a piercing screech that reverberated throughout the venue.","“Testing, testing. Hey, you two over there, mother and son, stop acting like you care so much about Jiaxi.”","Everyone turned to see Qin Xian and Ji Fei standing by the large screen, smiling and speaking into the microphone.","“You... This is our family’s internal affair. Please don’t interfere,” Qin Han immediately shouted.","“Oh, is that so?” Ji Fei replied with a smirk. “But I accidentally left my phone in Jiaxi’s room earlier, and even more accidentally, I had started recording before leaving.”","The crowd: ...Accidentally?","Regardless, it seemed they were about to witness a juicy revelation.","As the video started to play, Qin Han's face turned as pale as a ghost. He attempted to rush over but was kicked back by Third Uncle Qin.","Third Uncle Qin’s gaze was ice-cold as he stared down at the disheveled Qin Han, hoping that things weren't as bad as he feared.","But his hopes were dashed. As Qin Han struggled to his feet, his voice echoed from the speakers:","“Stay hidden under the bed. Wait for my sister to arrive. Once she enters, the trap will trigger, spraying the drug above, affecting both of you. Seize the opportunity, and you’ll become the son-in-law of the Qin Family.”","Everyone was utterly shocked, staring in disbelief at this daylight act of depravity.","A brother, bringing a stranger into his own sister’s room, hiding him under the bed, and setting up a trap himself.","This shattered Qin Han’s image as a noble gentleman, exposing the sordid and repugnant truth beneath.","“Good heavens, how could there be such a brother?”","“Even if you don’t like your sister, you can’t drug and force her like this!”","“What kind of hatred is this? They’re not siblings; they’re enemies!”","“I used to wonder if the rumors in college were a misunderstanding, but now I have no doubts. It’s a heartless, treacherous brother!”","“Forget about being a brother; he’s not even fit to be called human.”","Third Uncle Qin and Qin Jiaxi were both pale, staring in horror at the scenes unfolding, witnessing Qin Han’s ruthless actions without a trace of conscience.","By this point, Qin Han had completely panicked and stopped struggling. He knew it was all over, and his life would forever be tainted.","It was only now that he seemed to regret, how could he have listened to his mother and Yu Xin, taking such a risky step? He felt his mind was clouded and unclear.","Third Aunt Qin’s lips turned bloodless, trembling faintly. Beside her, Yu Xin’s voice broke the silence, “Auntie, what do we do?”","Third Aunt Qin tried to remain composed, thinking of ways to salvage the situation.","But the video continued to play.","The overweight man, finally overcome by fear, stammered, “Is this really going to be okay? Once the drug wears off, won’t your sister be suicidal? Your dad won’t let it go easily. Is my safety guaranteed?”","“Don’t worry,” Qin Han reassured coldly. “The rest will be handled by my mother. When she came up with this plan, she already had it figured out. The drug can't be detected after it wears off. Then you can claim you were both drunk. As long as you insist Jiaxi was willing, it’ll be fine. It’s a scandal, so if it gets out, it won’t be good for my sister. Dad won’t be so unreasonable, and Mom can feign worry and suffering, maybe even fake a stomachache. Dad definitely won’t push for an investigation, and Jiaxi won’t dare risk being blamed for causing Mom’s potential miscarriage. In the end, Mom can cry a bit, and you might even end up marrying my sister.”","“Will she agree? She didn’t seem willing today,” the overweight man questioned.","“Hmph, unwilling or not, she won’t have a choice. Then Mom can cry to the ladies in the social circle, letting everyone know my sister was 'with' you. Who would dare marry her for political alliance after that? Once you’re married, strictly control her. Don’t let her constantly oppose me and Yu Xin.” Qin Han spoke cruelly.","At this moment, the entire venue was so quiet that a pin drop could be heard, utterly silent.","Everyone stared at Third Aunt Qin, their minds filled with a single thought: The mother was actually involved in this too. The brother was disgusting enough, but the woman who had carried and given birth to the child wanted to offer her own daughter to a strange man. What kind of mind could conceive such a thing?!","Such a woman was still part of their elite social circle? Her former close friends now wanted to distance themselves as far as possible, even impulsively wanting to delete her contact information on the spot.","It was beyond the word “cruel” to describe her actions."]},{"number":384,"title":"Chapter 384: Daddy, I'm Going to Call the Police","paragraphs":["The surrounding crowd was already buzzing with chatter, and many people had suddenly realized the truth.","They wondered how these people dared to use such a crude scheme against Qin Jiaxi, only to realize later that it was because they thought they were dealing with her own mother, so they believed they could control and manipulate her at will.","And what’s more, they could use her as a pawn to achieve their own goals! Everything was justified by her pregnancy, and all problems could be easily resolved.","It was simply outrageous!","Third Aunt Qin felt all the blood in her body rushing in the wrong direction, and pain began to radiate from her lower body, not feigned, but real. She could barely stand, and Yu Xin quickly stepped in to support her.","Third Aunt Qin’s mind was in chaos. She turned to look at her husband, wanting to shake her head in denial, but all she saw was a pair of eyes filled with a murderous intent that terrified her to her core. Her legs almost gave out.","Yu Xin, meanwhile, had already started calculating how to ensure her own safe exit from the situation.","But then, she was betrayed.","Because Qin Han mentioned her, Fatty chimed in, \"Oh, why don’t you just marry my sister instead? And in return, I’ll marry your sister, a double celebration. Your dad won’t need to adopt her anyway.\"","Yu Xin’s face paled instantly, and the surrounding crowd began to murmur loudly—it turned out they were siblings.","So the entire family had been conniving under the help of Third Aunt Qin and Qin Han to scheme against Third Uncle Qin and his daughter?!","It was utterly unbelievable. Had Third Aunt Qin and Qin Han been bewitched?","Such accusations only made Third Uncle Qin suspect deeper truths. His body was trembling uncontrollably, as he couldn’t fathom what could have happened to his daughter and what kind of destruction their family might have faced if these schemes had remained undiscovered.","The video continued, and Qin Han ignored Fatty’s taunts, making his arrangements before leaving.","Fatty, on the other hand, lay leisurely under the bed, waiting for his prey to arrive.","Ji Fei fast-forwarded the video a bit, and soon the door was quietly opened—clearly not a normal visit.","Such a blatant act of breaking in, claiming it was just to have a chat, was something no one would believe.","When Su Ze saw himself on the screen, he finally panicked. \"Enough, stop it! You’re invading my privacy!\"","\"Oh, you still know how to write the word ‘privacy’?\" someone mocked.","\"I think he’s up to no good. Who knows if he was planning the same thing as Fatty.\"","Everyone was now curious about that scream.","But the Su family members weren’t looking too good. After a moment of hesitation, they tried to stop the video and prevent the exposure of more family scandals, but it was too late.","Around the bed, water droplets began to fall.","On the screen, Su Ze wiped his face in confusion and suddenly fell onto the bed. Fatty, hidden under the bed due to the sheets, couldn’t see who was there at first but received a text message. Hearing the noise, he eagerly crawled out, only to find a man lying there. He was momentarily stunned, but soon he, too, collapsed onto Su Ze, the effects of the drug taking hold. The two men struggled, trying to resist each other, but couldn’t help but embrace each other in a bizarre, grotesque scene that made many in the audience cover their eyes.","\"Stop it, stop it, ahh!\" Su Ze screamed frantically, but he was held down by the servants and couldn’t escape.","Suddenly, a piercing scream echoed from the video. Despite not having their pants off, it was clear that Fatty, now out of control, was preparing to force himself on Su Ze.","Frightened beyond measure, Su Ze let out a scream and began to fight back violently.","Then, the crowd rushed in.","Ji Fei shut off the video with a smile, putting away her phone.","[Alright, I probably shouldn’t have shown that last part, but I was just curious, and I think everyone else was, too. And after all, Qin Jiaxi has been bullied enough, and these people were even planning to force themselves on her. A little public humiliation is the least they deserve.]","Su Ze looked like a man devoid of all color, desperate to vanish on the spot.","Some laughed at the spectacle, while others saw nothing but pure hell unfolding.","Third Uncle Qin and Qin Jiaxi couldn’t bear to imagine what would have happened if this had actually occurred. With Qin Jiaxi’s fragile frame, she probably wouldn’t have even been able to scream or fight back.","Third Uncle Qin’s face had turned completely pale.","Fourth Uncle Qin, noticing the tension, stepped in, wary of what his brother might do in his fury. \"Third Brother, let’s call the police first and let them handle this,\" he suggested.","He was afraid that if Third Uncle Qin didn’t calm down soon, there might be serious consequences—perhaps even bloodshed.","\"No, we can’t call the police,\" Third Aunt Qin suddenly jumped in, surprising everyone.","The Su family members also stepped forward, trying to make their voices heard.","But Qin Jiaxi, her eyes red with tears, insisted, \"Dad, I want to call the police.\"","Third Uncle Qin suppressed his anger and nodded. \"Alright, we’ll call the police.\"","\"Dad, if you call the police, it’ll cause trouble for me,\" Qin Han pleaded immediately. \"Dad, I’m sorry, I really know I’m wrong.\"","Third Uncle Qin kicked him away without hesitation and dialed the police directly.","Qin Han’s face turned ashen.","Third Aunt Qin lunged at her husband, attempting to make a scene, but was caught by the wrist by Third Uncle Qin, who warned her coldly, \"We’ll settle things after I investigate. Don’t get in my way.\"","This was the first time Third Aunt Qin had seen her husband so ruthless, and she didn’t dare to struggle. She could only whimper weakly, \"Husband, don’t do this, I’m scared!\"","\"Then why don’t you think about whether your own daughter is scared or not!\" Third Uncle Qin hissed.","Fatty also panicked. \"Don’t call the police! If you insist on pressing charges, I... I’ll sue your son!\"","Qin Han stared at Fatty in disbelief. \"What?\"","Fatty quickly retorted, \"Your son slept with my sister! I haven’t even slept with your daughter yet—you’re the ones who got the better deal. If you sue me, I’ll sue Qin Han for raping my sister!\"","With that, Fatty turned to Yu Xin. \"Sister, help me, please! I can’t go to jail; Dad won’t allow it.\"","Yu Xin’s face twisted in disgust. She had just barely dealt with the nausea of her brother almost sleeping with her boyfriend, Su Ze, and now another truth was laid bare, making her unable to face Su Ze again.","\"You... you’re lying,\" she stammered.","In Yu Xin’s mind, she had to save at least one person. Qin Han was likely to be abandoned by the Qin family for his attempts to harm his own sister, but Su Ze might still have a chance. Besides, Qin Han wouldn’t want anyone to know about their relationship, so denying it was the safest option.","\"I saw it with my own eyes! Don’t deny it—my sister needs your help,\" Fatty urged desperately.","\"What?\" Su Ze’s voice suddenly rang out.","Despite the immense shock and the looming legal issues, the root of all this turmoil was his love for Yu Xin.","And now, someone had revealed that Yu Xin... had been with someone else?"]},{"number":385,"title":"Chapter 385: The Standoff in the Asura Field of Three","paragraphs":["The revelation hit Su Ze like a bombshell, the humiliation of being cuckolded consuming his mind in an instant. He grabbed Yu Xin, \"What do you mean by this? You betrayed me! Weren't you just his foster sister?!\"","At this moment, Qin Han seemed to finally catch on, his head buzzing. Earlier, he had already resigned himself to the situation, no matter how recklessly Fatty acted or how his relationship with Yu Xin was exposed. After all, Yu Xin was no longer his foster sister, so it shouldn't matter much, right? The real problem now was that his father was planning to report him to the police.","But seeing Su Ze confront Yu Xin, he was shocked.","What did this mean?","Wasn't she the delicate flower he had raised since childhood?","When did she start getting involved with his best friend? When did she truly steal his sister's boyfriend?","Yu Xin wasn't supposed to be wholeheartedly devoted to him, was she?","He had been making plans for her, paving the way for her brother, scheming against his father and sister.","\"What the hell is going on here? What's the deal between the two of you?!\"","In a flash, it became a confrontation among the three.","Yu Xin was filled with panic. The fact that she was dating two men at once couldn't be exposed under any circumstances, she had to find a way out.","But reality struck her cruelly again.","It was that damn microphone again.","\"Earlier, you always insisted that you were innocent, that Jiaxi was wrong about you, so we decided to investigate.\"","Ji Fei's voice rang out, clearly enjoying the drama.","Simultaneously, the large screen switched to another surveillance video.","It showed a hotel corridor, where Su Ze walked over to knock on a door. Yu Xin opened it, and the two immediately embraced and kissed right at the entrance. Eventually, Su Ze used his leg to close the door while his hand started to undress.","It was obvious what was about to happen. The footage fast-forwarded, and three hours later, Su Ze was buttoning up his shirt, escorted out by Yu Xin in a bathrobe. They lingered at the door, savoring their moment before finally parting.","Several hours later, the same day, evening, Qin Han arrived.","Yu Xin, still in her bathrobe, opened the door again. Qin Han seemed anxious, abruptly gripping the back of her head and forcefully kissing her. Instead of resisting, Yu Xin jumped up, wrapped her legs around him, and they kissed passionately as they moved into the room.","It wasn't until the next morning that Qin Han left.","The smooth movements suggested that none of this was their first time.","Yu Xin had been adept at juggling the two men.","Most people only knew she was involved with one of them.","This was the first time all the hidden truths exploded.","Yu Xin stared open-mouthed, her vision darkening.","Qin Han and Su Ze were utterly shocked.","Qin Han, while ostensibly doing what his mother said, was more so paving a path for the woman he loved, Yu Xin.","Su Ze had sided with Yu Xin against Qin Jiaxi, even considering helping her gain an identity so they could marry.","They had both given their hearts, believing Yu Xin felt the same undivided love for them. But now, they looked like fools, their green-lit heads on display for everyone to ridicule.","\"Bitch!\" Qin Han leapt forward, slapping Yu Xin across the face. \"I've ruined everything for you, made myself a laughingstock, been betrayed–are you playing me? Deceiving me? Using me?!\"","\"Yu Xin, when did you start seeing two men at once? Why did you do this to me? I loved you so much, I was ready to lose everything for you–how could you do this to me?\" Su Ze roared, \"Bitch! Bitch! Bitch!\"","The crowd moved back slightly but still encircled them, watching.","\"Never thought she had such charm, playing two rich heirs like puppets.\"","\"She’s pretty good at acting, and managing her time too.\"","\"Funny how a sister, a boyfriend, both ended up manipulating Qin Jiaxi for the sake of this woman. I wonder, if it had all worked out, would Yu Xin have kept juggling both?\"","\"Guess she'd be with her boyfriend at school and with her brother at home. Absolutely disgusting.\"","Yu Xin's face was nearly crimson with shame. Unable to bear it any longer, she exploded in fury.","\"Shut up! You think you're so great? You’re the real scum, the lowest of the low!\"","[Oh, here we go! It's the dog-eat-dog showdown! If Yu Xin has any guts, she'll spill all the dirt!]","Ji Fei said excitedly.","Meanwhile, Su Ze and Qin Han still portrayed themselves as the betrayed victims of a manipulative woman.","\"You shameless woman, how dare you curse at me?!\"","\"You have no conscience!\"","Yu Xin laughed coldly. \"Hah, I'm shameless, I have no conscience? And what about you? One claimed to love me, another acted all devoted–yet it was so easy for both of you to throw me away.\"","Yu Xin pointed at Qin Han. \"You think I don't know what you're thinking? Pretending to love me, even harming your own sister for me, always siding with me. But if you really loved me, why didn't you marry me? Forcing me to pretend to be your sister–isn't it because you think my background isn't good enough for being the Qin family's eldest son's wife? You believe your wife should be from a prestigious family, and I’m only fit to be your underground lover, sneaking around in the shadows. Making me your 'sister' was just for your own convenience; would you really allow me to marry normally? Or if I did, would you let me go? Forget about love–even if there was any affection, it always came after all your interests.\"","Upon hearing this, Qin Han was stunned, then exploded in anger.","The onlookers also felt, huh? That seems about right!","Clearly they were entangled, and for Yu Xin, Qin Han did many atrocious things, even harming his own sister horribly. If he valued her so much, why not just marry her? The Qin family wasn’t one that absolutely needed political or business alliances for marriages. If Qin Han had insisted, Yu Xin could have very possibly joined the Qin family.","And yet it never happened. Meaning Qin Han didn't want to marry Yu Xin in the first place, as she pointed out–it’s all about his interests.","Blaming her for infidelity and questioning love now seems rather ridiculous.","Qin Han, his veil of modesty torn away, roared in rage, wanting to hit someone, but Third Uncle Qin had his men restrain him.","\"And what about me! I was sincere with you, I truly planned to marry you, you knew that...\" Su Ze shouted.","Yu Xin smirked disdainfully.","Su Ze seemed to recall something and could only say, \"Now... it’s now, but back when we were together, I truly meant it! Why did you betray me, why did you cheat?!\"","\"Su Ze, stop kidding yourself. Do you really think you could act the deep lover for so long without believing it yourself? You want me to expose you right now?\" Yu Xin mocked.","\"What are you talking about?\" Su Ze was momentarily stunned."]},{"number":386,"title":"Chapter 386: It Should Be My Dad's Old Flame","paragraphs":["Yu Xin's smile seemed genuinely heart-wrenching.","\"Back then, I didn't want to be involved in the matters between the Qin Family and our family. I truly fell in love with you and wanted to elope with you, but how did you treat me?\" Yu Xin said.","Su Ze's face turned pale, but he remained stubborn. \"I was going to run away with you, you know that. It was Qin Jiaxi...\"","Qin Jiaxi, caught off guard by the sudden mention of her name, was still trying to process all the shocking revelations, her mind in a daze.","\"Spare me,\" Yu Xin cut in. \"When I met Qin Jiaxi in college, I realized she didn't know us at all. How could someone who completely ignored us back then have seen us eloping in high school and reported it to your parents? It's laughable. All that talk about Qin Jiaxi liking you first was just self-deception. You convinced yourself of a lie, even though you knew during your first interactions in college that she didn’t know you in high school. You just pretended not to know because you wanted to keep deceiving yourself!\"","\"The truth is, you deliberately led me toward Qin Jiaxi when she was passing by. She didn't even glance at us, but you told me she might have recognized us and was going to tell on us. I believed you and panicked, running away with you. But in reality, you never wanted to elope. You were too ashamed to admit you had second thoughts, so you cooked up this story to shift the blame. Before we left, you regretted your decision and tricked the housekeeper into reporting your disappearance, but when you saw no result, you concocted this whole scheme when you met Qin Jiaxi.\"","Su Ze's eyes widened in panic, wanting to interrupt.","Yu Xin, however, wasn't giving him the chance. \"From start to finish, it was me who genuinely wanted to run away with you, while you were just afraid of losing your privileged life as a young master.\"","\"No, it wasn't like that! Qin Jiaxi wanted to have me, so she purposely stopped us from eloping. It was her...\"","\"What are you talking about? I didn't even know you in high school!\" Qin Jiaxi finally cried out in surprise and anger.","Only then did she understand what Su Ze meant by claiming she had started it.","Yu Xin laughed. \"Qin Jiaxi, you don't need to argue. He won't admit what a despicable coward he is. One of the reasons he treated you so horribly in college was to cover up his own dirty deeds. By pretending you were the one who betrayed us and prevented us from being together, he justified his actions against you without any guilt.\"","Qin Jiaxi trembled, feeling a deep disgust. Unlike the hatred she felt toward her mother and brother, which was rooted in something real, this mindless malice was utterly nauseating. She had merely been in the wrong place at the wrong time, and now she was caught in this mess. It was all too revolting.","The surrounding crowd whispered among themselves, seeing Su Ze in a new light. He was even more despicable than they had imagined, utterly low and unworthy of being called a man.","\"No, what I said is the truth! I didn't wrong you; you wronged me!\" Su Ze stubbornly insisted.","But Yu Xin retorted, \"Then let me ask you this: If you really wanted to run away, why couldn't you come back a few days later or call me? You acted as if everything was decided that day, and if it failed, that was it. Don't treat me like I'm stupid. Your behavior proved you never wanted to elope with me in the first place. So what right do you have to blame me for being two-faced?\"","Su Ze crumpled, losing all his strength. His final shred of dignity had been stripped away.","His vile and ugly thoughts were now fully exposed, leaving him without any ground to argue or even question.","\"I just wanted to marry into wealth and live a comfortable life. Playing both of you was my way of ensuring the safest path, but neither of you were worth trusting. You're both worthless!\"","[Holy shit, I’m kind of impressed right now. I always thought Yu Xin was just a man-stealer, always chasing after guys. But damn... she’s not some lovesick idiot after all! This woman is ruthless. When she says she's exposing everything, she really means it. Even more thorough than my investigations!]","Qin Second and his family had similar thoughts. They felt that Yu Xin was now fearless, capable of anything. People who could throw everything away were the most terrifying.","Qin Jiaxi looked at Su Ze, feeling so disgusted that she was beyond anger—she was numb. Wasting her emotions on him was pointless.","Watching both Su Ze and Qin Han being manipulated by Yu Xin, Qin Jiaxi felt it was some kind of karmic retribution.","Third Uncle Qin patted his precious daughter's head. \"Don't dwell on it, don't let it get to you. It's all filth. Dad's got it all recorded, and I'll settle every bit of it for you.\"","Just as he finished speaking, his phone started vibrating. With one hand still holding Third Aunt Qin, he didn't intend to pick it up at first, but the persistent vibrations forced him to check.","Upon seeing the message, his fierce eyes sharpened. He quickly replied with one hand, then coldly glared at the stunned Third Aunt Qin.","The crowd was still buzzing with discussions about the messy love triangle.","Su Ze and Qin Han both gave Yu Xin fierce glares, their eyes practically saying they wouldn't let her off the hook.","But Yu Xin didn't care. With all her plans already failed, what else did she have to lose?","Not only did she have nothing to lose, but she also wanted to drag everyone else down with her. If she was going down, no one else would have it easy.","At that moment, her brother decided to kick her while she was down.","\"Yu Xin, are you out of your mind? Do you think you can just ruin everything and leave us hanging? I’m about to end up in jail because of you! Apologize right now, beg for their forgiveness, don’t drag me down with you!\"","\"Me dragging you down? You don't even have the right to say that. You've lived off me for half your life. What, now that something’s gone wrong, you can’t take any responsibility?\" Yu Xin coldly snapped back. \"You and Dad are both useless, you owe me your entire lives!\"","Hearing Yu Xin mention her father, Third Uncle Qin's grip on Third Aunt Qin tightened. Third Aunt Qin, too anxious to notice the pain, was afraid of what Yu Xin might reveal next.","\"Yu Xin, that's enough. You've said enough. Since reporting the incident has nothing to do with you, just leave,\" Third Aunt Qin said, feeling a creeping sense of danger as a woman’s intuition.","But Yu Xin smiled at Third Uncle Qin. \"Mr. Qin, I know I wronged your daughter. Here's a big secret I want to share with you as a way to make amends and ask for your forgiveness in the future.\"","Third Uncle Qin's expression changed, and his voice trembled slightly. \"Go ahead, but keep it quick.\"","Yu Xin didn't beat around the bush. \"Shut up!\" Third Aunt Qin suddenly shouted in panic.","\"If you're so scared, how could you have done it in the first place?\" Yu Xin chuckled lightly.","\"I didn't wrong you, did I?\" Third Aunt Qin asked nervously.","Yu Xin replied, \"What do you think? If not for your interference, I wouldn't have spent my childhood in an orphanage! I could have gone back home, not lived like a fake orphan! I was called a wild child with no parents. Has none of that been your fault? Mrs. Qin? Oh, I mean, my dad's old flame!\""]},{"number":387,"title":"Chapter 387: What Old Flame","paragraphs":["The crowd was still reeling from Yu Xin's recent revelation when another bombshell shook them to the core.","An old flame?","So, was Yu Xin the daughter of Third Madam Qin's old flame?","It suddenly made sense. How could a mother not love her own child unless she didn't love the child's father? Unless she loved someone else more.","So, Third Madam Qin, for the sake of her old flame's children, not only took in his daughter but also planned to marry her own daughter off to his son. No matter how despicable the latter's character was, Third Madam Qin saw him as perfect. Even if it meant ruining her own children, she would go to any lengths to support her old flame's family.","It was a complete betrayal, literally bending the elbow outward, and draining the Qin Family's resources to sustain her old flame's family.","Every eye in the room was like a sharpened blade, slicing mercilessly at Third Aunt Qin.","Third Aunt Qin's mind was blank, her lips trembling as she tried to deny it. But then a roar broke the silence: \"What old flame!\"","The one shouting wasn't Third Uncle Qin; he merely stood there, glaring at her with a chilling expression.","It was Qin Han who erupted, his face contorted with fury as he stared at his mother.","Seeing Yu Xin smirk contemptuously, she said, \"Idiot, do you really think we became friends just by chance? Your mother needed a cover, that's all. Everything she's done has been to maintain her connection with her old flame. You too are just a tool. Otherwise, why would she prefer me, an outsider, over her own daughter? You're the only fool who fell for her deception.\"","After hearing this, Qin Han's face went slack, his entire body seemingly drained of strength.","What had the two most important women in his life done to him?","Third Aunt Qin was already in tears, looking utterly wretched, but no one felt any sympathy for her now.","Yu Xin continued her verbal assault, disdainfully looking at Third Aunt Qin. \"You’re the one without shame, constantly seeking me out, insisting on raising the child of your old flame under the guise of charity. You kept funding me, knowing full well where that money would end up. You used me as a bridge to funnel money to your old flame. It's because of you that my father never came to take me away. He and my brother enjoyed normal lives back home, while I was left lonely and isolated in an orphanage. I could have had a normal life, not having to play games between two men. Do you really think I should be grateful to you?\"","At this point, Yu Xin’s cruel smile turned towards Third Uncle Qin. \"In fact, those two lifesaving acts? They were staged by her and her son to pave the way for you to adopt me. All fake.\"","Another truth was revealed, triggering another wave of gasps in the room.","Yu Xin had completely stripped Third Aunt Qin and Qin Han of their dignity, crushing it underfoot.","Third Uncle Qin chuckled coldly, \"Li Zixuan, you’ve done well. Very well. I’ve always thought I’ve done nothing to wrong you, but you’ve turned out to be so heartless.\"","Knowing there was no hope for rebuttal, Third Aunt Qin pathetically pleaded with Third Uncle Qin, \"Husband, my stomach hurts. It’s really painful. Just look at me, at this age, I’m still carrying your child. Please, don't treat me this way. You can't just... because I cared a bit more for the children of someone else.\"","\"Hahaha, Auntie, you really have no shame. You're using the child you had with my father to threaten Mr. Qin? You’ve got some nerve.\"","Yu Xin's words shattered Third Aunt Qin, who shrieked, \"You're lying! How can you slander me like this? I treated you so well, and you’re nothing but an ungrateful wretch.\"","Third Aunt Qin’s actions had always been secretive, even from Yu Xin, so she didn’t think Yu Xin could know, assuming she was just making false accusations. If she stayed resolute, the other party wouldn't dare to sling mud!","\"Hmph, did you think you were hiding it well? My father came here half a year ago and has been secretly meeting with you. You gifted him a house where I installed surveillance. I saw you two, old as you are, entangled on the living room sofa. It was disgusting. That time, you forgot yourself and told my father you were carrying his child. But since Mr. Qin was away on a business trip,you needed to get him back as soon as possible to register the child. Then, when I became your adopted daughter and my brother became your son-in-law, and with a younger brother to inherit everything, the Qin Family would all be yours. Then you could be together forever, without being torn apart.\"","Yu Xin spilled all the secrets, turning to Mr. Qin. \"These secrets should be enough to protect me, right? If you need evidence, I've got video backups.\"","\"No, no, husband, don't listen to this wicked woman. I didn't...\" Third Aunt Qin was utterly panicked, frantically trying to explain.","The surrounding people looked at Third Aunt Qin with pure contempt. Never had they imagined that someone could be so shameless. It was fortunate that she was exposed; otherwise, the Qin father and daughter would have been pure victims, schemed against from start to finish.","The Li Family, which Third Aunt Qin belonged to, had moved overseas years ago. The distant relatives attending this birthday party were too scared to step forward and secretly contacted the Li Family to inform them of the situation.","Qin Jiaxi, unable to withstand it any longer, collapsed and leaned on Qin Rong. Although she had long told herself not to care about this mother, the revelations kept getting more explosive. The shock she experienced today was enough to make her question life itself.","Other members of the Qin Family were understandably furious, realizing how badly their Third Uncle had been deceived.","Qin Wenqiang, who had nearly been fooled in a similar manner, was especially angry and stepped forward to scold her furiously.","Ji Fei and Qin Xian were purely enjoying the spectacle, as Yu Xin was fully unleashed, leaving no room for them to intervene.","\"Yu Xin is really fierce, even fiercer than my system. Looks like she's been harboring resentment since childhood. Although her life seemed provided with basic necessities, she was repeatedly abandoned, used, and placed second. No wonder she's so twisted. In her eyes, maybe neither family nor love can be trusted.\"","As she watched those people cry and beg, Yu Xin's eyes were filled with satisfaction, tinged with a hint of confusion.","Ji Fei turned to look at Third Uncle Qin and the others, her heart filled with a deep sense of regret.","\"Perhaps in the world of the wealthy, the Qin Family is truly an exception, with everyone being kind-hearted, never using their power to oppress others. Their excellent upbringing actually gave others the impression that they’re easy to deceive and manipulate. Some evil people are opportunistic bullies. They think that even if they offend the Qin Family, the worst they’ll face is discomfort, not death. So they dare to scheme against them. After all, just one successful gamble, and they can have whatever they want.\"","Hearing this inside thought, Qin Second’s family felt a bit awkward.","Meanwhile, Third Aunt Qin suddenly snapped, turning to Third Uncle Qin and declaring, \"If you don't believe me, then I might as well die together with this child.\"","With that, she made as if to jump into the nearby pool.","She was completely out of her mind. First a dramatic cry, then a temper tantrum, and now attempting suicide?","However, Third Uncle Qin had already completely disengaged, not paying her any attention. It was a guest who, fearing a fatality, instinctively stepped forward to stop her.","Third Aunt Qin suddenly stopped, collapsing in despair, wailing, \"If you don't believe me, what's the use of this child? I...\"","\"Is that so? Shouldn't you ask who the child's father is?\" Third Uncle Qin suddenly interjected."]},{"number":388,"title":"Chapter 388: Final Settlement","paragraphs":["Shortly after, two bodyguards brought in a middle-aged man from outside.","Instantly, Third Aunt Qin was dumbfounded.","\"Dad, save me!\" Fatty quickly cried out, \"Sister has gone crazy, she's revealed everything!\"","Yu Xin snorted, having no affection for this father of hers either.","Perhaps, back then, she didn't understand. She thought that her father truly loved her, taking her with him after divorcing her mother.","Only as she grew older did she gradually realize that a gambling addict like her father, taking his daughter away, could only mean trouble. He just wanted a valuable commodity in hand, in case of running out of money. His precious son, he wouldn't sell, but a daughter? That was no big deal.","It just so happened that he had reconnected with an old flame, so Yu Xin switched roles.","The man looked panicked, glancing at his detained son, then at his daughter, and finally at the deranged figure of Third Aunt Qin. His legs were already trembling.","He was too frightened to speak. He had been forcibly dragged out of his house by force, and he didn't dare confront what he considered a formidable family head-on. Let alone the fact that he had slept with the man's wife and planned to make him a cuckold.","Before Third Aunt Qin could speak again, the man, seeing Third Uncle Qin slowly approaching with a murderous aura, was completely terrified.","Without thinking, he blurted out, \"It's not my fault! Your wife was the one who couldn't stand being lonely and seduced me. I was desperate for money, and she forced me to be with her! It was all her initiative!\"","These words made Third Aunt Qin tremble all over, a chill spreading from her chest.","\"What... what did you say?\" Third Aunt Qin gazed at him like a betrayed, heartbroken woman.","The man didn't dare look at her. \"I already said no, but you kept seducing me. You didn't want a divorce, just wanted me as your lover, all in the name of the children. I told you it was immoral. I really didn't want to.\"","Naturally, few believed the man's words, as everyone knew he was shifting the blame.","But that made the situation even more ridiculous. A wealthy family's lady went to such lengths for him, yet received no genuine affection in return. One couldn't help but wonder how Third Aunt Qin felt, filled with regret.","Everyone looked at Third Aunt Qin, eager to see her reaction. However, she fainted, eyes rolling back—this time not faking it, but truly unconscious.","At the same moment, the police cars that had been called arrived.","This drama was about to pause.","Finally realizing what was happening, Qin Han, for the first time, showed no trace of his usual arrogance. He threw himself at Third Uncle Qin, tears of regret streaming down his face. \"Dad, I was wrong, I really was. I had no idea she was cheating. I was completely misled by those two women. Dad, don't let the police take me. I truly know I was wrong.\"","But Third Uncle Qin just stared at him emotionlessly.","Qin Han quickly turned to Qin Jiaxi. \"Sister, plead for me. I really know I was wrong. Remember when I used to be nice to you? I was just momentarily confused and brainwashed. We're blood relatives!\"","Qin Jiaxi closed her eyes. This was the first time she had seen her once-proud brother so humiliated. Yes, it was because Qin Han had once been a good brother to her that the following years had been so difficult. She had always held on to those memories, hoping for better days.","\"If I forgive you, it would mean I'm betraying all the suffering I endured. I can't forgive you, and I never will. Neither you nor that woman.\"","Qin Han was utterly desperate, resorting to screaming and pleading with other Qin family members, but no one sympathized with him. After all, plotting against his own sister was something the Qin family couldn't tolerate.","Qin Han was destined to be disowned by the Qin family.","Finally, Fourth Uncle Qin and Qin Xian stepped forward to help Third Uncle Qin escort the guests out. Third Uncle Qin took Qin Jiaxi and the detainees to the police station, leaving Third Aunt Qin with only distant relatives to care for her.","The departing guests whispered restrained yet excited comments. After all, such a grand spectacle of a wealthy family drama was a first for them, and they had witnessed it live. It was simply too exhilarating.","Among the guests were many with connections to the mainland. Such a big scandal was bound to spread quickly, and soon enough, the entire wealthy circle knew about it.","The mainland's wealthy families, immediately on alert, asked questions seemingly unrelated to Y City's wealthy families.","\"Um... Ji Fei, the newly appointed headmistress of the Qin family, was she also present?\"","Everyone recalled that not only was she present, but she had played a key role.","They were curious why such a question was asked.","The mainland's wealthy families merely responded: \"You're lucky. Your future won't be boring.\"","Y City's wealthy families: ?","Indeed, life wasn't boring, as the following days were filled with developments in the Qin family's affairs.","Qin Han and Fatty were imprisoned, though their sentences weren't long, they left a permanent criminal record.","Simultaneously, Third Uncle Qin announced publicly that Qin Han's inheritance rights were permanently revoked, and all property would be left to his daughter. Qin Han was no longer acknowledged as his son, and Qin Corporation would never hire him.","Su Ze received a verbal warning, but upon release, both he and his parents were promptly sent abroad by the Su family, effectively exiled to the fringes.","Yu Xin was left untouched by Third Uncle Qin; it was she who couldn't stay in school and chose to drop out, disappearing.","Third Uncle Qin filed for divorce, leaving Third Aunt Qin with nothing and demanding reimbursement for all expenses she had incurred for her old lover, along with damages.","Li Zixuan and her old lover certainly couldn't cover these debts. Ultimately, the Li Family overseas stepped in to fill the hole, promising Third Uncle Qin that they would never allow Li Zixuan or her old lover to return to Y City and that the Li Family would sever all ties with Li Zixuan.","Qin Xian told Ji Fei that the Li Family's actions were purely to avoid offending the Qin family; they certainly weren't trying to protect Li Zixuan.","So, the next day, when Ji Fei stumbled upon a new piece of gossip, she wasn't surprised.","[The Li Family personally escorted Li Zixuan and the man back to the man's city. Li Zixuan was forced to live with the man, yet still clung to her love for him? Impressive. But the man was originally a debt-evader, having squandered all the money he got from Li Zixuan. With no way to repay, the creditors came knocking...]"]},{"number":389,"title":"Chapter 389: Is it us going to meet her boyfriend who was bought with money","paragraphs":["【Li Zixuan finally discovered the truth, and combined with the hardships of her recent impoverished life, she simply couldn't adapt. She threw a tantrum with the man, ended up being pushed down, and suffered a miscarriage. Everything began to crumble. Now, Li Zixuan is desperately trying to return to her previous life with her uncle and Jiaxi, clearly wanting to go back to her past comfortable situation.】","Qin Second and his family, who had been eavesdropping, were thoroughly disgusted. Please, don't get in touch! Even knowing she won't come back, she could still ruin their mood!","Look at Jiaxi now. After a few days of sadness, she's been living quite happily.","Hahaha, it's quite ironic that before being sent away, the Li family confiscated all her electronic devices, so... she can't even remember her uncle and Jiaxi's contact information. She truly deserves it! Then, after trying to escape, she was caught by the man and taken back... forced to help repay his debts... Sigh, I can only say that karma always catches up. Leaving her life as a wealthy madame, abandoning her excellent husband and well-behaved daughter—she really brought this upon herself.","Qin Second's family was nodding in agreement internally: This ending is perfect!","Apart from Qin Second's family, who had already devoured all the gossip, others have lost interest in this matter.","Of course, Grandpa Qin, upon hearing about this, furrowed his brows so tightly it could have crushed a fly.","Within this short month, two marriages in the family have ended.","Grandpa Qin is considering whether to visit a temple to pray, even though he knows the truth protected his family. It's really been an unusual month.","He hopes that the return of his fifth and sixth sons won't bring any more trouble.","Otherwise, for the upcoming grand birthday celebration, the Qin family's numbers might be significantly reduced.","Regarding expelling Qin Han from the family, Grandpa Qin has no objections. Anyone who dares to harm a Qin family member deserves to be cast out. The Qin family must never turn against its own.","Later, Grandpa Qin not only visited a temple but also invited a master to check the family's feng shui. Ji Fei saw this and couldn't help but exclaim, \"Indeed, wealthy families still believe in this stuff.\"","That evening, Qin Xian, in a less-than-optimal mood, held Ji Fei in a passionate embrace filled with lingering kisses.","It almost escalated to a point of no return.","Ji Fei felt Qin Xian whispering in her ear, \"Feifei, I love you.\"","Ji Fei felt like she was in a steamer, her whole body heating up.","Ji Fei held Qin Xian's handsome face and kissed him fervently, watching his slightly trembling eyelashes, and asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Qin Xian complained, \"The master said that over the next two years, the Qin family's children's marriages are likely to face troubles. It's considered a big trial, which will pass once it's over. So, Grandpa suggested we postpone our wedding, fearing we might be affected.\"","Ji Fei blushed, though they hadn't explicitly discussed it, things had naturally progressed to that point.","Qin Xian suddenly looked up, kissed Ji Fei's forehead, and said seriously, \"I want to truly marry you. I had thought to wait until after Grandpa's birthday...\"","Ji Fei's heart skipped a beat at those words of \"truly marrying.\" Although Qin Xian didn't know it, for Ji Fei, that would be her real marriage.","Ji Fei couldn't help but be moved and kiss Qin Xian's lips, whispering sweet promises.","\"I don't believe in those things, so... everything is up to you!\"","After speaking, Ji Fei felt shy and quickly hid under the blanket. She didn't know when she had become so willing to completely give herself to Qin Xian.","She wondered if she was becoming a lovesick fool, as she had unwittingly placed full trust in Qin Xian.","That night, although they didn't go all the way, they still got as close as possible.","Qin Xian had a seemingly relentless desire. Even though Ji Fei showed no resistance or fear, he wanted to save their first time for their wedding night in their bridal chamber.","Even though they didn't finish, Ji Fei was so exhausted the next day that all she wanted to do was lie down.","...","That day, Ji Fei and others continued their laid-back play.","Today was rare, as Qin Fourth's twins had free time from the company and came to visit, saying they would take everyone out.","Qin Xiaoyu was especially excited, \"I noticed that Second Sister-in-law and Third Brother both play games, so how about we go see a celebrity esports match today? It's conveniently happening in Y City, and I'm a sponsor, by the way.\"","Ji Fei only plays occasionally, while Qin Zhao is more familiar with gaming.","【Oh, are we going to meet her boyfriend who she bought with money?】","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, upon hearing this, became intrigued.","Qin Xiaoyu didn't hide anything, straightforwardly stating, \"I'll also let you meet my boyfriend. If you all think he's qualified after your assessment, I'll bring him to Grandpa's birthday banquet.\"","In truth, Qin Xiaoyu was just joking; where's the need for their approval? She's quite decisive herself. She likes the man, so she doesn't care about other aspects.","This time, it's just for everyone to get acquainted with her boyfriend ahead of time. It's also been a while since she's seen him, so she really wanted to visit.","But her brother, Qin Jing, won't indulge her, directly stating, \"If I reject him, you'll break up with him?\"","Qin Xiaoyu immediately squinted and retorted, \"Then you better be careful. You've got a mysterious girlfriend who needs scrutiny too. If you don't mess with me, I'll let you off easily.\"","The siblings started bickering again.","While squabbling, everyone set off, with Qin Yi declining the noisy venue, and Qin Jiaxi having class. In the end, it was Qin Jing, Qin Xiaoyu, and Ji Fei along with a few others heading to the youth hotspot to watch an esports celebrity match.","As the major sponsor, Qin Xiaoyu was naturally escorted upon arrival, and they were led to the best VIP exclusive box.","But as soon as they entered, they heard commotion nearby.","\"Why did you let them in and not us? That box looks way better than ours. Are you secretly selling viewing spots? We are the invited guests, shouldn't we be well treated?\" A noisy woman's voice came through.","The Qin family ignored it and went straight into the box and sat down.","Ji Fei, never one to miss gossip, casually glanced over.","It was a group of people, led by a woman with a fierce, harsh face.","When the staff entered, Qin Xiaoyu inquired with authority, \"What's going on with those noisy people?\"","The staff member glanced cautiously at Qin Xiaoyu and replied, \"Miss Qin, that's Wen Bai's mother. The event organizer issued extra invitations for each team member to bring family and friends to Y City to watch the match and tour around.\"","Qin Xiaoyu was taken aback, \"Wen Bai's mother? Alright, I understand. You may leave.\"","The staff member then left.","Qin Xiaoyu felt a bit awkward. She hadn't heard Wen Bai mention bringing his mother along.","Earlier, she had completely ignored them; now, she wondered if that was a bit impolite considering their relationship."]},{"number":390,"title":"Chapter 390: You This Shameless Male Fox","paragraphs":["\"Should I go say hello? That's my boyfriend's mother,\" Qin Xiaoyu was feeling ambivalent. Just from hearing the woman's words, it was clear she was difficult to get along with, and Qin Xiaoyu felt a bit nervous.","\"Ugly brides have to meet their in-laws sooner or later, unless you don't plan to stick with him for long,\" Qin Jing commented.","Qin Zhao was curious and asked, \"What's his family background like, exactly?\"","In the past, they didn't consider family background, but after witnessing so many messy situations caused by mismatched families, they now believed matching social status was the most important factor to consider.","Qin Xiaoyu explained, \"His family is from an academic lineage, but it's kind of declined...\"","\"What? An academic family?\" Qin Rong couldn't believe it. She shot a questioning look at Qin Xiaoyu, wondering if she was joking. After all, just from that one shout from the aunt, she didn't seem like someone from an academic family.","Qin Jing chuckled and said, \"I've met that guy a few times. Though we didn't talk much, he seemed polite and had a decent impression. He's a bit servile, probably trying to please his sponsor's older brother. Other than that, no major issues. But seeing his mom today... Xiaoyu, you'd better keep your eyes open.\"","Qin Xiaoyu scratched her head and said, \"I only know that their ancestors were from an academic family. Later, their family fell on hard times, and now they're all ordinary salaried workers. He's talented at gaming and left early to compete. But his team has been performing poorly, with investors pulling out constantly...\"","\"And then you accidentally fell for him, started pouring money into the team, and became his girlfriend?\" Qin Rong was curious.","Qin Xiaoyu nodded.","\"Wait, aren't you worried he's only with you for the money?\" Qin Zhao couldn't help but ask.","Qin Jing immediately smirked, implying he had definitely brought this up with his sister before and didn't get a favorable response.","Qin Xiaoyu proudly lifted her chin. \"I don't care if Wen Bai is with me for the money. I never overthink such complicated issues. I have the money to invest in the team and let Wen Bai depend on me. That's my advantage. Some men love beautiful faces, some love cute personalities, some love money. Who's better than whom? As long as I always have money, and his team always needs money, we can maintain a happy relationship. It's a win-win. Besides, my dad doesn't care what kind of partner we choose to marry, as long as it makes us happy. I've already thought about it. If we really get married, I'll prepare a prenup. If he treats me right, we'll be happily ever after. If not, then goodbye.\"","Qin Rong was stunned but found the logic reasonable, at least safer than her older sister or cousin's relationships.","Qin Zhao had a sense of déjà vu with this approach.","Qin Jing was speechless every time he heard his sister's twisted logic. After all, he valued soul connections, which was why he was into online relationships.","[Qin Xiaoyu is not bad at all. She's truly captivated, genuinely likes him, but she's also practical. She knows the pros and cons and doesn't get hung up on unnecessary details. This is a good way to stay unfazed. After thinking about it, I don't need to investigate Wen Bai for her. Even if I discover his worst case is that he's with Qin Xiaoyu for her money, there's nothing much to say.]","Qin Xiaoyu is different from Qin Jiaxi. She doesn't need others' protection. She's already built her armor.","The conversation about this topic was quite lively, with both Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing passionately arguing due to their differing perspectives.","\"You're always talking about your online girlfriend's love story. How about you bring her out? I don't believe she's as cute as you say. I bet she's just a scammer. When you see her true face, you'll run for the hills. Then I'll laugh at your 'true love' for real!\" Qin Xiaoyu retorted.","Every time Qin Xiaoyu mentioned meeting in person, Qin Jing would back down. Recently, with his parents' upcoming big birthday, he had mentioned meeting several times, but the other party always found excuses to refuse, making his confidence waver a bit, though he didn't show it on the surface.","Today, he joined the group for fun not because he liked gaming, but because his girlfriend's account had this game's emblem. He guessed she might like it. Though after asking, she didn't seem too interested, he still wanted to seize the opportunity to take some photos and videos of the event and use that as an excuse to invite her to meet.","If she truly liked gaming and got a chance to meet star players, she might be willing.","Soon, the competition began, and everyone stopped talking about meeting parents.","Qin Xiaoyu thought it would be better to wait until after the match to go with Wen Bai.","Halfway through the game, Wen Bai's team was leading. Ji Fei, having eaten too many fruits, needed to go to the bathroom.","As soon as she stepped out the door and turned around, she almost got a fright. There was a middle-aged woman looking nervous and about to turn around.","\"What are you doing?\" Ji Fei recognized her as Wen's mother.","Wen's mother: \"Just passing by.\"","Ji Fei narrowed her eyes and turned to leave. After turning the corner, she immediately stopped and peeked back.","She saw Wen's mother return and sneakily lean against the door, as if trying to eavesdrop.","Ji Fei: ...","She thought Qin Xiaoyu should consider finding a new boyfriend. If she ended up with such a mother-in-law, wouldn't she be scared if the mother-in-law eavesdropped on them through the keyhole? Ji Fei had a mischievous fantasy of that scenario and felt goosebumps all over.","Just as she was about to make a sound to scare the woman, she heard Wen's mother murmur, \"I couldn't have been wrong, could I?\"","Ji Fei raised an eyebrow, thinking that Wen's mother might have seen Qin Xiaoyu's photo with her son and took Qin Xiaoyu as her future daughter-in-law. So now, she had come over to meet her son's girlfriend?","Or maybe she thought Qin Xiaoyu should come over to greet her?","Ji Fei wouldn't treat her politely just because of her identity. After all, she loved messing with people like that.","So Ji Fei leaned against the wall and loudly coughed towards the woman.","Wen's mother flinched and jumped, reflexively cursing.","Then she saw a stunningly beautiful woman giving her a knowing smile.","Wen's mother immediately felt embarrassed and quickly turned around to run off.","Ji Fei didn't continue to harass her, just wanted to scare her a bit.","After seven turns and eight bends, she finally found the restroom.","As she finished washing her hands and stepped out, she saw two distant figures in the corridor and the sound of shouting.","\"It's you! You shameless fox! Who gave you permission to seduce my son? You don't care about your face, but we do! We are from an academic family! We can't tolerate your kind of filth!\"","Wen's mother was shouting while waving her arms at the man, as if trying to slap him.","And the man was Qin Jing!"]},{"number":391,"title":"Chapter 391: Men Have a One-Track Mind When It Comes to Love, Women Have Good Character","paragraphs":["Ji Fei was totally stunned by this dramatic scene.","What was going on here?","Wen's mother, Qin Xiaoyu's boyfriend's mom, was accusing Qin Jing of being a male fox spirit who seduced her son?","How many sons did she have?","Wait, no, wasn't Qin Jing's partner a woman?","Could it be that he was actually a crossdresser pulling off an online scam?","Ji Fei suppressed her gossiping smile and quickly stepped forward to help.","After all, Qin Jing was the type who wouldn't be rude to women, and despite being livid with anger, he was helpless against the hysterical woman.","\"Ma'am, you've got the wrong person. No... have you misunderstood something? If you're talking about your son, Wen Bai, I barely know him, okay? And I'm not gay!\"","But Wen's mother was already red in the face with anger, truly furious, and wanted to slap him. Just as it seemed she might succeed, Qin Jing prepared to take the hit with his head, but the slap never came down.","A voice rang out.","\"If you hit someone first, for whatever reason, whether young or old, you'll have to go to the police station and pay compensation. Ma'am, make sure you have the money ready before you hit!\"","Wen's mother was stunned to see Ji Fei, the woman who had previously played a prank on her, holding her wrist.","\"You... mind your own business. Mixing with such filth, you're not any better!\"","Ji Fei raised an eyebrow and retorted, \"What you're doing now is a form of defamation. Do you want to pay a fine for that?\"","Ji Fei guessed that Wen's mother cared most about money, so she addressed the issue every time, and sure enough, Wen's mother froze. \"I'm not defaming anyone!\"","\"Do you have evidence? Show it to me.\" Ji Fei said directly.","Wen's mother was immediately speechless, perfectly demonstrating what it meant to be unreasonable.","Ji Fei pulled her away and asked Qin Jing, \"Are you okay?\"","Although Qin Jing was her brother-in-law, he was actually a bit older than Ji Fei. Being protected like this embarrassed him, and he blushed.","\"I'm fine. I have no idea what's going on. Could it be that she confused me with my sister?\" Qin Jing was feeling completely baffled.","He could only think of this possibility. After all, as identical twins, they did look somewhat alike, and Qin Xiaoyu also had short hair. If the photos were only partial shots and the impulsive woman saw them, then met Qin Jing in person, it wasn't entirely impossible for her to get confused.","Ji Fei's mouth twitched, and she didn't know the woman's name, so she couldn't uncover the truth. Qin Jing's explanation was somewhat plausible, though.","As they spoke, Wen's mother gradually calmed down, her eyes darting around inquisitively.","Qin Jing also regained his composure and said, \"Ma'am, your son is indeed dating my sister. If you don't believe me, after their competition ends, bring your son to our private room, and you can see for yourself.\"","Seeing that Wen's mother seemed quite shocked, she didn't say anything but just stared at him intently. Qin Jing found it extremely unpleasant and didn't want to go to the bathroom anymore. He called Ji Fei and left together.","Just before they left, Wen's mother couldn't resist adding a few more words, \"Hey, let me tell you, men who mess around with men are against nature. It's something only perverts would do. If I find out you're seducing my son, I won't let you off!\"","Qin Jing really wanted to turn around and curse, but his upbringing prevented him from engaging in such a futile argument with an old woman.","What a ridiculous situation! After saying all that, this woman still didn't believe him? And what did she have against homosexuality? Her extreme homophobia was truly uncomfortable. You could disagree, but why resort to insults?","Qin Jing returned to the private room in a huff. He shot his sister a glare, thinking about the kind of family she had gotten involved with.","\"What's wrong? Back so soon? Kidneys not functioning? Well, you can't blame me for that!\" Qin Xiaoyu joked.","Ji Fei couldn't help but laugh, \"We ran into some trouble.\"","The group immediately became curious.","Qin Jing grumbled and recounted what had just happened.","Qin Xiaoyu was utterly speechless. \"What kind of person is that?\"","\"Your boyfriend's mother, probably your future mother-in-law,\" Qin Jing said irritably.","\"Just because you two look alike, she thought her son was actually dating a man and just lost it?\" Qin Zhao was incredulous. \"That's terrifying. Having to deal with someone like that? Even more terrifying.\"","Qin Rong quickly said, \"Don't talk like that. He is he, and his mother is his mother.\"","It seemed both brothers were urging a breakup, and Qin Rong was worried Qin Xiaoyu might feel sad.","Qin Xiaoyu indeed felt a bit sad, not because of their urging to break up, but because she was also considering it. She genuinely liked Wen Bai and had thought about marriage, but she hadn't expected his mother to be like this, jumping to conclusions and acting so rashly and impolitely. She felt they didn't match in temperament.","After all, marriage was never just a matter of two people.","Qin Xiaoyu was also quite hesitant. If it really didn't work out, she might just date for now and then break up later. She lacked the confidence to overcome the obstacles and didn't want to put her boyfriend in a difficult position by making him choose. She thought that wouldn't be right.","\"Well, Wen Bai's family is technically a single-parent household. His parents have been separated for years, and his father lives overseas, so he's been relying on his mother. I once thought that if we were really together, we probably couldn't leave his mother alone. Even if we didn't live together, frequent interactions were inevitable. Now... I'm a bit worried,\" Qin Xiaoyu admitted honestly.","This was Qin Xiaoyu's life, and she had her own views, so no one would interfere. They just told her to think it through, as it wasn't fair to judge someone based on their mother's behavior alone.","Perhaps it was this kind of child-rearing situation that made Wen's mother particularly sensitive.","In the end, Qin Xiaoyu probably wanted to meet a few more times before making a decision. Later, she even promised to make sure her boyfriend and his mother clarified everything and apologized to her brother. Although she usually liked to tease her brother, she still stood by her brother in this situation. An apology was a must!","\"If you two break up, it would really be ridiculous,\" Qin Jing said. \"Dad said the master foretold that the Qin Family would have bad luck in marriage and relationships lately.\"","Ji Fei also remembered what Qin Xian had said and the sweetness of that night, couldn't help but share her love-drunk thoughts, \"Not really, my husband and I are doing great.\"","Everyone burst out laughing.","\"I've discovered a pattern,\" Qin Zhao chuckled. \"When a couple consists of a man who's love-drunk and a woman with good character, they can definitely grow old together! Like Aunt and Uncle, Dad and Mom. And Uncle Six and Aunt Six.\"","Qin Jing and Qin Xiaoyu immediately chimed in, \"And our parents too.\"","Although Aunt Four had passed away early, when she was alive, it was indeed this pattern. If it weren't for her husband's love-drunk nature, with his status and position, he wouldn't have raised a pair of children alone. It was said that even when someone sent a replacement, he would get angry, feeling it was an insult to his late wife.","\"What about Aunt Five and Uncle Five?\" Ji Fei wondered.","They were pretty respectful toward each other, seemed harmonious and peaceful, not the clingy, inseparable kind. Very model-like. That's why Uncle usually traveled for work, and Aunt stayed home to take care of the kids.","\"It's because the places Uncle did business were not very safe. Out of respect for Aunt, he didn't take her along, leaving her at home to be a dutiful wife and mother.\"","\"But there are also some trusted people from the Qin Family in those places, so it's easy to tell if Uncle is truly devoted to Aunt alone.\"","Everyone chatted away, gossiping about the older generation, though they skipped over Aunt Lu Meihe. They weren't really close, and she wasn't exactly a real relative, so they didn't mention her.","Soon the competition ended, and Wen Bai's team won. Qin Xiaoyu looked proud and happily went on stage to present the flowers.","The two hugged, and although they hadn't gone public, fans already knew, so the cheers grew louder and louder. After all, Qin Xiaoyu was not only good-looking but also a wealthy woman who had helped Wen Bai in his time of need. In the fans' eyes, it was a high-achieving rich sister.","In the private room, everyone watching the close-up on the big screen smiled.","The love could be seen pouring out of Wen Bai's eyes, proving that the two young people were still genuinely in love, though they had an unruly mother to deal with.","This only piqued Ji Fei's curiosity even more about Wen Bai himself."]},{"number":392,"title":"Chapter 392: Your Brother Is Very Nice","paragraphs":["The competition was drawing to a close, and Qin Xiaoyu didn't leave with Wen Bai. Instead, she briefly recounted the incident, adding, \"I believe that although Wen's mother is an elder, if she has made a mistake, she should still express her apologies. Otherwise, it would be difficult for me to explain to my family.\"","Wen Bai's face, which had been relatively handsome, was now a mix of red and green.","\"My mom... is she crazy? How... how could she act like this?!\"","\"She probably misunderstood out of concern,\" Qin Xiaoyu said, noting the embarrassment on Wen Bai's face and feeling a sense of relief. As long as her boyfriend could still discern right from wrong, there was still hope.","\"I'll definitely bring my mom to apologize. I'm truly sorry.\" Wen Bai quickly assured her.","Qin Xiaoyu smiled and said, \"Alright, I'll go back and explain first. Let's celebrate together after this matter is resolved.\"","\"Um... um... Your brother must be very angry, right? My mom said those things about him and even attacked him. Does he blame me? Is he going to dislike me?\" Wen Bai asked nervously.","Qin Xiaoyu laughed, touched by how much her boyfriend cared about her family.","\"No, my brother is very nice and magnanimous. As long as an apology is given, he'll be fine,\" Qin Xiaoyu reassured him.","A spark of light flashed in Wen Bai's eyes. \"Right, your brother is a great person. Will he be coming to tonight's celebration? I want to toast him and apologize.\"","Qin Xiaoyu considered it for a moment. \"It's a celebration, so most people will want to join in. I'll invite everyone, and my brother will naturally come along.\"","Wen Bai immediately responded, \"Great.\"","After Qin Xiaoyu left, Wen Bai went to find his mother.","As soon as he entered the lounge and saw Wen's mother, his expression darkened. \"Mom, what have you done?\"","Wen's mother wanted to erupt in anger but thought better of it and chose to swallow her pride. \"I saw a girl come up to give you flowers. I heard from your team staff that she's actually your girlfriend and also a sponsor of your team, right?\"","Wen Bai had never told his mother about his relationship with Qin Xiaoyu, but now that she knew, there was no point in hiding it. He nodded and said, \"Yes, she's my girlfriend. So why did you treat her brother like that? Do you know how difficult this makes things for me?\"","\"What? Difficult? Isn't she your girlfriend? If she can't even listen to you, is it because I said something about her brother that she's going to do something to your team?\" Wen's mother shot back, her eyes wide with indignation.","Wen Bai rubbed his temples wearily. \"Mom, can't you change your temper? It's exhausting for me to deal with this.\"","Wen's mother's eyes reddened immediately. \"Your father disliked me, and now you disapprove of me too?\"","Wen Bai's expression changed instantly. \"Enough, every time you bring that up. In any case, you've caused trouble for me. Later, I'll take you to apologize!\"","Wen's mother immediately turned furious. \"What? I'm an elder, and they didn't even come to greet me first. Now you're asking me to apologize? Do they think they're so great just because they have a bit of money? We come from a scholarly family...\"","\"If it weren't for the money, why would you have agreed to let me drop out of school to join the competition? Wasn't it because the signing bonus was high?\" Wen Bai exposed his mother's hypocrisy without hesitation. Normally, he would have had the patience to deal with her, but now, he was too anxious to play along.","Wen's mother immediately reverted to her dramatic self, but Wen Bai interrupted her before she could go any further.","\"If you don't apologize, I'll send you back home. I'll go and apologize myself. Someone has to take responsibility for what you've done. They're not ordinary people. Ask anyone in Y City about the Qin Family, and you'll know that they're not the kind of family you can bully just by acting like an elder.\" Wen Bai said coldly.","Realizing that her son was serious, Wen's mother knew she couldn't return home—she had to stay and watch over Wen Bai.","\"Alright, I understand. I'll apologize... I misunderstood,\" Wen's mother said.","Wen Bai gave his mother a look of doubt and uncertainty but could only proceed with this for now.","He turned and left, pulling out his phone to start typing. Wen's mother followed behind, watching her son's back and wanting to say something but ultimately keeping silent.","Meanwhile, Qin Xiaoyu had returned and explained the situation to everyone.","Originally, Qin Jing had no interest in the celebration. He had been sending photos from the event to his girlfriend, but she hadn't responded. Thinking about going home to have a video call with her that night, he felt uneasy as they rarely video chatted, mostly just texting. He wanted to see her more and try to persuade her.","Just as he was about to suggest a video call for the evening, his girlfriend responded with a series of messages, thanking him for the photos and expressing how much she liked them. She also said she missed him and then apologized for being unable to meet that night due to a gathering. She asked if he had any other plans, as if feeling guilty about standing him up.","Qin Jing mentioned that he had been invited to a celebration but preferred to video chat instead, intending to decline the invitation.","However, his girlfriend urged him to attend and take more photos from the event.","Unable to coordinate with his girlfriend, Qin Jing expressed his disappointment.","So, when Qin Xiaoyu invited him again, Qin Jing felt genuinely inclined to join for a drink.","Qin Zhao was interested, while Qin Rong was indifferent and followed Ji Fei's lead.","Ji Fei thought it would be nice to have a change of scenery and enjoy some wine with her husband, so she agreed to go.","As they were discussing this, someone knocked on the door. Everyone fell silent, glanced at each other, and assumed a composed posture, ready to greet the visitor."]},{"number":393,"title":"Chapter 393: If the Magic Mirror Knew His Soulmate","paragraphs":["Wen Bai brought his mother inside, and as soon as she entered, she began to look around, her gaze eventually falling on Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing.","Her expression, however, wasn't exactly friendly.","Wen Bai, upon entering, quickly glanced at Qin Jing before approaching Qin Xiaoyu and saying, \"Xiaoyu, I brought my mom over to apologize.\"","\"Mom, this is my girlfriend, Qin Xiaoyu, and this is her brother, Qin Jing. These are the others...\"","Qin Xiaoyu promptly introduced everyone, and they all smiled and greeted each other, except for Ji Fei.","Ji Fei was lost in the crowd, so no one paid much attention to her.","\"Mom, you misunderstood her brother earlier, so you should apologize,\" Wen Bai nudged his mother.","Wen's mother, though hesitant, still stepped forward and said to Qin Jing, \"I'm sorry, I misunderstood earlier. Please don't hold it against me, an older woman.\"","Wen Bai looked uncomfortable but also chimed in with several apologies.","Qin Jing, for the sake of Qin Xiaoyu's feelings, let it slide. Although he found it rather unpleasant that Wen's mother insisted on maintaining her seniority during the apology, it wasn't entirely incomprehensible—many older people are reluctant to apologize to their juniors.","Qin Xiaoyu, though also feeling uneasy, managed to swallow her discontent, as Wen Bai's efforts were otherwise commendable.","Wen Bai quickly changed the subject, steering the conversation away from his mother's presence.","Wen's mother, not causing any further trouble, quietly stood to the side, though her eyes continued to dart sneakily towards the twins.","Wen Bai didn't stay long, as he had teammates to meet up with for an upcoming event. He told Qin Xiaoyu they would see each other later at the victory banquet and left.","After they were gone, Qin Xiaoyu also ushered everyone to leave.","\"So, what do you guys think?\" Qin Xiaoyu asked with a smile as they walked.","Qin Jing replied, \"Other than your mom, who might be a bit much for you to handle, everything else is fine. Nobody's perfect.\"","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong also had a good impression of Wen Bai and agreed with Qin Jing. Then they turned to Ji Fei, knowing that she had a special insight into people.","At that moment, Ji Fei's expression was completely rigid, almost as if her actions of walking with them were purely mechanical, with her mind elsewhere.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong sensed something was terribly wrong. Could this mean Wen Bai was a jerk?","It wasn't until Qin Rong nudged Ji Fei that she snapped out of it, bewildered as she looked at the siblings walking ahead.","\"What a calamity! Those two siblings are in a real mess! If I hadn't come today, how much longer would they be deceived?\"","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong: !!!!!! There's a scandal!!!","But worst case scenario, he's in love with Qin Xiaoyu's money and not her. Does that even matter to her?","Or is it his mom who has some issues?","[Wen's mother wasn't wrong—she was actually interested in Qin Jing. It seems she stumbled upon it by accident, since Wen Bai's pillowcase was filled with photos of Qin Jing.]","Qin Zhao: !!!!!!","Qin Rong: ?????","[The photos were all taken secretly. Whenever Wen Bai met Qin Xiaoyu, he would occasionally see Qin Jing and seize the opportunity to take photos!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong: Wait, so Wen Bai is actually gay? And he's not in love with Qin Xiaoyu but with Qin Jing? Is he pretending to be straight and fooling Qin Xiaoyu?!","[I was joking before, but now it's actually true! Now I'm just curious about one thing—if Qin Jing knew that his soulmate was actually Wen Bai in disguise, would he still say that the soul is the most important thing?]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong both came to a sudden halt, unable to take another step, their eyes wide as they stared at the two people in front.","So... they're both being courted by the same person!!!","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong felt mentally scarred. This scandal was way too explosive. Their brains were about to short-circuit.","[Wen Bai is truly a genius. Despite being gay, he kept it deeply hidden due to his mother's disapproval. After joining a team that faced issues, he met Qin Xiaoyu, and her wealth forced him to bow to the capital's influence, pretending to be straight and dating Qin Xiaoyu. He initially thought he could break up later, but then he unexpectedly met Qin Xiaoyu's look-alike, Qin Jing, and he fell in love at first sight.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong's hair almost stood on end at this shameless melodrama!","[From then on, he fell ill with unrequited love, unable to stop himself from stealing Qin Jing's contact information from Qin Xiaoyu. He posed as a woman to add Qin Jing on social media, and after confirming that Qin Jing was straight, he had to continue pretending to be a woman. Eventually, they started a 'online relationship.' In order to have more chances to interact with Qin Jing, he couldn't break up with Qin Xiaoyu, and he even thought... I spit! What a deceitful man—he actually wanted to trick Qin Xiaoyu into being his 'same-sex wife,' so he could be together with his brother-in-law every day.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong: Ew, enough of that!","[Being gay is normal, but being gay and marrying someone of the opposite sex to deceive them is just too damn cruel!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong: It's the kind of cruelty that would make ancestors rise from their graves in protest!","How did he think things would go so smoothly for him? He wanted to have all the benefits?","[Earlier, I thought he looked at Qin Xiaoyu with love, but now I realize it's just the love of someone who sees her as a replacement!]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong: Now that you mention it, I remember that too. Shivers all over!","Just moments ago, they thought Wen Bai was decent. Now they felt tainted just by talking about him.","And they recalled how Qin Jing had once mentioned that Wen Bai seemed obsequious, but they assumed it was because of his brother-in-law. Little did they know, it was because of his crush!","Suddenly, they felt a wave of sympathy for the siblings. Both had given their hearts to someone who turned out to be deceiving them—and worse, it was the same person. Who could they even go to for comfort?","And then there was the impending revelation of the truth...","Will the siblings find out? If they do, what should they do?","It's usually complicated enough to tell a friend or sibling that their significant other is cheating on them, but how is one supposed to deal with not just one but two people, each unaware that they are both being cheated on by the same person—to the point of being deceived in parallel? The emotional shock would be double the heartache, could their familial bond withstand such a blow?","Ji Fei was also worried. [The truth must come out, obviously, but how to reveal it?! Should I go to Wen Bai's house and look for the photos, or should I steal his phone and find the chat records? Or should we catch them in the act?... Wait, nah, better not. I can't even imagine the mess that would create, especially when dealing with Qin Jing. It's way too scary.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong agreed,","They were deep in their worry, so they all coincidentally thought of the same thing at once and silently picked up their phones.","And so, Qin Xian, occupied in his office, received different messages.","Ji Fei: \"Honey, I encountered something weird today... Why would she call Qin Jing a 'cunning fox,' so strange... Could you help me think about it?\"","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong in the group chat: \"Big news from the sister-in-law! *crack*...*pop*! Second brother, come tonight, let's think of a solution!\"","The little family group, including the second older family, instantly burst into an uproar.","Qin Xian: ...."]},{"number":394,"title":"Chapter 394: Don't Really Get Sweet-talked by Men","paragraphs":["The victory celebration was held at a venue reminiscent of a bar, complete with a buffet of delicious food, gaming tournaments, and live performances. The atmosphere was lively but not too noisy.","This gathering included not only the staff and team members but also their families, as well as people brought by sponsors like Qin Xiaoyu.","Wen Bai had entrusted his mother to socialize with the other elders, advising her not to wander off, before heading to join Qin Xiaoyu and her group.","Still uneasy, Wen's mother secretly peeked from a corner, thinking to herself: Maybe those siblings are playing tricks on my son, but they hold his fate in their hands, so I must stay calm. As long as that cunning fox doesn't seduce my son, he'll be fine!","When Qin Xian arrived, he noticed an older woman lurking in the corner, observing a distant sofa.","Qin Xian passed by without expression, heading toward the group.","At that moment, Ji Fei and the others were watching the situation with amusement.","Wen Bai was seated next to Qin Xiaoyu, but his eyes frequently drifted to Qin Jing beside him. The twin siblings, being sensitive, didn’t notice anything unusual. Occasionally, Wen Bai would talk to Qin Jing over Qin Xiaoyu, laughing heartily, while Qin Xiaoyu leaned back and Qin Jing leaned in politely to listen.","No one noticed that Wen Bai's gaze was completely unfocused, lingering between the two.","Ji Fei and the others internally facepalmed, wondering why it was so hard to catch on.","Then, Qin Xian arrived.","Everyone greeted him immediately, and upon learning his identity, Wen Bai immediately stood up, showing great respect.","【Even with good manners, no points will be earned, because you're already in a dead end.】","Qin Xian calmly listened to his wife's complaints, then sat down, gently pulling Ji Fei into his arms and kissing her forehead.","It had become a habit, no matter the occasion, that every time they met, Qin Xian would always kiss her first.","Ji Fei was used to it, but others still found it a bit unsettling, given Qin Xian's typically cold exterior even with relatives.","\"Where are Cousin and Jiaxi?\" Ji Fei asked.","【There might be some good drama tonight, can't miss it.】","\"Cousin is home composing music, saying he doesn't need to accompany us and finally has time to work in peace. Jiaxi was invited by schoolmates to an event.\"","\"Cousin aside, Jiaxi is attending events now? Making friends?\" Ji Fei exclaimed excitedly.","Qin Xian nodded, \"That's what they told me when I returned home.\"","Ji Fei felt relieved and then turned her concern to Qin Xian, \"Have you eaten?\"","Qin Xian shook his head.","Ji Fei immediately cupped his face affectionately. \"Don't let my handsome guy starve.\"","She eagerly dragged him to get some food.","Upon returning, Ji Fei's attention was quickly diverted by what was happening across from them.","It seemed Qin Jing wanted something from the buffet but couldn’t reach, so he was about to stand up. Wen Bai quickly fetched the whole plate and brought it over.","Qin Jing was caught off guard by such thoughtful service, feeling a bit awkward and quickly said, \"Thank you.\"","【Wow! Pfft~ Although it's not right, I want to laugh.】","But the next moment, the laughter faded. Wen Bai was now making excuses to get both Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing to drink more.","【I bet he doesn't dare do anything else, but taking advantage of the drunkenness for some casual touches and affection might be inevitable. What a reckless audacity!】","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong couldn't stand it, especially worried about Qin Jing! Don't let him get molested by a man!","Already, Wen Bai was using the excuse of drinking to occasionally pat Qin Jing's hand or arm.","Such interactions were normal, and anyone not in the know wouldn't think much of it.","Ji Fei could only keep an eye on the situation.","Meanwhile, Qin Xian calmly ate, slowly finishing the food Ji Fei had chosen for him. Across from them, Wen Bai had already asked Qin Xiaoyu to move aside.","\"Come, let’s drink together, you go sit over there,\" he said.","Qin Xiaoyu, going with the flow, gave up her seat, allowing Wen Bai to sit beside the person he had been longing for.","Excited and trembling, he was about to put his arm around Qin Jing’s shoulder in a brotherly gesture.","Qin Zhao, Qin Rong, and Ji Fei were all about to come up with excuses to interrupt. But then, a cold voice cut through the air.","\"Qin Jing, where’s your girlfriend?\"","Qin Xian’s sudden question startled the three across from them.","Especially Wen Bai, whose actions froze immediately, quickly shrinking back with guilt.","\"Ah? Second brother, you forgot? I haven’t officially met my girlfriend yet. How could I have invited her here?\" Qin Jing replied.","Qin Xian's eyebrows furrowed, looking very serious. \"Haven’t met yet? Then it needs to be arranged soon. Grandma Lv asked me today whether to reserve a spot for your girlfriend. You need to confirm these things in advance so the family can plan accordingly.\"","At first, Ji Fei found it strange why Qin Xian suddenly brought this up. Upon hearing this, she felt it was the perfect opportunity!","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were internally giving their second brother a thumbs up. Impressive! And they suspected this was a real event, with Qin Xian bringing it up after talking to Grandma Lv, ensuring no loopholes would be left.","Even if Qin Jing later questioned it, it wouldn’t cause any issues.","Qin Jing nodded blankly, then said with a sigh, \"I feel like she probably won’t come. Meeting me is hard enough, let alone attending a big event like this.\"","Ji Fei and the others glanced at Wen Bai’s expression across from them. It was quite peculiar, looking almost hurt.","【He’s actually comforting himself by thinking he’s with Qin Xiaoyu, which is the same as being with Qin Jing. If Qin Jing knew your true identity, he wouldn’t want you around at all. Stop acting all passionate; it’s annoying!】","\"Have you told her about the event?\" Qin Xian continued.","Qin Jing paused, \"Not yet. I planned to arrange a meeting first.\"","Qin Xian slowly looked down. \"Perhaps, with such an important invitation, she’ll be more determined to meet you. Why don’t you contact her now and ask for her answer?\"","At these words, Wen Bai’s expression changed unnaturally.","Qin Zhao, however, became excited and urged, \"Think about it, all of our family is here, inviting her together. Quick, contact her!\"","Qin Jing was also moved, feeling his imaginary girlfriend was receiving such attention. Plus, under the influence of alcohol, he became impulsive and immediately pulled out his phone to send a message.","Of course, the message went unanswered.","Qin Xian directly said, \"Call her directly. Surely you have her contact details after all this time together.\"","Ji Fei's heartbeat quickened. Just a moment ago, Wen Bai was still putting on a brave front, but now his face was changing color, though he quickly regained his composure.","Despite Qin Jing's impulsive decision to call, the phone on the table, belonging to Wen Bai, remained silent."]},{"number":395,"title":"Chapter 395: Let's Not Contact Each Other For Now","paragraphs":["【Oh, dual SIM, dual system, quite the setup. You’ve really got it figured out.】","Qin Jing was feeling utterly dispirited as he listened to the repeated ringing that never got answered. After all, this was the norm. Out of ten calls, he’d be lucky to get through one or two. It was almost as if there was only a specific window of time when messages and calls could go through.","Qin Xian suddenly interjected, “Give me the number. I’ll have our tech team trace it.”","In an instant, Wen Bai’s wine glass trembled, spilling its contents directly onto Qin Xiaoyu, who was startled but more alarmed by Qin Xian’s suggestion.","Qin Jing froze, “Huh?”","Qin Xian, serious and cool, replied, “I’m suspicious that you’ve been scammed. I want to help you find out who this person really is.”","Qin Jing’s face immediately darkened. Anyone would feel offended being doubted about their online romance.","Of course, there was someone else whose face darkened even more. Wen Bai certainly didn’t doubt the prowess of the Qin family. If they wanted to trace him, it would be a piece of cake. Previously, he had relied on understanding Qin Jing’s personality to keep up this charade, but now, he was in real danger.","“Ah? That doesn’t seem right,” Qin Jing said.","Qin Xian, however, analyzed, “She’s been resistant to meeting you. It’s either because she has something she can’t talk about, or she’s been lying to you. Either way, taking the initiative isn’t a bad thing. A guy should be proactive when pursuing a girl.”","Qin Zhao immediately chimed in, “Right! If she has some kind of situation, you could secretly step in like a prince and help her out, and everyone would be happy. But if she’s a scammer, like maybe she’s not good-looking...”","“I don’t care!” Qin Jing quickly retorted.","Qin Zhao smirked, “What if she’s married? What if... heh... she’s actually a man?”","There was no hiding the panic on Wen Bai’s face, though the dim lighting made it hard to notice.","Qin Jing rushed to defend, “That’s impossible!”","It was clear he was more resistant to the idea of his online love being a man than being married.","“So, just try it. We’ll do it secretly. If she gets mad, blame it on us. We’ll help you apologize,” Qin Zhao continued to egg him on.","Even though Wen Bai weakly objected, “That’s not respectful to her,” even Qin Xiaoyu got caught up in the excitement, urging her brother to give in. After all, she was super curious about what kind of person this mysterious online lover was, never imagining that person was right next to her.","Ji Fei could already imagine how worried Wen Bai must be feeling.","But in the end, Qin Jing was soft-hearted and didn’t directly give the number to let Qin Xian’s team trace it. Instead, he said, “I’ll try contacting her again. If I can’t reach her, then we’ll talk.”","With that, he tried calling again.","Seeing his panic, Wen Bai quickly found an excuse to step out and head to the restroom.","Watching him dash off in a fluster, Ji Fei and the others couldn’t hold back their laughter.","Soon, Qin Jing’s call connected, and he excitedly turned on the speaker. A feminine voice came through from the other end.","【That’s a pretty advanced voice changer. Totally can’t tell.】","Ji Fei was impressed, and so were Qin Zhao and Qin Rong. Watching Qin Jing get carried away by the voice and coos from the other side was just too much to bear.","Wen Bai, however, was truly skillful. In just a few words, he almost had Qin Jing about to hang up the phone.","Qin Xian knocked on the table, reminding Qin Jing of the main point.","Qin Jing then brought up the matter of the birthday banquet, and there was a brief silence on the other end, likely because Wen Bai was too rushed to think of an excuse.","In the end, he came up with, “Actually... I’ve been in a bad mood lately because... my mother’s hospitalized. I have to go to the hospital every day after work to take care of her. I don’t have the time or the heart to meet you. I want our first meeting to be when I’m at my best. This is just bad timing. Let’s reschedule after my mom gets out of the hospital, okay?”","【Wow, does your mother know you’re using her health as an excuse like this?】","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were speechless. What kind of person would do that? And guess what, his mother was right there!","Qin Jing, however, immediately started worrying and asked about the situation, not suspecting a thing. He was completely taken in, which explained why he’d been scammed for so long.","After a round of reassurances and a few attempts to offer help, which were ultimately refused, the call finally ended.","“Hey, come on, you can’t believe that. It’s clearly just a last-minute excuse!” Qin Zhao couldn’t hold back.","“Well, no one would joke about their mother’s health, right?” Qin Jing reasoned, especially given his own mother’s early passing, making him even more sensitive to such things.","Ji Fei chimed in, “Don’t doubt it, people do that. You should be wondering, if it’s a lie, why would she go that far rather than just meeting you? What exactly is she hiding?”","Qin Jing was dumbfounded. Qin Xiaoyu had initially agreed with her brother but, after hearing everyone else’s reasoning, she couldn’t help but say, “Brother, I think everyone’s got a point.”","Just then, Wen Bai rushed back in, sweating from the run, clearly worried about the situation here. Ji Fei couldn’t help but laugh, knowing he’d be even more tense now.","Sure enough, as soon as he sat down, he heard the discussion about whether the story was a lie, and he was visibly uneasy, squirming in his seat.","Then Qin Xian added, “Qin Jing, contact her again. You didn’t mention earlier that we have the best medical resources. If her mother is really sick, I’m sure she wouldn’t object to providing the best care for her.”","Wen Bai’s cold sweat was practically dripping down.","Qin Jing slapped his forehead, “Right, I’ll call her now.”","Seeing his desperation, Wen Bai quickly pretended to have left something behind and rushed out again.","Qin Xiaoyu watched Wen Bai’s restless exit and murmured, “Why does it feel like he’s been off tonight?”","Meanwhile, Ji Fei and the others were practically dying of laughter.","Especially Ji Fei, who didn’t know Qin Xian was deliberately teasing but thought it was just a hilarious coincidence.","【Serves you right for trying to get cozy by pouring drinks. Now you’re kept on your toes, haha!】","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong couldn’t help but secretly give their brother a thumbs up.","Back at it, Qin Jing called twice before the other end finally picked up.","As soon as it connected, they could hear the other person panting heavily.","Qin Jing asked curiously, “What are you doing?”","“I... I was in a hurry to pick up your call.”","Qin Jing’s heart softened, and he immediately brought up Qin Xian’s suggestion.","There was a brief pause, and just as everyone wondered what excuse Wen Bai would come up with to avoid this, he suddenly exploded on the other end, angrily questioning whether Qin Jing didn’t trust her. He accused Qin Jing of inventing all these reasons just to see her, complaining that she didn’t want to and found his behavior controlling and unpleasant. Then, in a fit, he declared, “Let’s stop contacting each other for a while. Cooling off is good for both of us!”","It sounded like he was breaking up with Qin Jing.","Qin Jing was scared and quickly apologized, but the other side was resolute and hung up, leaving the line dead after that.","Qin Jing was left dumbfounded, looking at Qin Xian with aggrievement.","Qin Xian: ......","Looks like they’ve been one-upped."]},{"number":396,"title":"Chapter 396: We'll Lose a Lot of Little Money","paragraphs":["This whole ordeal made Qin Xian feel rather awkward. He couldn't exactly reveal the truth outright, so he simply bore his brother's slightly resentful gaze.","Qin Zhao, however, persisted, \"Breaking up like this is even stranger. Qin Jing, you really need to think this through. It all feels so fake.\"","Seeing her older brother so distressed, Qin Xiaoyu couldn't help but chime in, \"Maybe... maybe she's just really unique?\"","Qin Zhao retorted, \"Who knows if that's true or not? Why don't we have Second Brother investigate for you? Once we find her, you can beg for a reconciliation face to face.\"","Wen Bai walked in just as those words were spoken and was immediately panic-stricken.","Fortunately, Qin Jing intervened, \"No, I still want to respect her. I'm willing to wait, even if it turns out to be a scam in the end. At least during the process, I respected our feelings.\"","\"You're too naive...\" Qin Zhao nearly blurted out, but catching sight of Wen Bai's relieved expression, he almost snapped.","\"Alright, respect your decision,\" Qin Xian said directly.","Qin Jing managed a weak smile, \"It's my fault too. I was too eager to connect with her personally. I should apologize properly. I wonder when she'll forgive me.\"","Wen Bai's heart softened instantly. \"I believe she'll forgive you if you apologize sincerely.\"","【Damn, still expecting Qin Jing to apologize? You've got guts.】","Ji Fei wanted to say something too, but seeing how Qin Zhao's efforts were going nowhere, she gave up.","【Maybe I should just steal his phone and figure out a way to let Qin Jing and Qin Xiaoyu see the truth.】","At that moment, Qin Xian's eyes darkened, and he seemed displeased. Suddenly, he demanded Wen Bai's contact information.","Wen Bai was startled. While he knew Qin Xian was asking for his regular number, the string of incidents had him on edge.","\"Qin Corporation has a game endorsement coming up, and I think you'd be a good fit,\" Qin Xian began, causing Ji Fei to nearly explode.","【Ah, no! Don't use this jerk. If he gets exposed later, we'll lose a lot of money.】","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were puzzled but assumed there must be a plan.","Qin Xian, sensing his wife's unease, gently patted her back while holding her close. \"We'll probably need to interview you first before making a decision,\" he added, trying to ease the tension.","Qin Xiaoyu was immediately thrilled, thinking that her older brother's endorsement was a tacit approval of her boyfriend. Before Wen Bai could react, she was already urging him to give his number.","Realizing this was his chance to integrate further into the Qin family, Wen Bai eagerly handed over his number.","\"I'll have our staff contact you. You can add them later,\" Qin Xian said before reaching out to arrange it.","Ji Fei didn't pay attention to how he contacted Wen Bai, but she couldn't help but whisper to her husband, \"He's not up to par. I don't like him.\"","Qin Xian chuckled and whispered back, \"Don't worry. I'm just concerned about who our family members are associating with. I'll look into him.\"","Ji Fei's eyes lit up with a mischievous smile as she kissed Qin Xian on the cheek. \"You're such a reliable older brother.\"","Hearing himself called \"older brother,\" Qin Xian felt a shiver run down his spine. His gaze darkened, and he turned to kiss Ji Fei back.","Ji Fei, however, was already thinking ahead. 【Hehe, if they uncover anything, it'll just make things fall into place, right? Hopefully, it happens soon.】","Displeased, Qin Xian lightly bit Ji Fei's lip, causing the people at the table to look away, embarrassed.","Soon, Wen Bai received a message from someone claiming to be from Qin Corporation. They added him on the platform, explained the situation, and sent a contract link to review.","Wen Bai quickly clicked the link but found the contract too long to read thoroughly. The other party mentioned they were busy that night and would discuss it further tomorrow after Wen Bai had reviewed the contract.","Thinking it inappropriate to review the contract in front of Qin Xian, Wen Bai quickly agreed to talk tomorrow and set the matter aside.","Unbeknownst to him, his phone had already been compromised.","Qin Xian received the confirmation and knew he could manipulate the backend to switch systems and chat interfaces at any time.","The only question was finding the right moment—preferably when Qin Jing and Qin Xiaoyu were both present to witness it all at once, leaving no chance for Wen Bai to cover up or deny.","At that moment, the team leader began inviting members of the team to the stage to speak.","Qin Xiaoyu, watching her boyfriend shine on stage, was filled with pride.","Meanwhile, Qin Jing stared at his phone, feeling gloomy.","The event then transitioned to an interactive segment where guests could challenge team members to a game.","Qin Xiaoyu asked if anyone wanted to participate.","Ji Fei, seeing her skills would be displayed on the big screen, declined.","Qin Xian suddenly said, \"Qin Zhao wants to play.\"","Qin Zhao was caught off guard.","A look from Qin Xian, and Qin Zhao immediately understood. He stood up and declared, \"I'll challenge Wen Bai, of course.\"","Qin Xiaoyu laughed, \"You're in for a beating.\"","Qin Zhao smiled faintly. \"We'll see about that.\"","Though unsure what his older brother was planning, Qin Zhao had a hunch Wen Bai was about to meet his downfall.","They all used their own phones for the match, and the gameplay was projected onto the big screen.","The audience watched closely, including Wen Bai's mother, though she didn't fully understand what was happening.","Qin Jing, uninterested, kept sending messages and calling, pleading for forgiveness.","Just as Wen Bai coolly secured another kill, the audience erupted in applause. But then, an alert suddenly popped up on his screen.","The message read: \"Sweetie, I really made a mistake. You know I genuinely like you. Not being able to see you doesn't matter—I can wait. But the invitation to the birthday banquet was heartfelt. My sister's bringing a boyfriend, and I'll be all alone. It's kind of pitiful, don't you think? That's why I got a bit impatient.\"","In an instant, the lively atmosphere fell silent. Everyone stared at the message in disbelief.","Wen Bai's mind went blank. Instinctively, he tried to swipe the message away to make it disappear.","But it was too late.","Qin Jing hadn't noticed, but Qin Xiaoyu had been watching closely. She had seen it all too clearly—so clearly that her mind went blank.","What was that?","Was that what she thought it was?","It couldn't be that coincidental! Wasn't this something that happened to other people in other places at the same time?","But why did it appear on Wen Bai's phone?!","Even if it seemed too absurd to believe, Qin Xiaoyu couldn't deceive herself any longer.","As Wen Bai tried to pretend nothing had happened, continuing to play and targeting his motionless opponent, Qin Xiaoyu stormed onto the stage and snatched his phone.","\"Don't, Xiaoyu!\" Wen Bai tried to retrieve it.","But Qin Zhao, who had silently appeared behind him, intervened.","The audience, now in chaos, knew Qin Xiaoyu and Wen Bai were dating. The message clearly hadn't been sent by Qin Xiaoyu.","So their team captain was cheating? Not only was he enjoying the benefits of a wealthy woman's support, but he was also cheating—what kind of scumbag behavior was that?","Little did they know, an even more explosive revelation was about to unfold."]},{"number":397,"title":"Chapter 397: Mistakenly Thought to Be Evidence of Infidelity","paragraphs":["Ji Fei was dumbfounded, thinking that tonight would end here, but unexpectedly, there was a big twist.","【So it was because you rushed to answer the phone and made a mistake? Is that really bad luck? No, it should be called retribution.】","Qin Rong next to her naturally knew what had happened, immediately looking admiringly at her second brother.","Qin Xian looked calm as he turned to Qin Jing.","Because Qin Xiaoyu's movements were too sudden, Qin Jing naturally reacted. When he regained his senses and looked over, the large screen no longer showed the message he had just sent.","\"What's Xiaoyu doing? It seems like there's a conflict,\" Qin Jing stood up, ready to walk over.","Wen's mother, who had been spying from the shadows, also hurried over, \"What are you doing! Let go of my son!\"","At this moment, Qin Xiaoyu's fingers were moving incredibly fast. Her brain might not have been thinking about anything, but her heart felt as if it was being corroded by sulfuric acid, unbearably painful.","She had indeed prepared herself mentally for what would happen if Wen Bai only loved her money, but she couldn't tolerate that her boyfriend had been deceiving her all along!","And possibly, he had also deceived her brother...","The large screen displayed the phone screen, suddenly jumping to a chat interface.","At first, everyone thought it was evidence of infidelity.","But as they watched, they began to feel something was off.","After all, the avatar on Wen Bai's phone that was replying was a cute girl's avatar, and the tone of the words...","And the other party was clearly a man.","There was a nickname displayed on the chat box: Qin Jing.","Another Qin, and it seemed like they had heard the name somewhere before.","Just as everyone was thinking, a slim figure suddenly dashed onto the stage, snatched the phone from Qin Xiaoyu's hand, and began flipping through the chat records.","Then he pulled out his own phone and dialed a number. The next second, the phone he had just snatched started ringing.","Everyone was stunned.","All the scenes just now seemed to prove one thing.","Wen Bai had been secretly contacting, disguised as a female, his girlfriend's brother!","The next second, Qin Jing had already grabbed Wen Bai's collar fiercely, \"What is going on? Why is it you? You're... Little Bai!\"","Qin Jing was so stimulated that he could barely breathe.","At this moment, Wen Bai's face was already as pale as paper, devoid of blood. He had never imagined that it would be exposed in such a form, and he was completely stunned.","But facing the person he loved, he still chose to explain immediately, \"Qin Jing, I... I'm sorry, I...\"","Qin Jing didn't need his explanation and directly punched him.","Qin Zhao quickly backed away.","Qin Xiaoyu's eyes were already red with anger, and she couldn't hold back any longer, rushing up to kick him, \"Damn it, do you think you can play tricks on us siblings?!\"","Seeing her son being beaten, Wen's mother immediately rushed up to push away Qin Jing and Qin Xiaoyu, \"Don't touch my son, what do you want to do?\"","\"Hey, aunty, are you really stupid or pretending to be? Can't you see that your son was tricking a woman for money while pretending to be a woman to deceive a man's feelings?\" Qin Zhao summarized: \"And he even tricked both a brother and sister, you really know how to play!\"","Wen Bai was now covered in injuries, timidly unable to face the current situation.","\"Wen Bai, I treated you well, how could you do this to me, and my brother! You deserve to die!\" Qin Xiaoyu roared.","Qin Jing was also trembling with anger, barely able to stand. Just moments ago, he had humbly begged for reconciliation because he was angry for his girlfriend, but now he was told that the person he had considered his soulmate was actually such a person.","If he had just been a man unknown to anyone, Qin Jing wouldn't have been so furious. Perhaps he couldn't accept being with a man and would feel deceived, but he wouldn't have hated the man to the point of wanting to really kill him.","How could someone be so shameless, dangling his sister while also having an online romance with himself? He didn't even want to imagine what him and his sister had gone through with such disgusting things.","\"What is your purpose, what exactly is your purpose!\" Qin Jing was even starting to suspect if it was some kind of commercial spy deliberately disrupting their siblings.","Although both siblings were heartbroken, seeing them unite against the outsider, the other Qin family members felt relieved.","The surrounding people were already whispering among themselves, as this matter was too explosive. Wen Bai was also a celebrity with some reputation, how could such a thing happen?","\"I always felt it was strange before. Wen Bai never talked about his girlfriend when we were together. We thought it was because he only loved her for her money, so he didn't want to discuss it, but I didn't expect it was because he didn't even love her, he loved her brother!\"","\"Come to think of it, Wen Bai was not cold nor hot towards President Qin, but ever since President Qin's brother came to pick him up once, they met, and then Wen Bai began to be enthusiastic.\"","\"Wen Bai just loved President Qin's money and President Qin's brother's person, that's really a double kill!\"","\"So, is our captain gay?\"","\"Definitely, look at him online dating, not asking for anything, focusing on companionship, that's real sincerity.\"","The gossip finally pierced Wen's mother's heart, as if she had been stimulated, and began hugging her son, yelling wildly, \"You all stop talking nonsense, my son can't be such a pervert, my son is normal, he likes girls, it must be this brother and sister using their wealth and power to play with my son!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Wen Bai, who was hugged by her, suddenly stiffened.","Aunty, even if you want to twist the truth and find a reason to support it, here is clear evidence. The two people involved were both deceived; who is really playing with whom!\" Qin Zhao mocked.","No, no, it's you... Wen's mother immediately pointed at Qin, ridiculing and angrily saying: \"It must be you who are shameless, seducing my son. My son is normal, if it weren't for you seducing him, taking advantage of your relationship with the executor to deceive people, my son wouldn't be like this...\"","\"It was your son who deceived me, I like women! He disguised himself as a woman and cheated me!\" Qin Jing couldn't hold back any longer and roared.","\"If you think that liking men makes someone a pervert, then you're just scolding your own son, it has nothing to do with my brother!\" Qin Xiaoyu immediately defended her brother, \"My brother was deceived by a man, he hasn't even complained about the bad luck yet!\"","Wen's mother was already out of control, tears streaming down her face, \"No, it must be a conspiracy, no... son, you say, you don't like men, say it!\"","Wen's mother suddenly grabbed Wen Bai's shoulders and shook him wildly, as if forcing him to swear to the heavens.","In fact, Wen Bai had imagined various explanations in his mind, such as just a prank, or wanting to learn more about his girlfriend's family, but all were very forced, after all, his account had indeed been in an online romance with Qin Jing, how to explain was useless.","Hearing the surrounding discussions, he also realized that his career was probably over, not only because of the surrounding people's discriminatory gaze, but also because Qin Xiaoyu would no longer sponsor him foolishly, and even offending this brother and sister, he might be banned and retaliated.","Facing his mother who was drivelling, he was also really tired.","As if breaking free from shackles, he pushed away Wen's mother, struggling to get up, struggling with everything, struggling—as proven. In her setting, it was proven that the copper was broken: \"Others were lies, but I was telling the truth to you! I really like you.\"","【Choosing to confess at such a time, this scum-bag is also a brave man, does he not think that it is very deep for himself.】"]},{"number":398,"title":"Chapter 398: Never Expected to Enjoy Melons Within Melons","paragraphs":["Qin Jing didn't feel anything deep; he only felt goosebumps all over his body.","After all, this person had just been holding hands with his sister, and now they were confessing to him. Even though he knew it was his online partner, he still felt utterly disgusted.","Gritting his teeth, his fists clenched tightly.","Wen Bai then turned to Qin Xiaoyu and said, \"I'm sorry, Xiaoyu, but... anyway, you didn't seem to care if I liked you or not. You just wanted to be my girlfriend, right? So I... let myself fall for someone else.\"","Qin Xiaoyu immediately burst out laughing in anger, \"You think you're so wronged, and I should be grateful for the opportunity you've given me! If I had known you were gay, I wouldn't have even looked at you.\"","Even if she didn't have feelings now, emotions could be cultivated over time. But if someone wasn't on the same page, why waste effort?","It's innate orientation, not something that can be \"fixed\" like a bent object.","Wen Bai felt embarrassed by her words, especially seeing the hostile looks from both siblings. He couldn't help but feel wronged, \"I lied to you, and it's my fault, but you both said you loved him and wanted to bring him to the family celebration. What about now?\"","Seeing Wen Bai's retort, Qin Jing and Qin Xiaoyu nearly burst out laughing in anger simultaneously.","A teammate stepped forward to persuade Wen Bai to stop, knowing they couldn't afford to offend Qin Xiaoyu.","Wen's mother, hearing her son's words, went completely mad.","She leaped up, grabbed Wen Bai, and with a fierce glare, shouted, \"What are you saying? What are you talking about! How could you possibly...?\"","\"Enough! I like men. Do you get it? I like men!\" Wen Bai finally lost control and shouted at his mother.","His mother responded with a fierce slap, knocking him back down.","\"You're sick! You need treatment! Just like your father, you're both sick! You're both perverts.\" Wen's mother trembled, her eyes vacant. \"But it's okay, Mom will help you get better. You'll soon return to normal.\"","As she said this, she started to nervously attempt to help Wen Bai up again.","The surrounding crowd was in an uproar. So, Wen's father was also gay? But he had a child with Wen's mother, so she must have been deceived. No wonder she's so homophobic.","People couldn't help but feel sympathy for her.","But Wen Bai pushed his mother away angrily, \"You destroyed my dad, and now you want to destroy me too? My dad wronged you, but he tried his best to make up for it. He's been gone for so long, yet you can't let go of him, and now you won't let me go either?\"","Wen's mother instantly looked heartbroken and desperate.","The bystanders felt Wen Bai's words were unfair. After all, Wen's mother was the victim in this situation.","Although she seemed like a shrew now, she was pushed to this point.","[So that's how it was... Wen's father, when he married Wen's mother, didn't know about his sexual orientation. In that era, there was little information about such matters, so he simply followed tradition and married, having a child. Although he was reluctant about intimate matters, he thought it was just personal preference. He worked hard to support the family and took good care of his wife and child. But later, when he met a man, he realized his true orientation. He initially wanted to keep it hidden but decided it wouldn't be fair to Wen's mother's life, so he was honest and asked for forgiveness, promising to leave everything to her. He even planned to leave with nothing.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong didn't expect to get such juicy gossip. Earlier, they felt Wen's mother, despite being overbearing and unreasonable, was pitiful due to the deception. But hearing the background, they felt it was all rather inevitable.","[But this news was like the heavens falling for Wen's mother. Both families were from scholarly backgrounds, so they were extremely traditional, believing that same-sex relationships went against their ancestors. She loved Wen's father deeply, and his gentle care was something she could boast about in her social circle. Everyone envied her for having a good husband and a good son, living the perfect life. She couldn't accept this drastic change and tried everything to stop Wen's father from leaving.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong remembered Qin Xiaoyu mentioning that Wen Bai's father had left.","[Wen's father tried to reason with her, stating it was for her own good, but she refused to believe him. In the end, to stop Wen's father, she revealed the secret to both sets of parents. The older generation, who prided themselves on their scholarly background, absolutely forbade such things. After discussion, they sent Wen's father to a mental hospital, not a proper one, and kept him locked up. The conditions in that dubious hospital nearly drove him insane. It was only the man he had met earlier who rescued Wen's father and took him away, leaving the country. They lost all contact afterward.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong were stunned. They couldn't imagine how horrendous it would be for a normal person to be locked in an unethical mental hospital, treated for 'being gay,' especially when it was his own relatives who did it.","[Wen Bai had witnessed all this, leaving deep scars. After his father left, his mother became somewhat obsessed, constantly cursing at homosexuals and strictly watching her son, fearing he might make a wrong step. Because of this, Wen Bai became afraid of being treated like his father and kept denying his feelings, even forcing himself to date girls to 'straighten out.' Otherwise, Wen's mother wouldn't have, after using up the money left by Wen's father, sent Wen Bai to work in an all-male environment, as she believed that being gay was a disease, and her son was perfectly fine.]","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong here, could only sigh at how one family’s issues affected so many people.","Others, unlike them, didn’t easily learn the truth behind the scenes. Naturally, their focus wasn’t on this. Instead, they were shocked that not only had their team leader cheated, but he'd also come out! It was too shocking.","Wen's mother still tried to persuade Wen Bai.","Wen Bai, however, shouted, \"If you hadn't constantly pushed me, I could have lived freely! In this day and age, unlike my father's time, I could choose to be with the man I like! It's all your fault for making me scared and anxious! Otherwise, I wouldn't have ended up cheating on them and forcing myself. Everything is your fault!\""]},{"number":399,"title":"Chapter 399: The Offending Object is Always the Same Person","paragraphs":["After shouting, Wen Bai felt as if all his strength had been drained. As someone who had grown up with his mother, rebelling against her was truly exhausting, both physically and mentally.","If it weren't for today's events, he probably would never have been able to confront her like this in his entire life.","But now that everything was out in the open, he felt a wave of confusion.","Wen Bai's mother was completely stunned and couldn't hold herself up any longer, collapsing to the ground and wailing, cursing Wen Bai.","Wen Bai was too mentally exhausted to care anymore. He turned his head and looked at Qin Jing.","Qin Xiaoyu stepped in front of him to block his view, saying coldly, \"Don't ever contact us again, or don't blame us for resorting to extreme measures.\"","After saying that, she pulled her brother and left.","Qin Zhao also followed, leading the group away from the noisy scene.","But to everyone's surprise, Wen Bai still insisted on chasing after them. It seemed he truly liked Qin Jing.","\"You can genuinely like me even without seeing me, so isn't that liking my soul? Why, after seeing the real me, do you regret it? I didn't have real feelings for your sister, but I genuinely care for you. Don't you even give me a chance?\"","Qin Jing was instantly furious and took another swing at him, yelling, \"Shut up! Just for pretending to be straight and tricking my sister, I could beat you to death. And here you are, playing games between us, thinking you’re something special!\"","Qin Xiaoyu, too, was infuriated by Wen Bai's comment about not having real feelings. She had loved him, but he hadn't felt the same.","\"I had no choice, I really had no choice. I admit I made a lot of mistakes, but... but isn't being born gay enough reason to not deserve true love?\" Wen Bai continued to plead.","\"Stop spouting nonsense! You tried to trade fake emotions for real love, what a bold thought! Even con artists would bow to you as their master,\" Qin Zhao rebuked angrily.","\"How could you possibly understand? My life is a tragedy. Loving is forbidden, yet there's no one to hate.\" Wen Bai lamented.","Ji Fei also found Wen Bai rather laughable.","\"Half of your life’s tragedy is your mother's fault, but the other half is your own choice. Stop pretending to be so tragic. Let me guess, if today's events hadn't been exposed, what would you have done?\"","Wen Bai was stunned, and the others were also puzzled by Ji Fei's sudden question.","Ji Fei smiled and continued, \"You wouldn't have broken up with Qin Xiaoyu, because you needed her money to support the team. You also needed her as a bridge to get close to Qin Jing. But you knew Qin Jing wouldn't accept a man, which is why you never revealed your true identity. So, the only way you could stay close to the person you love was by marrying Qin Xiaoyu and interacting with Qin Jing as family. Just like tonight, you’d pretend to be with your girlfriend while secretly finding ways to get closer to Qin Jing. If the relationship deepened, you'd satisfy your own selfish desires even more.\"","As Ji Fei spoke, Wen Bai's face grew increasingly horrified, as Ji Fei had accurately described his plan.","Meanwhile, Qin Jing and Qin Xiaoyu's expressions grew darker and darker, worse than eating countless flies.","Their glares at Wen Bai were as sharp as knives.","Ji Fei truly despised Wen Bai.","\"Unlike his father, who initially didn't understand his situation but left his mother once he did, ultimately making amends. But Wen Bai was fully aware of who he was yet still chose to deceive others, and he deceived two people at once. What was he trying to do? Enjoy the best of both worlds? He wanted a reputation and to cling to the person he liked? Flawless thinking.\"","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong agreed wholeheartedly with Ji Fei's assessment.","This type of person had the audacity to show up again, truly shameless. If he had his own struggles, that was his problem, not something others should have to pay for.","This time, Qin Xiaoyu went up and kicked Wen Bai away, and he didn't dare to resist, just standing there in a daze.","Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing left without sparing him another glance, as looking at him now was an insult.","It wasn't appropriate to discuss this in front of the twins, so the group quietly returned to the old manor.","Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing went straight to their rooms.","Fourth Uncle Qin had planned to talk to them, as Qin Xian had suggested earlier, wanting to confirm the guest list urgently. So, Fourth Uncle Qin intended to prod the twins about bringing their partners along.","\"What's wrong with them? Didn't they see me?\" Fourth Uncle Qin approached from the side, raising his hand to call them over, but the two disappeared before he could.","The other young members of the Qin family were gathered in the hall. Hearing this, they curiously looked at the returning group of people, wondering why they looked so lost, as if their souls had left their bodies. Only Qin Yan seemed embarrassed, as she had heard about it in her gossip group.","\"They're in a bad mood,\" Qin Xian explained.","\"Ah? What happened? Didn't they go to watch their boyfriend's game? Did Xiaoyu have a fight with her boyfriend? I still need to confirm with them if their partners are coming,\" Fourth Uncle Qin sighed helplessly.","Qin Zhao replied, \"To put it simply, something quite bizarre happened to the two of them tonight. Since they didn't say it was a secret, I’ll just tell you straight.\"","Everyone was annoyed by his teasing tone, so they urged him to get on with it.","\"One nearly became a victim of a gay man hiding his identity, and the other was deceived by a man pretending to be straight. Specifically, the culprit behind both cases is the same person.\"","Qin Zhao certainly knew how to drop a bombshell. This shocking revelation left everyone in a daze, struggling to process the information.","Finally, Fourth Uncle Qin stumbled, but Qin Xian quickly caught him and helped him sit on the sofa.","Soon, the usually calm Fourth Uncle Qin burst out, cursing, \"Damn it! Who dared to hurt my children!\"","He then rushed upstairs.","Qin Yi, who was still processing the information, translated in disbelief, \"So, Qin Xiaoyu’s boyfriend, the one she invested in, pretended to be a woman and was actually Qin Jing’s online lover?!\"","Everyone nodded.","Qin Wenqiang asked, \"Was this revealed tonight?\"","Everyone nodded again.","Then, Qin Zhao and Qin Rong recounted the dramatic events of the evening.","Qin Jiaxi, trembling with shock, quickly drank some tea to calm herself, finding the whole situation incredibly unbelievable.","Everyone was left stunned as they digested the drama, and the next day they approached the twins cautiously. While Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing had red, swollen eyes, they didn't seem particularly off.","Still, for the twins, this was undoubtedly a watershed moment in their romantic history.","Fourth Uncle Qin had wanted to confront Wen Bai, but Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing stopped him, feeling there was no need to confront him further.","Qin Jing blocked all contact and deleted all records, while Qin Xiaoyu withdrew her investment.","They didn’t explicitly blacklist Wen Bai, but word of the incident would inevitably spread. Given Wen Bai's immoral actions, he would naturally face consequences, such as being banned from the competition for a period.","Originally, considering his age, he was nearing the end of his career anyway, but this scandal sealed his fate, ending it on a decidedly low note. There would be no further collaborations, and any hope of a coaching, livestreaming, or tutoring career evaporated. Even without direct ties to Qin Corporation, no one dared to support this kind of scumbag, fearing consequences from Qin Corporation. So, Wen Bai was forced to quietly disappear from the scene.","What happened after that, including how he would deal with conflicts with his family, was no longer Ji Fei's concern.","It was just a small episode in their lives.","Such minor events didn't need to be shared with the elders, or they might have worried, and Grandpa would inevitably call for prayers again.","However, the prophecies from that renowned master seemed to be continuing.","One day, while they were playing at the old manor, they heard that something had happened at the main building, and Grandpa was livid.","The younger generation didn't dare approach, until someone came over to tell them it was about Fifth Aunt.","Her husband and her were returning to finalize their divorce, and she had informed the family in advance.","Someone exclaimed, \"Oh no, another divorce?\""]},{"number":400,"title":"Chapter 400: The Melon of Aunt Five Isn't Actually That Delicious","paragraphs":["Despite the previous divorces being due to Ji Fei discovering the truth, this one had nothing to do with her at all; she was just a pure bystander catching up on the gossip.","It seemed the problem lay in the Feng Shui of the Qin family.","This time, Ji Fei obediently stayed on the sidelines, eating her fill of the drama, as she hadn't met the two people involved and had no idea what had happened.","Qin's Father, Qin's Mom, and their uncles were all quite angry.","\"Zhao Jianghe, I thought he was a decent man before. Before marrying Fifth Sister, he was always discreet and had no interest in women. Now look at him, he’s divorcing Fifth Sister for someone else.\"","\"Fifth Sister has always kept the household in immaculate order and has supported him in his business, managing all the logistics. How could he let himself be blinded by infatuation and fall for another woman?\"","\"Who knows! Fifth Sister didn’t explain clearly. We’ll have to interrogate them properly when they return.\"","\"What about the Zhao Family? What do they think?\"","\"The Zhao Family realizes they’re in the wrong and hopes the couple won’t divorce, but they don’t intend to force the other woman away. That’s their family style—keep the red flag at home while the colorful banners fly outside. They want Fifth Sister to remain the first lady of the Zhao Family, but the other woman will stay with Zhao Jianghe at his workplace.\"","Ji Fei frowned as she listened, and Qin Xian noticed, quietly explaining to her, \"The Zhao Family’s main business is in third-world countries. After marrying Zhao Jianghe, Fifth Sister moved to the most prosperous and wealthy country in that continent, living with the Zhao Family. However, Zhao Jianghe’s business requires him to stay in a dangerous country for long periods, possibly only returning home for two or three days a month to transport goods.\"","I get it now. They want Fifth Sister to be the symbol of their prestigious family, but they're also fine with their son having a caring companion outside. So they believe there's no need for Fifth Sister to divorce. Unfortunately, the women raised in the Qin Family probably can't play along with this noble family game, where both husband and wife have their own affairs. They can only choose to divorce. But from what I hear, Zhao Jianghe isn’t against the divorce either, even though his infidelity is despicable. If he cuts his losses, it might be the best choice for Fifth Sister. After all, once the heart changes, it’s no longer pure. Continuing the marriage would only be a waste of Fifth Sister’s life.","Originally, Qin's Father and Qin's Mom were fuming, but after hearing Ji Fei’s mumbling, they suddenly felt that realizing the truth early and turning away might not be such a bad thing.","Now that they had calmed down, they decided to focus on securing more benefits for Fifth Sister. After all, they couldn’t lose both the person and the money. The affair came first, after all.","With limited information, everyone was frustrated, but there was nothing more to discuss. They could only wait until the next day when they would meet Fifth Sister.","The next day, Ji Fei woke up early.","Since Qin Xian, who usually dealt with company matters, hadn't gone to work because they were meeting relatives, he got to enjoy a rare moment of waking up with his wife in his arms. But then he felt her getting up.","\"Why are you waking up so early?\"","\"I need to prepare early; Fifth Sister and her family are arriving.\" Ji Fei said excitedly.","Qin Xian chuckled, \"Don’t get too excited over the gossip, though. It’s Fifth Sister's divorce, and she still has feelings for Zhao Jianghe. After all, they’ve been married for twenty years and were once in love.\"","Ji Fei paused and then gave a simple smile.","[Pfft, there’s not much to gossip about with Fifth Sister’s drama. It’s just the classic story of a man falling for another woman, cheating, and then divorcing his wife. It’s so clichéd; there’s probably no explosive news to dig up. I’m excited because I can finally see if there’s anything off about Fifth Sister’s family, not because of the gossip.]","Qin Xian was taken aback, and his heart swelled uncontrollably. His gaze toward Ji Fei had already changed.","Just as Ji Fei was about to get up, Qin Xian pulled her back into his embrace.","Ji Fei’s cheek pressed against his solid abs, and she immediately softened, taking the opportunity to nibble playfully.","But her little jest was enough for Qin Xian to keep her in bed.","The two of them blushed and lingered in the room for quite a while, with only their gradually calming breaths remaining.","By the time they came downstairs, they were almost late—the car had already pulled into the courtyard.","Ji Fei calmly took a seat, accepting everyone’s gaze. \"Relax, it still takes five minutes to get from the gate to here.\"","Everyone smiled knowingly, remarking that their pair might just be the solution to the Qin Family’s recent troubles. Out of all of them, only they were in a sweet, loving relationship.","Qin Xian went to fetch breakfast for Ji Fei. While others rushed to the square to watch, Qin Xian insisted on Ji Fei finishing her breakfast first.","\"Aren’t we being rude?\"","\"There’ll probably be a commotion.\"","Qin Xian calmly poured milk for Ji Fei. Sure enough, the noise from outside grew loud.","The commotion didn’t die down until they had finished breakfast.","Ji Fei gave Qin Xian a thumbs up. \"You really hit the nail on the head.\"","\"My dad, Third Uncle, and Fourth Uncle all protect Fifth Sister fiercely. After all, she’s their sister.\"","The implication being that the initial meeting wouldn’t be a polite, friendly exchange. There would inevitably be some arguing and maybe even roughhousing before they could enter the main building.","\"Let’s go,\" Qin Xian said, leading Ji Fei toward the main building.","Halfway there, they ran into Qin Yi.","\"You two were really taking it easy. It was terrifying just now. I’ve never seen the uncles get physical before.\" Qin Yi wiped the sweat from his forehead.","\"What happened?\" Qin Xian asked.","Qin Yi briefly recounted the incident,","\"Zhao Jianghe wasn’t hurt; someone else got hurt by mistake. It was a woman, which was awkward.\" Qin Yi shook his head, \"She’s been taken to a guest room to rest for a bit.\"","“What?” Ji Fei said in surprise, “A woman? But that’s not right, Fifth Sister only has one son, Zhao Chengle, right? Where did this...”","At this point, Ji Fei covered her mouth, her expression suddenly puzzled as she looked at Qin Yi, \"Could it be... she brought her along to the visit?\"","Realizing Ji Fei had misunderstood, Qin Yi quickly explained, \"No, no, the woman is an acquaintance of my aunt’s out there. They’re really close, her name is Lu Yunqing. She almost became Zhao Chengle’s godmother.\"","Ji Fei’s face twisted in discomfort.","\"What’s wrong?\" Qin Xian chuckled.","\"It’s just... hearing words like ‘god’ or ‘foster’ now, it feels off. I’m not used to it anymore.\"","Everyone was reminded of the previous incident involving someone almost becoming a foster child, which indeed made such terms feel uncomfortable.","\"This one should be fine, though. She’s reportedly been trying to persuade them not to divorce and has been speaking up for my aunt.\""]}]);
